rs.githubusercontent.com/u/9310348?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcarr-rh","id":9310348,"login":"bcarr-rh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzMTAzNDg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/commits/205189a9ab56fbed0f7ac3ab9574d61dab1b80bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:34:01Z","email":"9310348+bcarr-rh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Benjamin Carr"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:34:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Group cluster-set labels by ordering, not by heading rows (#64)\n\nThe Labels view put a full-width heading row above each concern group,\ninside a table that already had a Label/Value header row. Two header\ntreatments meaning different things, stacked: one naming columns, one\nnaming a category of rows.\n\nThe markup said so too. PatternFly''s isSubheader is documented as \"part\nof a subheader of a nested header\" — a second tier of *column* headings\n— and the row carried scope=\"colgroup\", which claims to head a group of\ncolumns while describing a group of rows. A screen reader was told the\nwrong thing; scope=\"rowgroup\" is the correct value for what this was.\n\nRather than fix the scope and restyle, the headings go. The rows already\nsay what they are: Channel, Version, Catalog and Image read as a set\nwithout a caption announcing them. LABEL_CONCERN_ORDER still orders the\ngroups, which is what it was for — keeping aap-channel away from\naap-controller-replicas — so nothing about the reading order changes.\nGroups are separated by a rule instead, which needs a class because\nstylelint''s selector-max-type forbids a bare tbody + tbody.\n\nThe feature''s own on/off label is no longer listed. Measured against the\ncaptured live fixture, the State group was a single row for 71-87% of\nfeatures and appeared for all 39 of them, restating the value already\nshown in the State column of the row the panel expands from. Source and\nversion, by contrast, carries a median of 4 rows and is a lone row only\n0-5% of the time, so it was never the clunky half. Dropping the toggle\nrow takes 23 of the 39 features down to a single group, where no\nseparator is drawn at all; the 14 that genuinely span categories keep\ntheir structure. Sub-toggles such as aap-hub-disabled are untouched.\n\nTwo features in that fixture have no labels but their own switch, so\nthat case now renders an empty state rather than a header above nothing.\nA groupLabelFamilies test pins the shape it depends on.","tree":{"sha":"da2fd0555fb7f05d7884bbc5bb2e779538709e1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/git/trees/da2fd0555fb7f05d7884bbc5bb2e779538709e1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/git/commits/205189a9ab56fbed0f7ac3ab9574d61dab1b80bf","verification":{"payload":"tree da2fd0555fb7f05d7884bbc5bb2e779538709e1b\nparent d6f3469a9aae4cc2ab5fc7236762c7766928a5c1\nauthor Benjamin Carr <9310348+bcarr-rh@users.noreply.github.com> 1788968041 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788968041 -0600\n\nGroup cluster-set labels by ordering, not by heading rows (#64)\n\nThe Labels view put a full-width heading row above each concern group,\ninside a table that already had a Label/Value header row. Two header\ntreatments meaning different things, stacked: one naming columns, one\nnaming a category of rows.\n\nThe markup said so too. PatternFly''s isSubheader is documented as \"part\nof a subheader of a nested header\" — a second tier of *column* headings\n— and the row carried scope=\"colgroup\", which claims to head a group of\ncolumns while describing a group of rows. A screen reader was told the\nwrong thing; scope=\"rowgroup\" is the correct value for what this was.\n\nRather than fix the scope and restyle, the headings go. The rows already\nsay what they are: Channel, Version, Catalog and Image read as a set\nwithout a caption announcing them. LABEL_CONCERN_ORDER still orders the\ngroups, which is what it was for — keeping aap-channel away from\naap-controller-replicas — so nothing about the reading order changes.\nGroups are separated by a rule instead, which needs a class because\nstylelint''s selector-max-type forbids a bare tbody + tbody.\n\nThe feature''s own on/off label is no longer listed. Measured against the\ncaptured live fixture, the State group was a single row for 71-87% of\nfeatures and appeared for all 39 of them, restating the value already\nshown in the State column of the row the panel expands from. Source and\nversion, by contrast, carries a median of 4 rows and is a lone row only\n0-5% of the time, so it was never the clunky half. Dropping the toggle\nrow takes 23 of the 39 features down to a single group, where no\nseparator is drawn at all; the 14 that genuinely span categories keep\ntheir structure. Sub-toggles such as aap-hub-disabled are untouched.\n\nTwo features in that fixture have no labels but their own switch, so\nthat case now renders an empty state rather than a header above nothing.\nA groupLabelFamilies test pins the shape it depends on.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoXxpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjloQAGwFPYsVVH5