rr-rh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcarr-rh","id":9310348,"login":"bcarr-rh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzMTAzNDg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/commits/e7a6965a6e6c265fc75dd469ca33b32ac1cd6c9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:08:50Z","email":"9310348+bcarr-rh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Benjamin Carr"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:08:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Read the rebuild matrix from the released tag, not the branch (#58)\n\n* Read the rebuild matrix from the released tag, not the branch\n\nThe weekly rebuild exists to refresh the base packages under released\ncode, so it resolves the newest v*.*.* tag and checks it out. The matrix\nit fans out over was read from the default branch instead, which was\nharmless only while both listed the same targets.\n\nAdding 4.20 and 4.21 breaks that: main now declares three targets while\nthe newest tag, v0.0.1, contains only 4.22 and has no targets/4.20 or\ntargets/4.21 directory. Those legs would check out the tag and fail on\ncd, every Monday, until a release is cut that contains them.\n\nReading the list from the tag keeps the matrix and the source in step,\nand has the same effect for scan-published, which would otherwise try to\nscan :ocp4.20 before any such image had been pushed.\n\nWith no release tag at all there is nothing to rebuild, but an empty\nmatrix vector is a workflow error rather than a skip, so that case falls\nback to the checked-out file and leaves the existing \"found\" guard in\nthe rebuild job to skip the work.\n\n* Stamp the released version from the git tag\n\nThe release workflow used the tag only for the image tag and the OCI\nlabel. consolePlugin.version, which is what reaches plugin-manifest.json\nand is therefore the version the console reports, came from the\ncommitted package.json and was never touched. v0.0.1 was consistent only\nbecause the file already happened to say 0.0.1; tagging v0.0.2 would\nhave published images named v0.0.2-ocp4.2x whose manifests all reported\n0.0.1, and nothing would have failed.\n\nRequiring a bump commit before every tag would work, but it is a step\nthat has to be remembered, and getting it wrong is invisible until\nsomebody reads a manifest. The tag is already the single source of\ntruth for the release, so the workflow derives the version from it and\npackage.json carries a 0.0.0-dev placeholder, which is also a more\nhonest thing for an untagged local build to report.\n\nRewriting the checkout is safe and already precedented by the scheduled\nrebuild, which repins base digests the same way: the checkout is\nephemeral and nothing is committed, so the placeholder only moves by PR.\nyarn.lock records the workspace as 0.0.0-use.local rather than the real\nversion, so --immutable is unaffected — verified on all four lockfiles.\n\nsync-targets.mjs no longer copies the root version into the target\ndirectories. Nothing read it there, and the coupling would have made\nscripts/sync-targets.mjs --check fail inside the same release run that\ndid the stamping.\n\nVerified end to end: a tree stamped v0.0.2 produces a manifest reporting\n0.0.2, in the local bundle and inside the built image, while the image\nlabel keeps the per-target v0.0.2-ocp4.22 form. Non-semver tags are\nrejected before anything is built.","tree":{"sha":"3c8aa8a7d75225e618be77d9413ee0def6aed740","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/git/trees/3c8aa8a7d75225e618be77d9413ee0def6aed740"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/git/commits/e7a6965a6e6c265fc75dd469ca33b32ac1cd6c9d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c8aa8a7d75225e618be77d9413ee0def6aed740\nparent 1512964cb7f96876ec925cd497f912c9b85596bc\nauthor Benjamin Carr <9310348+bcarr-rh@users.noreply.github.com> 1788466130 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788466130 -0600\n\nRead the rebuild matrix from the released tag, not the branch (#58)\n\n* Read the rebuild matrix from the released tag, not the branch\n\nThe weekly rebuild exists to refresh the base packages under released\ncode, so it resolves the newest v*.*.* tag and checks it out. The matrix\nit fans out over was read from the default branch instead, which was\nharmless only while both listed the same targets.\n\nAdding 4.20 and 4.21 breaks that: main now declares three targets while\nthe newest tag, v0.0.1, contains only 4.22 and has no targets/4.20 or\ntargets/4.21 directory. Those legs would check out the tag and fail on\ncd, every Monday, until a release is cut that contains them.\n\nReading the list from the tag keeps the matrix and the source in step,\nand has the same effect for scan-published, which would otherwise try to\nscan :ocp4.20 before any such image had been pushed.\n\nWith no release tag at all there is nothing to rebuild, but an empty\nmatrix vector is a workflow error rather than a skip, so that case falls\nback to the checked-out file and leaves the existing \"found\" guard in\nthe rebuild job to skip the work.\n\n* Stamp the released version from the git tag\n\nThe release workflow used the tag only for the image tag and the OCI\nlabel. consolePlugin.version, which is what reaches plugin-manifest.json\nand is therefore the version the console reports, came from the\ncommitted package.json and was never touched. v0.0.1 was consistent only\nbecause the file already happened to say 0.0.1; tagging v0.0.2 would\nhave published images named v0.0.2-ocp4.2x whose manifests all reported\n0.0.1, and nothing would have failed.\n\nRequiring a bump commit before every tag would work, but it is a step\nthat has to be remembered, and getting it wrong is invisible until\nsomebody reads a manifest. The tag is already the single source of\ntruth for the release, so the workflow derives the version from it and\npackage.json carries a 0.0.0-dev placeholder, which is also a more\nhonest thing for an untagged local build to report.\n\nRewriting the checkout is safe and already precedented by the scheduled\nrebuild, which repins base digests the same way: the checkout is\nephemeral and nothing is committed, so the placeholder only moves by PR.\nyarn.lock records the workspace as 0.0.0-use.local rather than the real\nversion, so --immutable is unaffected — verified on all four lockfiles.\n\nsync-targets.mjs no longer copies the root version into the target\ndirectories. Nothing read it there, and the coupling would have made\nscripts/sync-targets.mjs --check fail inside the same release run that\ndid the stamping.\n\nVerified end to end: a tree stamped v0.0.2 produces a manifest reporting\n0.0.2, in the local bundle and inside the built image, while the image\nlabel keeps the per-target v0.0.2-ocp4.22 form. Non-semver tags are\nrejected before anything is built.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmdPSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkCAQAHcSquk3JZBf13mwdKBzEnOC\nGbxWyNoNLs7O+GEPfgkJ4A9wdnD76Qa999Kde71YeYBPb7cE9+xQjMza0WN2q+dg\ng/l4C29NsJboGBVSpBNxbe7q9YPXBmhaw/DCpGuh2vaXkicMjqexNznTzJsszMAW\nScNBCaCGAwelLT1HmVPJ7jgL7hPy+Jrx2kTSj5C8jchLrFX7NaBIKaM+/krpdlFd\nulouloAsjpQd3mUMVN7EAUELVmpYaUSgF51xuVEdzDsm8RxmtT9M1E7fyTotAci9\nPW4auCw13l7Hk2ehD+bDMEdo4e27DumoHyFNLpIWo+RenGNjf6qLZangfnI9MmrO\nqmPU6b83a1wg9Th66ppIvrjNy0NyEngB9QnzER3TSlLpIRTwHTMH0P81d87/tu8L\nJHYUtz3cKHtAecTXwYC93eU6fsxLPY1wf20vKK21qxpvvmrAeCEsA+TYmVlhGeMX\nQcR2/+X4iIygomwd6V5P6PGAhXpdSBeEOENH+ciBmfFgCpCFx6KB//CepRMP7DSC\nAHRfmkOoPX7lcdMZk+fBpJmTfVdn7OdWl0BohLIDz2G3CQxOeIiVXGlS1r/Ty6Wr\nDAAEDnTrvch7MNsENjU1y0Z5vo8HqDXPbWzeCG81b0kwJsyZpZxYRc1qWCtJu4li\nKt5LovY5HXUTzljYiu2t\n=V5c6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T20:08:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/commit/e7a6965a6e6c265fc75dd469ca33b32ac1cd6c9d","node_id":"C_kwDOTye_OtoAKGU3YTY5NjVhNmU2YzI2NWZjNzVkZDQ2OWNhMzNiMzJhYzFjZDZjOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/commit/1512964cb7f96876ec925cd497f912c9b85596bc","sha":"1512964cb7f96876ec925cd497f912c9b85596bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/commits/1512964cb7f96876ec925cd497f912c9b85596bc"}],"sha":"e7a6965a6e6c265fc75dd469ca33b32ac1cd6c9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/commits/e7a6965a6e6c265fc75dd469ca33b32ac1cd6c9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9310348?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bcarr-rh","id":9310348,"login":"bcarr-rh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzMTAzNDg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bcarr-rh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/commits/1512964cb7f96876ec925cd497f912c9b85596bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:18:46Z","email":"9310348+bcarr-rh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Benjamin Carr"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:18:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Build for OpenShift 4.20 and 4.21 alongside 4.22 (#53)\n\n* Build for OpenShift 4.20 and 4.21 alongside 4.22\n\nThe console supplies react, react-router and react-i18next as shared\nsingletons, and 4.20/4.21 predate the move to React 18 that landed in\n4.22. Verified against the SDKs'' own peerDependencies:\n\n  4.20/4.21  react ^17.0.1  react-router 5.3.x   react-i18next ^11.12.0\n  4.22       react ^18.3.1  react-router ~7.13.1 react-i18next ~16.5.8\n\nso adding them is not the data-only change ocp-targets.json anticipated.\nThree things had to move.\n\nRouting. react-router 5.3 exports neither Link nor useSearchParams; the\nReact 17 consoles share react-router-dom-v5-compat, which does, and 4.22\ndoes not share it at all. Components now import from ''@compat/router'',\nand each target supplies a one-line re-export naming its shared package\nliterally — module federation matches on the request string, so aliasing\nwould bundle a private copy of a singleton and fail silently at load.\n\nTest tooling. @testing-library/react 16 requires react-dom/client, which\ndoes not exist on React 17, and setup-tests.ts imported it globally, so\nevery suite failed to load on the older targets. configure() now comes\nfrom @testing-library/dom, which is version-independent; the React\nwrapper stays pinned per target for tests that render.\n\nDependency trees. The per-target lockfile layout ocp-targets.json\ndescribed is not buildable: Yarn 4 removed lockfileFilename, so\nyarn-4.20.lock cannot sit beside yarn.lock. A directory each is the only\nlayout Yarn 4 supports, and the only unit Dependabot updates — so both\n--immutable and automated bumps are kept, rather than trading one away.\nThe split is by axis, not by package: the toolchain is target-\nindependent and stays at the root under one bot-maintained lockfile,\nwhile everything bundled or read from the build cwd lives per target.\nscripts/sync-targets.mjs owns the contract pins and the router shim;\nDependabot owns the rest of each target file, and the two never write\nthe same field.\n\nTwo findings worth recording. ConsoleRemotePlugin reads package.json\nfrom process.cwd() to derive the shared-module set and to glob away\nPatternFly''s CSS, so the build must run from the target directory —\nscripts/ocp.sh does that. And its DynamicModuleImportPlugin appends a\nloader as a bare specifier after loader resolution, so resolveLoader\nnever sees it; NODE_PATH is what lets that require reach the target''s\nSDK. 4.20''s older SDK does not use that loader, which is exactly the\nkind of difference found only on whichever target was tried second.\n\nAlso declares comment-json at the root: i18next.config.ts imports it\ndirectly but relied on hoisting from the SDK, which no longer sits in\nthe root tree.\n\nVerified per target: lint clean, 95/95 tests, webpack build, and\n`yarn install --immutable` on all four lockfiles. Images build for 4.20\nand 4.22 and declare the right pluginAPI range; the emitted bundles\nreference react-router-dom-v5-compat on 4.20 and react-router on 4.22.\n\n* Bump UBI base images to clear fixable nginx and sqlite CVEs\n\nThe image scan gates on fixable HIGH/CRITICAL, and the pinned bases had\ngone two weeks stale:\n\n  nginx        CVE-2026-60005              1.26.3-9...24501 -> ...24599\n  sqlite-libs  CVE-2026-11822, -11824      3.34.1-10.el9_8  -> -11.el9_8\n\nDependabot #40 and #41 do not fix this. Their digests were resolved on\n24 Aug and still carry the vulnerable builds — verified by running rpm\nagainst each candidate — so merging them would leave the gate red. These\nare the digests currently behind :latest, which do carry the fixes.\n\nThat is the weekly rebuild''s job, not a PR''s, but the rebuild only\nrefreshes the published image; the committed pin is what ordinary PR\nbuilds are scanned against, so it has to move here.","tree":{"sha":"3ef47403fe491f9113364d823159a9fe0b1d4be1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/git/trees/3ef47403fe491f9113364d823159a9fe0b1d4be1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/auto-shift/autoshift-console-plugin/git/commits/1512964cb7f96876ec925cd497f912c9b85596bc","verification":{"payload":"tree 3ef47403fe491f9113364d823159a9fe0b1d4be1\nparent 7b431d6c69bd38d2bd4b294f1021aaa1eb7c1cdf\nauthor Benjamin Carr <9310348+bcarr-rh@users.noreply.github.com> 1788463126 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788463126 -0600\n\nBuild for OpenShift 4.20 and 4.21 alongside 4.22 (#53)\n\n* Build for OpenShift 4.20 and 4.21 alongside 4.22\n\nThe console supplies react, react-router and react-i18next as shared\nsingletons, and 4.20/4.21 predate the move to React 18 that landed in\n4.22. Verified against the SDKs'' own peerDependencies:\n\n  4.20/4.21  react ^17.0.1  react-router 5.3.x   react-i18next ^11.12.0\n  4.22       react ^18.3.1  react-router ~7.13.1 react-i18next ~16.5.8\n\nso adding them is not the data-only change ocp-targets.json anticipated.\nThree things had to move.\n\nRouting. react-router 5.3 exports neither Link nor useSearchParams; the\nReact 17 consoles share react-router-dom-v5-compat, which does, and 4.22\ndoes not share it at all. Components now import from ''@compat/router'',\nand each target supplies a one-line re-export naming its shared package\nliterally — module federation matches on the request string, so aliasing\nwould bundle a private copy of a singleton and fail silently at load.\n\nTest tooling. @testing-library/react 16 requires react-dom/client, which\ndoes not exist on React 17, and setup-tests.ts imported it globally, so\nevery suite failed to load on the older targets. configure() now comes\nfrom @testing-library/dom, which is version-independent; the React\nwrapper stays pinned per target for tests that render.\n\nDependency trees. The per-target lockfile layout ocp-targets.json\ndescribed is not buildable: Yarn 4 removed lockfileFilename, so\nyarn-4.20.lock cannot sit beside yarn.lock. A directory each is the only\nlayout Yarn 4 supports, and the only unit Dependabot updates — so both\n--immutable and automated bumps are kept, rather than trading one away.\nThe split is by axis, not by package: the toolchain is target-\nindependent and stays at the root under one bot-maintained lockfile,\nwhile everything bundled or read from the build cwd lives per target.\nscripts/sync-targets.mjs owns the contract pins and the router shim;\nDependabot owns the rest of each target file, and the two never write\nthe same field.\n\nTwo findings worth recording. ConsoleRemotePlugin reads package.json\nfrom process.cwd() to derive the shared-module set and to glob away\nPatternFly''s CSS, so the build must run from the target directory —\nscripts/ocp.sh does that. And its DynamicModuleImportPlugin appends a\nloader as a bare specifier after loader resolution, so resolveLoader\nnever sees it; NODE_PATH is what lets that require reach the target''s\nSDK. 4.20''s older SDK does not use that loader, which is exactly the\nkind of difference found only on whichever target was tried second.\n\nAlso declares comment-json at the root: i18next.config.ts imports it\ndirectly but relied on hoisting from the SDK, which no longer sits in\nthe root tree.\n\nVerified per target: lint clean, 95/95 tests, webpack build, and\n`yarn install --immutable` on all four lockfiles. Images build for 4.20\nand 4.22 and declare the right pluginAPI range; the emitted bundles\nreference react-router-dom-v5-compat on 4.20 and react-router on 4.22.\n\n* Bump UBI base images to clear fixable nginx and sqlite CVEs\n\nThe image scan gates on fixable HIGH/CRITICAL, and the pinned bases had\ngone two weeks stale:\n\n  nginx        CVE-2026-60005              1.26.3-9...24501 -> ...24599\n  sqlite-libs  CVE-2026-11822, -11824      3.34.1-10.el9_8  -> -11.el9_8\n\nDependabot #40 and #41 do not fix this. Their digests were resolved on\n24 Aug and still carry the vulnerable builds — verified by running rpm\nagainst each candidate — so merging them would leave the gate red. These\nare the digests currently behind :latest, which do carry the fixes.\n\nThat is the weekly rebuild''s job, not a PR''s, but the rebuild only\nrefreshes the published image; the committed pin is what ordinary PR\nbuilds are scanned against, so it has to move here.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmcgWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT5EQAAnKXJpVQV3R4JXLzKRzzqHd\nsMJbj7bBeXlwS630p1VgDsrUkxRSM4tqL4+GS0dHxYEx+5mG+0fcoqblKGf8Fkr4\nCW7dsFIl499TlJPwQWzVQ4o9UYlnYC6NjTplW4MC+CZZHAxX0TSBH1Qx3AnGMpLZ\nch7/bVelp2kef07egcVc6ZsfOZQ8r1DYK2EBE5ZEToWNPyiaDpQ87Xg66+IfQjFD\n4hGsQ1GhPGgdHPWGNQ+ZA