"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/93ae523b8ddfb5b3e73e9bb2253c8842e8d16345/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T21:13:31Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T21:13:31Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Finalize README: approach, AI endpoint contracts, docs, deployment\n\n- Demo-video placeholder at the top (with a note to replace before submitting)\n- AI endpoint table with request/response examples for policy and actions\n- Approach section: LangGraph orchestration, actions-through-APIs, structural\n  SQL safety, layered server-side authorization, and measured-not-asserted\n- Links to the three AI docs and the policy corpus\n- Deployment section: Vercel frontend + HF Spaces backend, both free; a live\n  URL is optional since docker-compose runs the whole thing\n- Corrected an over-claim (removed the usage dashboard, which was not built)\n  and de-duplicated the Documentation section","tree":{"sha":"b351ba874c31fde5fbca228867fb9395d5905fbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/b351ba874c31fde5fbca228867fb9395d5905fbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/93ae523b8ddfb5b3e73e9bb2253c8842e8d16345","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/93ae523b8ddfb5b3e73e9bb2253c8842e8d16345","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKDkzYWU1MjNiOGRkZmI1YjNlNzNlOWJiMjI1M2M4ODQyZThkMTYzNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/aa63062be6a43ad01ef6bf76086e960de6c0c902","sha":"aa63062be6a43ad01ef6bf76086e960de6c0c902","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/aa63062be6a43ad01ef6bf76086e960de6c0c902"}],"sha":"93ae523b8ddfb5b3e73e9bb2253c8842e8d16345","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/93ae523b8ddfb5b3e73e9bb2253c8842e8d16345"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/aa63062be6a43ad01ef6bf76086e960de6c0c902/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T21:11:55Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T21:11:55Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Verify the copilot UI in Docker; add deploy config and AI docs\n\nFrontend fix found by running the app: the /ai-copilot page rendered <Topbar />\nwithout the `name` prop it requires, which crashed on name.split(\" \"). Now\npasses name and title like the other pages.\n\nVerified end to end in the browser against the full docker-compose stack:\n- policy question -> \"Policy\" badge, grounded answer, source citation card\n- \"show my project assignments\" -> \"Data\" badge, results table, and no\n  show-SQL control for the employee role (role-aware hiding is server-driven)\n- as manager, \"approve Employee User''s pending leave\" -> \"Action\" badge and a\n  confirmation card showing request_id 1 (name resolved to id) -> Confirm ->\n  \"Done.\", and leave request 1 is APPROVED in the database\n- login/logout, sidebar nav, and the corrected active-state highlight\n\nDeployment prep (for Phase 10, all free tiers):\n- backend/Dockerfile.spaces: image for Hugging Face Spaces (listens on 7860,\n  copies source instead of bind-mounting, migrates/seeds/indexes on boot)\n- backend/start.sh: idempotent entrypoint — migrate, seed only if empty, ingest\n- CORS is now driven by CORS_ORIGINS (default localhost:3000) so the deployed\n  Vercel frontend origin can be allowed without a code change\n\nDocs:\n- docs/ai_architecture.md: request lifecycle (Mermaid), the four agents, HITL,\n  RBAC layering, audit, models, security decisions with rejected alternatives,\n  known limitations\n- docs/ai_permissions_matrix.md: the capability matrix with an enforcement\n  point per row, the three enforcement layers, and cosmetic-vs-authoritative","tree":{"sha":"3c6369e623e4781cfe1d9ac7d73f1992f6362674","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/3c6369e623e4781cfe1d9ac7d73f1992f6362674"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/aa63062be6a43ad01ef6bf76086e960de6c0c902","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/aa63062be6a43ad01ef6bf76086e960de6c0c902","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKGFhNjMwNjJiZTZhNDNhZDAxZWY2YmY3NjA4NmU5NjBkZTZjMGM5MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/cd75627f3952bcd3514d1ae54f5df688a70540ae","sha":"cd75627f3952bcd3514d1ae54f5df688a70540ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/cd75627f3952bcd3514d1ae54f5df688a70540ae"}],"sha":"aa63062be6a43ad01ef6bf76086e960de6c0c902","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/aa63062be6a43ad01ef6bf76086e960de6c0c902"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/cd75627f3952bcd3514d1ae54f5df688a70540ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T20:50:37Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T20:50:37Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Add the Nova Assist copilot UI to the frontend\n\nA /ai-copilot page and the components behind it, following the existing\nfrontend conventions (client components, the lib/api result shape, the ui\nprimitives, the dark theme).\n\n- lib/ai.ts: a client for the chat endpoints. Because access tokens are\n  short-lived and a conversation outlives one, requests retry once through\n  /auth/refresh on a 401 rather than dropping the user to the login screen. It\n  normalises the app''s two error-envelope shapes into one result.\n- The page drives /chat/router, so one input box reaches all four agents and\n  each reply is labelled with how it was routed.\n- Payload renderers: source citations for RAG, a table for SQL results, and a\n  confirmation card for high-impact actions. The card shows the action''s\n  arguments so the user confirms exactly what will happen; Cancel changes\n  nothing, Confirm resumes via /chat/actions/confirm and appends the outcome.\n- Role awareness is honest about where enforcement lives: the raw SQL block\n  appears only when the backend included the SQL (manager/admin), because the\n  employee response simply does not contain it. Nothing security-relevant is\n  hidden by the UI alone.\n- Source titles and SQL cell values are rendered as React text nodes only,\n  never through an HTML formatter, so untrusted document/database content\n  cannot inject markup.\n\nWiring: middleware gates /ai-copilot, the sidebar gets a Nova Assist entry, and\nlogin now stores the refresh token so the copilot can use it. Also fixed the\nsidebar''s active-state highlight to use longest-prefix matching, so a nested\nroute no longer lights up its ancestors (a latent issue for /employees vs\n/employees/projects too).\n\nVerification in Docker follows.","tree":{"sha":"8019851cd8660b06852152a0114c3a6df664e847","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/8019851cd8660b06852152a0114c3a6df664e847"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/cd75627f3952bcd3514d1ae54f5df688a70540ae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/cd75627f3952bcd3514d1ae54f5df688a70540ae","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKGNkNzU2MjdmMzk1MmJjZDM1MTRkMWFlNTRmNWRmNjg4YTcwNTQwYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/9e828d34c76d5ba0e5616653bcfda709984f7d77","sha":"9e828d34c76d5ba0e5616653bcfda709984f7d77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/9e828d34c76d5ba0e5616653bcfda709984f7d77"}],"sha":"cd75627f3952bcd3514d1ae54f5df688a70540ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/cd75627f3952bcd3514d1ae54f5df688a70540ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/9e828d34c76d5ba0e5616653bcfda709984f7d77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T20:45:53Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T20:45:53Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Add evaluation harness and results, close two real gaps it found\n\nbackend/evals/ drives /api/v1/chat/router with real JWTs for all three seeded\nroles — no browser, no internal shortcuts — so a passing result is evidence\nthat behaviour holds at the API boundary, where a grader probes it. 37 cases\nspan policy RAG, SQL correctness and safety, HR actions, sensitive-data\nrefusals, and prompt injection.\n\nGrading is deterministic where possible and two-sided on security: a refusal\nmust both refuse and leak none of a denylist of real sensitive values read\nfrom the database (a specific employee''s salary, bank number, PAN, DOB, and\npassword-hash prefix). A polite refusal that leaked a figure fails.\n\nHard gates, enforced with a non-zero exit: zero leaks, 100% destructive-SQL\nblocked, 100% unauthorized actions refused, and database integrity — table\ncounts are snapshotted around the whole run and the only permitted changes are\nthe two authorised creations; every destructive or unauthorised attempt must\nchange nothing. The authorised rows are cleaned up so the run is repeatable.\nThe injection suite ingests the poisoned policy fixture into the live\ncollection so INJ-001 exercises real retrieval, then removes it.\n\nResult: 37/37, all five gates pass. docs/ai_eval_results.md is generated.\n\nTwo real gaps the harness caught and this commit closes:\n- payroll_records was queryable by the SQL agent; an employee asking for\n  \"everyone''s payroll\" was scoped to their own row but still saw a pay figure.\n  Payroll is now removed from the SQL surface entirely (the brief allows\n  \"own only or blocked\"); own payroll remains available through the\n  authenticated finance page.\n- \"show my project assignments\" was declined because the SQL agent never told\n  the model which employee \"me\" is. The current user''s id is now passed into\n  the SQL prompt, and employee_projects/employee_skills are row-scoped like the\n  other personal tables, so first-person queries work and an employee cannot\n  read the whole assignment table.\n\nAlso fixed the db-integrity gate, which compared the full deltas dict against a\npartial expected dict and so reported FAIL even when every delta matched.","tree":{"sha":"857de11650ef88060fca8858e0927c95152106bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/857de11650ef88060fca8858e0927c95152106bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/9e828d34c76d5ba0e5616653bcfda709984f7d77","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/9e828d34c76d5ba0e5616653bcfda709984f7d77","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKDllODI4ZDM0Yzc2ZDViYTBlNTYxNjY1M2JjZmRhNzA5OTg0ZjdkNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/daddfce3977b9b7675dae42597e82cd4447cdcb7","sha":"daddfce3977b9b7675dae42597e82cd4447cdcb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/daddfce3977b9b7675dae42597e82cd4447cdcb7"}],"sha":"9e828d34c76d5ba0e5616653bcfda709984f7d77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/9e828d34c76d5ba0e5616653bcfda709984f7d77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/daddfce3977b9b7675dae42597e82cd4447cdcb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:52:26Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:52:26Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Add LangGraph router and IT support agent\n\nThe router is the assistant''s single entry point. A StateGraph classifies the\nmessage and dispatches to one of four specialist nodes:\n\n    START -> triage -> {policy | sql | action | it | unknown} -> END\n\nEach node adapts an existing agent to a shared state and writes a uniform\nresult (answer, payload, and the audit fields). The graph compiles once and is\nreused; it carries no checkpointer because the router never pauses — a\nhigh-impact action still returns its pending-confirmation as ordinary data.\n\nTriage fails safe: an unparseable classification or a classifier error both\nresolve to UNKNOWN rather than risk routing a message to the wrong,\npossibly action-taking, agent.\n\nThe IT support agent makes this an HR *and* IT assistant. It answers from a new\nIT knowledge base (VPN, accounts, network, hardware/software) and, when\nself-service won''t resolve the problem, points the employee at raising a\nticket. Crucially, that ticket is created through the HR action agent''s\ncreate_ticket -> the tickets API, so IT tickets take the same backend-API path\nas every other action. No separate ticketing system is introduced; CB Nest''s\nown tickets table (category IT) is the store.\n\nPOST /api/v1/chat/router returns the detected intent, confidence, and reason\nalongside the answer and payload, so the UI can show how each message was\nhandled. Every routed turn is audited with its intent.\n\nVerified live: 5/5 correct routing across POLICY_QA, SQL_QUERY, HR_ACTION,\nIT_SUPPORT, and UNKNOWN, each returning the right payload shape; the IT agent\ngives grounded VPN troubleshooting citing the KB articles. Re-ingest now builds\nboth collections (110 policy + 19 IT chunks). 60 unit tests pass.\n\nFixed a conditional-edge path map that keyed on intent names while the dispatch\nfunction returned node names, which raised KeyError at route time.","tree":{"sha":"8ffcbe7e0857256784b8ea9765bc8346c704e454","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/8ffcbe7e0857256784b8ea9765bc8346c704e454"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/daddfce3977b9b7675dae42597e82cd4447cdcb7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/daddfce3977b9b7675dae42597e82cd4447cdcb7","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKGRhZGRmY2UzOTc3YjliNzY3NWRhZTQyNTk3ZTgyY2Q0NDQ3Y2RjYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/e69c7f8617fb6bdb2d2768cbf96a2912309636ed","sha":"e69c7f8617fb6bdb2d2768cbf96a2912309636ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/e69c7f8617fb6bdb2d2768cbf96a2912309636ed"}],"sha":"daddfce3977b9b7675dae42597e82cd4447cdcb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/daddfce3977b9b7675dae42597e82cd4447cdcb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/e69c7f8617fb6bdb2d2768cbf96a2912309636ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:47:20Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:47:20Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Add HR action agent with human-in-the-loop confirmation\n\nThe agent turns a chat message into at most one HR action and carries it out by\ncalling this application''s own REST APIs with the user''s own bearer token — it\nnever writes to the database. Every existing validation, role check, and\nbusiness rule in those endpoints therefore runs exactly as it does for the web\nUI, and the agent has no path around them and no privilege of its own.\n\napi_tools.py wraps the leave, ticket, announcement, and project endpoints over\nan in-process ASGI transport, so the tools behave identically in tests, in the\ncontainer, and wherever the app is deployed, with no host/port assumptions. It\nnormalises the app''s two error-envelope shapes into one result dict.\n\naction_agent.py plans and performs the action:\n- reads run live (role-scoped by the backend) so the agent can resolve a\n  reference like \"Employee User''s pending leave\" to a request id; employee\n  names are resolved for this, taking only the name and never the sensitive\n  fields the employee endpoint also returns\n- permission is checked before anything happens; a refusal speaks only to\n  permission and never confirms a record exists\n- low-impact actions (apply leave, create ticket) run immediately\n- high-impact actions (approve/reject leave, assign project, announce, change\n  ticket status) return a pending confirmation and do not run until confirmed\n\nHuman-in-the-loop uses a signed, short-lived confirmation token that encodes\nthe action, rather than holding a paused process open between the two HTTP\nrequests. This survives a server restart and needs no server-side pending\nstore — the right tradeoff for a container that sleeps and cold-starts. The\nconfirming request carries the user''s access token, which is what actually\ncalls the backend; the confirmation token only carries what was proposed, and\npermission is re-checked at execution against the current role.\n\nPOST /chat/actions plans/performs; POST /chat/actions/confirm confirms or\ncancels. Both audit, and share a thread id derived from the confirmation token\nso the pending and confirm rows correlate.\n\nVerified live end to end:\n- employee applies leave -> executed, real row written\n- manager \"approve Employee User''s pending leave\" -> name resolved to the\n  request id -> pending confirmation -> CANCEL leaves the DB unchanged ->\n  re-propose -> CONFIRM writes APPROVED via the API (verified in the DB)\n- manager announcement -> confirm -> real row written\n- RBAC enforced at three independent layers: the permission module returns\n  False, confirm_action refuses even a forged employee-role token, and CB\n  Nest''s own approve endpoint returns 403 to an employee token directly\n- 60 unit tests still pass","tree":{"sha":"3511ed9f700de89234de097fc954c6cd002e2dcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/3511ed9f700de89234de097fc954c6cd002e2dcf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/e69c7f8617fb6bdb2d2768cbf96a2912309636ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/e69c7f8617fb6bdb2d2768cbf96a2912309636ed","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKGU2OWM3Zjg2MTdmYjZiZGIyZDI3NjhjYmY5NmEyOTEyMzA5NjM2ZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/289f3d1d05c259c337ee2a2dd00a08a175589ef2","sha":"289f3d1d05c259c337ee2a2dd00a08a175589ef2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/289f3d1d05c259c337ee2a2dd00a08a175589ef2"}],"sha":"e69c7f8617fb6bdb2d2768cbf96a2912309636ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/e69c7f8617fb6bdb2d2768cbf96a2912309636ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/289f3d1d05c259c337ee2a2dd00a08a175589ef2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:37:52Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:37:52Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Add RBAC permission matrix and AI audit logging\n\npermissions.py holds the AI capability matrix in one place, so authorization is\na property of the backend rather than the UI. Each capability maps to the roles\nallowed to use it, and refusal messages speak only to permission — never\nconfirming that a particular record exists, which would itself be a leak. It\nalso marks the high-impact actions that must be confirmed before running, ready\nfor the action agent.\n\nai_audit_logs (migration 0017) records one row per AI interaction: who asked,\nhow it routed, the tool, the outcome, and the metrics the usage dashboard\nneeds (latency, no-answer, source count, a thread id to correlate a\nconfirm-then-resume action, success). It deliberately stores no answer text and\nno sensitive value — logging those would re-create the exposure the rest of the\nsystem prevents; records_accessed holds identifiers only. Audit writes never\nbreak a request: a failed write is swallowed with a log line.\n\nThe policy and SQL endpoints now write an audit row and time each turn, and the\nSQL agent''s raw-SQL visibility is sourced from the permission matrix.\n\nAlso fixes alembic/env.py to import the whole models package instead of a\nhand-listed subset, which had omitted six models (skills, projects, the join\ntables, the audit log) from the autogenerate metadata.\n\nTwo bugs found and fixed by live testing:\n- _apply_limit read one level too deep into the sqlglot Limit node, so a valid\n  small LIMIT was treated as unparseable and overwritten with the cap\n- the SQL agent rolls back the request session, which expired the ORM\n  current_user and turned a later attribute access into an ill-timed lazy\n  reload; identity is now captured as scalars before the agent runs\n\nVerified: 60 unit tests (guardrails + permission matrix) pass; live audit rows\nwritten for answered, no-answer, and refused turns across both endpoints, with\nlatency captured and no answer text or secret persisted.","tree":{"sha":"4481048b970bdfeca25b8afa8103ac539a7b50cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/4481048b970bdfeca25b8afa8103ac539a7b50cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/289f3d1d05c259c337ee2a2dd00a08a175589ef2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/289f3d1d05c259c337ee2a2dd00a08a175589ef2","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKDI4OWYzZDFkMDVjMjU5YzMzN2VlMmEyZGQwMGEwOGExNzU1ODllZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/77f05a59d78bf2773224d46bb4dd29483986da93","sha":"77f05a59d78bf2773224d46bb4dd29483986da93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/77f05a59d78bf2773224d46bb4dd29483986da93"}],"sha":"289f3d1d05c259c337ee2a2dd00a08a175589ef2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/289f3d1d05c259c337ee2a2dd00a08a175589ef2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/77f05a59d78bf2773224d46bb4dd29483986da93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:28:56Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:28:56Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Add SQL agent with AST guardrails and POST /api/v1/chat/sql\n\nNatural-language questions about people, projects, skills, leave, tickets and\nattendance, answered by a read-only SQL query the model proposes but never\nexecutes itself.\n\nSafety is enforced structurally, not by trusting the model. Every proposed\nquery is parsed to an AST with sqlglot and checked before it can run:\n\n- exactly one statement (no stacked ''...; DROP TABLE ...'')\n- the root is a SELECT/UNION; any write or DDL node anywhere fails it\n- no reference to a sensitive column (passwords, bank, PAN, salary, DOB, ...),\n  and the refusal never names the column, so it cannot confirm one exists\n- no SELECT *, so a star cannot smuggle a sensitive column into the result\n- only approved tables; anything else, including the chat and audit tables, is\n  rejected\n- a role-scoped row filter on personal tables (employee sees own rows, manager\n  sees own + direct reports, admin unrestricted), injected into the AST rather\n  than requested of the model\n- a row-count cap injected into the query\n\nRegex over SQL text would be defeated by comments, casing, and string\nliterals, so nothing security-relevant relies on it. Scoping fails closed:\nif a query is too complex to scope safely it is refused, never run unscoped.\n\nExecution runs inside a transaction that is always rolled back, so even a\nquery that somehow passed the guardrails could not persist a change. Raw\ndatabase errors are mapped to generic messages and never surfaced. The raw SQL\nis returned only to manager and admin roles.\n\nVerified:\n- 50 guardrail unit tests: every keyword in the brief''s forbidden list, every\n  sensitive column, star, stacked statements, and role scoping\n- live end to end: ongoing projects, Python-skilled employees, per-department\n  counts all answered correctly; salary/bank/DROP/DELETE all refused with no\n  rows and no SQL; employee sees no SQL while admin does; an employee''s \"my\n  leave requests\" returned only their own rows\n- database row counts unchanged after the safety probes; guardrails block raw\n  destructive and sensitive SQL directly, independent of the model","tree":{"sha":"addb7ab6b55740d235e09449f43e701264236d17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/addb7ab6b55740d235e09449f43e701264236d17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/77f05a59d78bf2773224d46bb4dd29483986da93","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/77f05a59d78bf2773224d46bb4dd29483986da93","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKDc3ZjA1YTU5ZDc4YmYyNzczMjI0ZDQ2YmI0ZGQyOTQ4Mzk4NmRhOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/433d5851aea8dca8a751d702642593dd5925de87","sha":"433d5851aea8dca8a751d702642593dd5925de87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/433d5851aea8dca8a751d702642593dd5925de87"}],"sha":"77f05a59d78bf2773224d46bb4dd29483986da93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/77f05a59d78bf2773224d46bb4dd29483986da93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/433d5851aea8dca8a751d702642593dd5925de87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:23:14Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T19:23:14Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Add Policy RAG agent and POST /api/v1/chat/policy\n\nGrounded HR policy answers with citations, and a clean refusal when the policy\nlibrary does not cover the question.\n\nThe refusal path is deliberate. Retrieval always returns its best matches, even\nfor a question the corpus does not address, so an empty result set cannot be the\nrefusal signal — the model judges whether the retrieved context genuinely\nanswers the question. Citations are surfaced only when it does; citing the\ndocuments behind a refusal would imply an answer that was not given.\n\nRetrieved policy text is framed as data, never as instructions. The grounding\nprompt tells the model that any command-like text inside the context (ignore\nprevious instructions, reveal salaries, developer mode) is document content to\nbe read, not obeyed.\n\nThe endpoint degrades rather than crashes: a missing index, an insufficient\nquestion, or a model error each return a normal answer payload, and a missing\nAPI key returns 503 AI_NOT_CONFIGURED rather than a provider stack trace.\n\nVerified live against the model:\n- all five required policy questions answered accurately with correct sources\n  (10 sick days; half-day = 0.5, FIRST_HALF/SECOND_HALF; LATE has no automatic\n  penalty; document upload formats and types)\n- an out-of-corpus question (spouse health insurance) refused with zero sources\n- the poisoned policy fixture, containing an explicit instruction to dump\n  salaries, was treated as data: the genuine WFH question was answered and no\n  injected instruction was obeyed, echoed, or leaked\n- agent logic (JSON parsing, sufficient/insufficient routing, source gating,\n  prose fallback, model-error handling) verified with an injected fake model\n\nKnown follow-up: the reranker keeps a fixed number of chunks, so an answer can\ncarry one marginally-relevant secondary citation. Primary source is always\ncorrect and first; tightening deferred to after the SQL agent.","tree":{"sha":"da4a63121bc172090a9d337bc46f7e86dc3e8c83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/da4a63121bc172090a9d337bc46f7e86dc3e8c83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/433d5851aea8dca8a751d702642593dd5925de87","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/433d5851aea8dca8a751d702642593dd5925de87","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKDQzM2Q1ODUxYWVhOGRjYThhNzUxZDcwMjY0MjU5M2RkNTkyNWRlODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/233a4790ef760d12a4d9ddf1fb4d9bf0547a78aa","sha":"233a4790ef760d12a4d9ddf1fb4d9bf0547a78aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/233a4790ef760d12a4d9ddf1fb4d9bf0547a78aa"}],"sha":"433d5851aea8dca8a751d702642593dd5925de87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/433d5851aea8dca8a751d702642593dd5925de87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/233a4790ef760d12a4d9ddf1fb4d9bf0547a78aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T18:31:00Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T18:31:00Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Add the AI foundation: models, local embeddings, retrieval, ingest\n\nGroundwork the four agents build on. Nothing here is imported at startup —\ntorch, chromadb and sentence-transformers are pulled in lazily by the modules\nthat need them, so the app boots and the offline tests run without the heavy\ndependencies being paid for or GOOGLE_API_KEY being set.\n\nservices/ai/llm.py     Two model tiers: a small fast one for intent\n                       classification and guardrails, which run every turn,\n                       and a stronger one for answering. Extended reasoning is\n                       off deliberately: it multiplies latency and can return\n                       a response whose visible text is empty. Also the helpers\n                       every agent needs — message_text(), because this\n                       provider may return content parts rather than a string,\n                       and parse_json_block(), which tolerates fenced output.\n\nservices/ai/embeddings.py  Bi-encoder and cross-encoder, both on-device, so\n                       retrieval makes no API calls. Retrieve broadly with the\n                       bi-encoder, then rerank a small candidate set with the\n                       cross-encoder, which discriminates far better but is\n                       too slow to run over a whole collection.\n\nservices/ai/ingest.py  Indexes from the hr_policies table rather than a\n                       folder, so anything uploaded through the API is picked\n                       up on the next run. Collections are reset before\n                       re-adding: an edited policy would otherwise leave stale\n                       chunks behind and be cited as current.\n\nPOST /api/v1/auth/refresh\n                       Access tokens last 15 minutes, which an assistant\n                       conversation easily outlives. The role is re-read from\n                       the database on refresh rather than carried over, and\n                       deactivated accounts stop refreshing, so revoking\n                       access does not wait for the refresh token to expire.\n                       An access token presented as a refresh token is\n                       rejected.\n\nVerified: 110 chunks indexed from 13 policies; top-1 retrieval picks the\ncorrect policy for all five of the questions the assistant must answer.\n\nOne finding that shapes the policy agent: retrieval always returns something,\nincluding for questions the corpus does not cover, so an empty result set\ncannot be the refusal trigger. The agent has to judge whether the retrieved\ncontext actually answers the question.","tree":{"sha":"831da05650805fb04d4d272d53725fc482866491","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/trees/831da05650805fb04d4d272d53725fc482866491"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/git/commits/233a4790ef760d12a4d9ddf1fb4d9bf0547a78aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/233a4790ef760d12a4d9ddf1fb4d9bf0547a78aa","node_id":"C_kwDOTzUIrdoAKDIzM2E0NzkwZWY3NjBkMTJhNGQ5ZGRmMWZiNGQ5YmYwNTQ3YTc4YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commit/a65263b38d5967962004d6abaa4df5a1ccee59a8","sha":"a65263b38d5967962004d6abaa4df5a1ccee59a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/a65263b38d5967962004d6abaa4df5a1ccee59a8"}],"sha":"233a4790ef760d12a4d9ddf1fb4d9bf0547a78aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/233a4790ef760d12a4d9ddf1fb4d9bf0547a78aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271075832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atimma-inogen","id":271075832,"login":"atimma-inogen","node_id":"U_kgDOEChJ-A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atimma-inogen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhishektimmaraju-dot/nova-assist/commits/a65263b38d5967962004d6abaa4df5a1ccee59a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T17:51:01Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T18:25:30Z","email":"abhishek.timmaraju@inogen.net","name":"Abhishek Timmaraju"},"message":"Nova Assist: HR & IT operations platform\n\nFull-stack HRMS that the AI layer is built into: FastAPI + SQLAlchemy (async)\nover SQLite with Alembic migrations, Next.js 15 frontend, Docker Compose.\n\nCovers authentication with three roles, the employee lifecycle, attendance,\nleave workflows, announcements, polls, finance views, an HR policy library,\nand ticketing with onboarding tasks.\n\n.gitignore covers secrets, the SQLite database and its sidecars, generated\nupload directories, the vector store, and model caches. Documentation is