b.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/66e94cbfc7b70f521ff2a2246e6fe63df7c709f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T17:05:14Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T17:05:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(usage-limit): list workspace limits in a billing tab (#25741)\n\n<img width=\"1151\" height=\"313\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-10 at 16 21 26\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f9fb580a-94cb-4fc1-8a6c-290cd88c5bbb\"\n/>\n\n\nSecond of three stacked PRs. **Depends on #25740** (the server API) —\nreview that one first; this diff is front only.\n\nAdds a **Limits tab** to Settings > Billing, after Plans, listing every\nquota the workspace owns. Read only: creating and editing them is #NEXT.\n\n## What you get\n\n- A row per limit: the usage it covers (`AI · AI chat`), the spender\nwith its real name and picture (workspace logo, member avatar, app logo,\nor a type icon for API keys and agents), how much is already spent, and\nthe period.\n- **Used** is a percentage plus a progress ring, blue until 60%, orange\npast it, red past 80% or once nothing is left. Hovering gives the\nabsolute figures.\n- **Search** covers the usage and the spender, so the workspace''s own\nname matches. The **filter** narrows by usage or by spender type, and\nonly offers values the rows actually hold.\n\n## Shared surfaces touched\n\n- `ProgressRing` moved out of `modules/ai/components/internal` into\n`@/ui/feedback/progress-ring` so billing can reuse it; the AI chat\nwrapper keeps its own colour thresholds and behaves exactly as before.\n- `SettingsTableListSection`''s chevron column had an `auto` track, which\nresolved narrower in the header (an empty cell) than in the body,\npushing right-aligned columns out of line. It is now a fixed track.\n**This also fixes the workspace unsubscribe-topics and email-groups\ntables**, which use the same component — worth a look when reviewing.\n\n## Note\n\n`generated-metadata/graphql.ts` here still declares the three documents\nbelonging to the next PR in the stack. It is a superset, everything\ncompiles, and it corrects itself in #NEXT; regenerating on this branch\nalone would drop them.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25741?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"2c738a902051b3f3a1e59e272530761f03725af5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/2c738a902051b3f3a1e59e272530761f03725af5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/66e94cbfc7b70f521ff2a2246e6fe63df7c709f7","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c738a902051b3f3a1e59e272530761f03725af5\nparent 2769f54b959afe02bb1e6bbddeaab2a3b41872f4\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1789146314 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789146314 +0000\n\nfeat(usage-limit): list workspace limits in a billing tab (#25741)\n\n<img width=\"1151\" height=\"313\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-10 at 16 21 26\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f9fb580a-94cb-4fc1-8a6c-290cd88c5bbb\"\n/>\n\n\nSecond of three stacked PRs. **Depends on #25740** (the server API) —\nreview that one first; this diff is front only.\n\nAdds a **Limits tab** to Settings > Billing, after Plans, listing every\nquota the workspace owns. Read only: creating and editing them is #NEXT.\n\n## What you get\n\n- A row per limit: the usage it covers (`AI · AI chat`), the spender\nwith its real name and picture (workspace logo, member avatar, app logo,\nor a type icon for API keys and agents), how much is already spent, and\nthe period.\n- **Used** is a percentage plus a progress ring, blue until 60%, orange\npast it, red past 80% or once nothing is left. Hovering gives the\nabsolute figures.\n- **Search** covers the usage and the spender, so the workspace''s own\nname matches. The **filter** narrows by usage or by spender type, and\nonly offers values the rows actually hold.\n\n## Shared surfaces touched\n\n- `ProgressRing` moved out of `modules/ai/components/internal` into\n`@/ui/feedback/progress-ring` so billing can reuse it; the AI chat\nwrapper keeps its own colour thresholds and behaves exactly as before.\n- `SettingsTableListSection`''s chevron column had an `auto` track, which\nresolved narrower in the header (an empty cell) than in the body,\npushing right-aligned columns out of line. It is now a fixed track.\n**This also fixes the workspace unsubscribe-topics and email-groups\ntables**, which use the same component — worth a look when reviewing.\n\n## Note\n\n`generated-metadata/graphql.ts` here still declares the three documents\nbelonging to the next PR in the stack. It is a superset, everything\ncompiles, and it corrects itself in #NEXT; regenerating on this branch\nalone would drop them.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25741?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-n