:"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/2769f54b959afe02bb1e6bbddeaab2a3b41872f4","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDI3NjlmNTRiOTU5YWZlMDJiYjFlNmJiZGRlYWFiMmEzYjQxODcyZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/1dd8bad5a9d6012c74ca1692bf5aabb938e311bf","sha":"1dd8bad5a9d6012c74ca1692bf5aabb938e311bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/1dd8bad5a9d6012c74ca1692bf5aabb938e311bf"}],"sha":"2769f54b959afe02bb1e6bbddeaab2a3b41872f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/2769f54b959afe02bb1e6bbddeaab2a3b41872f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45695613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/1dd8bad5a9d6012c74ca1692bf5aabb938e311bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:31:01Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:31:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(usage-limit): expose usage limits over the metadata API (#25740)\n\nFirst of three stacked PRs adding usage-limit management to Settings >\nBilling. This one is server only: it exposes the API the next two\nconsume, and nothing in the product calls it yet.\n\n## What it adds\n\n- **Queries**: `usageQuotasWithConsumption` (every limit the workspace\nowns, with what it has already spent), `usageQuotaDefinitions` (the\nresources, operations, spenders and meters a limit may be scoped to,\nplus the workspace''s entitlement), and `usageQuotaScopeConsumption`\n(what a given scope has spent this period).\n- **Mutations**: `createUsageLimit`, `updateUsageLimit`,\n`deleteUsageLimit`, with `assertScopeIsFree` refusing a scope another\nlimit already covers.\n- Reads live in `UsageQuotaConsumptionService`, allow-lists in\n`UsageQuotaDefinitionService`, so the resolver no longer reaches into\nthe enforcement service.\n\n## Refactors carried along\n\n- **Every ClickHouse query now sits in `UsageAnalyticsService`**; the\nquota engine calls it rather than writing SQL. The consumption queries\ngroup on the full projection key, so `consumption_by_scope` and\n`billing_by_workspace_period` are actually used — checked with\n`force_optimize_projection=1`.\n- `computeQuotaConsumed` takes only the four fields it matches rows on,\ninstead of a whole counter.\n- `INTERNAL_CREDITS_PER_DISPLAY_CREDIT` moves to twenty-shared,\nreplacing the copies in the billing resolver, the admin panel and the\nproduct formatter.\n\n## Tests\n\nUnit tests on every new util, and 9 integration tests over create /\nupdate / delete and the list, including the scope-conflict refusals.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **this PR** — server API\n2. list the limits in a billing tab\n3. create and edit them\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25740?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"6f1d574c56b915d71b1ea1a634ece4a6f999ec97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/6f1d574c56b915d71b1ea1a634ece4a6f999ec97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/1dd8bad5a9d6012c74ca1692bf5aabb938e311bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f1d574c56b915d71b1ea1a634ece4a6f999ec97\nparent f10eaacacd126e4022c7133290aecbb9f3cb2105\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1789144261 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789144261 +0000\n\nfeat(usage-limit): expose usage limits over the metadata API (#25740)\n\nFirst of three stacked PRs adding usage-limit management to Settings >\nBilling. This one is server only: it exposes the API the next two\nconsume, and nothing in the product calls it yet.\n\n## What it adds\n\n- **Queries**: `usageQuotasWithConsumption` (every limit the workspace\nowns, with what it has already spent), `usageQuotaDefinitions` (the\nresources, operations, spenders and meters a limit may be scoped to,\nplus the workspace''s entitlement), and `usageQuotaScopeConsumption`\n(what a given scope has spent this period).\n- **Mutations**: `createUsageLimit`, `updateUsageLimit`,\n`deleteUsageLimit`, with `assertScopeIsFree` refusing a scope another\nlimit already covers.\n- Reads live in `UsageQuotaConsumptionService`, allow-lists in\n`UsageQuotaDefinitionService`, so the resolver no longer reaches into\nthe enforcement service.\n\n## Refactors carried along\n\n- **Every ClickHouse query now sits in `UsageAnalyticsService`**; the\nquota engine calls it rather than writing SQL. The consumption queries\ngroup on the full projection key, so `consumption_by_scope` and\n`billing_by_workspace_period` are actually used — checked with\n`force_optimize_projection=1`.\n- `computeQuotaConsumed` takes only the four fields it matches rows on,\ninstead of a whole counter.\n- `INTERNAL_CREDITS_PER_DISPLAY_CREDIT` moves to twenty-shared,\nreplacing the copies in the billing resolver, the admin panel and the\nproduct formatter.\n\n## Tests\n\nUnit tests on every new util, and 9 integration tests over create /\nupdate / delete and the list, including the scope-conflict refusals.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **this PR** — server API\n2. list the limits in a billing tab\n3. create and edit them\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25740?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCzVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe/wQAGWc4MqLCBhfTrHhH72dSzV6\nMP1nsmDok/vZKmn6neBr64fIkN9LtLXXpFdNn2aJTjqidGXE8B3RZUg+nHJjTTdP\nPxHy51C26vq0bqRkGG9wB/DKRVR8tknSfriJKpfdzZEu23F43+pHSIYLGXWw063B\nZTW9+Vc4Xg7dp4nlvlIP78X2x4Tow4kzcnpZN4jDRS1hjXLIzs/bhz84KKwATMgo\n6jd0Ips2ga+a37KV/tMutn01i7yj9mCEJkSTBsdH2K9yLjtj5kMg2WiT7RCF+cDc\nr35FhQW91kbOy6epnX2+hInI5Z3d0joNrbvDjaTIB5spb4bLwZ4De1g4zp0ScJs0\nU7XPFTaXESXj6LKjtdXFuIzPCSoKo3RSYzCRIRfhsUY02Ul8xh14Ms48RrciN6pB\nv2wZ6+P6SWnGdzfCvNpq8PAuTIsmdDzMEcGoSBIhpQx90YCBt8QHZB60/04XROfE\ncdY8ETC/HiaXJg5nfNbISRmlU8yWJ1nmL1AMCgqhMaaSz78AZHkH8Q9wszVX+AbI\ny0JaFIEYcQrySDe053DMiWEOxvaCXCd7TO/98dTtv20iD2t36QIAC+ZAqQtSqgP2\n5PUNu5SMusyWL85WOgZ9wFs6ROakbWFGMVUWBvQVwSCnWr3Mldy8IjhuC73CieA8\nD9beUIbiwcwEMrBWrhrr\n=rFRh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/1dd8bad5a9d6012c74ca1692bf5aabb938e311bf","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDFkZDhiYWQ1YTlkNjAxMmM3NGNhMTY5MmJmNWFhYmI5MzhlMzExYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/f10eaacacd126e4022c7133290aecbb9f3cb2105","sha":"f10eaacacd126e4022c7133290aecbb9f3cb2105","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/f10eaacacd126e4022c7133290aecbb9f3cb2105"}],"sha":"1dd8bad5a9d6012c74ca1692bf5aabb938e311bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/1dd8bad5a9d6012c74ca1692bf5aabb938e311bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/f10eaacacd126e4022c7133290aecbb9f3cb2105/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:23:45Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:23:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"List every kind pull does not export yet (#25811)\n\n## What\n\nThe sync and recovery page tells a developer what `yarn twenty pull`\ndoes not write, and the \"Not exported yet\" bullet is incomplete. It\nnames roles and permissions, command menu items, logic functions and\nfront components. Seven more kinds are also not exported.\n\nThat page is the contract someone reads before deciding whether a pulled\ntree is safe to apply, so a partial list reads as a promise that\neverything else round-trips.\n\n## How\n\nCompleted the bullet against what\n`application-manifest-export.service.ts` actually assembles. The\nexporter hardcodes nine sections to `[]`:\n\n```ts\nlogicFunctions: [],   frontComponents: [],  permissionFlags: [],\nroles: [],            skills: [],           agents: [],\npublicAssets: [],     commandMenuItems: [], timelineActivityTypes: [],\n```\n\nand two more never reach the manifest at all: `connectionProviders` is\nan optional key the export never sets, and\n`application.applicationVariables` is not emitted by\n`fromFlatApplicationToApplicationManifest`.\n\nSo the bullet gains skills and agents, connection providers, application\nvariables, public assets and timeline activity types. Permission flags\nstay folded into the existing \"roles and permissions\".\n\nNothing else on the page changes. The advice immediately below it is\nalready correct and unchanged:\n\n> push a pulled tree back with `yarn twenty apply --no-delete` until the\nmissing kinds are covered. A pruning `yarn twenty apply` would delete\nthem\n\n## Why it matters\n\nDeletion inference destroys any row of the application that the incoming\nmanifest does not mention, so every kind on that list is destroyed by a\npruning apply of a pulled tree. Measured on a seeded dev workspace,\npulling the Custom application and applying without `--no-delete`\ndestroyed 19 rows, and because `core.\"roleTarget\".\"roleId\"` is `ON\nDELETE CASCADE` it left 1004 of 1005 members with no role.\n\nConnection providers are the reason this is worth correcting rather than\nleaving to the export work.\n`core.\"connectedAccount\".\"connectionProviderId\"` is `ON DELETE CASCADE`\nand is the only inbound cascade on that table, so losing a provider\ntakes its connected accounts with it, along with their encrypted access\nand refresh tokens. A developer who read the old list would have no\nreason to expect that.\n\nThe list shrinks again as each kind gets exported.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25811?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"29baed73fc1c4cbeeacdd96b89bdeb2173c49728","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/29baed73fc1c4cbeeacdd96b89bdeb2173c49728"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/f10eaacacd126e4022c7133290aecbb9f3cb2105","verification":{"payload":"tree 29baed73fc1c4cbeeacdd96b89bdeb2173c49728\nparent e1eb3f6026e1d2b464bd45d2c3dcadf60a740abd\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789143825 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789143825 +0200\n\nList every kind pull does not export yet (#25811)\n\n## What\n\nThe sync and recovery page tells a developer what `yarn twenty pull`\ndoes not write, and the \"Not exported yet\" bullet is incomplete. It\nnames roles and permissions, command menu items, logic functions and\nfront components. Seven more kinds are also not exported.\n\nThat page is the contract someone reads before deciding whether a pulled\ntree is safe to apply, so a partial list reads as a promise that\neverything else round-trips.\n\n## How\n\nCompleted the bullet against what\n`application-manifest-export.service.ts` actually assembles. The\nexporter hardcodes nine sections to `[]`:\n\n```ts\nlogicFunctions: [],   frontComponents: [],  permissionFlags: [],\nroles: [],            skills: [],           agents: [],\npublicAssets: [],     commandMenuItems: [], timelineActivityTypes: [],\n```\n\nand two more never reach the manifest at all: `connectionProviders` is\nan optional key the export never sets, and\n`application.applicationVariables` is not emitted by\n`fromFlatApplicationToApplicationManifest`.\n\nSo the bullet gains skills and agents, connection providers, application\nvariables, public assets and timeline activity types. Permission flags\nstay folded into the existing \"roles and permissions\".\n\nNothing else on the page changes. The advice immediately below it is\nalready correct and unchanged:\n\n> push a pulled tree back with `yarn twenty apply --no-delete` until the\nmissing kinds are covered. A pruning `yarn twenty apply` would delete\nthem\n\n## Why it matters\n\nDeletion inference destroys any row of the application that the incoming\nmanifest does not mention, so every kind on that list is destroyed by a\npruning apply of a pulled tree. Measured on a seeded dev workspace,\npulling the Custom application and applying without `--no-delete`\ndestroyed 19 rows, and because `core.\"roleTarget\".\"roleId\"` is `ON\nDELETE CASCADE` it left 1004 of 1005 members with no role.\n\nConnection providers are the reason this is worth correcting rather than\nleaving to the export work.\n`core.\"connectedAccount\".\"connectionProviderId\"` is `ON DELETE CASCADE`\nand is the only inbound cascade on that table, so losing a provider\ntakes its connected accounts with it, along with their encrypted access\nand refresh tokens. A developer who read the old list would have no\nreason to expect that.\n\nThe list shrinks again as each kind gets exported.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25811?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCsRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALH4QAJYgYPoyRn6Vj/Wg/j1PG8KN\n0GNS8fiMuS1dSC3c90Iyqphz6+joFkqsf6qj8RjXkXK0wcoTyNhV+5QLD4gG2v+W\n/uQ5FAdZ2M1shyGf3hXOJeEIcPt/LTGwkJgiTCpuz8WT63yy6tIFUkCudSph/9Me\n6d/e7F4kruoK2I4rEf5KO54a7hipKZflIZAz+gwdcNBbH8ArhQnm/VqEAGGN4pb6\nMYPtoeMITMRLVGZkUDVrUCDeWe7TmNl/ScI0KTPfT2bKGJ+R99OD4p99MrIbA+km\nPC6gT3Y97Ww/OkB20I9OVgtGDYk6mmzbqTHNugb9/xxF1geGu3Gv/sF4WRt/Zvs8\nMxr7xBJHI9NxIe3UYpl2Po/UuMPQ1qKhXgqfRrQumWn3gvrZFPKb6InOVIYTXpPE\nmVU1h8BOKTn23QMvE3zp47zy6yjKPBtW1mS53F1LTI69ccw71XzSbanUw0pvm2wy\nd5Xup0Umt/cYDuVOhvOiQK3UpQe6A69+jUr6bxDCU3z/pMWo8uC5lS7XOsHW9TpO\nXQOm52YcSTth0BOFrKpY0FvDg4bzma1vBmEkhcTpkTLuo1Ol7z52xU0Txjji7+0n\nst1N/82TJ1ErL0eWAI41B9uAL0UaAPPbMsMbcNUvccFYwd5mHTc0PO7Mb9iD7eIx\nH3GUNgdCGAd1Q1FMYEw7\n=hGeU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/f10eaacacd126e4022c7133290aecbb9f3cb2105","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGYxMGVhYWNhY2QxMjZlNDAyMmM3MTMzMjkwYWVjYmI5ZjNjYjIxMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/e1eb3f6026e1d2b464bd45d2c3dcadf60a740abd","sha":"e1eb3f6026e1d2b464bd45d2c3dcadf60a740abd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/e1eb3f6026e1d2b464bd45d2c3dcadf60a740abd"}],"sha":"f10eaacacd126e4022c7133290aecbb9f3cb2105","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/f10eaacacd126e4022c7133290aecbb9f3cb2105"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19412894?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonapara","id":19412894,"login":"Bonapara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDEyODk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/e1eb3f6026e1d2b464bd45d2c3dcadf60a740abd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:55:03Z","email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:55:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Migrate existing Canvas tabs to vertical lists (#25511)\n\n## Intro\n\nThis follows my previous layout PRs. They introduced explicit widget\nheight behavior and simpler manifests; this migration updates existing\nworkspace-created Canvas tabs to use those settings.\n\n## Changes\n\nConvert a Canvas tab to a vertical list with one `TAB_VIEWPORT` widget\nonly when both the tab and widget belong to the workspace''s custom\napplication. App-owned tabs and widgets keep their Canvas data and\noverrides so older manifests can still sync. App authors can migrate\ntheir manifests explicitly.\n\nLeave empty tabs, tabs without exactly one undeleted active widget,\nauthored non-Canvas positions, and cross-tab widget overrides unchanged.\n\nThe migration is forward-only, with no backup table. Each workspace''s\ntab and widget updates are atomic. Retries also flush both page-layout\ncaches if a previous attempt committed before cache invalidation failed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 20 PostgreSQL migration tests, also run against the actual Twenty\nschema.\n- 9 app-sync integration tests, including migration followed by syncing\nan unchanged Canvas manifest with a position override. The regression\nfails before the fix and passes after it.\n- Server typechecking and focused lint pass.\n\nStack 4/4. Merge the prerequisites first.\n\nCloses twentyhq/core-team-issues#2877.\n\nReview and merge order:\n\n1. [App CI repairs](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25531)\n2. [Widget height\nbehavior](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25512)\n3. [Manifest authoring](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25513)\n4. [Existing Canvas data\nmigration](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25511)","tree":{"sha":"cbdb53a42c907fcab03d840712ad3ae47020f8fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/cbdb53a42c907fcab03d840712ad3ae47020f8fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/e1eb3f6026e1d2b464bd45d2c3dcadf60a740abd","verification":{"payload":"tree cbdb53a42c907fcab03d840712ad3ae47020f8fd\nparent 94272b6080665735e14b5afa27a4e369e1e24668\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789142103 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789142103 +0000\n\nMigrate existing Canvas tabs to vertical lists (#25511)\n\n## Intro\n\nThis follows my previous layout PRs. They introduced explicit widget\nheight behavior and simpler manifests; this migration updates existing\nworkspace-created Canvas tabs to use those settings.\n\n## Changes\n\nConvert a Canvas tab to a vertical list with one `TAB_VIEWPORT` widget\nonly when both the tab and widget belong to the workspace''s custom\napplication. App-owned tabs and widgets keep their Canvas data and\noverrides so older manifests can still sync. App authors can migrate\ntheir manifests explicitly.\n\nLeave empty tabs, tabs without exactly one undeleted active widget,\nauthored non-Canvas positions, and cross-tab widget overrides unchanged.\n\nThe migration is forward-only, with no backup table. Each workspace''s\ntab and widget updates are atomic. Retries also flush both page-layout\ncaches if a previous attempt committed before cache invalidation failed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 20 PostgreSQL migration tests, also run against the actual Twenty\nschema.\n- 9 app-sync integration tests, including migration followed by syncing\nan unchanged Canvas manifest with a position override. The regression\nfails before the fix and passes after it.\n- Server typechecking and focused lint pass.\n\nStack 4/4. Merge the prerequisites first.\n\nCloses twentyhq/core-team-issues#2877.\n\nReview and merge order:\n\n1. [App CI repairs](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25531)\n2. [Widget height\nbehavior](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25512)\n3. [Manifest authoring](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25513)\n4. [Existing Canvas data\nmigration](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25511)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCRnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqjwQAALiMWuSHrlupcDgu9BeVd3N\n5VvobyqgcB/Eplme7of9JyN2UcIKphvTu3R55Gj221/Kr/mVMZa7WgM34Y3FHWKp\nQEBajqIgNOXQRFf6Zis/qJaUYzyAJLgNTThjLP7xICcJuRlc+Ca/rcgp+8hyAYIl\nGduuCo7dTbDMffC5L77LhU3rwM+tL3ZkDCl9Oq/NupST5k5T1GhedkMqCxHBjEVy\nwvzglBZCbYcgGVJ2y+8DcFtYWpO1YR/9SvQp8bCFzwGZ0ptnihN3Ts2j76XsoSDx\nEJ4YfzZ9mJg+SrwvGoP5fGZP/OulHtEbyA85dzZE89Ghz8R82UR3TZ+JguWJgoMD\nXzUuFNC2u0M/pGdMGqfsNDUpK2kuoF/HmtXs67K1A+UXvEKP3h2HN0A1dg1KaMdU\nsOfXzOCpzcTvZ01ULj1EDHnJOMvcm8N7tuhn9OW9qPYBkkIECMJ29ctVA9o6omPa\niEC8r52AgV45D8xX0HvYAyk7a06TbENaVlAhrFb30/Jr06ctNCLMhMWKQ27ln7Lq\n5+3edogDlQJ/2YykGjrE76yWoAVnh9le47Llz/nMY7bLt501FQWreDC/zyqvKrLQ\nPKeCsB/a3XBLtsYaITb1pb6luoM+TeowcYk46JBH2ZduK62UTG96NaEP3J/ppRBW\nM3GjGCnmYdfLQBsKOv/w\n=/IgD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/e1eb3f6026e1d2b464bd45d2c3dcadf60a740abd","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGUxZWIzZjYwMjZlMWQyYjQ2NGJkNDVkMmMzZGNhZGY2MGE3NDBhYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/94272b6080665735e14b5afa27a4e369e1e24668","sha":"94272b6080665735e14b5afa27a4e369e1e24668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/94272b6080665735e14b5afa27a4e369e1e24668"}],"sha":"e1eb3f6026e1d2b464bd45d2c3dcadf60a740abd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/e1eb3f6026e1d2b464bd45d2c3dcadf60a740abd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45695613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/94272b6080665735e14b5afa27a4e369e1e24668/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:47:53Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:47:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop re-checking already-warned workspaces every hour in CleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob (#25800)\n\n## Problem\n\n`CleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob` runs hourly over ~2850 suspended\nworkspaces on prod-eu and takes **1 to 10 minutes** (median ~5 min). The\nSentry cron monitor budgets 5 minutes, so the monitor sits right on its\nthreshold and flips between resolved and regression nearly every hour.\nThe issue is at 3471 occurrences.\n\nRuntimes from the worker logs over 24h:\n\n```\n09-10 20:00  605s      09-11 04:00  509s\n09-10 22:00  538s      09-11 08:00  312s\n09-10 23:00  436s      09-11 10:00  602s\n09-11 00:00  322s      09-11 11:00  475s\n```\n\nAlmost all of that time is spent on workspaces that were already warned.\n`warnWorkspaceMembers` loaded the full workspace ORM context via\n`loadWorkspaceMembers`, then read one user var per member (each\n`userVarsService.get` fans out to 3 core queries), and only then\ndiscovered the workspace was already warned, logged `already warned`,\nand returned.\n\nProd logs show **~986 of those per run**, against ~8 workspaces that\nactually get a new warning. The job also stalls the worker event loop\nfor 10-95s at a time while doing it, which is enough for BullMQ to\ndeclare the job stalled and hand it to a second pod.\n\n## Change\n\nResolve the already-warned workspaces up front with a single query on\n`keyValuePair`, and skip them before touching the workspace ORM. ~986\nworkspace ORM loads per run become 0.\n\nThat check is now keyed on the workspace rather than on its current\nmembers. So reactivation has to clear every warn var of the workspace\ninstead of only those belonging to members it can still load, otherwise\na departed member''s stale row would suppress a later warning. That also\ncollapses `CleanWorkspaceDeletionWarningUserVarsJob` to a single delete.","tree":{"sha":"9331c666298b8a6990aac7095e1d158ea671c798","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/9331c666298b8a6990aac7095e1d158ea671c798"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/94272b6080665735e14b5afa27a4e369e1e24668","verification":{"payload":"tree 9331c666298b8a6990aac7095e1d158ea671c798\nparent 8f1355d96892e650d47c9955b65aae0eace09f1c\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1789141673 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789141673 +0000\n\nStop re-checking already-warned workspaces every hour in CleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob (#25800)\n\n## Problem\n\n`CleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob` runs hourly over ~2850 suspended\nworkspaces on prod-eu and takes **1 to 10 minutes** (median ~5 min). The\nSentry cron monitor budgets 5 minutes, so the monitor sits right on its\nthreshold and flips between resolved and regression nearly every hour.\nThe issue is at 3471 occurrences.\n\nRuntimes from the worker logs over 24h:\n\n```\n09-10 20:00  605s      09-11 04:00  509s\n09-10 22:00  538s      09-11 08:00  312s\n09-10 23:00  436s      09-11 10:00  602s\n09-11 00:00  322s      09-11 11:00  475s\n```\n\nAlmost all of that time is spent on workspaces that were already warned.\n`warnWorkspaceMembers` loaded the full workspace ORM context via\n`loadWorkspaceMembers`, then read one user var per member (each\n`userVarsService.get` fans out to 3 core queries), and only then\ndiscovered the workspace was already warned, logged `already warned`,\nand returned.\n\nProd logs show **~986 of those per run**, against ~8 workspaces that\nactually get a new warning. The job also stalls the worker event loop\nfor 10-95s at a time while doing it, which is enough for BullMQ to\ndeclare the job stalled and hand it to a second pod.\n\n## Change\n\nResolve the already-warned workspaces up front with a single query on\n`keyValuePair`, and skip them before touching the workspace ORM. ~986\nworkspace ORM loads per run become 0.\n\nThat check is now keyed on the workspace rather than on its current\nmembers. So reactivation has to clear every warn var of the workspace\ninstead of only those belonging to members it can still load, otherwise\na departed member''s stale row would suppress a later warning. That also\ncollapses `CleanWorkspaceDeletionWarningUserVarsJob` to a single delete.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCK5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABTIQAE3e65qhgfIQYtRc6TN+lPhZ\nc9TNUdgwGhaN2j38nudFxFkQDpreGJkLTEruLLkE2oGlKj48F7GRie2aMJ+YNyao\nuJ8m3Ci4mgVhy9ch/APpH/OMHeExnliQ1K0Lj2T7sTR0cL3mqbeEcT7TNfc93W0/\nxJlwkEFBoPBGsQjWEQdkGbBryMPVL5rEDatDxkppbWu9CM5BuXK6/v2wKzP8fhDK\nCeGn23b2wfvJFjeLO1mF/Bvl86PgFxmtZdIxamuqZD9vqjrNBoWn0A+01d6BxT1x\nTbC5Ced4tbxPZo/L8NwB6M2Z7o4wzz6vwzkfhVONxUkQ5kVwRIn0qhBOZYT+3y+Q\nLqFMy/5d+IhO9MuifyXMU+ijZQ7tWXI+nsyV272xGJwcv1QYfFhV+3Vwa8Rv6c24\nX2RSES53Pcy5JNrpUcMWZss5raZ4o/BQAFqLxHPvbzJvBENZCnrr06PdjJ4Q3dkp\nvw+fTnu8VF5PN09Zpkz3s3N9n77iH9XChPjw9JCm7pszuL/muPwNjwBKp5XF3gml\niCebIUz7QHJKvfX0oCyXTo/djuhajT7o43OZ+uz+fbZqa4V86vU7JmvxY087PUR0\nreTTrqYXZelaf4zhdoJ5JLg8ustd6Y41S2UjjOKt3nwxwZ31KLmPNUHCTtFO7LcC\nQizIYS3lVcEKrPsXdRT3\n=C6gC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/94272b6080665735e14b5afa27a4e369e1e24668","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDk0MjcyYjYwODA2NjU3MzVlMTRiNWFmYTI3YTRlMzY5ZTFlMjQ2Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/8f1355d96892e650d47c9955b65aae0eace09f1c","sha":"8f1355d96892e650d47c9955b65aae0eace09f1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8f1355d96892e650d47c9955b65aae0eace09f1c"}],"sha":"94272b6080665735e14b5afa27a4e369e1e24668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/94272b6080665735e14b5afa27a4e369e1e24668"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8f1355d96892e650d47c9955b65aae0eace09f1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:42:16Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:42:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Point pull users at the apply flag that protects what it could not write (#25808)\n\n## What\n\n`pull` signs off with `Next: yarn twenty plan --no-delete`. `plan` is\nread-only, so the flag does nothing there. The command that acts on the\npulled tree is `apply`, and a user following the printed guidance runs\nit without the flag.\n\n`pull` is experimental and says so. It reports the rows it could not\nexport, and then writes a manifest that omits them. Applying that tree\nwith deletion inference on, which is the default, reads those rows as\nentities the developer removed and destroys them.\n\nMeasured on a seeded dev workspace, pulling the Custom application and\napplying the result:\n\n```\nPlan: 0 to add, 0 to change, 19 to destroy.\n```\n\nThose 19 are exactly the rows the pull report had just listed as \"not\nwritten, unsupported by this version\": 4 roles, 4 command menu items, 3\nfront components, 3 logic functions, 2 object permissions, 2 field\npermissions, 1 role permission flag. Destroying the 4 roles cascades,\nbecause `core.\"roleTarget\".\"roleId\"` is `ON DELETE CASCADE` and six\ntables hang off `core.role`:\n\n```\nroleTarget   1012 -> 8     (member-bound 1005 -> 1)\nrole            5 -> 1\nobjectPermission / fieldPermission / rolePermissionFlag  -> 0\n```\n\n1004 of 1005 workspace members were left with no role. Nothing prompted,\nbecause `DESTRUCTIVE_METADATA_NAMES` covers only `objectMetadata` and\n`fieldMetadata`, so `hasDestructiveActions` was false and the run exited\n0.\n\nThe same tree applied with `--no-delete` is a true fixpoint: nothing\ndestroyed, every count unchanged, and a fresh pull afterwards is\nbyte-identical in both source and coverage report.\n\n## How\n\n- The two `Next:` hints name `apply --no-delete` instead of `plan\n--no-delete`.\n- `apply` warns before it acts when the tree carries a\n`.twenty/pull-base.json` and deletion inference is on. It is silent\nunder `--no-delete`, and silent for a project that was never pulled\ninto, so a hand-authored app that genuinely drops a role still deletes\nit with no new noise.\n- `hasPullBaseFile` is deliberately existence-only rather than reusing\n`readPullBaseManifest`, which returns null for a base it cannot parse or\nwhose application does not match. A project pulled into by an older\nversion still deserves the warning.\n\n## What this does not do\n\nIt does not stop the deletion, and it is not the fix. The underlying\ndefect is that deletion inference treats \"our exporter could not write\nthis\" as \"the user deleted this\", and no rule reading the manifest alone\ncan tell an empty section apart from an unexpressed one. Fixing that\nneeds the producer to declare its coverage on the sync input, so it also\ncovers install and upgrade paths where no CLI is in the loop. That\nbelongs with the export work that removes the trigger.\n\nScope of the exposure, for whoever picks that up: the exported manifest\nhardcodes `logicFunctions`, `frontComponents`, `permissionFlags`,\n`roles`, `skills`, `agents`, `publicAssets`, `commandMenuItems` and\n`timelineActivityTypes` to `[]`, and omits `connectionProviders` and\n`application.applicationVariables` entirely. The 19 rows above are what\nthis particular workspace happened to contain, not a ceiling. A\nworkspace with connection providers would also lose them, and\n`connectedAccount.connectionProviderId` is `ON DELETE CASCADE`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Unit spec on `hasPullBaseFile`: absent base, present base, and an\nunparseable base that must still count as present.\n- Verified live against a dev workspace on the measured state above: the\nhint now reads `Next: yarn twenty apply --no-delete`; a bare `apply`\nprints the warning before touching the server; `apply --no-delete`\nprints nothing, reports \"No changes\", and leaves all 1005 member\nassignments, 5 roles and 2 object permissions intact.\n- Full SDK unit suite (118 files, 854 tests), tsgo, oxlint and prettier\nclean.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25808?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"9596f1c25ce53c5f715f2064e10c83dad5dbbd76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/9596f1c25ce53c5f715f2064e10c83dad5dbbd76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/8f1355d96892e650d47c9955b65aae0eace09f1c","verification":{"payload":"tree 9596f1c25ce53c5f715f2064e10c83dad5dbbd76\nparent d168df965e105f0f5def19c120632957433ec132\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789141336 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789141336 +0000\n\nPoint pull users at the apply flag that protects what it could not write (#25808)\n\n## What\n\n`pull` signs off with `Next: yarn twenty plan --no-delete`. `plan` is\nread-only, so the flag does nothing there. The command that acts on the\npulled tree is `apply`, and a user following the printed guidance runs\nit without the flag.\n\n`pull` is experimental and says so. It reports the rows it could not\nexport, and then writes a manifest that omits them. Applying that tree\nwith deletion inference on, which is the default, reads those rows as\nentities the developer removed and destroys them.\n\nMeasured on a seeded dev workspace, pulling the Custom application and\napplying the result:\n\n```\nPlan: 0 to add, 0 to change, 19 to destroy.\n```\n\nThose 19 are exactly the rows the pull report had just listed as \"not\nwritten, unsupported by this version\": 4 roles, 4 command menu items, 3\nfront components, 3 logic functions, 2 object permissions, 2 field\npermissions, 1 role permission flag. Destroying the 4 roles cascades,\nbecause `core.\"roleTarget\".\"roleId\"` is `ON DELETE CASCADE` and six\ntables hang off `core.role`:\n\n```\nroleTarget   1012 -> 8     (member-bound 1005 -> 1)\nrole            5 -> 1\nobjectPermission / fieldPermission / rolePermissionFlag  -> 0\n```\n\n1004 of 1005 workspace members were left with no role. Nothing prompted,\nbecause `DESTRUCTIVE_METADATA_NAMES` covers only `objectMetadata` and\n`fieldMetadata`, so `hasDestructiveActions` was false and the run exited\n0.\n\nThe same tree applied with `--no-delete` is a true fixpoint: nothing\ndestroyed, every count unchanged, and a fresh pull afterwards is\nbyte-identical in both source and coverage report.\n\n## How\n\n- The two `Next:` hints name `apply --no-delete` instead of `plan\n--no-delete`.\n- `apply` warns before it acts when the tree carries a\n`.twenty/pull-base.json` and deletion inference is on. It is silent\nunder `--no-delete`, and silent for a project that was never pulled\ninto, so a hand-authored app that genuinely drops a role still deletes\nit with no new noise.\n- `hasPullBaseFile` is deliberately existence-only rather than reusing\n`readPullBaseManifest`, which returns null for a base it cannot parse or\nwhose application does not match. A project pulled into by an older\nversion still deserves the warning.\n\n## What this does not do\n\nIt does not stop the deletion, and it is not the fix. The underlying\ndefect is that deletion inference treats \"our exporter could not write\nthis\" as \"the user deleted this\", and no rule reading the manifest alone\ncan tell an empty section apart from an unexpressed one. Fixing that\nneeds the producer to declare its coverage on the sync input, so it also\ncovers install and upgrade paths where no CLI is in the loop. That\nbelongs with the export work that removes the trigger.\n\nScope of the exposure, for whoever picks that up: the exported manifest\nhardcodes `logicFunctions`, `frontComponents`, `permissionFlags`,\n`roles`, `skills`, `agents`, `publicAssets`, `commandMenuItems` and\n`timelineActivityTypes` to `[]`, and omits `connectionProviders` and\n`application.applicationVariables` entirely. The 19 rows above are what\nthis particular workspace happened to contain, not a ceiling. A\nworkspace with connection providers would also lose them, and\n`connectedAccount.connectionProviderId` is `ON DELETE CASCADE`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Unit spec on `hasPullBaseFile`: absent base, present base, and an\nunparseable base that must still count as present.\n- Verified live against a dev workspace on the measured state above: the\nhint now reads `Next: yarn twenty apply --no-delete`; a bare `apply`\nprints the warning before touching the server; `apply --no-delete`\nprints nothing, reports \"No changes\", and leaves all 1005 member\nassignments, 5 roles and 2 object permissions intact.\n- Full SDK unit suite (118 files, 854 tests), tsgo, oxlint and prettier\nclean.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25808?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCFnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEEsQAJ4ohkpaMKSJSsTWv+iuDad8\ne2mVBLLpd8ztCYP8mbxaBJFYtpajG0U4/vNr+M+IsXGa6jnCH6suVNH9f5wXKJf3\n2NYAvB5aNHcgk7ktuZHnYbZZfdCmX4cQBD+cLbOzTzKH3shUuoSH68nrlGfUJ6ay\nOdRJFe7bOuT/pdoInMTscwjayI39pZXp8h2mv7OWuAEkRaBjTuWwvBmBaDgiFrWu\notCDlMMWD5g8p4jSzVWxgUGxp5fuieuqD0yAp