/git/trees/c2b71ffb121320385779e85525a6d29073b7c7e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/244b02fd88c84a7436824c3315943138c8ab948d","verification":{"payload":"tree c2b71ffb121320385779e85525a6d29073b7c7e0\nparent 9a28e5648363e134ade2fa68a698ade37fb79ec2\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1789140347 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789140347 +0000\n\nfix(front): hide connection provider avatar when there is no logo (#25797)\n\nFollow-up to https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25419.\n\nThe connections settings tab rendered an `Avatar` adornment next to\nevery provider title, falling back to a letter placeholder built from\n`displayName` when the provider manifest declares no logo. Providers\nwithout a logo now render no adornment at all.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `SettingsApplicationConnectionsSection` only passes the `Avatar`\nadornment to `H2Title` when `logoUrl` is a non-empty string.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpB2KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmgoQADJy7qQJ5u01UC6mCNEWXD55\n6CcC5rXqXi5VI1LNCPfpiDp9nLDrk42WxR1ldsdoMiEU3BIP4WuoSoeJ9phB7Ocs\nF/PwtSJuJW3+NsPmXswBhuYrvjuOWVucQicUE8rEcq25ePc6J8419m1Rk+qsTPc9\nw6Iqh6geB4oidPyM7hxiSZwXTFLSopXBtqCY+P1XoARBIivLU+UkNIcA11qwSv10\nsvwUkXuQT9lgoCVdD2Yi4WpHi2bq5WwKFk/CSQdAmqd0/oX1M6B/o0o3Xmaxt8kX\nst4C9LDtpgJQK0nuNOZ53zLCR72+2fFgUNYBaFjpwPv2LFqKuDp9n/e7Uv3qkFRs\nEjZy394sdF6tcg8WeTLkZO+4+t8Xi6zYNuaTCnZl0eVFBg2NyurRFu/uij3CiL1M\nJQItSRE7DQD9OOV4cRSsBlQTvG0qEbI9ObDJz1zFEnKyCblk/0NcCJVjpwlvCEC9\n4SwvWCNL3quofxBlpIopicdr2ceLjjEWhl0sChUa+j7oA2zjMjg7Rs3TwZpCgJ/a\ny0YMGJ7jhUSYWc0xSnN25Wf3W+zJWBVYjaB4oPAU4fv8BN0Q+o6b1Log61pFWgEZ\ncl+uhp8Immuer+6gOXdcXFaAGa9GUVL6ugNWQbkcr+5GP8JQ1FsMYwzi8DDqKrmF\nJqmkBhfiUbaS4EYloWHF\n=ISI1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/244b02fd88c84a7436824c3315943138c8ab948d","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDI0NGIwMmZkODhjODRhNzQzNjgyNGMzMzE1OTQzMTM4YzhhYjk0OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/9a28e5648363e134ade2fa68a698ade37fb79ec2","sha":"9a28e5648363e134ade2fa68a698ade37fb79ec2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9a28e5648363e134ade2fa68a698ade37fb79ec2"}],"sha":"244b02fd88c84a7436824c3315943138c8ab948d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/244b02fd88c84a7436824c3315943138c8ab948d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45695613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9a28e5648363e134ade2fa68a698ade37fb79ec2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:21:32Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:21:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Give each Sentry cron monitor its own max runtime (#25801)\n\n## Problem\n\n`SentryCronMonitor` hardcodes `maxRuntime: 5` minutes for all 35 cron\nmonitors, so a job that drops workspace schemas shares a budget with one\nthat rotates a signing key.\n\n`CleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob` runs hourly and took between 1 and 10\nminutes on prod-eu over the last 24h, measured from the `processed on\nqueue cron-queue in Xms` worker logs. It sits right on the 5 minute\nthreshold, so it reports a timeout check-in most hours and its monitor\nflaps between resolved and regression. The Sentry issue is at 3471\noccurrences.\n\n## Change\n\nMake the runtime an option on the decorator, keeping 5 minutes as the\ndefault so no other monitor changes, and give\n`CleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob` 15 minutes: above its worst observed run,\nstill well inside its hourly period so a real hang alerts within the\nhour.\n\n#25800 separately removes the work that makes that job slow. This one\nstops the monitor lying about a job that is simply heavier than the\ndefault budget assumes.","tree":{"sha":"4a0d64829a164d536c3a8b609cbb547688bb5d76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/4a0d64829a164d536c3a8b609cbb547688bb5d76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/9a28e5648363e134ade2fa68a698ade37fb79ec2","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a0d64829a164d536c3a8b609cbb547688bb5d76\nparent 4d8503f0aabe092164bf20e8d1b2d39b0fa840ae\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1789140092 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789140092 +0000\n\nGive each Sentry cron monitor its own max runtime (#25801)\n\n## Problem\n\n`SentryCronMonitor` hardcodes `maxRuntime: 5` minutes for all 35 cron\nmonitors, so a job that drops workspace schemas shares a budget with one\nthat rotates a signing key.\n\n`CleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob` runs hourly and took between 1 and 10\nminutes on prod-eu over the last 24h, measured from the `processed on\nqueue cron-queue in Xms` worker logs. It sits right on the 5 minute\nthreshold, so it reports a timeout check-in most hours and its monitor\nflaps between resolved and regression. The Sentry issue is at 3471\noccurrences.\n\n## Change\n\nMake the runtime an option on the decorator, keeping 5 minutes as the\ndefault so no other monitor changes, and give\n`CleanSuspendedWorkspacesJob` 15 minutes: above its worst observed run,\nstill well inside its hourly period so a real hang alerts within the\nhour.\n\n#25800 separately removes the work that makes that job slow. This one\nstops the monitor lying about a job that is simply heavier than the\ndefault budget assumes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpByMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwBMQAC/hda0tFvctGSIx7VZTAGx9\nhc5ev68L4Nf3bHRyclOCDTY6g/QywS6/eBiNS1gD7FWFr1psNP1v8QW6qHenZCys\n/AtkgCoXKAUedyZwGYtOzDTHIdoFqWU6rSo9bFJ+lbsdNUk0JPdwhbkVDBySsloA\nLqz+4lrn/jEEWINVxhgvais1nTMXXdAvgkXhzedZZw0PcW9ujYgQZVRfzfwJLKHk\nrKgXZvDtiaR9oOEfS6O1u4U9MvATbbhuvT/S14ONXJr3Q3oz27pMLVamNPAomnvB\nxCGftUT4n7ca7V/US51kk8d/F3cnyYJR/dU7nxzD2nEVLYtVT04Bo1Rd42AKk86F\neKcA6Sf8Rs+ltS/Wr9jfbS9K7PaaYOLScIv7pWS8atuBSHbll5Bo/m8izP4hy3gr\nZozMHdoqaJR4TL0RYk40v4tC+bGz1SFkJ90OkjB+sFaTosJh6ixWKXrXYS1hYRzs\nmEFV69Cx300d1Qiy+Snrd9DvxyDG94JzBOIILRl7dSWAZ7+KlOBiNXehBAYYvSwf\nEawN3yOAWFMg/TspScCcUFjQgLpXhKeftHY93M0Jzyd51eAc5q8DLwdGgkrJcAr+\nx2vcG/wZWUiDtxeEJUcWEigqzAj39ZkElqbo8eb1ZRADNbauqaVxCicEiUqR1Zwj\nxK+yklAcN1ISXQ1tGpKn\n=Vite\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/9a28e5648363e134ade2fa68a698ade37fb79ec2","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDlhMjhlNTY0ODM2M2UxMzRhZGUyZmE2OGE2OThhZGUzN2ZiNzllYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/4d8503f0aabe092164bf20e8d1b2d39b0fa840ae","sha":"4d8503f0aabe092164bf20e8d1b2d39b0fa840ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/4d8503f0aabe092164bf20e8d1b2d39b0fa840ae"}],"sha":"9a28e5648363e134ade2fa68a698ade37fb79ec2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9a28e5648363e134ade2fa68a698ade37fb79ec2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/4d8503f0aabe092164bf20e8d1b2d39b0fa840ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:07:13Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:07:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Never infer deletion for rows a manifest cannot express (#25752)\n\n## What\n\nDeletion inference destroyed any row carrying an application''s id that\nthe incoming manifest did not mention. A workspace''s member role\nassignments all carry the Custom application''s id, so a sync wiped them:\n1006 rows in the workspace I reproduced this on.\n\nDeletion is now inferred only for rows a manifest can actually express.\n\n## How\n\nOne predicate, `canManifestExpressFlatEntity`, added to the deletion\nfilter next to the existing `isSystemSideEffectFlatEntity` guard. A row\nis not expressible when:\n\n- **it binds to live workspace state** the manifest has no way to name:\n`userWorkspaceId`, `apiKeyId`, `workflowVersionId`, `targetRecordId`.\nThat covers member and API key role assignments, workflow trigger\ncommands, and personal and record-pinned navigation items.\n- **its kind has no manifest representation at all**: webhooks, the one\nkind with no converter and no foreign key to key on.\n- **it is a command menu item with no front component**.\n`CommandMenuItemManifest.frontComponentUniversalIdentifier` is required,\nso such a row cannot round-trip. `classifyFlatEntity` already reported\nit as `EXCLUDED, ''command without front component''` and deletion\ninference destroyed it anyway.\n\n### Why the binding column rather than the metadata name\n\nThe first pass switched on metadata name. That is the wrong axis,\nbecause it fails in the destructive direction exactly when it is\nneglected: a kind promoted to a syncable entity later falls through to\n`default` and becomes deletable with no compile error and no failing\ntest. Promotion is a standing workstream here, seven kinds in recent\nhistory.\n\n`ConnectedAccountEntity` is the concrete case. It already carries\n`userWorkspaceId NOT NULL` and `applicationId`, already lives under\n`metadata-modules/`, and its sibling `ConnectionProviderEntity` is\nalready syncable. Under a name switch, the day it is promoted every\nconnected account in the workspace becomes hard-deletable on app sync,\ntaking its message channels with it through `onDelete: CASCADE`, with\nencrypted tokens that cannot be recovered. Under a column list it is\nprotected by the column it already has.\n\nThe columns are an exact-name list, not a suffix rule.\n`view.createdByUserWorkspaceId`, `objectMetadata.dataSourceId`,\n`fieldMetadata.morphId` and `agent.modelId` are the other pointers out\nof the metadata graph and all four must stay deletable; a suffix rule\nwould make every object and every UI-created view permanently\nundeletable.\n\nNo manifest-expressible row can carry one of the four.\n`fromAgentManifestToUniversalFlatRoleTarget` hard-codes\n`userWorkspaceId: null, apiKeyId: null`;\n`frontComponentUniversalIdentifier` is a required manifest field; and\n`CHK_CMD_MENU_ITEM_ENGINE_KEY_COHERENCE` makes `workflowVersionId` and\n`frontComponentId` mutually exclusive in Postgres.\n\n### What this does not change\n\nExport coverage is untouched. The reasons shown in `yarn twenty pull`\noutput stay in the two classifiers that display them, so this change\ntouches the deletion path only. `EXCLUDED` is not a deletion-protection\nmarker and is not treated as one: an agent-bound role assignment is\n`UNSUPPORTED` and still deleted, correctly, because the agent''s manifest\nrecreates it.\n\nThe `as unknown as MetadataUniversalFlatEntity<AllMetadataName>` cast on\nthe adjacent `isSystemSideEffectFlatEntity` filter turned out to be\nunnecessary in that position and is gone. `classifyFlatEntity` already\ncalled it without one.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Spec covers every protected case and its counterpart: member and API\nkey role assignments protected, agent-bound still deleted; webhooks\nprotected; workflow trigger commands and commands without a front\ncomponent protected, commands with one still deleted; personal and\nrecord-pinned navigation items protected, plain workspace items still\ndeleted. 13 tests.\n- Mutation-checked rather than assumed: dropping the front-component\nclause and misspelling one binding column reddens 3 of the 13.\n- tsgo, oxlint and oxfmt clean. 70 suites, 375 tests green in\n`core-modules/application`.","tree":{"sha":"a3a4c454304f2d3c92879f71f110fe4cf60f3694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/a3a4c454304f2d3c92879f71f110fe4cf60f3694"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/4d8503f0aabe092164bf20e8d1b2d39b0fa840ae","verification":{"payload":"tree a3a4c454304f2d3c92879f71f110fe4cf60f3694\nparent d6dc77d198f580d29595fe56b8fa63b5ae7ebda1\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789139233 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789139233 +0000\n\nNever infer deletion for rows a manifest cannot express (#25752)\n\n## What\n\nDeletion inference destroyed any row carrying an application''s id that\nthe incoming manifest did not mention. A workspace''s member role\nassignments all carry the Custom application''s id, so a sync wiped them:\n1006 rows in the workspace I reproduced this on.\n\nDeletion is now inferred only for rows a manifest can actually express.\n\n## How\n\nOne predicate, `canManifestExpressFlatEntity`, added to the deletion\nfilter next to the existing `isSystemSideEffectFlatEntity` guard. A row\nis not expressible when:\n\n- **it binds to live workspace state** the manifest has no way to name:\n`userWorkspaceId`, `apiKeyId`, `workflowVersionId`, `targetRecordId`.\nThat covers member and API key role assignments, workflow trigger\ncommands, and personal and record-pinned navigation items.\n- **its kind has no manifest representation at all**: webhooks, the one\nkind with no converter and no foreign key to key on.\n- **it is a command menu item with no front component**.\n`CommandMenuItemManifest.frontComponentUniversalIdentifier` is required,\nso such a row cannot round-trip. `classifyFlatEntity` already reported\nit as `EXCLUDED, ''command without front component''` and deletion\ninference destroyed it anyway.\n\n### Why the binding column rather than the metadata name\n\nThe first pass switched on metadata name. That is the wrong axis,\nbecause it fails in the destructive direction exactly when it is\nneglected: a kind promoted to a syncable entity later falls through to\n`default` and becomes deletable with no compile error and no failing\ntest. Promotion is a standing workstream here, seven kinds in recent\nhistory.\n\n`ConnectedAccountEntity` is the concrete case. It already carries\n`userWorkspaceId NOT NULL` and `applicationId`, already lives under\n`metadata-modules/`, and its sibling `ConnectionProviderEntity` is\nalready syncable. Under a name switch, the day it is promoted every\nconnected account in the workspace becomes hard-deletable on app sync,\ntaking its message channels with it through `onDelete: CASCADE`, with\nencrypted tokens that cannot be recovered. Under a column list it is\nprotected by the column it already has.\n\nThe columns are an exact-name list, not a suffix rule.\n`view.createdByUserWorkspaceId`, `objectMetadata.dataSourceId`,\n`fieldMetadata.morphId` and `agent.modelId` are the other pointers out\nof the metadata graph and all four must stay deletable; a suffix rule\nwould make every object and every UI-created view permanently\nundeletable.\n\nNo manifest-expressible row can carry one of the four.\n`fromAgentManifestToUniversalFlatRoleTarget` hard-codes\n`userWorkspaceId: null, apiKeyId: null`;\n`frontComponentUniversalIdentifier` is a required manifest field; and\n`CHK_CMD_MENU_ITEM_ENGINE_KEY_COHERENCE` makes `workflowVersionId` and\n`frontComponentId` mutually exclusive in Postgres.\n\n### What this does not change\n\nExport coverage is untouched. The reasons shown in `yarn twenty pull`\noutput stay in the two classifiers that display them, so this change\ntouches the deletion path only. `EXCLUDED` is not a deletion-protection\nmarker and is not treated as one: an agent-bound role assignment is\n`UNSUPPORTED` and still deleted, correctly, because the agent''s manifest\nrecreates it.\n\nThe `as unknown as MetadataUniversalFlatEntity<AllMetadataName>` cast on\nthe adjacent `isSystemSideEffectFlatEntity` filter turned out to be\nunnecessary in that position and is gone. `classifyFlatEntity` already\ncalled it without one.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Spec covers every protected case and its counterpart: member and API\nkey role assignments protected, agent-bound still deleted; webhooks\nprotected; workflow trigger commands and commands without a front\ncomponent protected, commands with one still deleted; personal and\nrecord-pinned navigation items protected, plain workspace items still\ndeleted. 13 tests.\n- Mutation-checked rather than assumed: dropping the front-component\nclause and misspelling one binding column reddens 3 of the 13.\n- tsgo, oxlint and oxfmt clean. 70 suites, 375 tests green in\n`core-modules/application`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpBkwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANN0QAKFaqgSBxeMZFCZsdjycKX5a\nwdEb8zB1fNMOAjKij+hwrdmBy6TFCVibYC1bUcqd2cSIPrLBbLuRTGkNyR5CLI3L\nx+zZVK4ssktTFPBhuMQBB6FKzDW+9SlTbUq6ngKcV7aL/6mhweXnMGTS3t1EDTNE\n8tbT1nIcwB2BunLR557yHmuJ6SN3gRWa3DH87f2d7+y3MbUbEyrxCoSc42DM/Fke\nPvTLSV4BvXgyFzDOD/pvIh2p/bPC1bHnsxSOaw6kWrDOkr/LM7PTcgevzinDuGFG\nIn3T9lcVNbyDwjk3RxhjLMu9yt1fsmfJcGK2+a7KBynKP4YTooEscSmxgbQ1x/fF\n3erGgE+5Dw31XIdguSN1dcZa5CfZ5Vp1k7T82pEJZP92wO/CTAkQlNafIuyc4S0/\nRylT3SLQf8ofYrsJjanxCkFUle6NTK7Q66rMolGxSu0zV54Hmb4CyCzDpqo+6zMl\nyjkDPYdin32tpFr6O6dSZJTl6idGoEBJT8erkqJb9yIF4yI2E/G0z6qX9BlEoF5m\n/KfZh2p3lq4hS10qM6hz4ju+CJbDnpYRPzmvaax1tVnxSg1JKIyVQFn0PSOi8fxh\nOMNAxK6ESkFpyeW1avI/l7qUfzCNd25Jud+MBXCCpalikK8UHMJJu41gczZVXlQX\nTITVXvoWW3Z55QJ2qgrY\n=wMI7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/4d8503f0aabe092164bf20e8d1b2d39b0fa840ae","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDRkODUwM2YwYWFiZTA5MjE2NGJmMjBlOGQxYjJkMzliMGZhODQwYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/d6dc77d198f580d29595fe56b8fa63b5ae7ebda1","sha":"d6dc77d198f580d29595fe56b8fa63b5ae7ebda1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/d6dc77d198f580d29595fe56b8fa63b5ae7ebda1"}],"sha":"4d8503f0aabe092164bf20e8d1b2d39b0fa840ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/4d8503f0aabe092164bf20e8d1b2d39b0fa840ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19412894?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonapara","id":19412894,"login":"Bonapara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDEyODk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/d6dc77d198f580d29595fe56b8fa63b5ae7ebda1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:59:32Z","email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:59:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Support explicit widget height behavior (#25512)\n\n## Intro\n\nThis follows my previous PRs on page layouts. The goal is to let\nvertical lists contain both widgets that fit their content and widgets\nthat fill the tab, so we no longer need Canvas just to make a widget\nfull-height.\n\nThis first PR adds the height setting. The next two simplify layout\nauthoring and migrate existing workspace-created single-widget Canvas\ntabs while preserving legacy app manifests.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd an optional `FIT_CONTENT` / `TAB_VIEWPORT` height behavior to\nvertical-list widget positions. Explicit choices override the shared\nwidget-type default. Rendering, insertion, drag and drop, saving,\nGraphQL/REST, and server validation use the same contract. A tab can\ncontain one active viewport widget, placed last.\n\nKeep legacy Canvas rendering working while existing tabs remain. Widget\npadding retains its existing rules. Include the shared types, generated\nclients, and focused tests with the behavior they support.\n\nStack 2/4: runtime height support → manifest authoring → existing-data\nmigration. The next two PRs add the authoring API and migrate stored\nCanvas tabs.\n\nCI prerequisite: #25531 contains the registry and Last Contact test\nrepairs, kept separate from the layout changes.\n\nReview and merge order:\n\n1. [App CI repairs](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25531)\n2. [Widget height\nbehavior](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25512)\n3. [Manifest authoring](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25513)\n4. [Existing Canvas data\nmigration](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25511)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25512?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"6b6c9cfac83cea3ceb2af12804329069f3b6304c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/6b6c9cfac83cea3ceb2af12804329069f3b6304c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/d6dc77d198f580d29595fe56b8fa63b5ae7ebda1","verification":{"payload":"tree 6b6c9cfac83cea3ceb2af12804329069f3b6304c\nparent 464eda6174316d6d3af1fbb4482ef86f2d168e40\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789138772 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789138772 +0000\n\nSupport explicit widget height behavior (#25512)\n\n## Intro\n\nThis follows my previous PRs on page layouts. The goal is to let\nvertical lists contain both widgets that fit their content and widgets\nthat fill the tab, so we no longer need Canvas just to make a widget\nfull-height.\n\nThis first PR adds the height setting. The next two simplify layout\nauthoring and migrate existing workspace-created single-widget Canvas\ntabs while preserving legacy app manifests.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd an optional `FIT_CONTENT` / `TAB_VIEWPORT` height behavior to\nvertical-list widget positions. Explicit choices override the shared\nwidget-type default. Rendering, insertion, drag and drop, saving,\nGraphQL/REST, and server validation use the same contract. A tab can\ncontain one active viewport widget, placed last.\n\nKeep legacy Canvas rendering working while existing tabs remain. Widget\npadding retains its existing rules. Include the shared types, generated\nclients, and focused tests with the behavior they support.\n\nStack 2/4: runtime height support → manifest authoring → existing-data\nmigration. The next two PRs add the authoring API and migrate stored\nCanvas tabs.\n\nCI prerequisite: #25531 contains the registry and Last Contact test\nrepairs, kept separate from the layout changes.\n\nReview and merge order:\n\n1. [App CI repairs](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25531)\n2. [Widget height\nbehavior](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25512)\n3. [Manifest authoring](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25513)\n4. [Existing Canvas data\nmigration](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25511)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25512?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpBdkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6oYQAAp1Paa7O+pJRIpXuQsv2Oum\nE93D4LTrUBwHhCmHcLY/c/gudUTbNCjulnraxjHUl3VQSa9I+HA6CuSTZSzPqM1u\nqByZE6R6qjcQY7gfaM4zh8dn6nmiOawPhNLFN+DgT2pWVF4vuG5ghW3EzW4xvE2+\nfaghK2tiulaW4Kpo0rMpQMR334+mkqWBDY0bhbyuzcnMTs/HthLxmmp/UYai2Rz2\ndTlSPLVzdmb7nP1j8yQ/R+SG1JN8tM+VNFFI76WB89FJFJVkIXRSmBXaQEHeRbCU\n2kJesmlHHZxb0hqHEjBR3EJJ7b4IW2DIOpKsfRBuZhPwykVLyv1W4QGiA0L3T/c0\nWaR0znXGIzqsfhEhXFiTnyeUHCaGGwZosbI55aKKb/bVQv9YZgQbK2nXmUM136zm\nCCOIOPSfB0cd/WLkDSJjPZfenZX96mYgbl4neZSVWUB7T9Hlh175QPMUqdmV8EJ+\nmaFDbvNrx+FLMjiuIaaY3xf83FuhIOWxtIzzpcCwiWhhcTb98NMmbf8DefkOO7W4\nCuFytuZczcmlf6BtDrUP0ZzEBn5BeWcDUHUPwrnZOwJYzoAEkXfns+ve21+r7j3s\nKNIJy9Gmf9lZRiphU8eqAFEjFJjNw20XD3k6436IR8FjSdSlM/2iNthOB0acMjZ8\nLUyEozg+V68qsXCDxC/h\n=8djK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_