ps://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/464eda6174316d6d3af1fbb4482ef86f2d168e40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:51:30Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:51:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(front): open the view picker on the id its dropdown listens to (#25799)\n\nFollow-up to a review nit on #25790.\n\n`useOpenCreateViewDropdown` built the dropdown id from its optional\n`viewBardId` argument, while `ViewPickerDropdown` builds it from\n`recordIndexId`. A caller passing a `viewBardId` that differs from\n`recordIndexId` would open an id no dropdown is listening on — the same\nread/write divergence #25790 removed everywhere else.\n\nBoth sides now derive the id from `recordIndexId`. Latent today: the two\ncallers pass either nothing or `recordIndexId`, so behaviour is\nunchanged.\n\nChecked in a browser against a local stack on this commit: the view\npicker''s \"Add view\" button and the options dropdown''s \"Create custom\nview\" entry both still open the create-view form.\n\n[Review in\ncubic](https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25799?utm_source=github)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015hjgTjDmBnCsTdnozEQSgp","tree":{"sha":"2a652dd231f6f34ca205942bcddddd851a58c75a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/2a652dd231f6f34ca205942bcddddd851a58c75a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/464eda6174316d6d3af1fbb4482ef86f2d168e40","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a652dd231f6f34ca205942bcddddd851a58c75a\nparent b25c8d248dfe50e8ef567322224fdf7d98182ecd\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789138290 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789138290 +0200\n\nfix(front): open the view picker on the id its dropdown listens to (#25799)\n\nFollow-up to a review nit on #25790.\n\n`useOpenCreateViewDropdown` built the dropdown id from its optional\n`viewBardId` argument, while `ViewPickerDropdown` builds it from\n`recordIndexId`. A caller passing a `viewBardId` that differs from\n`recordIndexId` would open an id no dropdown is listening on — the same\nread/write divergence #25790 removed everywhere else.\n\nBoth sides now derive the id from `recordIndexId`. Latent today: the two\ncallers pass either nothing or `recordIndexId`, so behaviour is\nunchanged.\n\nChecked in a browser against a local stack on this commit: the view\npicker''s \"Add view\" button and the options dropdown''s \"Create custom\nview\" entry both still open the create-view form.\n\n[Review in\ncubic](https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25799?utm_source=github)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015hjgTjDmBnCsTdnozEQSgp","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpBVyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOxQQAIwgzIHedi7+P65osmmcdzVs\nNBa3QIMvQKTMHI13E0eGt20+V8Bsq/ptPxLS/1F7/hQ2CNeU1YDNsHZx+NMfAGTB\ng2xZqPwcV5f4JA2V2NHYwd2OKAv3Omzqt9aSeG1CW491jfIGU69aGxF9HgwYUEl+\njLsbMu1rYygWFEIvLn/v6c5xBj8l/13aVVwCLP5J0e2KbTbjvcCMMyQMMaUdclr3\n7blA7kC88QrEzDEpl6C2QJGtoowF7S74h+jDaD6lDfbdH17tfhkx/tXd/D2sNc3v\n03FpwE5RWXZVfg9+pHcwTaUy0lHduFKJTadeouOlFThw1IV3+vdwr4dk2mRUaadf\ns7n0zxQVfbl0u8hUfgBWxzaFf8xnEB7okHj8OXtDKha5QFhtn9YBP95aOVEBI9WD\nUgd4Z5WXa9vYxoJ6SsVGFmyI6X8mhxj0Rh9wAMk3cumXhn5doUzBe1ttkt5r/fOy\nn1CZk/TcKgHh+Fm2qFB+w+Y0uVIfSDFkKu7+1EWiOAIMbJsCoC0ipY9XxxSsSeF+\nF++ANJf03YgpcNYqrFEzAhoAr6oHPmQ7xuwFWXnTG0weH0LOkP7GhpuQtMCIABsa\nx97dZ/VInrHbVGWVVqDRrWFMXacuuccgjMCBr4Zprwg5uUKQMfLYR7bARzH18t8x\nw951R8E5PDsoO9TEvzmb\n=SO1e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/464eda6174316d6d3af1fbb4482ef86f2d168e40","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDQ2NGVkYTYxNzQzMTZkNmQzYWYxZmJiNDQ4MmVmODZmMmQxNjhlNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/b25c8d248dfe50e8ef567322224fdf7d98182ecd","sha":"b25c8d248dfe50e8ef567322224fdf7d98182ecd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b25c8d248dfe50e8ef567322224fdf7d98182ecd"}],"sha":"464eda6174316d6d3af1fbb4482ef86f2d168e40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/464eda6174316d6d3af1fbb4482ef86f2d168e40"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b25c8d248dfe50e8ef567322224fdf7d98182ecd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:12:31Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:12:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Migrate Tag to the new twenty-ui API (#25786)\n\nMigrate Tag from text/Icon props to children/startIcon, with\nsoft/solid/outline/ghost variants, native props and refs, and Base UI\nkeyboard/disabled behavior. Update consumers and menu/select adapters,\npreserving filled colors and dashed outlines, and add conformance,\nlight/dark catalog, and React/Preact renderer coverage.\n\nMarketplace apps use their independently installed published UI package.\nSlack''s `package.json` declares `twenty-ui: ^1.0.0-alpha.1`, its own\n`yarn.lock` resolves `twenty-ui@npm:1.0.0-alpha.1`, and the root Yarn\nworkspaces exclude `packages/twenty-apps/public/slack`. Slack''s\n`tsconfig.json` only aliases `src/*` and `~/*`, so its three `Tag text=`\nusages in `SlackUserLinksList.tsx` correctly target the published API\nand must stay unchanged until that dependency is upgraded.\n\nValidation: 16 targeted UI browser stories and 6 React/Preact renderer\nchecks pass. UI, frontend, and renderer direct typechecks,\nregular/individual UI builds, lint, and formatting pass.\n\n[Status #25785](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25785) has\nmerged. Review this PR against `main`; merge the remaining stack in this\norder:\n\n[Tag #25786](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25786) → [Avatar\n#25787](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25787) → [Chip\n#25788](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25788)","tree":{"sha":"8fb37ba581a231b9160bcd00ffd346626920b91a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/8fb37ba581a231b9160bcd00ffd346626920b91a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/b25c8d248dfe50e8ef567322224fdf7d98182ecd","verification":{"payload":"tree 8fb37ba581a231b9160bcd00ffd346626920b91a\nparent 3c128b3dae052bda8a857f9cb6e2207daf45bc1f\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1789135951 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789135951 +0000\n\nMigrate Tag to the new twenty-ui API (#25786)\n\nMigrate Tag from text/Icon props to children/startIcon, with\nsoft/solid/outline/ghost variants, native props and refs, and Base UI\nkeyboard/disabled behavior. Update consumers and menu/select adapters,\npreserving filled colors and dashed outlines, and add conformance,\nlight/dark catalog, and React/Preact renderer coverage.\n\nMarketplace apps use their independently installed published UI package.\nSlack''s `package.json` declares `twenty-ui: ^1.0.0-alpha.1`, its own\n`yarn.lock` resolves `twenty-ui@npm:1.0.0-alpha.1`, and the root Yarn\nworkspaces exclude `packages/twenty-apps/public/slack`. Slack''s\n`tsconfig.json` only aliases `src/*` and `~/*`, so its three `Tag text=`\nusages in `SlackUserLinksList.tsx` correctly target the published API\nand must stay unchanged until that dependency is upgraded.\n\nValidation: 16 targeted UI browser stories and 6 React/Preact renderer\nchecks pass. UI, frontend, and renderer direct typechecks,\nregular/individual UI builds, lint, and formatting pass.\n\n[Status #25785](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25785) has\nmerged. Review this PR against `main`; merge the remaining stack in this\norder:\n\n[Tag #25786](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/