the local\nregistry rejects the SDK publish payload with HTTP 413, and the Last\nContact fixture tries to create a platform-owned message-channel\nassociation.\n\nRaise the test registry request limit to 50 MB and remove the unused\nassociation from the Last Contact fixture. Production permissions stay\nunchanged.\n\nSplit out of #25513 so the widget/layout stack can be reviewed\nindependently. Call Recorder already has its fixture repair on main in\n#25412, so that duplicate change is omitted.\n\nValidation: these two fixes are unchanged from the passing CI run on\n#25513. The new branch runs CI independently against main.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25531?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"ae99ef9768ad78805f1048912afe2b29dc28b561","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/ae99ef9768ad78805f1048912afe2b29dc28b561"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/3c128b3dae052bda8a857f9cb6e2207daf45bc1f","verification":{"payload":"tree ae99ef9768ad78805f1048912afe2b29dc28b561\nparent 39acdbb46c28b365b23aeb27623adbde682b0240\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789135711 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789135711 +0000\n\nFix app CI fixtures and registry upload limit (#25531)\n\nThe app CI jobs fail before exercising the app behavior: the local\nregistry rejects the SDK publish payload with HTTP 413, and the Last\nContact fixture tries to create a platform-owned message-channel\nassociation.\n\nRaise the test registry request limit to 50 MB and remove the unused\nassociation from the Last Contact fixture. Production permissions stay\nunchanged.\n\nSplit out of #25513 so the widget/layout stack can be reviewed\nindependently. Call Recorder already has its fixture repair on main in\n#25412, so that duplicate change is omitted.\n\nValidation: these two fixes are unchanged from the passing CI run on\n#25513. The new branch runs CI independently against main.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25531?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpAtwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/S8QAJXSxe9w0D2fE7NU6/FoLMCr\nl73cf/OIue1BKGOQSBxOZ54Nxti9j9K3rWsHeusIuokdvjAJfdsXBOsMvfc8SVHt\nOI2cO70D9I/jUsoN2Sobjv4GeXZ/I8CQZdVCXWtST/ygDrpBFyAmL6q8yTtB828Y\nVgHave+G1rF0hVNw6mX4xfhEpA/bBnQKkL3rPQBWK1H9Yd/7Vi6PZDxS8DcvdBNK\nz5q7/1b0Jj0IkiVGWKTR13FcxEe/NskvRVgC/foaDO57Wf9az4T6ERR2CV97k5Bp\n/Qpbxg0a9WSw8VVWEtF95ETx/JEgjRz/mq9/FrCvObudlSGO4nUSSccPhv6iAApP\n3FqybI4tq1jxssA0m7W6XpbQAx80hjPA+yGtQDzbFo1enWuA3MOSQTwtviWve34/\nkPi6k1CGvK9BUp53iVybG+nRCvAA8v+vPB+fh4eoJ7HGit53Kbpu9Cddtq0yIkQH\nrPW/scmDI5Pb8uwdTIGgHy3ussSL/RuMkGPPq3bhdIu7G8PQBuLIU9c1t8qVlXD6\nrvxcSs0nddM6YFGVg8ONoLZh4wngFzI30OUsenCtrlJXVcqyu5BPgqml2+8siRhz\n5huVfgcjTF+yOcnoOOskyI4RDyGTx+y9lwRYhhoe4HTtsijdVELGhFV41FVdIbao\n4YgTjf1DWNeo7tAx/N1w\n=mtm/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/3c128b3dae052bda8a857f9cb6e2207daf45bc1f","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDNjMTI4YjNkYWUwNTJiZGE4YTg1N2Y5Y2I2ZTIyMDdkYWY0NWJjMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/39acdbb46c28b365b23aeb27623adbde682b0240","sha":"39acdbb46c28b365b23aeb27623adbde682b0240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/39acdbb46c28b365b23aeb27623adbde682b0240"}],"sha":"3c128b3dae052bda8a857f9cb6e2207daf45bc1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/3c128b3dae052bda8a857f9cb6e2207daf45bc1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/39acdbb46c28b365b23aeb27623adbde682b0240/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:59:47Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:59:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Keep a stored file''s identifier when its content is uploaded again (#25748)\n\n## What\n\nRe-uploading a file an application already stores rewrites that file\nrow''s primary key. When something references the row, the write is\nrejected and the whole sync fails.\n\n`yarn twenty apply` on the workspace Custom application always fails at\nthe upload step:\n\n```\nRegistering application...\nUploading 1 file...\nFailed to upload .twenty/output/package.json: update or delete on table \"file\"\nviolates foreign key constraint \"FK_3818380258798f9ffa9963b6dc4\" on table \"application\"\n```\n\n`application.packageJsonFileId` references `core.file(id)` with `ON\nDELETE RESTRICT`, so changing that row''s id is refused. `yarnLockFileId`\nis the same shape. Applications whose pointers are null, which is every\nSDK app, never notice: their row''s id silently changes on each upload\ninstead.\n\nMeasured on a dev workspace, uploading an unchanged `package.json` once\nfor an application with a null pointer:\n\n```\nbefore   f23e6ffb-36f2-4ecc-85bc-97d102767882   dependencies/package.json\nafter    1a27d934-7dff-4611-b6e4-b5488699a0af   dependencies/package.json\n```\n\nOne row throughout, new identity.\n\n## How\n\nBoth write paths, `writeFile` and `createPendingFile`, upsert on the\nnatural key `(''path'', ''workspaceId'', ''applicationId'')` while passing a\nfreshly generated `id` in the values. On conflict the generated column\nlist includes `id`, so the update rewrites the primary key of the row it\njust matched.\n\nThey now look the row up first and keep its identifier when one is\nalready stored at that path, so an upsert that matches an existing row\nleaves its identity alone and only refreshes the mutable columns. A path\nwith no row still inserts under the generated identifier, and\n`writeFile` still lets the database generate one when the caller passes\nnone.\n\nThe callers are unaffected: `createUploadTargetsBatch` already builds\nits upload target from the returned row''s `id` rather than the one it\ngenerated.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New spec on `FileStorageService`: the upsert receives the stored row''s\nidentifier when a row exists at that path, and the generated one when it\ndoes not. The first case fails against the previous code.\n- The mechanism was measured live, as quoted above, before making the\nchange.\n- Found while exercising `yarn twenty pull` end to end: pulling the\nCustom application works, but pushing that tree back with `yarn twenty\napply --no-delete` could not get past the upload.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25748?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"8897ebeeec006e852b2bb6b38a338fac24d2e674","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/8897ebeeec006e852b2bb6b38a338fac24d2e674"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/39acdbb46c28b365b23aeb27623adbde682b0240","verification":{"payload":"tree 8897ebeeec006e852b2bb6b38a338fac24d2e674\nparent 8e70bd9cf8851879146f8d339c1859c3647ac462\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789135187 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789135187 +0000\n\nKeep a stored file''s identifier when its content is uploaded again (#25748)\n\n## What\n\nRe-uploading a file an application already stores rewrites that file\nrow''s primary key. When something references the row, the write is\nrejected and the whole sync fails.\n\n`yarn twenty apply` on the workspace Custom application always fails at\nthe upload step:\n\n```\nRegistering application...\nUploading 1 file...\nFailed to upload .twenty/output/package.json: update or delete on table \"file\"\nviolates foreign key constraint \"FK_3818380258798f9ffa9963b6dc4\" on table \"application\"\n```\n\n`application.packageJsonFileId` references `core.file(id)` with `ON\nDELETE RESTRICT`, so changing that row''s id is refused. `yarnLockFileId`\nis the same shape. Applications whose pointers are null, which is every\nSDK app, never notice: their row''s id silently changes on each upload\ninstead.\n\nMeasured on a dev workspace, uploading an unchanged `package.json` once\nfor an application with a null pointer:\n\n```\nbefore   f23e6ffb-36f2-4ecc-85bc-97d102767882   dependencies/package.json\nafter    1a27d934-7dff-4611-b6e4-b5488699a0af   dependencies/package.json\n```\n\nOne row throughout, new identity.\n\n## How\n\nBoth write paths, `writeFile` and `createPendingFile`, upsert on the\nnatural key `(''path'', ''workspaceId'', ''applicationId'')` while passing a\nfreshly generated `id` in the values. On conflict the generated column\nlist includes `id`, so the update rewrites the primary key of the row it\njust matched.\n\nThey now look the row up first and keep its identifier when one is\nalready stored at that path, so an upsert that matches an existing row\nleaves its identity alone and only refreshes the mutable columns. A path\nwith no row still inserts under the generated identifier, and\n`writeFile` still lets the database generate one when the caller passes\nnone.\n\nThe callers are unaffected: `createUploadTargetsBatch` already builds\nits upload target from the returned row''s `id` rather than the one it\ngenerated.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New spec on `FileStorageService`: the upsert receives the stored row''s\nidentifier when a row exists at that path, and the generated one when it\ndoes not. The first case fails against the previous code.\n- The mechanism was measured live, as quoted above, before making the\nchange.\n- Found while exercising `yarn twenty pull` end to end: pulling the\nCustom application works, but pushing that tree back with `yarn twenty\napply --no-delete` could not get past the upload.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25748?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpAliCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZIIQAEwO0J5ECjoAxx28dRhaLK4J\n+HoeujGTJHRt0XWCp3WZLhvdZNYqXSNGBIVxZMmREyydsJJlUEdc9IfYbQlx60CX\nYs1XNL/NU5AWmEGEVWaxWcMXSy+tjpSJdA1VSFOUbVc7vaXBdiqYmIOd4W8bBMs1\nzPcjI4k7eEofM2OsDl3ztV0UtWk+WG3Vupik4C8UOIMqOXx4g1hWtDRreiuefWlg\nGrHTopp5sw3ZW8P0rooWpSdgRnAX0X4bA2XVCAFrQDHjpMgHncVseJYW5/opc87C\nX0xMKcFO5vkH0YCwSQ8z7yvhT/Km/61O/VfMXfbugLDwJ4oV16gLD36oTqIu7O6G\nI2LDJJ1dh4ICwEtKnWVU8+e4DUSyByS6SuwOTy/Q71ajWFUeuA9cIyJI/zZetl+1\nwinC/mR/MUv+x4TV9WHWGGqgeQBSwtfIQFuLFTBhAdABGPOELf0XdudFrmJbMURh\ncRB3EjxFbPVElqiQPZFngyotP5j0YfnwdZ6qQZmLnZn1IEolzGgTnnd/KQHZKA5M\ngtuRwfJRvev9/Qnf3+bTUbdLujJoysguqSyq8O7Ynvi1o95yHQVV/WigvrVI1xxx\nDzIQf0t8lMJG3U8yrO0A0Ygrxohjq1WSTVqOXtqfjSDzF1eZgEt0clSu4eFJNCoJ\nLT9puUhk0dt2HrWnwhoS\n=Std+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/39acdbb46c28b365b23aeb27623adbde682b0240","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDM5YWNkYmI0NmMyOGIzNjViMjNhZWIyNzYyM2FkYmRlNjgyYjAyNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/8e70bd9cf8851879146f8d339c1859c3647ac462","sha":"8e70bd9cf8851879146f8d339c1859c3647ac462","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8e70bd9cf8851879146f8d339c1859c3647ac462"}],"sha":"39acdbb46c28b365b23aeb27623adbde682b0240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/39acdbb46c28b365b23aeb27623adbde682b0240"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8e70bd9cf8851879146f8d339c1859c3647ac462/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:57:39Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:57:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(skills): split agent-only skills from user skills, rewrite the catalog (#25798)\n\nFollow-up to #25778, which added the `/` skill picker to the AI chat\ncomposer. Typing `/` today lists the agent''s internal know-how —\n`metadata-building`, `code-interpreter`, `view-filters-and-sorts` —\nbecause every standard skill is offered to the user. The catalog is also\nalmost entirely technical: it teaches the agent how to build views,\nworkflows and dashboards, but has nothing for the day-to-day CRM work a\nsalesperson actually does.\n\n## `isSystem` on Skill\n\nA new `isSystem` column separates the two kinds of skill. System skills\nstay fully loadable by the agent, but are hidden from:\n\n- the composer''s `/` picker (`useSkillSuggestionSearch`)\n- the settings skills list, unless advanced mode is on\n\nThe settings behaviour mirrors the existing \"System objects\" switch in\nthe data-model settings — same `isAdvancedModeEnabled && showX` pattern,\nsame `IconSettings`, so there is no new UI concept to learn.\n\n`isSystem` is wired through the entity, the DTO and its mappers, the\napp-manifest converter (app-shipped skills are never system) and the\ncreate-input mapper (user-created skills are never system).\n\n## Catalog changes\n\n**Removed three skills:**\n\n- `view-filters-and-sorts` — folded into `view-building`. The split\nforced the agent to load two skills to answer one question; the operator\ntable, sort/group rules and composite-field notes now live in\n`view-building` directly.\n- `research` — superseded by the web search tool, and replaced below by\n`enrich`, which actually writes back to the CRM.\n- `custom-objects-cleanup` — its only caller was\n`workspace-demo-seeding`, which now inlines the two-line archive step\n(`get_object_metadata`, filter `isCustom`, one\n`update_many_object_metadata`).\n\n**Marked the remaining 12 as system** and rewrote every description as a\ntrigger phrase. The description is what the agent matches against when\ndeciding whether to load a skill, so `\"Use when the data model itself\nchanges: adding or editing objects, fields, relations…\"` is worth more\nthan `\"Metadata building\"`.\n\n**Added four user-facing skills:**\n\n| Skill | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Meeting Prep** | Reads a person/company and everything hanging off\nit, produces a five-part brief with every record referenced. Read-only.\n|\n| **Deal Review** | Judges deal health on five signals — momentum,\ncontact, threading, hygiene, commitments — and names the signal behind\nevery risk call. Read-only. |\n| **CRM Hygiene** | Audits duplicates (via the object''s\n`duplicateCriteria`), missing fields, stale records and broken links;\nreports counts first, fixes only what''s approved. Never deletes, and\nnever merges — see below. |\n| **Enrich** | Drives the preloaded `app_exa_web_search` with `category`\nset to company / people / news, reconciles only empty fields, shows a\ntable of proposed changes before writing. |\n\n`enrich` is the Exa one — Exa is installed on all cloud workspaces and\n`app_exa_web_search` is already in `AI_CHAT_TOOL_NAMES_TO_PRELOAD`, so\nit calls the tool directly with no discovery round-trip.\n\n## Migration\n\nTwo commands, because the schema change alone would have left the\nfeature inert on every existing workspace:\n\n- `2-40-instance-command-fast-1789129759228-add-is-system-to-skill.ts`\nadds the column with `DEFAULT false`, with a matching `down`.\n-\n`2-40-workspace-command-1789129759229-reconcile-standard-skills.command.ts`\nreconciles the catalog itself.\n\nThe second one exists because of a review finding worth spelling out.\n`synchronizeTwentyStandardApplicationOrThrow` is the only full\ncreate/update/delete reconciliation of standard entities, and it has\nexactly two callers: `WorkspaceManagerService.init` (workspace creation)\nand the dev seeder. The two existing skill backfill commands (1-22,\n2-27) hardcode `flatEntityToUpdate: []` and `flatEntityToDelete: []`,\nand are pinned to versions a current workspace has already passed. So\nwithout a new command, existing workspaces would have kept `isSystem =\nfalse` on all 12 system skills, kept the three removed skills, and never\nreceived the four new ones.\n\nThe new command populates all three arrays: create by missing\n`universalIdentifier`, update the catalog-owned fields that drifted,\ndelete standard-app skills whose `universalIdentifier` left the catalog.\nDeletion is scoped to the standard application''s `applicationId`, so\ncustom and app-shipped skills are untouched. `isActive` is\nworkspace-owned, so a skill someone deactivated stays deactivated.\n\n## Worth flagging\n\n- **`workspace-demo-seeding` was kept, not deleted.** It contradicts\n`WORKSPACE_SETUP_SYSTEM_PROMPT` (\"Set up a real workspace this team will\nkeep using, not a demo… When in doubt, propose less\"), so it probably\nshouldn''t exist — but I don''t know whether sales demos depend on it.\nIt''s marked system for now, which at least takes it out of users'' way.\nHappy to drop it in a follow-up.\n- **The agent cannot merge records.** `database-tool.provider.ts`\nexposes find/create/update/upsert/delete and no merge; merging is a UI\naction only. CRM Hygiene therefore reports duplicate pairs and leaves\nthe merge to the user, with an explicit rule against faking one by\ncopying fields across and deleting the loser. Exposing a merge tool\nwould be a separate PR.\n- **No validator change.** I considered enforcing the trigger-phrase\ndescription shape in the flat-skill validator, but it would reject\nexisting custom skills, so it''s left out.\n- All four new skills are read-first and confirm before writing. None of\nthem can delete a record.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `npx nx test twenty-server` — 1185 suites, 8658 tests green\n- New unit tests for the reconcile command: create, delete, the\n`isSystem` flip preserving `isActive`, skills owned by another\napplication left alone, the no-op re-run, and dry run\n- New test asserting system skills are hidden by default, plus one that\nenables advanced mode and exercises both states of the \"System skills\"\nswitch\n- `nx run twenty-front:typecheck` — 0 errors; `tsgo --noEmit` clean on\ntwenty-server\n- `oxlint --type-aware` and `oxfmt --check` clean on every changed file\n- Metadata GraphQL regenerated against a locally running server\n\nNot verified in a browser — preview environments are unreachable from\nthis session''s network.","tree":{"sha":"6be5236fb1b4f9bab57c788797b159b10d195941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/6be5236fb1b4f9bab57c788797b159b10d195941"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/8e70bd9cf8851879146f8d339c1859c3647ac462","verification":{"payload":"tree 6be5236fb1b4f9bab57c788797b159b10d195941\nparent 302be2bc7a41b6cbe25cfb5cf489a0da86eedf1a\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789135059 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789135059 +0200\n\nfeat(skills): split agent-only skills from user skills, rewrite the catalog (#25798)\n\nFollow-up to #25778, which added the `/` skill picker to the AI chat\ncomposer. Typing `/` today lists the agent''s internal know-how —\n`metadata-building`, `code-interpreter`, `view-filters-and-sorts` —\nbecause every standard skill is offered to the user. The catalog is also\nalmost entirely technical: it teaches the agent how to build views,\nworkflows and dashboards, but has nothing for the day-to-day CRM work a\nsalesperson actually does.\n\n## `isSystem` on Skill\n\nA new `isSystem` column separates the two kinds of skill. System skills\nstay fully loadable by the agent, but are hidden from:\n\n- the composer''s `/` picker (`useSkillSuggestionSearch`)\n- the settings skills list, unless advanced mode is on\n\nThe settings behaviour mirrors the existing \"System objects\" switch in\nthe data-model settings — same `isAdvancedModeEnabled && showX` pattern,\nsame `IconSettings`, so there is no new UI concept to learn.\n\n`isSystem` is wired through the entity, the DTO and its mappers, the\napp-manifest converter (app-shipped skills are never system) and the\ncreate-input mapper (user-created skills are never system).\n\n## Catalog changes\n\n**Removed three skills:**\n\n- `view-filters-and-sorts` — folded into `view-building`. The split\nforced the agent to load two skills to answer one question; the operator\ntable, sort/group rules and composite-field notes now live in\n`view-building` directly.\n- `research` — superseded by the web search tool, and replaced below by\n`enrich`, which actually writes back to the CRM.\n- `custom-objects-cleanup` — its only caller was\n`workspace-demo-seeding`, which now inlines the two-line archive step\n(`get_object_metadata`, filter `isCustom`, one\n`update_many_object_metadata`).\n\n**Marked the remaining 12 as system** and rewrote every description as a\ntrigger phrase. The description is what the agent matches against when\ndeciding whether to load a skill, so `\"Use when the data model itself\nchanges: adding or editing objects, fields, relations…\"` is worth more\nthan `\"Metadata building\"`.\n\n**Added four user-facing skills:**\n\n| Skill | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Meeting Prep** | Reads a person/company and everything hanging off\nit, produces a five-part brief with every record referenced. Read-only.\n|\n| **Deal Review** | Judges deal health on five signals — momentum,\ncontact, threading, hygiene, commitments — and names the signal behind\nevery risk call. Read-only. |\n| **CRM Hygiene** | Audits duplicates (via the object''s\n`duplicateCriteria`), missing fields, stale records and broken links;\nreports counts first, fixes only what''s approved. Never deletes, and\nnever merges — see below. |\n| **Enrich** | Drives the preloaded `app_exa_web_search` with `category`\nset to company / people / news, reconciles only empty fields, shows a\ntable of proposed changes before writing. |\n\n`enrich` is the Exa one — Exa is installed on all cloud workspaces and\n`app_exa_web_search` is already in `AI_CHAT_TOOL_NAMES_TO_PRELOAD`, so\nit calls the tool directly with no discovery round-trip.\n\n## Migration\n\nTwo commands, because the schema change alone would have left the\nfeature inert on every existing workspace:\n\n- `2-40-instance-command-fast-1789129759228-add-is-system-to-skill.ts`\nadds the column with `DEFAULT false`, with a matching `down`.\n-\n`2-40-workspace-command-1789129759229-reconcile-standard-skills.command.ts`\nreconciles the catalog itself.\n\nThe second one exists because of a review finding worth spelling out.\n`synchronizeTwentyStandardApplicationOrThrow` is the only full\ncreate/update/delete reconciliation of standard entities, and it has\nexactly two callers: `WorkspaceManagerService.init` (workspace creation)\nand the dev seeder. The two existing skill backfill commands (1-22,\n2-27) hardcode `flatEntityToUpdate: []` and `flatEntityToDelete: []`,\nand are pinned to versions a current workspace has already passed. So\nwithout a new command, existing workspaces would have kept `isSystem =\nfalse` on all 12 system skills, kept the three removed skills, and never\nreceived the four new ones.\n\nThe new command populates all three arrays: create by missing\n`universalIdentifier`, update the catalog-owned fields that drifted,\ndelete standard-app skills whose `universalIdentifier` left the catalog.\nDeletion is scoped to the standard application''s `applicationId`, so\ncustom and app-shipped skills are untouched. `isActive` is\nworkspace-owned, so a skill someone deactivated stays deactivated.\n\n## Worth flagging\n\n- **`workspace-demo-seeding` was kept, not deleted.** It contradicts\n`WORKSPACE_SETUP_SYSTEM_PROMPT` (\"Set up a real workspace this team will\nkeep using, not a demo… When in doubt, propose less\"), so it probably\nshouldn''t exist — but I don''t know whether sales demos depend on it.\nIt''s marked system for now, which at least takes it out of users'' way.\nHappy to drop it in a follow-up.\n- **The agent cannot merge records.** `database-tool.provider.ts`\nexposes find/create/update/upsert/delete and no merge; merging is a UI\naction only. CRM Hygiene therefore reports duplicate pairs and leaves\nthe merge to the user, with an explicit rule against faking one by\ncopying fields across and deleting the loser. Exposing a merge tool\nwould be a separate PR.\n- **No validator change.** I considered enforcing the trigger-phrase\ndescription shape in the flat-skill validator, but it would reject\nexisting custom skills, so it''s left out.\n- All four new skills are read-first and confirm before writing. None of\nthem can delete a record.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `npx nx test twenty-server` — 1185 suites, 8658 tests green\n- New unit tests for the reconcile command: create, delete, the\n`isSystem` flip preserving `isActive`, skills owned by another\napplication left alone, the no-op re-run, and dry run\n- New test asserting system skills are hidden by default, plus one that\nenables advanced mode and exercises both states of the \"System skills\"\nswitch\n- `nx run twenty-front:typecheck` — 0 errors; `tsgo --noEmit` clean on\ntwenty-server\n- `oxlint --type-aware` and `oxfmt --check` clean on every changed file\n- Metadata GraphQL regenerated against a locally running server\n\nNot verified in a browser — preview environments are unreachable from\nthis session''s network.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpAjTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS5kQAKnszj61U8tCI1w8IwRw3W/y\nmZqbxmAS6qzivBeQSA42xw79M037hMsFpea0TLD//m5MO8BSen9CmhLRjPMjZixm\nRTG3qBseOwjy07xfDEy5xOGZDBd7SPCShS15cGz+aVEiXmc77n9inSVZOjmKDR5i\nT13l31pgqJbv5M/F7vSfa3CLi8dljkkB0tFUIVXSJkATxxevwRR55SI3c2qJu00G\n8UPFuDLOixfWxX34OSl/lASfAS+/uxRnyIK0VX8LyPtg+xoJBqTCoCrc5FoQcX/t\n5m8/oKvaE1GYe4UMF4q59lkiUj+Ckx6/vOARVnnsRuGtnytJ2UBpcE61WgqI5xCk\nJmWE9K0KluAyKG9eA4/t2a/czKjeFpVoiWcxMVRwchn1nChSm3EuMv1y9UDwhLLn\n3kRSYWkM2nVQdHc5CheMHuhUdQEa0eNFCtJziEXZawkbI+GgHY7GDd06crVeAGGv\naL9FUv+/++Arfngewo7hibtkN7xMLAtplyFlcD2/Uaivf41TJ+lC0LV9dDOjQ+3J\nyUaUB6ihi5MYJlI2j/IjP/IckQJab6FH3C4DEV/WDrHFv+wwZEBEzXDi+l+PvLAt\nU9/dA7cB26mI9H+4pmVZquPJasEGvItJ99AldGMwSLnDzKf4agZd+2Xn+spdpFhw\n8GtE8Cwjo4od70ySAacv\n=qeMA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/8e70bd9cf8851879146f8d339c1859c3647ac462","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDhlNzBiZDljZjg4NTE4NzkxNDZmOGQzMzljMTg1OWMzNjQ3YWM0NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/302be2bc7a41b6cbe25cfb5cf489a0da86eedf1a","sha":"302be2bc7a41b6cbe25cfb5cf489a0da86eedf1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/302be2bc7a41b6cbe25cfb5cf489a0da86eedf1a"}],"sha":"8e70bd9cf8851879146f8d339c1859c3647ac462","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8e70bd9cf8851879146f8d339c1859c3647ac462"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142569587?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ehconitin","id":142569587,"login":"ehconitin","node_id":"U_kgDOCH9wcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/302be2bc7a41b6cbe25cfb5cf489a0da86eedf1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:41:14Z","email":"142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nitin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:41:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Finish call recordings without a transcript when Recall rejects the transcript request (#25794)\n\nStacked on #25793.\n\nWhen Recall rejects the transcript request with a non-retryable status,\nthe recording finishes without a transcript (an \\`EMPTY\\` marker\ncarrying the status as sub code) instead of staying in PROCESSING.\nRetryable and lost-response failures behave as before.\n\nDeferred: 401, 402 and 403 are Twenty-side and transient (key or Recall\nbalance); narrowing the terminal set so those stay in PROCESSING for the\ndaily reconciler to retry.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25794?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"754ad3b7694ced621faee436d42e1424f1fe03f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/754ad3b7694ced621faee436d42e1424f1fe03f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/302be2bc7a41b6cbe25cfb5cf489a0da86eedf1a","verification":{"payload":"tree 754ad3b7694ced621faee436d42e1424f1fe03f9\nparent 00598ef1ed537b4dec6214f2f68f6f5fdd430b6e\nauthor nitin <142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com> 1789134074 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789134074 +0000\n\nFinish call recordings without a transcript when Recall rejects the transcript request (#25794)\n\nStacked on #25793.\n\nWhen Recall rejects the transcript request with a non-retryable status,\nthe recording finishes without a transcript (an \\`EMPTY\\` marker\ncarrying the status as sub code) instead of staying in PROCESSING.\nRetryable and lost-response failures behave as before.\n\nDeferred: 401, 402 and 403 are Twenty-side and transient (key or Recall\nbalance); narrowing the terminal set so those stay in PROCESSING for the\ndaily reconciler to retry.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25794?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpAUJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHhcQACiLeAW3/ivh1ijQksoZD7Ds\nL3u535f4Vj2WT69vqbZ3RURSMASbfM0BGbM3PuuLg+btc4NFU8Pld4cSvHk/BNgo\nAyKt26/tx6/Ts7lIodvOX5k/+KMIODyEp7hDN04JGmbstt8tnsL/AsxlL664Fpj2\n/Q74k/2i2uv87EbQlfMkkxk/d0BwfHE91vkQUp+JRNEIHKD2fR6+eKoU74F40MB/\nGkTPePp8ESjkp9Ec8V5QGm1liSE0QeAqvJSm/e63rtTJeRLnbWk+usGQcWmonFhZ\n6TbQK9/LqpTGk6gh+4TzHIGqiDe+uP4N+nFv