ayload":"tree e4387551e568b03e8a469f7110844b69071dc0ee\nparent 489118f25b44af148937450cc8678b5093200243\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1789129848 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789129848 +0000\n\nMigrate Status to the new twenty-ui API (#25785)\n\nStatus used heading markup and custom keyboard handling for interactive\ncontent. Migrate it to children/loading, native props and refs, and Base\nUI button behavior when onClick is provided. Update consumers and add\nconformance, light/dark catalog, and React/Preact renderer coverage.\n\nValidation: 11 unit tests, 6 UI browser stories, and 4 renderer checks\npass. UI, frontend, and renderer direct typechecks, regular/individual\nUI builds, lint, and formatting pass.\n\nPart 1 of 4. Review against `main` and merge in this order:\n\n[Status #25785](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25785) → [Tag\n#25786](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25786) → [Avatar\n#25787](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25787) → [Chip\n#25788](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25788)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo/SICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPbgQAJWOOl3cIQAEDt3algiEN6vE\ntxlDMibNCxHJa0lFBEppEksIlIkPMGn7ASlSLTO0KZTEDeBcXxIdRryfyUPLvJuL\n8F8gQW0lkLAYP6I5g0zTxCiXLhBfw9oJOF/rU42nLYn6Zcy1g9DttPp+Ak7IzaIf\nvycK7ETiw8V5i7PMhqlQUW284RzSCYbpoa0NNRE4jSO1nLqcCvO/zN/o0dYtwD1V\nV+YwAgbdVSCmxz25f8SNhcnM8RLwA0FhHAHD877u0g7ti1Vih0WP0VxTieU0b7r7\ncCWOVGJYKXjwbciy6kATeiU6aWryisoU6RYDzX98vTtj91yJ6dA/AvA3daW/529A\ndNX/At7gM88jvZPS7aSbcqCj/4aVxmNf/ezqhcYMhqLbA4SKEkfbcgBiaTezRfXc\n2TfDTE39o6tL/NVmHPp0F8iMmexfr63y4FWRldOirGvmMA65qs+1z0thc6vWtf1f\nM6eB9Hr6Xk7/75ns0a9yv8SuAJA8tKbK7VqzVlrpu4ok7Rth3UOLvbkXKcYDfy+T\njQWrB8bO7stHEut643zA73Moq8XYyiVT45zGmLFTywhrVvHxQfYxCQu/lEP8JxfN\n0VGLLfdzn1KrD6F+cNNwULx8n9th8/LWLFXmTR7sE1VfrrP5jU3ybpEnh/qF8gJC\nkdUUcIhV9naBbgJGYeHc\n=penz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/7522e1deaab1ef6e39ced1c5a2c0ee2923b15fcc","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDc1MjJlMWRlYWFiMWVmNmUzOWNlZDFjNWEyYzBlZTI5MjNiMTVmY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/489118f25b44af148937450cc8678b5093200243","sha":"489118f25b44af148937450cc8678b5093200243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/489118f25b44af148937450cc8678b5093200243"}],"sha":"7522e1deaab1ef6e39ced1c5a2c0ee2923b15fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/7522e1deaab1ef6e39ced1c5a2c0ee2923b15fcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/489118f25b44af148937450cc8678b5093200243/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:17:24Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:17:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(ai): seed the agent and skill settings forms from the loaded record (#25764)\n\nFollow-up to #25753, which memoized the callbacks that made the agent\npage loop but left the mechanism in place.\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe agent and skill pages mounted an empty form, fired the query, and\nthen an effect copied the loaded record into form state. That form\nexisted in a wrong state for a render, a cache update after autosave or\na refetch re-ran the copy over what the user was typing, and the\neffect''s dependency list was a trap: the loop in #25753 came from two\nunstable callbacks in it, and the skill page carried an\n`initializedSkillId` guard against the same class of problem.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Shell and content**: `SettingsAgentForm` and `SettingsSkillForm` now\nonly own the query. They render the skeleton page while loading, render\nnothing while a missing record or a failed query redirects to the 404\npage with a snackbar, and otherwise mount `SettingsAgentFormContent` /\n`SettingsSkillFormContent` with the record as a prop, keyed by its id so\nswitching records is a remount rather than a re-seed. Create mode mounts\nthe content with no record.\n- **State seeded from props**: `useSettingsAgentFormState` takes initial\nvalues instead of a mode; `getSettingsAgentInitialFormValues` and\n`getSettingsSkillInitialFormValues` hold the mapping the effects used to\ndo, with unit tests. The autosave baseline starts from the same object,\nso the comparison is meaningful from the first render. The load effects,\nthe `resetForm` callback and its memoization comment, and the skill\npage''s `initializedSkillId` guard are gone.\n- **Readonly is derived, not state**: for a skill, `!skill.isCustom`.\nFor an agent, `isOwnedByInstalledApplication`, the rule the tools tab\nalready used and now shares: owned by an application other than the\nworkspace''s own. The old rule, any `applicationId` at all, has marked\nevery agent created in the UI as readonly since the column became\nmandatory\n(`1768213174274-makeAgentUniversalIdentifierAndApplicationIdNotNullable`),\nso the agent settings could not be edited at all. Found while moving the\nflag, fixed here since it is the line being rewritten.\n- **Skill instructions editor**: it was keyed on\n`originalFormValues.content`, which changed after every autosave and\nremounted the editor mid-typing. It now mounts once with the seeded\ncontent.\n- **Autosave like the other settings forms**: the field change handlers\nschedule the debounced save, as the AI overview tab, the tool detail\npage and the workspace member page do. Role permissions are edited by\nthe shared roles module through Jotai state with no change handler, so\nthat trigger stays an effect on `isRoleDirty` inside the save hook, as\nthe name fields do for state-driven saves.\n- **Hooks and components**: create, update and autosave handlers live in\n`useSettingsAgentSave` and `useSettingsSkillSave`; the failed-load\nredirect in `useNavigateToNotFoundOnLoadFailure`. The skill danger zone\n(deactivate, activate, delete, confirmation modal) is\n`SettingsSkillDangerZone`. No component calls `useEffect`. Shared\nbreadcrumb links for the AI settings pages, and the two tabs import the\nform values type from the schema file.\n\n## Verification\n\n- oxlint, `tsgo` and the ai settings suites pass.\n- Browser on a local instance: agent edit page seeded with the record,\nstandard application agent readonly, custom agent editable with a\ndescription autosaved once and kept in the field afterwards, create page\nsaving and returning to the list, a bad id redirecting to 404, skill\nedit page seeded and readonly for a standard skill. No \"Maximum update\ndepth\" output on any of them.","tree":{"sha":"8ff61c67f38ce41829e2244a552a80690544c0e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/8ff61c67f38ce41829e2244a552a80690544c0e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/489118f25b44af148937450cc8678b5093200243","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ff61c67f38ce41829e2244a552a80690544c0e2\nparent ed653db19cb0ce5790bb666cca011a7b723bba58\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789129044 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789129044 +0200\n\nrefactor(ai): seed the agent and skill settings forms from the loaded record (#25764)\n\nFollow-up to #25753, which memoized the callbacks that made the agent\npage loop but left the mechanism in place.\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe agent and skill pages mounted an empty form, fired the query, and\nthen an effect copied the loaded record into form state. That form\nexisted in a wrong state for a render, a cache update after autosave or\na refetch re-ran the copy over what the user was typing, and the\neffect''s dependency list was a trap: the loop in #25753 came from two\nunstable callbacks in it, and the skill page carried an\n`initializedSkillId` guard against the same class of problem.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Shell and content**: `SettingsAgentForm` and `SettingsSkillForm` now\nonly own the query. They render the skeleton page while loading, render\nnothing while a missing record or a failed query redirects to the 404\npage with a snackbar, and otherwise mount `SettingsAgentFormContent` /\n`SettingsSkillFormContent` with the record as a prop, keyed by its id so\nswitching records is a remount rather than a re-seed. Create mode mounts\nthe content with no record.\n- **State seeded from props**: `useSettingsAgentFormState` takes initial\nvalues instead of a mode; `getSettingsAgentInitialFormValues` and\n`getSettingsSkillInitialFormValues` hold the mapping the effects used to\ndo, with unit tests. The autosave baseline starts from the same object,\nso the comparison is meaningful from the first render. The load effects,\nthe `resetForm` callback and its memoization comment, and the skill\npage''s `initializedSkillId` guard are gone.\n- **Readonly is derived, not state**: for a skill, `!skill.isCustom`.\nFor an agent, `isOwnedByInstalledApplication`, the rule the tools tab\nalready used and now shares: owned by an application other than the\nworkspace''s own. The old rule, any `applicationId` at all, has marked\nevery agent created in the UI as readonly since the column became\nmandatory\n(`1768213174274-makeAgentUniversalIdentifierAndApplicationIdNotNullable`),\nso the agent settings could not be edited at all. Found while moving the\nflag, fixed here since it is the line being rewritten.\n- **Skill instructions editor**: it was keyed on\n`originalFormValues.content`, which changed after every autosave and\nremounted the editor mid-typing. It now mounts once with the seeded\ncontent.\n- **Autosave like the other settings forms**: the field change handlers\nschedule the debounced save, as the AI overview tab, the tool detail\npage and the workspace member page do. Role permissions are edited by\nthe shared roles module through Jotai state with no change handler, so\nthat trigger stays an effect on `isRoleDirty` inside the save hook, as\nthe name fields do for state-driven saves.\n- **Hooks and components**: create, update and autosave handlers live in\n`useSettingsAgentSave` and `useSettingsSkillSave`; the failed-load\nredirect in `useNavigateToNotFoundOnLoadFailure`. The skill danger zone\n(deactivate, activate, delete, confirmation modal) is\n`SettingsSkillDangerZone`. No component calls `useEffect`. Shared\nbreadcrumb links for the AI settings pages, and the two tabs import the\nform values type from the schema file.\n\n## Verification\n\n- oxlint, `tsgo` and the ai settings suites pass.\n- Browser on a local instance: agent edit page seeded with the record,\nstandard application agent readonly, custom agent editable with a\ndescription autosaved once and kept in the field afterwards, create page\nsaving and returning to the list, a bad id redirecting to 404, skill\nedit page seeded and readonly for a standard skill. No \"Maximum update\ndepth\" output on any of them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo/FUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqEMQAJ/c696hAn3EE/TddR8mdd0V\nF6kU47CtYbBWhbEKuYm1DKSCOCghosJqlUANGiQV9X+THZrGwl5AP1DEdL00AvJo\nhmHX+Vc4ilm1Y4sL36iLHQfXkb5OQ0I0kfwAMecwtyO6E6y2VZDaI0Edqu+Wr2iV\nLXWX7/+88c/HE1W+dCEvqzD+5oLVgZP42LtLEVCJ1aYfkgP7WdWGXS89tLn9Vwg8\nKyVpyieQuosqgoLKgBkaxBDumwDxlKAlPfquDsaBtTjBIWZEbX8+ZvdVEj4or52S\n9cGDJnnxo9Wu619tdvxZQePBKCWBuptjI6K9ydBkbqN3pZjOm91SKofCM+jEGWlL\n7JS9rtsH343wiK+BclpqZMF2yJAnvbbQNEy8/vgJqsbHAZALnkgeRUEn8xBBWQ1R\nbQmdpUOQOlxJKsHGrSB0fTDw0pW0XHPlk27guNwrTXITu/+NA7W9DxBNjg5Jy2sR\nxBp9QUSqYWt1RDs4KHO7H/Tq3ohPr1WDmrTjZI37fgF4EM6Rvj0dc+UEVODvKiIs\n68vW+7h1Eb8sP1Un444GCF6IYPEcRagSF+ITITBOTaweo7/9cudu7rA5OdpGncBy\nCnppREHTTVmEKqPhygYcn4w+aXs9BjBj30Fw1Fhvopc+ihULAjTW5VrCGFs/qI5A\nW83WT16rWC4lin9J2i8f\n=ZRbw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/489118f25b44af148937450cc8678b5093200243","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDQ4OTExOGYyNWI0NGFmMTQ4OTM3NDUwY2M4Njc4YjUwOTMyMDAyNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/ed653db19cb0ce5790bb666cca011a7b723bba58","sha":"ed653db19cb0ce5790bb666cca011a7b723bba58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/ed653db19cb0ce5790bb666cca011a7b723bba58"}],"sha":"489118f25b44af148937450cc8678b5093200243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/489118f25b44af148937450cc8678b5093200243"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/ed653db19cb0ce5790bb666cca011a7b723bba58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:16:29Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:16:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(front): create component instance ids once instead of rewriting them per surface (#25790)\n\nFixes #25755.\n\n## Root cause\n\nComponent state is keyed by an `instanceId`. Since the side-panel work,\nfive shared components (`Dropdown`, `ModalStatefulWrapper`,\n`SelectableList`, `TabList`, `ScrollWrapper`) plus `SortableTableHeader`\n/ `useSortedArray` / `useScrollRestoration` and the `useOpenDropdown` /\n`useCloseDropdown` / `useToggleDropdown` / `useModal` /\n`useSelectableList` hooks silently rewrote the id they were given by\nappending the workspace surface instance id. Every reader that held the\noriginal id therefore read a different atom in a side panel: the country\npicker''s `SelectableList` wrote its selection under `<id>-<panel>` while\nthe `AddressInput` hotkeys compared against `<id>`, so Enter and the\nclick handler never fired. The same divergence sat behind dead keyboard\nnavigation in every side-panel dropdown, focus ids that never matched,\nand readers that always got the default value.\n\nThe previous attempts patched readers one by one (a `-resolver` hook,\nper-callsite `useWorkspaceSurfaceScopedComponentInstanceId`, and\n#25780''s lint rule) and each added code on top of the rewriting.\n\n## Fix: an id is created once, from the identity of the thing it belongs\nto\n\n- The shared components and hooks use the id they are given, verbatim.\nNo rewriting anywhere in `ui/`.\n- Every reader-side `useWorkspaceSurfaceScopedComponentInstanceId(...)`\ncall is gone (about 45 files). Readers use the same id as the provider.\n- The only tree that genuinely mounts twice at once across surfaces is\nthe record index (a table in the main view and another in a routed side\npanel). Its chrome ids now derive from `recordIndexId`, which already\ncarries the surface: `getObjectOptionsDropdownId(recordIndexId)`,\n`getObjectSortDropdownId`, `getViewBarFilterDropdownId`,\n`getViewBarAdvancedFilterDropdownId`, `getAnyFieldSearchDropdownId`,\n`getViewPickerDropdownId`, `getRecordIndexRemoveSortingModalId`,\n`getRecordGroupReorderConfirmationModalId`. Sub-dropdowns and lists hang\noff their parent id (`${dropdownId}-field-list`,\n`${dropdownId}-view-type`, …), which lets `FILTER_FIELD_LIST_ID` and the\nthree view-picker sub-dropdown constants go away.\n- `useWorkspaceSurfaceScopedComponentInstanceId` survives only where an\nid is created for something a page mounts once per surface (record index\nid, record show page, page layout tab lists, the settings tab bars, the\nsettings scroll container). Its comment now says so.\n- Creators that were relying on the components to rewrite the id now\nhand their id to every consumer: the role assignment confirmation modal,\nthe field permission table sort header, `useSettingsActiveTabId`.\n\nNet effect on the tree: 143 files, +566 / -695 lines, fewer hooks, fewer\nconstants, no lint rule, and one rule to remember: *never rewrite an id;\nderive it once where the thing is created.*\n\n## Tests\n\n- `AddressInput.surfaceScope.test.tsx` reproduces #25755 (country picker\ninside a side-panel surface: click and keyboard both select).\n- `Select.surfaceScope.test.tsx` covers the same for the generic\n`Select`.\n- `SettingsRoutedFlowStateScope.test.tsx` probes now create their ids\nwith the helper once and use them verbatim.\n- `useSelectableList.surfaceScope.test.tsx` asserted the old\nwrite-scoped / read-raw mismatch and is removed.\n-\n`useInitializeFilterOnFieldMetadataItemFromViewBarFilterDropdown.test.tsx`\nexpects the focus id that the filter dropdown context provides.\n\n## Residual sharing (unchanged from before the surface refactor, listed\nso nobody mistakes it for a regression)\n\nIds that are still plain constants collide only when the same widget is\nopen on both surfaces at the same time: field pickers such as\n`getEditableChipDropdownId`, `PREVIEW_MODAL_ID`, the settings tab-bar\nconstants on single-surface pages, and the dashboard side-panel writers\nthat build a page-layout tab id from raw metadata\n(`setRecordPageActiveTabId`, `SidePanelPageLayoutTabSettingsContent`).\nEach of those now has exactly one place to derive an id from if it ever\nneeds to.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015hjgTjDmBnCsTdnozEQSgp\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_015hjgTjDmBnCsTdnozEQSgp)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25790?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"737fd67cb9f61b0a59af5ac42b3db297fe333dc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/737fd67cb9f61b0a59af5ac42b3db297fe333dc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/ed653db19cb0ce5790bb666cca011a7b723bba58","verification":{"payload":"tree 737fd67cb9f61b0a59af5ac42b3db297fe333dc7\nparent 5d7ffd7694c2db7f801abc48edb47cbc204ad68f\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789128989 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789128989 +0200\n\nfix(front): create component instance ids once instead of rewriting them per surface (#25790)\n\nFixes #25755.\n\n## Root cause\n\nComponent state is keyed by an `instanceId`. Since the side-panel work,\nfive shared components (`Dropdown`, `ModalStatefulWrapper`,\n`SelectableList`, `TabList`, `ScrollWrapper`) plus `SortableTableHeader`\n/ `useSortedArray` / `useScrollRestoration` and the `useOpenDropdown` /\n`useCloseDropdown` / `useToggleDropdown` / `useModal` /\n`useSelectableList` hooks silently rewrote the id they were given by\nappending the workspace surface instance id. Every reader that held the\noriginal id therefore read a different atom in a side panel: the country\npicker''s `SelectableList` wrote its selection under `<id>-<panel>` while\nthe `AddressInput` hotkeys compared against `<id>`, so Enter and the\nclick handler never fired. The same divergence sat behind dead keyboard\nnavigation in every side-panel dropdown, focus ids that never matched,\nand readers that always got the default value.\n\nThe previous attempts patched readers one by one (a `-resolver` hook,\nper-callsite `useWorkspaceSurfaceScopedComponentInstanceId`, and\n#25780''s lint rule) and each added code on top of the rewriting.\n\n## Fix: an id is created once, from the identity of the thing it belongs\nto\n\n- The shared components and hooks use the id they are given, verbatim.\nNo rewriting anywhere in `ui/`.\n- Every reader-side `useWorkspaceSurfaceScopedComponentInstanceId(...)`\ncall is gone (about 45 files). Readers use the same id as the provider.\n- The only tree that genuinely mounts twice at once across surfaces is\nthe record index (a table in the main view and another in a routed side\npanel). Its chrome ids now derive from `recordIndexId`, which already\ncarries the surface: `getObjectOptionsDropdownId(recordIndexId)`,\n`getObjectSortDropdownId`, `getViewBarFilterDropdownId`,\n`getViewBarAdvancedFilterDropdownId`, `getAnyFieldSearchDropdownId`,\n`getViewPickerDropdownId`, `getRecordIndexRemoveSortingModalId`,\n`getRecordGroupReorderConfirmationModalId`. Sub-dropdowns and lists hang\noff their parent id (`${dropdownId}-field-list`,\n`${dropdownId}-view-type`, …), which lets `FILTER_FIELD_LIST_ID` and the\nthree view-picker sub-dropdown constants go away.\n- `useWorkspaceSurfaceScopedComponentInstanceId` survives only where an\nid is created for something a page mounts once per surface (record index\nid, record show page, page layout tab lists, the settings tab bars, the\nsettings scroll container). Its comment now says so.\n- Creators that were relying on the components to rewrite the id now\nhand their id to every consumer: the role assignment confirmation modal,\nthe field permission table sort header, `useSettingsActiveTabId`.\n\nNet effect on the tree: 143 files, +566 / -695 lines, fewer hooks, fewer\nconstants, no lint rule, and one rule to remember: *never rewrite an id;\nderive it once where the thing is created.*\n\n## Tests\n\n- `AddressInput.surfaceScope.test.tsx` reproduces #25755 (country picker\ninside a side-panel surface: click and keyboard both select).\n- `Select.surfaceScope.test.tsx` covers the same for the generic\n`Select`.\n- `SettingsRoutedFlowStateScope.test.tsx` probes now create their ids\nwith the helper once and use them verbatim.\n- `useSelectableList.surfaceScope.test.tsx` asserted the old\nwrite-scoped / read-raw mismatch and is removed.\n-\n`useInitializeFilterOnFieldMetadataItemFromViewBarFilterDropdown.test.tsx`\nexpects the focus id that the filter dropdown context provides.\n\n## Residual sharing (unchanged from before the surface refactor, listed\nso nobody mistakes it for a regression)\n\nIds that are still plain constants collide only when the same widget is\nopen on both surfaces at the same time: field pickers such as\n`getEditableChipDropdownId`, `PREVIEW_MODAL_ID`, the settings tab-bar\nconstants on single-surface pages, and the dashboard side-panel writers\nthat build a page-layout tab id from raw metadata\n(`setRecordPageActiveTabId`, `SidePanelPageLayoutTabSettingsContent`).\nEach of those now has exactly one place to derive an id from if it ever\nneeds to.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015hjgTjDmBnCsTdnozEQSgp\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_015hjgTjDmBnCsTdnozEQSgp)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25790?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo/EdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARjgQAJhCyql9qPDmMAj22lqfbKYV\nADN+2Eklk2Ee70x2VKXpGAgnvBjdhXVIdpxzQIssg6D8SYkdBhgyqtuqQTK7DGj3\nawxw37O6MZ1rvjgfn5aC/V3X/BiadKKAtxOH61oi8WzGW97hkP+Cbii87qN8FsXc\n35EXeyLih1eiKJnTFqPjj4l8zOUmwNmeuILwjI+CiO/zknFOfgCxomi9MSSocmpD\nn3Hf4nDqDE7ee2q/ly8jeM3fjzDkWIQ5HOcULzyxB6+140mLgzUJWDSPrwvJ78YU\nF6vONiK6z6gyJH0XKal+v+MCTlkqDyp+rZIFBmQQZ0oP3tLAqID+eZL1N5b0EMiF\nmx/+W9ZveHjR3udOLYDZ1irMnb51dgplthKtuaeNLlO5EjyjcvJ3M6S2Myp8PiMi\nXOw8ZBNOuJhl21DU6JNYxglYU6QRHWelpVHgiIZyG/hgyQ3CKtKAWKZoIcE/OkyB\n+Wp/WBL2DgIVV9O66mdf0k72p1CP+ZvDm/6dRoLxdh50MbG0qrpB3/eAdnvJXNZr\nG46Ma8ucOG5b1OnPQDebZr/xwKvndBi8NRbBjKu75D8ED6QhXdFMVtxU7iy+ttKz\nyFYci1bZatWXVBYRNxmg1APMA0yY4dxefZ58I5aWhPgiYa83FzrsHXPASSe5iQ80\nj/fUO1E9+EE01eqFOtUK\n=yygF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/ed653db19cb0ce5790bb666cca011a7b723bba58","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGVkNjUzZGIxOWNiMGNlNTc5MGJiNjY2Y2NhMDExYTdiNzIzYmJhNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/5d7ffd7694c2db7f801abc48edb47cbc204ad68f","sha":"5d7ffd7694c2db7f801abc48edb47cbc204ad68f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5d7ffd7694c2db7f801abc48edb47cbc204ad68f"}],"sha":"ed653db19cb0ce5790bb666cca011a7b723bba58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/ed653db19cb0ce5790bb666cca011a7b723bba58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5d7ffd7694c2db7f801abc48edb47cbc204ad68f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:23:10Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:23:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ai-chat): hint @ and / in composer placeholder, add / skill suggestions (#25778)\n\n## Summary\n\nFew people know the AI chat composer supports `@` to reference records.\nThis PR makes that discoverable and adds `/` to reference a skill.\n\n- **Placeholder** now reads \"Ask anything, @ a record or / a skill...\"\n(also updated the matching Storybook story, with a `play` step).\n- **`/` skill suggestions**: typing `/` in the AI chat composer opens a\nmenu of the workspace''s active skills, filtered by name or label as you\ntype. Rows show the skill icon and label only; a preview card to the\nright of the selected row (flipping left when there is no room) shows\nthe icon, label, `/name` and full description, like the record preview\ncard in search.\n- **Skill chips**: picking a skill inserts a `skillTag` node rendered as\na chip that links to the skill''s settings page. It is serialized to the\nagent as `[[skill:skillId:label]]`, mirroring record mentions, and sent\nmessages render it as a chip through a new `skill` chat-reference kind.\n- **Preloading**: skills referenced in user messages are inlined into\nthe system prompt under \"Referenced Skills\", so the agent follows them\ndirectly instead of spending a round trip on `load_skills`.\n- **Permissions**: `SkillResolver` reads now sit under the `AI`\npermission and mutations under `AI_SETTINGS`, mirroring `AgentResolver`,\nso members with Ask AI but no AI settings can use the picker.\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- New `skill-suggestion` module in twenty-front mirrors the existing\n`mention` module (Tiptap `Suggestion` extension, `SkillTag` node, chip\nnode view, shared `SuggestionMenu`), wired into\n`AI_CHAT_EDITOR_PROFILE`.\n- `SuggestionMenu` gained an optional `selectedItemPreview` slot\n(anchored `AppTooltip`, same mechanics as the search preview) so the `@`\nmenu can adopt it later.\n- The picker uses a slim `FindManySkillsForSuggestion` query (`id name\nlabel description icon isActive`, no `content`) on the metadata Apollo\nclient. It fetches `network-only` when the menu opens and `cache-first`\nwhile narrowing, so skills deleted or deactivated in settings drop out\non the next open.\n- `twenty-shared` gains `formatSkillReference` and a `skillTag` case in\n`tipTapDocumentToMarkdown`. The server matches references by the\n`[[skill:<uuid>:` prefix only, so a label containing brackets still\npreloads.\n- The `/` trigger relies on Tiptap''s default prefix rule (same as `@`\nmentions): it opens at line start, after a space, or after a hard break,\nand stays closed inside a word such as `https://`. This is pinned by\ntests.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `SkillSuggestion`, `SkillTag` and `formatSkillReference` unit\ntests; `parseChatReferences` and `ChatReferenceChip` cover the new\n`skill` kind\n- [x] Server specs for `collectReferencedSkillIds`,\n`buildReferencedSkillsSection` and `buildFullSystemPrompt`\n- [x] twenty-front typecheck clean for changed files; oxlint/oxfmt clean\non all three packages\n- [x] `generated-metadata/graphql.ts` regenerated with `graphql:generate\n--configuration=metadata` against a local server\n- [ ] Manual: open AI chat as a member with Ask AI only, type `/`, pick\na skill, check the chip and preview card, send, confirm the agent\nfollows the skill without calling `load_skills`\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25778?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture>``&lt;source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;&lt;source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"&gt;&lt;img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;``</picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"8ddf5216acd80b40814ca80b300c36989aa85016","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/8ddf5216acd80b40814ca80b300c36989aa85016"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/5d7ffd7694c2db7f801abc48edb47cbc204ad68f","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ddf5216acd80b40814ca80b300c36989aa85016\nparent 33829b9973ef4f6fce895ea74176fe4c02221be4\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789125790 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789125790 +0200\n\nfeat(ai-chat): hint @ and / in composer placeholder, add / skill suggestions (#25778)\n\n## Summary\n\nFew people know the AI chat composer supports `@` to reference records.\nThis PR makes that discoverable and adds `/` to reference a skill.\n\n- **Placeholder** now reads \"Ask anything, @ a record or / a skill...\"\n(also updated the matching Storybook story, with a `play` step).\n- **`/` skill suggestions**: typing `/` in the AI chat composer opens a\nmenu of the workspace''s active skills, filtered by name or label as you\ntype. Rows show the skill icon and label only; a preview card to the\nright of the selected row (flipping left when there is no room) shows\nthe icon, label, `/name` and full description, like the record preview\ncard in search.\n- **Skill chips**: picking a skill inserts a `skillTag` node rendered as\na chip that links to the skill''s settings page. It is serialized to the\nagent as `[[skill:skillId:label]]`, mirroring record mentions, and sent\nmessages render it as a chip through a new `skill` chat-reference kind.\n- **Preloading**: skills referenced in user messages are inlined into\nthe system prompt under \"Referenced Skills\", so the agent follows them\ndirectly instead of spending a round trip on `load_skills`.\n- **Permissions**: `SkillResolver` reads now sit under the `AI`\npermission and mutations under `AI_SETTINGS`, mirroring `AgentResolver`,\nso members with Ask AI but no AI settings can use the picker.\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- New `skill-suggestion` module in twenty-front mirrors the existing\n`mention` module (Tiptap `Suggestion` extension, `SkillTag` node, chip\nnode view, shared `SuggestionMenu`), wired into\n`AI_CHAT_EDITOR_PROFILE`.\n- `SuggestionMenu` gained an optional `selectedItemPreview` slot\n(anchored `AppTooltip`, same mechanics as the search preview) so the `@`\nmenu can adopt it later.\n- The picker uses a slim `FindManySkillsForSuggestion` query (`id name\nlabel description icon isActive`, no `content`) on the metadata Apollo\nclient. It fetches `network-only` when the menu opens and `cache-first`\nwhile narrowing, so skills deleted or deactivated in settings drop out\non the next open.\n- `twenty-shared` gains `formatSkillReference` and a `skillTag` case in\n`tipTapDocumentToMarkdown`. The server matches references by the\n`[[skill:<uuid>:` prefix only, so a label containing brackets still\npreloads.\n- The `/` trigger relies on Tiptap''s default prefix rule (same as `@`\nmentions): it opens at line start, after a space, or after a hard break,\nand stays closed inside a word such as `https://`. This is pinned by\ntests.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `SkillSuggestion`, `SkillTag` and `formatSkillReference` unit\ntests; `parseChatReferences` and `ChatReferenceChip` cover the new\n`skill` kind\n- [x] Server specs for `collectReferencedSkillIds`,\n`buildReferencedSkillsSection` and `buildFullSystemPrompt`\n- [x] twenty-front typecheck clean for changed files; oxlint/oxfmt clean\non all three packages\n- [x] `generated-metadata/graphql.ts` regenerated with `graphql:generate\n--configuration=metadata` against a local server\n- [ ] Manual: open AI chat as a member with Ask AI only, type `/`, pick\na skill, check the chip and preview card, send, confirm the agent\nfollows the skill without calling `load_skills`\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25778?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture>``&lt;source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;&lt;source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"&gt;&lt;img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;``</picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo+SeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAikgQADRGE5IEUBs8Egmn6m7+YCtj\nuZCFY0RcJ38cVDvsO9jiv5qHZ2wuukp145EKvyLmYHBXoGzkQInyrlaD7KPzgl8x\nT361mdWh+E2kUwdiLW/5m+2YGZQHxQs9GSWuP/7QOP85QdYAV6phfRWSYpYVVa/t\n7t4jHDiDFSaJgx1D4O+/FFED9BJzEFw8q7uhgZeoXzYUCH2g+/Q4Gp96u7wODgum\nmKeBqYxKdWPdjBOwFzHjtycOuy8FxN6uO6E2WJ06wnzXCVycZ8+KeyVSnWmjfbqA\nPrVUn25Qsh5+UpFBXnI6tY/Ap7HrEGe4Agl8QouywKcbGcjkRWAc8n4MIPXvxFEx\nMUCmUQqHCh0gxIllEdbOI1f+R7jNrDds5a5Wo8v4J79TB3rXWNO+pplSR+c9+1IY\nLQYCKcJeUVmL/BOoY3KidtRX2GL3j8CkMTLBLcZk+H5gXZPQj7OYBFXPVKu0+clS\nRa/ByJ8Ajd5XoIRF/aMkvO/qqF+G4EREVLu6myppPq4bCjy+0sZ0ki9eg9He9nC1\nK0yF7EuPOk3OA/kU5mEkDfaVdLwArxVMHrO363/4