://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/079b6e0ce37920fd97ba8c4b6e2d81c9ad78d158/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:43:48Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:43:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(server): extract a single LRU eviction primitive (#25733)\n\n## Why\n\nFollow-up to #25659, addressing @Weiko''s review comment:\n\n> We already have LRU eviction in\n`CoreEntityCacheService.evictLRUEntriesIfNeeded` and `sweepLocalCache`.\nNeither is directly reusable for a plain Map, but we could extract a\nshared primitive instead of adding a third eviction implementation?\n\nThe comment is right, and the count was worse than it looked. There were\n**four** copies of the same algorithm:\n\n| # | Site | Ranked by |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `campaign-variable.service.ts` `evictLeastRecentlyUsedSchemas` |\ninsertion order |\n| 2 | `lru-map.util.ts` `writeLruEntry` (added in #25659) | insertion\norder |\n| 3 | `sweep-local-cache.util.ts` `evictLeastRecentlyRead` |\n`lastReadAt` |\n| 4 | `core-entity-cache.service.ts` `evictLRUEntriesIfNeeded` |\n`lastHashCheckedAt` |\n\n1 and 2 are the same code written twice — #25659 added its own without\nnoticing `campaign-variable` already had it. 3 and 4 likewise.\n\nThis PR takes **4 → 2**. Adopting the util in `campaign-variable` alone\nwould only return the count to its pre-#25659 value of 3, so the\n`sweepLocalCache` delegation is the load-bearing part.\n\n## What\n\nInsertion-order LRU and timestamp LRU are not two algorithms. Both rank\ncandidates worst-first and delete the first K; they differ only in where\nthe rank comes from — the `Map`''s own iteration order, or an accessor on\nthe value. So one function serves both:\n\n```ts\nevictLeastRecentlyUsed({ map, maxEntries, minEvict?, recencyOf?, matches? }): number\n```\n\n- `sweepLocalCache` keeps its three stages (TTL expiry → per-prefix caps\n→ global cap) and its `lastReadAtOf`, now passed as `recencyOf`. Its\nprivate `evictLeastRecentlyRead` is deleted.\n- `campaign-variable.service.ts` uses `readLruEntry` / `writeLruEntry`;\nits `evictLeastRecentlyUsedSchemas` is deleted.\n\nTwo call-site simplifications in the sweep are provable no-ops: the\nper-prefix pass drops `minEvict: 0` (now the default), and the global\npass drops `matches: () => true` (with no filter, `candidates.length ===\nmap.size`, so the early return is identical). The global pass\ndeliberately **keeps** `recencyOf` — dropping it would silently switch\nglobal eviction to insertion order, which is the one way this refactor\ncould go wrong quietly.\n\n## Behaviour change\n\nExactly one, and it is a fix. In `CampaignVariableService`, a\n**stale-hash miss** called `set` on a key already present, and `Map.set`\npreserves the original insertion position — so a workspace whose\nmetadata changes on every request kept its old LRU slot and was evicted\nfirst despite being the hottest. `writeLruEntry`''s delete-then-set\ncorrects it.\n\nEverything else is behaviour-preserving.\n\n## Tests\n\n`sweep-local-cache.util.spec.ts` is **unchanged** and still green — that\nis the regression proof for the delegation. The 5 pre-existing\n`lru-map.util.spec.ts` cases are also unchanged.\n\n9 new cases cover the primitive: both ranking modes, `matches` scoping,\n`minEvict` as a batch floor, the return count, and that omitting\n`recencyOf` matches supplying one that follows insertion order. One is\nnamed for `CoreEntityCacheService`''s exact shape (timestamp recency +\nbatch floor) to pin that the primitive already expresses site 4, so\nmigrating it later is a call swap rather than a redesign.\n\nNo service spec for `CampaignVariableService`, deliberately: #24094\nremoved 203 `*.service.spec.ts` in favour of util specs, and the review\nnit on #25659 was specifically against unit-testing a DI service through\nmocks and private-field access. The corrected behaviour is covered by\nthe `writeLruEntry` specs.\n\n## Not in scope\n\n- **`CoreEntityCacheService`** (site 4). No test coverage, and it sits\non the JWT auth path with five `get` calls per request. It also ranks by\n`lastHashCheckedAt`, which `flush()` sets to `0` — and that is\n**correct, not a bug**: `flush()` `mdel`s the Redis hash and every hash\nis minted as `crypto.randomUUID()`, so a tombstoned entry can never\nre-match and its data is unreachable. Evicting it first is right.\nMigrating it to `lastReadAt` would lose that unless paired with making\n`flush()` delete the entry outright. That deserves its own PR with tests\nand a watched deploy.\n- **`cleanupStaleVersions`**, byte-for-byte identical between\n`WorkspaceCacheService` and `CoreEntityCacheService`. Same follow-up.\n- **`get-data-from-cache-with-recompute.service.ts`** — an unrelated\ngenuinely unbounded cache keyed `${workspaceId}-${cachedVersion}` that\nnever drops old versions. Possibly dead code; worth its own look.","tree":{"sha":"a89f09da29b729f8249878de336f722924d28653","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/a89f09da29b729f8249878de336f722924d28653"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/079b6e0ce37920fd97ba8c4b6e2d81c9ad78d158","verification":{"payload":"tree a89f09da29b729f8249878de336f722924d28653\nparent b2bfbbe46ba3a8856fad8028f866504a77a99cde\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1789116228 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789116228 +0000\n\nrefactor(server): extract a single LRU eviction primitive (#25733)\n\n## Why\n\nFollow-up to #25659, addressing @Weiko''s review comment:\n\n> We already have LRU eviction in\n`CoreEntityCacheService.evictLRUEntriesIfNeeded` and `sweepLocalCache`.\nNeither is directly reusable for a plain Map, but we could extract a\nshared primitive instead of adding a third eviction implementation?\n\nThe comment is right, and the count was worse than it looked. There were\n**four** copies of the same algorithm:\n\n| # | Site | Ranked by |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `campaign-variable.service.ts` `evictLeastRecentlyUsedSchemas` |\ninsertion order |\n| 2 | `lru-map.util.ts` `writeLruEntry` (added in #25659) | insertion\norder |\n| 3 | `sweep-local-cache.util.ts` `evictLeastRecentlyRead` |\n`lastReadAt` |\n| 4 | `core-entity-cache.service.ts` `evictLRUEntriesIfNeeded` |\n`lastHashCheckedAt` |\n\n1 and 2 are the same code written twice — #25659 added its own without\nnoticing `campaign-variable` already had it. 3 and 4 likewise.\n\nThis PR takes **4 → 2**. Adopting the util in `campaign-variable` alone\nwould only return the count to its pre-#25659 value of 3, so the\n`sweepLocalCache` delegation is the load-bearing part.\n\n## What\n\nInsertion-order LRU and timestamp LRU are not two algorithms. Both rank\ncandidates worst-first and delete the first K; they differ only in where\nthe rank comes from — the `Map`''s own iteration order, or an accessor on\nthe value. So one function serves both:\n\n```ts\nevictLeastRecentlyUsed({ map, maxEntries, minEvict?, recencyOf?, matches? }): number\n```\n\n- `sweepLocalCache` keeps its three stages (TTL expiry → per-prefix caps\n→ global cap) and its `lastReadAtOf`, now passed as `recencyOf`. Its\nprivate `evictLeastRecentlyRead` is deleted.\n- `campaign-variable.service.ts` uses `readLruEntry` / `writeLruEntry`;\nits `evictLeastRecentlyUsedSchemas` is deleted.\n\nTwo call-site simplifications in the sweep are provable no-ops: the\nper-prefix pass drops `minEvict: 0` (now the default), and the global\npass drops `matches: () => true` (with no filter, `candidates.length ===\nmap.size`, so the early return is identical). The global pass\ndeliberately **keeps** `recencyOf` — dropping it would silently switch\nglobal eviction to insertion order, which is the one way this refactor\ncould go wrong quietly.\n\n## Behaviour change\n\nExactly one, and it is a fix. In `CampaignVariableService`, a\n**stale-hash miss** called `set` on a key already present, and `Map.set`\npreserves the original insertion position — so a workspace whose\nmetadata changes on every request kept its old LRU slot and was evicted\nfirst despite being the hottest. `writeLruEntry`''s delete-then-set\ncorrects it.\n\nEverything else is behaviour-preserving.\n\n## Tests\n\n`sweep-local-cache.util.spec.ts` is **unchanged** and still green — that\nis the regression proof for the delegation. The 5 pre-existing\n`lru-map.util.spec.ts` cases are also unchanged.\n\n9 new cases cover the primitive: both ranking modes, `matches` scoping,\n`minEvict` as a batch floor, the return count, and that omitting\n`recencyOf` matches supplying one that follows insertion order. One is\nnamed for `CoreEntityCacheService`''s exact shape (timestamp recency +\nbatch floor) to pin that the primitive already expresses site 4, so\nmigrating it later is a call swap rather than a redesign.\n\nNo service spec for `CampaignVariableService`, deliberately: #24094\nremoved 203 `*.service.spec.ts` in favour of util specs, and the review\nnit on #25659 was specifically against unit-testing a DI service through\nmocks and private-field access. The corrected behaviour is covered by\nthe `writeLruEntry` specs.\n\n## Not in scope\n\n- **`CoreEntityCacheService`** (site 4). No test coverage, and it sits\non the JWT auth path with five `get` calls per request. It also ranks by\n`lastHashCheckedAt`, which `flush()` sets to `0` — and that is\n**correct, not a bug**: `flush()` `mdel`s the Redis hash and every hash\nis minted as `crypto.randomUUID()`, so a tombstoned entry can never\nre-match and its data is unreachable. Evicting it first is right.\nMigrating it to `lastReadAt` would lose that unless paired with making\n`flush()` delete the entry outright. That deserves its own PR with tests\nand a watched deploy.\n- **`cleanupStaleVersions`**, byte-for-byte identical between\n`WorkspaceCacheService` and `CoreEntityCacheService`. Same follow-up.\n- **`get-data-from-cache-with-recompute.service.ts`** — an unrelated\ngenuinely unbounded cache keyed `${workspaceId}-${cachedVersion}` that\nnever drops old versions. Possibly dead code; worth its own look.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo79UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqoMQAJfAYhJ9gNiPAsjwspyp2Vuc\nHXd+uV0oZ822xJPBKol3ouOxmNY572YW0aiJ0N+jQ8RALFsfkQ6SwRz0Zig1RNkp\nxO1rp6PxZGCL8N5jkqKhBIbryx5ldpPV5bnrlWI8Q9C2goKjvgfkfOLZ8wdrW468\nR4JRV5UWuBmW3uASbnYHNcGK1m5wXSizX4BjigSk6S/cUldbOUPpYVdIUsoSqYZi\nuMWBGtAjVLnLuC1TZwaIbn+JIC4eqXeReGmZbqzS8sit5kzn3gP3SE5aJdVkcG1I\nTHuy/oNsUf6ZrJLF2FapEkb+GtXjER3oM+OqcCSJYG2ZuXYmSiIu+gWbxQlGNjRp\nS1mnh2D7OagojPv6oBhVVVNOKmeDj1/rGYcd8RlOzZUGBU/g+JGWZ93/q+LvCPXW\nzUDNxPVqMo3dwhrdXdSrx7fXieTE/nRwN65Oou9l6d+3wYmL3A70Bm7Rtx2I6IXB\nTIINlF2exUbx8o7O7dgrBd/ODmL0RLtFnp0jFVia1h3LmRagSrRt+UEK296bajwU\ntnSBmpnBsEHTXNX8ijikYS+PfNJB/yts6ZK+1Fikr6VknDxaPGHXeinPxxER1XOw\nBuOCdNuX1wPqkVn5LGy8Jq4j+me3PWnaq8DdEyj0wl91tPQngMfhfihMgGqT/OcV\nuLLaTacjCH6RcPAjOUvn\n=sqSu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/079b6e0ce37920fd97ba8c4b6e2d81c9ad78d158","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDA3OWI2ZTBjZTM3OTIwZmQ5N2JhOGM0YjZlMmQ4MWM5YWQ3OGQxNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/b2bfbbe46ba3a8856fad8028f866504a77a99cde","sha":"b2bfbbe46ba3a8856fad8028f866504a77a99cde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b2bfbbe46ba3a8856fad8028f866504a77a99cde"}],"sha":"079b6e0ce37920fd97ba8c4b6e2d81c9ad78d158","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/079b6e0ce37920fd97ba8c4b6e2d81c9ad78d158"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b2bfbbe46ba3a8856fad8028f866504a77a99cde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:39:49Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:39:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Backfill twenty-ui front component renderer stories (#25719)\n\nThe Twenty UI Gallery was missing front component renderer coverage for\nmigrated components. Add 30 React/Preact stories alongside its existing\n24 stories, covering Field and text controls, display helpers, ListItem,\nTabs, Popover, Menu, Select, Toast, AlertDialog, Switch, Checkbox,\nSlider, Radio, RadioGroup, and CardPicker.\n\nKeep the gallery and its extracted utilities. All stories use\n`createGalleryStory` with an explicit bundle, runtime, and play\nfunction. Focused fixtures import public twenty-ui entry points and use\n`TwentyUiGalleryCard` for the theme, mount marker, and stylesheet. The\nstory builder resolves `twenty-ui/style.css` to the CSS produced\nalongside the individual JavaScript build.\n\nThe latest coverage checks Checkbox states and activation, separates\nSlider''s hidden single-value control from its range registration\nfailure, and exercises Radio and CardPicker choices through controlled\nand uncontrolled RadioGroups. The input catalog''s expected failures\nmatch the merged Radio migration. Shared assertions check working\nbehavior and require specific known sandbox limitations where\ninteractions are blocked, including missing DOM and PointerEvent APIs,\nincomplete forwarded events, layout measurements, and React boolean ARIA\nserialization. These stories are not skipped; fixes must replace the\ncorresponding failure expectations with successful behavior checks.\n\nValidation:\n- All 54 gallery stories pass in Chromium with retries disabled.\n- Fresh UI/shared builds and React/Preact fixture builds pass (264\nbundles per runtime).\n- Renderer direct TypeScript check, changed-file lint, formatting, and\ndiff checks pass.","tree":{"sha":"b8b277a44d569121729ce2623aec57c2960cbda0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/b8b277a44d569121729ce2623aec57c2960cbda0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/b2bfbbe46ba3a8856fad8028f866504a77a99cde","verification":{"payload":"tree b8b277a44d569121729ce2623aec57c2960cbda0\nparent 262b54e06bec5912b6c5fd9088a1fbe56d95a5f0\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1789115989 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789115989 +0000\n\nBackfill twenty-ui front component renderer stories (#25719)\n\nThe Twenty UI Gallery was missing front component renderer coverage for\nmigrated components. Add 30 React/Preact stories alongside its existing\n24 stories, covering Field and text controls, display helpers, ListItem,\nTabs, Popover, Menu, Select, Toast, AlertDialog, Switch, Checkbox,\nSlider, Radio, RadioGroup, and CardPicker.\n\nKeep the gallery and its extracted utilities. All stories use\n`createGalleryStory` with an explicit bundle, runtime, and play\nfunction. Focused fixtures import public twenty-ui entry points and use\n`TwentyUiGalleryCard` for the theme, mount marker, and stylesheet. The\nstory builder resolves `twenty-ui/style.css` to the CSS produced\nalongside the individual JavaScript build.\n\nThe latest coverage checks Checkbox states and activation, separates\nSlider''s hidden single-value control from its range registration\nfailure, and exercises Radio and CardPicker choices through controlled\nand uncontrolled RadioGroups. The input catalog''s expected failures\nmatch the merged Radio migration. Shared assertions check working\nbehavior and require specific known sandbox limitations where\ninteractions are blocked, including missing DOM and PointerEvent APIs,\nincomplete forwarded events, layout measurements, and React boolean ARIA\nserialization. These stories are not skipped; fixes must replace the\ncorresponding failure expectations with successful behavior checks.\n\nValidation:\n- All 54 gallery stories pass in Chromium with retries disabled.\n- Fresh UI/shared builds and React/Preact fixture builds pass (264\nbundles per runtime).\n- Renderer direct TypeScript check, changed-file lint, formatting, and\ndiff checks pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo75lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwd4QAAIin7aTuvmzDZE62HMa2gBT\nd8YBosUTlMXL6m40UiymHRfjOpO7cbPOqDgZ6cwp44esZDzISHt2LgGOI3j9iWn7\n/8E0h4FXP/XnAw7h7fijyW1ZQHRVnkz1kvSm4dRvNZ2Np0ie5Xiu6VO+kRjG9to7\niIg+H1QSskNaMCE8ZWYoBO6Wf2sFAtQLeu0Nkru17NN5b2w/cUdUxlyI1+Yx3ky+\n4q5tZMleuIEvGdeAmsUD43IIgd3UZvfAXq7YyIqXSQufMT/AHfnP09yevhfvm3zq\ncYwvc82ZtiSaall7NlG/d9DRTLPjCtoyKxhMelTlSIGmfrL40TlCmzpFLa3McO+N\nJGAL7X6thl6hVGR+VlQDxkzxqXf1hxuY/vrVrUOBFS41aZA1tSVeOhzLzTlLeJEY\nUV5I2w2ORq3T9zdgb6Mj6uBaqMfkuDXyEZX94pqujXaQ4tHTGdbpDwbhWP0B8IWq\ny9ZagoYzXeFfJ02Iwe894WxuEDcuovqM5XsjYSsr1G/ZWkjNiiMhXwqcxeo1hFtx\nwi5+L+RCem/aLxZwT/KEsNJODqdh+0GIKjkR8wdN0R//dnDD0VDamTb95REL3yAO\nh3meXy+G55qppLj8xjrc4WBCFq3X9u/jHeYldnfBWI8HnbEEThe1H/UmR9RoSmYe\n+83rltUmuD3feEWkOaaY\n=z30c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/b2bfbbe46ba3a8856fad8028f866504a77a99cde","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGIyYmZiYmU0NmJhM2E4ODU2ZmFkODAyOGY4NjY1MDRhNzdhOTljZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/262b54e06bec5912b6c5fd9088a1fbe56d95a5f0","sha":"262b54e06bec5912b6c5fd9088a1fbe56d95a5f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/262b54e06bec5912b6c5fd9088a1fbe56d95a5f0"}],"sha":"b2bfbbe46ba3a8856fad8028f866504a77a99cde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b2bfbbe46ba3a8856fad8028f866504a77a99cde"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62795688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/neo773","id":62795688,"login":"neo773","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzk1Njg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/262b54e06bec5912b6c5fd9088a1fbe56d95a5f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:35:06Z","email":"62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com","name":"neo773"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:35:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Propagate SMTP send failures so the email job actually retries (#25776)\n\nFixes #24194\n\n`SmtpDriver.send()` never returned or awaited its `sendMail()` chain,\nand its `.catch()` swallowed the rejection, so the job always resolved\nsuccessfully and BullMQ never used the 4 attempts it was already\nenqueued with. Now awaits and rethrows, with an exponential backoff so\nretries don''t hammer a relay that just throttled us.\n\nAlso enables nodemailer''s pooled transport so a burst of emails reuses\none connection instead of opening one per message, which is what tripped\nthe relay''s per-source-IP connection throttle in the first place. No new\nconfig variables; nodemailer''s own defaults apply.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25776?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"d60f291df25e3d81b5013204a4ffd2be19577927","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/d60f291df25e3d81b5013204a4ffd2be19577927"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/262b54e06bec5912b6c5fd9088a1fbe56d95a5f0","verification":{"payload":"tree d60f291df25e3d81b5013204a4ffd2be19577927\nparent 08738e93c1c8d2d6617265ad210b662e630863a7\nauthor neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com> 1789115706 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789115706 +0000\n\nPropagate SMTP send failures so the email job actually retries (#25776)\n\nFixes #24194\n\n`SmtpDriver.send()` never returned or awaited its `sendMail()` chain,\nand its `.catch()` swallowed the rejection, so the job always resolved\nsuccessfully and BullMQ never used the 4 attempts it was already\nenqueued with. Now awaits and rethrows, with an exponential backoff so\nretries don''t hammer a relay that just throttled us.\n\nAlso enables nodemailer''s pooled transport so a burst of emails reuses\none connection instead of opening one per message, which is what tripped\nthe relay''s per-source-IP connection throttle in the first place. No new\nconfig variables; nodemailer''s own defaults apply.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25776?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo71JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuuUQAGO3SaNmrmGQjVOzkyfVR3Hk\n1Qmd6j+jY7PLiaKhGbff8fOwD7Diverq221gpSHIwNvxEzm0qyJwGq3f0bL5VBKY\nizICSCK8RhbJ0qDjSOl145uaOxoNkRPe/95yL0j6aeVUEH3Ej9y993/AzZBA9tsX\nzZKhNBuTf0G/RS+SJ+d0InOLS1YRsoafOGADSDmHac4cF6FM0rAyRYRzX11x3lCl\nHdoF5XBkhyCGDYBuuyEOn67uSX+zV3Z7FLZgFMxgsYtqEUnrpMUYCoEwbcUEHsEB\naUsziLHaK2qNmb1OxP0iGQT1QFI5Xh4QltlNZ+6SsAXpyN88d2Fhokg8spowzODS\nLXBXcNuTSHl9WO9x8HRxzpqTwZ+lf7hcS3Is9UauZMuXZ9q3+jKcEJeRStBdhIXC\nLEuGFEYtzFGbLCDBq+t+tUDEM0Coly5s+p2COoo1ha3QgkeDindyZNEBz2OoEU0Q\n2s2iyY5hQTcBygQrOXVD8TLV3LE0WOOvktHnSJi5HJlbmnMhLnLYgIN0QOtUteZY\nYKATGgLYQ4ATke+47XcIpg6TUFz/zEQSVnjx9PN9chw3I0l0yCMiswlqyrVxFGbq\nNLEQuFZzWNjs3ZVZVExs0g7QaYlUEfF2R/Lrc2fzzsnoYzh1pSCQlZtF2pBrbtnj\n5JN89BIGRcy7U0nbP07a\n=XM/U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/262b54e06bec5912b6c5fd9088a1fbe56d95a5f0","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDI2MmI1NGUwNmJlYzU5MTJiNmM1ZmQ5MDg4YTFmYmU1NmQ5NWE1ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/08738e93c1c8d2d6617265ad210b662e630863a7","sha":"08738e93c1c8d2d6617265ad210b662e630863a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/08738e93c1c8d2d6617265ad210b662e630863a7"}],"sha":"262b54e06bec5912b6c5fd9088a1fbe56d95a5f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/262b54e06bec5912b6c5fd9088a1fbe56d95a5f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/08738e93c1c8d2d6617265ad210b662e630863a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:48:39Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:48:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fill the empty Type column in Skills settings with the owning app (#25766)\n\n## The bug\n\nIn **Settings → AI → Skills**, the `Type` column is empty for every row\n— no chip, no label, ever.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`SettingsSkillTableRow` renders that cell with `SettingsItemTypeTag`,\nwhich since #19897 (\"replace ''Managed'' label with actual app name\") keys\nentirely off `applicationId`:\n\n```tsx\nif (isDefined(applicationId)) return <AppChip applicationId={applicationId} />;\nelse if (isRemote === true) return <Chip label={t`Remote`} … />;\nelse return null;\n```\n\nThe `SkillFields` fragment never selected `applicationId`, so Apollo\nhands the row `applicationId: undefined` for every skill — and `Skill`\nhas no `isRemote` — so the tag falls through to `null`. The server side\nwas already correct: `SkillDTO` exposes `applicationId`, and standard\nskills are stamped with the Twenty standard application id.\n\nThe leftover from the old world is in `SettingsSkillTableMetadata`:\n`fieldLabel: Type` paired with `fieldName: ''isCustom''`, which dates from\n#16865, when the tag still rendered Custom/Standard from `isCustom`.\nThat pairing is also a live crash — `useSortedArray` has only string and\nnumber branches, so clicking the `Type` header calls `.localeCompare` on\na boolean and throws.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`skillFragment`**: select `applicationId` (regenerated\n`generated-metadata`).\n- **`SettingsSkillTableMetadata`**: `Type` → `App`, matching what the\ndata model table already calls this column, and sort it on the resolved\napplication label instead of the boolean.\n- **`SettingsAgentSkillsTab`**: resolve `applicationId` against\n`currentWorkspace.installedApplications` into an `applicationLabel` on\nthe table item, and search on it too, so typing an app''s name finds its\nskills.\n- **`getApplicationDisplayName`**: extracted from\n`useApplicationChipData`. The chip renders *translated*\n`Standard`/`Custom` labels, so resolving the table''s label from the raw\napplication name meant that in a non-English locale, searching for the\nlabel visible in the App column matched nothing and the sort order could\ndisagree with the rows on screen. Both paths now resolve through this\none function.\n- **Name column**: sorted on `name`, while the cell displays `label`.\nThat is why `docx` (\"Word Documents\") and `xlsx` (\"Excel &\nSpreadsheets\") sat out of alphabetical order in the list. It now sorts\non the label it displays.\n\nStandard skills therefore show the `Standard` chip, workspace-created\nones `Custom`, and skills shipped by an installed app that app''s name\nand logo — the same three cases as the data model table.\n\n## Verification\n\n`SettingsAgentSkillsTab.test.tsx` renders the tab against a mocked\n`FindManySkills` and a workspace with three installed applications\n(standard, workspace-custom, third-party), asserting on user-visible\ntext: the app label per row, the row order, and search-by-app in both\nEnglish and `fr-FR`.\n\nEach case was checked against the code it is meant to catch — reverting\na fix fails exactly the test that covers it, and only that one:\n\n| Reverted | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `applicationId` out of the query document | ✕ shows the application\neach skill belongs to, ✕ filters skills by application name |\n| Name column back to `fieldName: ''name''` | ✕ orders skills by the label\nit displays |\n| `applicationLabel` back to the raw application name | ✕ filters skills\nby the application label shown in the current locale |\n| nothing | 4 passed |\n\nBecause the test drives the real `FindManySkillsDocument` through\n`MockedProvider`, its cache strips any field the document does not\nselect — so the first row of that table is a genuine guard against this\nexact regression, not just against the rendering. The `fr-FR` case works\nthe same way: that locale translates `Custom` to `Personnalisé`, which\nis the string the chip shows and therefore the one search has to match.\n\n`tsgo --noEmit` on twenty-front reports the same 78 pre-existing errors\nas before the change, all in `src/modules/front-components/**` cascading\nfrom the unbuilt `twenty-front-component-renderer`; none in the touched\nfiles. oxlint and oxfmt are clean.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25766?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture>``&lt;img alt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;``</picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"e4e9cf252787b15a25320ce66dae77b6c5931128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/e4e9cf252787b15a25320ce66dae77b6c5931128"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/08738e93c1c8d2d6617265ad210b662e630863a7","verification":{"payload":"tree e4e9cf252787b15a25320ce66dae77b6c5931128\nparent 37a26f0326e07346101e30b0ba9175986d05e89d\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789112919 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789112919 +0200\n\nFill the empty Type column in Skills settings with the owning app (#25766)\n\n## The bug\n\nIn **Settings → AI → Skills**, the `Type` column is empty for every row\n— no chip, no label, ever.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`SettingsSkillTableRow` renders that cell with `SettingsItemTypeTag`,\nwhich since #19897 (\"replace ''Managed'' label with actual app name\") keys\nentirely off `applicationId`:\n\n```tsx\nif (isDefined(applicationId)) return <AppChip applicationId={applicationId} />;\nelse if (isRemote === true) return <Chip label={t`Remote`} … />;\nelse return null;\n```\n\nThe `SkillFields` fragment never selected `applicationId`, so Apollo\nhands the row `applicationId: undefined` for every skill — and `Skill`\nhas no `isRemote` — so the tag falls through to `null`. The server side\nwas already correct: `SkillDTO` exposes `applicationId`, and standard\nskills are stamped with the Twenty standard application id.\n\nThe leftover from the old world is in `SettingsSkillTableMetadata`:\n`fieldLabel: Type` paired with `fieldName: ''isCustom''`, which dates from\n#16865, when the tag still rendered Custom/Standard from `isCustom`.\nThat pairing is also a live crash — `useSortedArray` has only string and\nnumber branches, so clicking the `Type` header calls `.localeCompare` on\na boolean and throws.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`skillFragment`**: select `applicationId` (regenerated\n`generated-metadata`).\n- **`SettingsSkillTableMetadata`**: `Type` → `App`, matching what the\ndata model table already calls this column, and sort it on the resolved\napplication label instead of the boolean.\n- **`SettingsAgentSkillsTab`**: resolve `applicationId` against\n`currentWorkspace.installedApplications` into an `applicationLabel` on\nthe table item, and search on it too, so typing an app''s name finds its\nskills.\n- **`getApplicationDisplayName`**: extracted from\n`useApplicationChipData`. The chip renders *translated*\n`Standard`/`Custom` labels, so resolving the table''s label from the raw\napplication name meant that in a non-English locale, searching for the\nlabel visible in the App column matched nothing and the sort order could\ndisagree with the rows on screen. Both paths now resolve through this\none function.\n- **Name column**: sorted on `name`, while the cell displays `label`.\nThat is why `docx` (\"Word Documents\") and `xlsx` (\"Excel &\nSpreadsheets\") sat out of alphabetical order in the list. It now sorts\non the label it displays.\n\nStandard skills therefore show the `Standard` chip, workspace-created\nones `Custom`, and skills shipped by an installed app that app''s name\nand logo — the same three cases as the data model table.\n\n## Verification\n\n`SettingsAgentSkillsTab.test.tsx` renders the tab against a mocked\n`FindManySkills` and a workspace with three installed applications\n(standard, workspace-custom, third-party), asserting on user-visible\ntext: the app label per row, the row order, and search-by-app in both\nEnglish and `fr-FR`.\n\nEach case was checked against the code it is meant to catch — reverting\na fix fails exactly the test that covers it, and only that one:\n\n| Reverted | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `applicationId` out of the query document | ✕ shows the application\neach skill belongs to, ✕ filters skills by application name |\n| Name column back to `fieldName: ''name''` | ✕ orders skills by the label\nit displays |\n| `applicationLabel` back to the raw application name | ✕ filters skills\nby the application label shown in the current locale |\n| nothing | 4 passed |\n\nBecause the test drives the real `FindManySkillsDocument` through\n`MockedProvider`, its cache strips any field the document does not\nselect — so the first row of that table is a genuine guard against this\nexact regression, not just against the rendering. The `fr-FR` case works\nthe same way: that locale translates `Custom` to `Personnalisé`, which\nis the string the chip shows and therefore the one search has to match.\n\n`tsgo --noEmit` on twenty-front reports the same 78 pre-existing errors\nas before the change, all in `src/modules/front-components/**` cascading\nfrom the unbuilt `twenty-front-component-renderer`; none in the touched\nfiles. oxlint and oxfmt are clean.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25766?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture>``&lt;img alt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;``</picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo7JXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPwkQAI+6dBE7xv7PxxNq/CPMBbap\npSk5Llm2PyIasGx5kBnMKRpLQCOnsUvHYX3ghM7eOpjpgCM+oaYBmSXHBZx1NV3W\nXKInuXAttuh+6WXACUKe8TUkvbiLa5hwafWWFUNY+I/MQixb03xzbFYkH19HshW/\nTomxsmTgTdvPn1X7P2+rKmF2brNhv2cAIHs0BSxchs6YW3UJ9wiLfYM3/qnReIpJ\nOeMtP+xbAwCZeXo4IDeHEo7oxugdSmf+Tlhp/vqpANZ+pf3DkzqOQ58hrMUVw05g\nxNQDYS/u4eFHOl+NmHTUQjffgVI/KIv7slq0k2xthaM5LR0MH2COiSuW8PHmBmRV\n5WRFML7iJtTcyo/VmjJBSQ/czURwDbmXCC+OX/uD6bLcKT1OQJcq+hY2nCWTyCGF\neT6pv6cE7Lvsc77X/McCvl/0yW7TLYdZtuXNopsAbODlsep5RLe6OwhqrBsroMMb\nVghbTMTNVcjYmuemZv3MHUhxtiCpf7WTDSR1JtuDJvxjl8hfF19K1mIaqNfDiHd2\ndp0hi6qwr35UhEK6r0NZcQi1qLUtqMArfEPut2BkdtZrdpVcNvon14Jh8e/nTiXj\n/dvmp+GdeN7QqGQ3BayfOi0iY/GpErxotr4ns0FBO3yv/hpN9RCwXr2ZAAqDYK4X\nK+XPOV1faI+1MVKZChZl\n=9WNb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/08738e93c1c8d2d6617265ad210b662e630863a7","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDA4NzM4ZTkzYzFjOGQyZDY2MTcyNjVhZDIxMGI2NjJlNjMwODYzYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/37a26f0326e07346101e30b0ba9175986d05e89d","sha":"37a26f0326e07346101e30b0ba9175986d05e89d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/37a26f0326e07346101e30b0ba9175986d05e89d"}],"sha":"08738e93c1c8d2d6617265ad210b662e630863a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/08738e93c1c8d2d6617265ad210b662e630863a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/37a26f0326e07346101e30b0ba9175986d05e89d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:34:56Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:34:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Read the deprecated flag from the model config when picking a tier default (#25769)\n\n## What\n\n`twenty-server` does not typecheck on main:\n\n```\nsrc/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/ai-model-registry.service.ts(452,43):\nerror TS2339: Property ''isDeprecated'' does not exist on type ''RegisteredAiModel''.\n```\n\nThis blocks `server-lint-typecheck` for every pull request that touches\nthe server. It went unnoticed because that job is changed-files gated,\nso pushes to main that touch no server file skip it and the run reports\ngreen.\n\n## How\n\n`findDefaultModelForTier` falls back to the first allowed model that is\nnot deprecated, and read the flag straight off the registered model.\n`RegisteredAiModel` does not carry it: the registry entries are built\nwith `modelId`, `sdkPackage`, `model`, `supportsReasoning`,\n`providerName` and `modelsDevName`, while `isDeprecated` belongs to\n`AiModelConfig`, which is where the catalog writes it.\n\nThe flag is now read from the config, which is what the transcription\npath a hundred lines above already does:\n\n```ts\nthis.getTranscriptionModelConfig(model.modelId)?.isDeprecated !== true\n```\n\nAdding `isDeprecated` to `RegisteredAiModel` would have silenced the\ncompiler and left the behaviour broken: nothing populates that property\non a registered model, so the predicate would read `undefined !== true`\nfor every candidate and the fallback would always return the first\nallowed model, deprecated or not. Reading the config makes the filter do\nwhat it says.\n\n`getModelConfig` refreshes the catalog and registers a variant before\nreading its cache, so it resolves both the composite identifiers and the\nconfigured variant identifiers that appear in this list.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npx tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` no longer reports anything for\nthis file.\n- The ai-models suites pass, 11 files and 76 tests.\n- Lint and prettier on the changed file.\n\nNo test is added: the service has no spec today, and the repository\nprefers integration tests over unit tests with a mocked dependency graph\nfor services. The behaviour this restores was never exercised, since the\npredicate silently matched every model.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25769?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"d148c4cda7619eb07bac15d7361b60b83c5c30da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/d148c4cda7619eb07bac15d7361b60b83c5c30da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/37a26f0326e07346101e30b0ba9175986d05e89d","verification":{"payload":"tree d148c4cda7619eb07bac15d7361b60b83c5c30da\nparent 38b55f8890b02060b3fde15faf9c6aacf1eb790b\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789112096 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789112096 +0000\n\nRead the deprecated flag from the model config when picking a tier default (#25769)\n\n## What\n\n`twenty-server` does not typecheck on main:\n\n```\nsrc/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/ai-model-registry.service.ts(452,43):\nerror TS2339: Property ''isDeprecated'' does not exist on type ''RegisteredAiModel''.\n```\n\nThis blocks `server-lint-typecheck` for every pull request that touches\nthe server. It went unnoticed because that job is changed-files gated,\nso pushes to main that touch no server file skip it and the run reports\ngreen.\n\n## How\n\n`findDefaultModelForTier` falls back to the first allowed model that is\nnot deprecated, and read the flag straight off the registered model.\n`RegisteredAiModel` does not carry it: the registry entries are built\nwith `modelId`, `sdkPackage`, `model`, `supportsReasoning`,\n`providerName` and `modelsDevName`, while `isDeprecated` belongs to\n`AiModelConfig`, which is where the catalog writes it.\n\nThe flag is now read from the config, which is what the transcription\npath a hundred lines above already does:\n\n```ts\nthis.getTranscriptionModelConfig(model.modelId)?.isDeprecated !== true\n```\n\nAdding `isDeprecated` to `RegisteredAiModel` would have silenced the\ncompiler and left the behaviour broken: nothing populates that property\non a registered model, so the predicate would read `undefined !== true`\nfor every candidate and the fallback would always return the first\nallowed model, deprecated or not. Reading the config makes the filter do\nwhat it says.\n\n`getModelConfig` refreshes the catalog and registers a variant before\nreading its cache, so it resolves both the composite identifiers and the\nconfigured variant identifiers that appear in this list.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npx tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` no longer reports anything for\nthis file.\n- The ai-models suites pass, 11 files and 76 tests.\n- Lint and prettier on the changed file.\n\nNo test is added: the service has no spec today, and the repository\nprefers integration tests over unit tests with a mocked dependency graph\nfor services. The behaviour this restores was never exercised, since the\npredicate silently matched every model.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25769?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo68wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOF0QAF9FnC32dghysVZM80Y3vVoS\nQKpBJJFBCtZcQ0dT3mT80WJk+SMJikDP9SRTNCDJKHGYU6mvEB2G1UxKaY7I0+0W\nLQ3qLnnO/sAtLfMXejOc5OpXLYxqjTHZyBxSTx09fTDps8W9Uwi21xpoE8TLHu4V\nQS9OAd3YQECSKm5VSgxopKvczBtOMfRDMdwJgqFijDf5q5pYTfh8qPvDEuLzy2xy\naUbuWOxHhzJG2LbrnFqXHwP/pd4tUjd8o2o6fVRz3tctxljJQXLqb1tTxcUevZ7Q\noWY6xAYDyV3qya3l4CONOFjGopkEK/TibUaovMsatdw5LHWEzIn4dqlG34ZVT/ir\nu/ul+qqH3qxwcSPCRL5yarJH3+klMruBgNpz3Z9xaD3sbs9pWiDjrn2dJkXR2/+Q\nrsXiCNp1mZDMeEveuvwwrmrRs4sqIDMd5k5bMfBueIN9T4ixBro7vSxvzw284zEb\noMcQErn3Vj6hWN2qESGeM/YyR2812EnnppjrQPiyDmvkB3ExF6D8X728EEWPhfB1\nUciHo5NpojwOdG07x6E5KsfKZuZbfnvbWbKArpa+Ijnt+w26/PtnYv42p34AbN81\n3RPfNpYT292c42MC0jkLNWp/K9T58QAzxpe0HGHeRGnV7ARXfhBSkOqjfLQfM8GY\naewKsEGT5/Z6hPmjDNFD\n=rUvL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/37a26f0326e07346101e30b0ba9175986d05e89d","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDM3YTI2ZjAzMjZlMDczNDYxMDFlMzBiMGJhOTE3NTk4NmQwNWU4OWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/38b55f8890b02060b3fde15faf9c6aacf1eb790b","sha":"38b55f8890b02060b3fde15faf9c6aacf1eb790b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/38b55f8890b02060b3fde15faf9c6aacf1eb790b"}],"sha":"37a26f0326e07346101e30b0ba9175986d05e89d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/37a26f0326e07346101e30b0ba9175986d05e89d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/38b55f8890b02060b3fde15faf9c6aacf1eb790b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:16:26Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:16:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Block private-network SSO issuers and replace the safe-mode toggle with an internal host allowlist (#25756)\n\nFixes #25638. Supersedes #25647, which was closed pending a decision on\nself-hosted deployments that run their identity provider on an internal\nnetwork.\n\n## What\n\n**SSO requests now go through the SSRF-safe agent.**\n`Issuer.discover()`, the JWKS fetch during ID token validation, and the\ntoken and userinfo calls were the only outbound requests not going\nthrough `SecureHttpClientService`, so a workspace admin with the\n`SECURITY` permission could point them at internal targets. They are\nwired through openid-client''s `custom.http_options` hook. openid-client\nresolves that hook on whichever object issues the request (the `Issuer`\nclass for discovery, the issuer instance for JWKS, the client instance\nfor token and userinfo), so it is set on all three. #25647 only covered\nthe first, which left the endpoints in an attacker-controlled discovery\ndocument unprotected. `OidcAuthGuard` now calls\n`SsoService.discoverOidcIssuer` rather than `Issuer.discover` itself, so\nsetup and login share one path.\n\n**`OUTBOUND_HTTP_SAFE_MODE_ENABLED` is replaced by\n`OUTBOUND_HTTP_ALLOWED_INTERNAL_HOSTS`.** Self-hosters commonly run\ntheir IdP, mail or calendar server on a private address (a sibling\ndocker-compose container, a LAN host). The only escape hatch was the\nglobal toggle, which also disables protection for webhooks and workflow\nactions, and applying it to SSO would have locked SSO-only workspaces\nout on upgrade since discovery runs on every login. The new variable is\na comma-separated list of hostnames or IP literals that may be reached\non a private network. Matching is exact and case-insensitive on the\nhostname, with no wildcard or suffix patterns; a pasted issuer URL or\n`host:port` is reduced to its hostname. `*` allows all, which is what\nthe old `false` did. Everything else stays protected, and an allowlisted\nhost can never reach the link-local range (`169.254.0.0/16`,\n`fe80::/10`) where cloud metadata services live, so a DNS change cannot\nturn an allowlisted name into a path to instance credentials.\n\n**Deprecation.** The old boolean stays declared, marked deprecated, and\n`false` is honoured as `*` in\n`SecureHttpClientService.getAllowedInternalHosts()` so existing\nself-hosted setups keep working after upgrading. While it is `false` the\nallowlist is ignored; the server logs a warning once per process saying\nso. It can be deleted in a later release; that is the only remaining\nreference.\n\n**Setup-time error.** A blocked issuer used to surface as a bare\n\"Invalid issuer\". The underlying reason (e.g. `Request to internal IP\naddress 172.18.0.5 is not allowed.`) is now included in the setup error\nso the admin can diagnose it there. At login the failure only shows as a\nredirect.\n\n## Config\n\n| Value | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| empty (default) | private-network addresses are blocked for HTTP\nworkflow actions, webhooks, SSO and IMAP/SMTP/CalDAV |\n| `keycloak,mail.internal,192.168.1.10` | those hosts may reach private\nnetworks (never link-local) |\n| `*` | protection off (previous\n`OUTBOUND_HTTP_SAFE_MODE_ENABLED=false`) |\n\n## Tests\n\n- Unit: allowlist cases for the agent and hostname utils (private\naddress allowed, link-local still blocked, wildcard), `isLinkLocalIp`, a\n`SecureHttpClientService` spec covering `*`, the deprecated fallback\nwith its one-time warning and URL/`host:port` entry normalisation, and\nan `SsoService` spec that builds the real `SecureHttpClientService` and\nasserts the agent refuses `169.254.169.254` for discovery, JWKS, token\nand userinfo.\n- Integration: the suites that flipped the toggle off to reach the\ndovecot, greenmail, radicale and webhook-receiver containers now set the\nlist to `[''*'']`. `imap-smtp-outbound` sets it to the actual container\nhost instead, so the per-host exemption is exercised end to end.\n- `npx tsgo --noEmit`, oxlint and oxfmt are clean on the changed files.\n\n## Docs\n\nThe self-hosting note in the calendar and emails guide now points at the\nallowlist instead of telling people to turn safe mode off, and the\nself-host setup guide gains an \"Outbound Connections to Internal Hosts\"\nsection. Translated copies under `l/` are left to the i18n pipeline.\n\n## Release note\n\nSelf-hosted deployments whose identity provider, mail or calendar server\nresolves to a private address should add its hostname or IP to\n`OUTBOUND_HTTP_ALLOWED_INTERNAL_HOSTS`. Deployments that set\n`OUTBOUND_HTTP_SAFE_MODE_ENABLED=false` keep working unchanged for now,\nbut that flag overrides the new list, so remove it when migrating.\n\nSession: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WPVhQuV1QgbTS63ivuTjjH","tree":{"sha":"747d624188e168585cab052f0118e8e3597f18d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/747d624188e168585cab052f0118e8e3597f18d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/38b55f8890b02060b3fde15faf9c6aacf1eb790b","verification":{"payload":"tree 747d624188e168585cab052f0118e8e3597f18d6\nparent 61f66bc162d1b5d853e8d1896b26c9b27f9dc514\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789110986 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789110986 +0200\n\nBlock private-network SSO issuers and replace the safe-mode toggle with an internal host allowlist (#25756)\n\nFixes #25638. Supersedes #25647, which was closed pending a decision on\nself-hosted deployments that run their identity provider on an internal\nnetwork.\n\n## What\n\n**SSO requests now go through the SSRF-safe agent.**\n`Issuer.discover()`, the JWKS fetch during ID token validation, and the\ntoken and userinfo calls were the only outbound requests not going\nthrough `SecureHttpClientService`, so a workspace admin with the\n`SECURITY` permission could point them at internal targets. They are\nwired through openid-client''s `custom.http_options` hook. openid-client\nresolves that hook on whichever object issues the request (the `Issuer`\nclass for discovery, the issuer instance for JWKS, the client instance\nfor token and userinfo), so it is set on all three. #25647 only covered\nthe first, which left the endpoints in an attacker-controlled discovery\ndocument unprotected. `OidcAuthGuard` now calls\n`SsoService.discoverOidcIssuer` rather than `Issuer.discover` itself, so\nsetup and login share one path.\n\n**`OUTBOUND_HTTP_SAFE_MODE_ENABLED` is replaced by\n`OUTBOUND_HTTP_ALLOWED_INTERNAL_HOSTS`.** Self-hosters commonly run\ntheir IdP, mail or calendar server on a private address (a sibling\ndocker-compose container, a LAN host). The only escape hatch was the\nglobal toggle, which also disables protection for webhooks and workflow\nactions, and applying it to SSO would have locked SSO-only workspaces\nout on upgrade since discovery runs on every login. The new variable is\na comma-separated list of hostnames or IP literals that may be reached\non a private network. Matching is exact and case-insensitive on the\nhostname, with no wildcard or suffix patterns; a pasted issuer URL or\n`host:port` is reduced to its hostname. `*` allows all, which is what\nthe old `false` did. Everything else stays protected, and an allowlisted\nhost can never reach the link-local range (`169.254.0.0/16`,\n`fe80::/10`) where cloud metadata services live, so a DNS change cannot\nturn an allowlisted name into a path to instance credentials.\n\n**Deprecation.** The old boolean stays declared, marked deprecated, and\n`false` is honoured as `*` in\n`SecureHttpClientService.getAllowedInternalHosts()` so existing\nself-hosted setups keep working after upgrading. While it is `false` the\nallowlist is ignored; the server logs a warning once per process saying\nso. It can be deleted in a later release; that is the only remaining\nreference.\n\n**Setup-time error.** A blocked issuer used to surface as a bare\n\"Invalid issuer\". The underlying reason (e.g. `Request to internal IP\naddress 172.18.0.5 is not allowed.`) is now included in the setup error\nso the admin can diagnose it there. At login the failure only shows as a\nredirect.\n\n## Config\n\n| Value | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| empty (default) | private-network addresses are blocked for HTTP\nworkflow actions, webhooks, SSO and IMAP/SMTP/CalDAV |\n| `keycloak,mail.internal,192.168.1.10` | those hosts may reach private\nnetworks (never link-local) |\n| `*` | protection off (previous\n`OUTBOUND_HTTP_SAFE_MODE_ENABLED=false`) |\n\n## Tests\n\n- Unit: allowlist cases for the agent and hostname utils (private\naddress allowed, link-local still blocked, wildcard), `isLinkLocalIp`, a\n`SecureHttpClientService` spec covering `*`, the deprecated fallback\nwith its one-time warning and URL/`host:port` entry normalisation, and\nan `SsoService` spec that builds the real `SecureHttpClientService` and\nasserts the agent refuses `169.254.169.254` for discovery, JWKS, token\nand userinfo.\n- Integration: the suites that flipped the toggle off to reach the\ndovecot, greenmail, radicale and webhook-receiver containers now set the\nlist to `[''*'']`. `imap-smtp-outbound` sets it to the actual container\nhost instead, so the per-host exemption is exercised end to end.\n- `npx tsgo --noEmit`, oxlint and oxfmt are clean on the changed files.\n\n## Docs\n\nThe self-hosting note in the calendar and emails guide now points at the\nallowlist instead of telling people to turn safe mode off, and the\nself-host setup guide gains an \"Outbound Connections to Internal Hosts\"\nsection. Translated copies under `l/` are left to the i18n pipeline.\n\n## Release note\n\nSelf-hosted deployments whose identity provider, mail or calendar server\nresolves to a private address should add its hostname or IP to\n`OUTBOUND_HTTP_ALLOWED_INTERNAL_HOSTS`. Deployments that set\n`OUTBOUND_HTTP_SAFE_MODE_ENABLED=false` keep working unchanged for now,\nbut that flag overrides the new list, so remove it when migrating.\n\nSession: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WPVhQuV1QgbTS63ivuTjjH","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo6rKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlGgQAIvMvZDwfnF5FN+/gLe9E/VG\nr/nSj02JItO6QroekYwWqkA2vlJtVOSJlVOj+m2BcMMAHkGaHIhTW4YVU2iBQlnD\nSaKD8ePyQie2Scod46Ki/W7Psnf2tipMcCUyFDMwAfR370281oRSGrZiO0jR6V0F\nl9v9tEaczP4G5Gg3jAdRfWgFI2gC3OquSz8QgwxaKfoyWuA2KAO5psSVZQgwQsRV\nEeH3fsMzvA2MikcE8/NeP9BkDTsH/fXeDQtYA81OyInn1hL8gUnZdlBnnZgNOVHi\nxydaqYjVkwxlC4c9Kn1i4VaLCymrH6AKGeDgmiz3UkT2QeQxYcjk6LDNrih9jPa7\ndC7fJW7FbvX47sxeuKLqyJWVT67PgyW8DxzVp9axvacu1p69DMU9que46HpVVyVH\nkSRaNhaF+Tkm23Mn6U44l7LYs1OsFcCKNCnQJQwaL3wQFA9Rx0txbw57eBvsVQcz\nll2iBUqv4IMbrZiXlYEBhaVw/vO/MJjTCDyUXlFfsVjK3OndhAL+0Tt9OFInynHB\nlYNzWDiwIFRbQoPJsnhR8rQ9JZWhYvARc3GigiEtnzouhJjARkiVkiEmFzseYq+s\n2ewJg0viaAQkRDGTImlFFf18IYj8BY5c59q0UiFqVvid71G05K9kU6kcPyMMs77f\nSsmVGdSaWa5E+7Wv75hV\n=outB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/38b55f8890b02060b3fde15faf9c6aacf1eb790b","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDM4YjU1Zjg4OTBiMDIwNjBiM2ZkZTE1ZmFmOWM2YWFjZjFlYjc5MGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/61f66bc162d1b5d853e8d1896b26c9b27f9dc514","sha":"61f66bc162d1b5d853e8d1896b26c9b27f9dc514","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/61f66bc162d1b5d853e8d1896b26c9b27f9dc514"}],"sha":"38b55f8890b02060b3fde15faf9c6aacf1eb790b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/38b55f8890b02060b3fde15faf9c6aacf1eb790b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/61f66bc162d1b5d853e8d1896b26c9b27f9dc514/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:11:52Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:11:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Keep only compliance badges on the import-contacts onboarding step (#25774)\n\n## What\n\nThe trust badge row on the \"Import your contacts\" onboarding step\ncarried three badges: SOC2, a partner-logo badge labelled \"+10k\", and\nGDPR. This removes the middle partner-logo badge so the row only carries\nthe compliance badges we actually publish on trust.twenty.com (SOC 2\nType 2 and GDPR).\n\n## Changes\n\n\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/onboarding/components/import-contacts/OnboardingTrustBadges.tsx`:\n\n- Removed the middle badge and the logo list that fed it.\n- Removed `StyledLogoCluster` and `StyledClusterLogo`, which only\nexisted to lay that badge out.\n- Removed the `hasClusterLeading` prop. It was the only prop\n`StyledBadge` took, so `StyledBadge` is no longer a generic styled\ncomponent and its conditional left padding collapses to a constant.\n- Collapsed `TrustBadge`''s `leading: ReactNode` prop to a plain\n`sealSrc: string`. The `ReactNode` indirection existed only so the\nremoved badge could pass a logo cluster instead of a seal; both\nremaining badges are a seal plus a label.\n\nAlso deleted the two partner logo assets under\n`packages/twenty-front/public/images/onboarding/trust-badges/`, which\nnothing else referenced. The marketing site''s logo bar\n(`packages/twenty-website`) has its own separate copies and is\nuntouched.\n\nNet: 8 insertions, 53 deletions.\n\n## Before / after\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Before | SOC2 · +10k · GDPR |\n| After | SOC2 · GDPR |\n\n## Testing\n\n- Rendered the real `ImportContacts` page component against a Vite dev\nserver and screenshotted the step — the row goes from 3 badges to 2\n(`SOC2`, `GDPR`), with the remaining badges unchanged in appearance.\n- `tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` on `twenty-front`: clean.\n- `oxlint --type-aware` and `oxfmt --check` on the changed file: clean.","tree":{"sha":"fa20662cc0c9b25188fc555bec4a2ac3ef6438d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/fa20662cc0c9b25188fc555bec4a2ac3ef6438d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/61f66bc162d1b5d853e8d1896b26c9b27f9dc514","verification":{"payload":"tree fa20662cc0c9b25188fc555bec4a2ac3ef6438d4\nparent d2e291d6a48322a29f8259c489ae48b03994c6e3\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789110712 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789110712 +0200\n\nKeep only compliance badges on the import-contacts onboarding step (#25774)\n\n## What\n\nThe trust badge row on the \"Import your contacts\" onboarding step\ncarried three badges: SOC2, a partner-logo badge labelled \"+10k\", and\nGDPR. This removes the middle partner-logo badge so the row only carries\nthe compliance badges we actually publish on trust.twenty.com (SOC 2\nType 2 and GDPR).\n\n## Changes\n\n\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/onboarding/components/import-contacts/OnboardingTrustBadges.tsx`:\n\n- Removed the middle badge and the logo list that fed it.\n- Removed `StyledLogoCluster` and `StyledClusterLogo`, which only\nexisted to lay that badge out.\n- Removed the `hasClusterLeading` prop. It was the only prop\n`StyledBadge` took, so `StyledBadge` is no longer a generic styled\ncomponent and its conditional left padding collapses to a constant.\n- Collapsed `TrustBadge`''s `leading: ReactNode` prop to a plain\n`sealSrc: string`. The `ReactNode` indirection existed only so the\nremoved badge could pass a logo cluster instead of a seal; both\nremaining badges are a seal plus a label.\n\nAlso deleted the two partner logo assets under\n`packages/twenty-front/public/images/onboarding/trust-badges/`, which\nnothing else referenced. The marketing site''s logo bar\n(`packages/twenty-website`) has its own separate copies and is\nuntouched.\n\nNet: 8 insertions, 53 deletions.\n\n## Before / after\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Before | SOC2 · +10k · GDPR |\n| After | SOC2 · GDPR |\n\n## Testing\n\n- Rendered the real `ImportContacts` page component against a Vite dev\nserver and screenshotted the step — the row goes from 3 badges to 2\n(`SOC2`, `GDPR`), with the remaining badges unchanged in appearance.\n- `tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` on `twenty-front`: clean.\n- `oxlint --type-aware` and `oxfmt --check` on the changed file: clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo6m4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACcAQACE1GK00zJJNb+7KWXrsMEyC\nTbUElsYsSTdaKZcmOCF9Rqx+FeFPQx637mOX2eGWwmkWYHMSFU8fXZ3Z8T46WqHM\nTLSii+7vT5NiuFnrv4Bogby/XAEq4eHwUssasQzeyUFRBBVPGFo29Mnqu6FG7B3X\nastaOWg6+DOGQCOGsZBuUEr4OiJGBoTqMmzXnh3fVVqxHcVIwuqi00HDPyMSAHa+\nL1l6ADQ6Ib7kFfW7HKiSwEp4V/whVm1A2y8a1VhEn28s/y3T3DqETy7W7g4uWHvQ\nlZlhrjRPaJY++JDpVWBeQHYOB7LaS63Y1/s5l39F0bqQLL1Rg6OymUQm/+rS6nau\npz55UPnxiv0haRfo6i0GYuuYmp+1OldJeHYTt3n//V5sy5ae1vivWIbBG67xtyEy\nlVDRRj3HKDAkP47DpIq4yOeVy5PsfIFXY4YFzQBeMUHsXQMP/gEC4BcqgAZVZSs7\n1lRtCFxXN1enIgvJus1qmFUfwE2E6sY6xA+5BzChBL5eyy9ugfUIZEqNPVAlAjba\nKfn9PsXhhEd3Ac8d35aRYCo6gOQl8XlhGJ4o4f6tLIw3DouHQquOOF7oske/5zrP\nPc19SATwG0aa4ORape6VaZETfTbnOh8MVCLoewJc43D+V6OyTRreupF5mQpW+hxM\n4CIggvT6nF3A8N17+935\n=3hrS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_