312f46fd58638d0"}],"sha":"1f7050e917f894d86a5822c5743af81b437d86ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/1f7050e917f894d86a5822c5743af81b437d86ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/123f463eea7501ed4b55a24b2312f46fd58638d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T21:44:33Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T21:44:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Tell pull users their project cannot build what pull just wrote (#25747)\n\n## What\n\n`yarn twenty pull` into a project that has a `package.json` but no\ninstalled `twenty-sdk` wrote the whole tree, declared success and then\npointed at a command that cannot work:\n\n```\n✓ Pulled Custom into /path/to/my-app\nBase recorded in .twenty/pull-base.json\nNext: yarn twenty plan --no-delete\n```\n\nRunning that next step fails immediately with `Could not resolve\n\"twenty-sdk/define\"`, because nothing in the project provides the\ndefiners the written files import. Pull''s only precondition is that a\n`package.json` exists, so a project assembled by hand rather than\nscaffolded lands here.\n\n## How\n\nPull now checks whether `twenty-sdk/define` resolves from the project,\nand says so instead of pretending the next step will work:\n\n```\n✓ Pulled Custom into /path/to/my-app\nBase recorded in .twenty/pull-base.json\ntwenty-sdk is not installed here, so the written files cannot build yet.\nNext: install your dependencies, then yarn twenty plan --no-delete\n```\n\nA project with the SDK installed is unchanged and still prints the plain\nnext step.\n\nThe check resolves the `./define` subpath rather than the package root,\nbecause `twenty-sdk` has no root export and resolving the bare name\nfails even when it is installed. It follows normal Node resolution from\nthe project, so a workspace that hoists its dependencies is detected\ncorrectly.\n\nPull still writes the files. They are the point of the command, and they\nare what you want on disk before installing.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New spec on the check: false for a project with only a package.json,\ntrue for one that exposes the define entry point. It builds its own\nfixture, so it does not depend on twenty-sdk being built.\n- Verified live against a dev workspace, both branches: a hand-made\nproject gets the warning and the corrected next step, a scaffolded one\nis unchanged.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25747?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"db97acd45cca821dda49edfdc5a0c44988906a45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/db97acd45cca821dda49edfdc5a0c44988906a45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/123f463eea7501ed4b55a24b2312f46fd58638d0","verification":{"payload":"tree db97acd45cca821dda49edfdc5a0c44988906a45\nparent a79814a9ace386bccc80c4bf4ccb35198af575df\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789076673 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789076673 +0000\n\nTell pull users their project cannot build what pull just wrote (#25747)\n\n## What\n\n`yarn twenty pull` into a project that has a `package.json` but no\ninstalled `twenty-sdk` wrote the whole tree, declared success and then\npointed at a command that cannot work:\n\n```\n✓ Pulled Custom into /path/to/my-app\nBase recorded in .twenty/pull-base.json\nNext: yarn twenty plan --no-delete\n```\n\nRunning that next step fails immediately with `Could not resolve\n\"twenty-sdk/define\"`, because nothing in the project provides the\ndefiners the written files import. Pull''s only precondition is that a\n`package.json` exists, so a project assembled by hand rather than\nscaffolded lands here.\n\n## How\n\nPull now checks whether `twenty-sdk/define` resolves from the project,\nand says so instead of pretending the next step will work:\n\n```\n✓ Pulled Custom into /path/to/my-app\nBase recorded in .twenty/pull-base.json\ntwenty-sdk is not installed here, so the written files cannot build yet.\nNext: install your dependencies, then yarn twenty plan --no-delete\n```\n\nA project with the SDK installed is unchanged and still prints the plain\nnext step.\n\nThe check resolves the `./define` subpath rather than the package root,\nbecause `twenty-sdk` has no root export and resolving the bare name\nfails even when it is installed. It follows normal Node resolution from\nthe project, so a workspace that hoists its dependencies is detected\ncorrectly.\n\nPull still writes the files. They are the point of the command, and they\nare what you want on disk before installing.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New spec on the check: false for a project with only a package.json,\ntrue for one that exposes the define entry point. It builds its own\nfixture, so it does not depend on twenty-sdk being built.\n- Verified live against a dev workspace, both branches: a hand-made\nproject gets the warning and the corrected next step, a scaffolded one\nis unchanged.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25747?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoyTQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyAEQAHGY4PZATueB6jVy24jBnvMB\nLrg06npdoWKaLo7tFzSAai5s1wFDl1vhKnTKm1C2SX1ElYVTWimwxM6PUsr6e3Nq\nrsVp6M131K1PKkL8jU3OsRgqTqbLot6MEqNKYPdcgk2dcjT2qrDGYPDgRWwr1apN\n9WE20bPO1qNHKOU/mVU4wr8Ka8gZzwZqP3AkyZcgax7UbxzcJK6KZFgIXeniyKzq\nBhhsHkFRYKPCvE9Bt+zJ6o/FR+FymzbE189xusPkSCCnXhaMfUmnhMQ4dHDQPaOy\n40knFPBdmtes9rnoMkhcOaPCX1TIrVmbXLPjUBG7JaonPs0wUSiSz6rHgq04kiO7\niIKruNFTf7M7tV1HeTrQFEK43CZYc2fvtx2s3UJ8Z44XMwTB32lIF7Xm3B0hr7se\n8dX9qu/GSyi0OThzcnCRPetziBHiYmzIqU+mtLwC8dsViveil4S6lusTi4NMIS0F\nfrCdl+/NBnveHlFj3dKLAGvB/BJojg4ngI0vLJFA5ACadb2OaMBTBXCKBUM8pDax\nNembbrSJLA3mYVVkx3xt7i9FATilxcvIntfEgKyt+j/S19q9FpPnORd8ciIi2FNU\n81UO6ZpPLrq5fWhc/+ULJ81NhiMGOCYVWf2MeUMI/E6ilCXEmxhLdozTe9EGHi/2\nOGddG6GXZrYtpuvOmu5H\n=iv22\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/123f463eea7501ed4b55a24b2312f46fd58638d0","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDEyM2Y0NjNlZWE3NTAxZWQ0YjU1YTI0YjIzMTJmNDZmZDU4NjM4ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/a79814a9ace386bccc80c4bf4ccb35198af575df","sha":"a79814a9ace386bccc80c4bf4ccb35198af575df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/a79814a9ace386bccc80c4bf4ccb35198af575df"}],"sha":"123f463eea7501ed4b55a24b2312f46fd58638d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/123f463eea7501ed4b55a24b2312f46fd58638d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/a79814a9ace386bccc80c4bf4ccb35198af575df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T21:22:25Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T21:22:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop calling a local file unknown to the workspace when the export reported it (#25746)\n\n## What\n\nThe pull report contradicted itself. A define file for an entity the\nworkspace really has, but that this version of pull cannot write, was\nlisted under \"Local entities the workspace does not have (left\nuntouched)\" while the same report said the workspace has those entities.\n\nPulling the Custom application into a tree holding a `defineRole()` file\nfor one of its real roles printed both of these, a few lines apart:\n\n```\nLocal entities the workspace does not have (left untouched):\n  src/roles/guest.role.ts\n\nNot written, unsupported by this version (19 row(s)):\n  ...\n  role                              4\n```\n\nRead literally, the first line invites you to delete a file that\ndescribes a role the workspace is using.\n\n## How\n\nThe local-only list was everything scanned that the writer did not write\nand the base did not know. Since roles, command menu items, logic\nfunctions and front components are not written by this version, every\nfile for them qualified.\n\n`planPullWrites` now also receives the universal identifiers the export\nreported in its coverage, which is every row the workspace holds for\nthis application whatever its status, and excludes them. What remains in\nthe list is what the heading claims: a file whose entity the workspace\ngenuinely does not have, such as one authored locally and never pushed.\n\nFiles for kinds pull cannot write yet stay untouched on disk, as before,\nand the coverage section keeps reporting their entities.\n\n## Verification\n\n- A new case asserts a scanned file whose identifier the export reported\nis not listed as local-only. It fails against the previous code.\n- The existing case for a genuinely unknown local entity still reports\nit.\n- Verified live: the reproduction above no longer prints the \"Local\nentities\" section at all.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25746?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"50750fb887470bb78771e9a17de48dca3ed89ee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/50750fb887470bb78771e9a17de48dca3ed89ee9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/a79814a9ace386bccc80c4bf4ccb35198af575df","verification":{"payload":"tree 50750fb887470bb78771e9a17de48dca3ed89ee9\nparent e8f9a165c7b581894a16648974ee9e8c2b68706c\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789075345 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789075345 +0000\n\nStop calling a local file unknown to the workspace when the export reported it (#25746)\n\n## What\n\nThe pull report contradicted itself. A define file for an entity the\nworkspace really has, but that this version of pull cannot write, was\nlisted under \"Local entities the workspace does not have (left\nuntouched)\" while the same report said the workspace has those entities.\n\nPulling the Custom application into a tree holding a `defineRole()` file\nfor one of its real roles printed both of these, a few lines apart:\n\n```\nLocal entities the workspace does not have (left untouched):\n  src/roles/guest.role.ts\n\nNot written, unsupported by this version (19 row(s)):\n  ...\n  role                              4\n```\n\nRead literally, the first line invites you to delete a file that\ndescribes a role the workspace is using.\n\n## How\n\nThe local-only list was everything scanned that the writer did not write\nand the base did not know. Since roles, command menu items, logic\nfunctions and front components are not written by this version, every\nfile for them qualified.\n\n`planPullWrites` now also receives the universal identifiers the export\nreported in its coverage, which is every row the workspace holds for\nthis application whatever its status, and excludes them. What remains in\nthe list is what the heading claims: a file whose entity the workspace\ngenuinely does not have, such as one authored locally and never pushed.\n\nFiles for kinds pull cannot write yet stay untouched on disk, as before,\nand the coverage section keeps reporting their entities.\n\n## Verification\n\n- A new case asserts a scanned file whose identifier the export reported\nis not listed as local-only. It fails against the previous code.\n- The existing case for a genuinely unknown local entity still reports\nit.\n- Verified live: the reproduction above no longer prints the \"Local\nentities\" section at all.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25746?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqox+hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqokQAC+EACwmoGIpTSN6Dk/t7f86\nVzwHG8I2vRSPotIbNCL5xc8nOzuMi52kCNLPU0Py86dERxbVZfz67whst9qDJqYE\nkWmTKVySVmDeOY+EusCBJtD7gS55ELmg7eJXCL/KX/vnj0AmsebUGYLPoToTgy0U\nBjfgQpRXEMIc/8yT5XgAqZAdGjHXJi4dNl9DU7KJrptn4N2kJCfEaf/L8AUwhuom\nixnp4cvv8uCoEOd1rRNT/tTTL+QGTnEnz6KbBoHhU6Mt+Oqqd8u8dMwDRJQ96ZUj\nUeqYfgoPSRt8TkADKFy51aSer2V+c5R6aZE14uJVdJc0xLfpDMI1cn8D73Gw26sS\n27bT1ekUvA5EpIGZPKI1h5cgPXlO0z966menl5dLcZH0Dj3zIA+DMyEndeGCBhQK\nMrzWiTMuBkBYuBD2MQyBlJSsgpA1g4fhlLNneNXRJC4WiE75RqW0eY1sb7JDl165\nMZ7MA7Cqn/TaCOR+x0bCgMcp8BouqfxplpwSFu0PzsGguj6mivYOkOklpahJAWYh\nbRHbrj8M7v2RXAlQpTckVpznJYEaxwevNobA3ddah52Yp3ybNt6Ub73hsrt6K7cp\nrfVeD+YfCFUC/DvvPLvMRQKL3+mA/bTkuGVDn3RSDxeZzlkVD8zpDpEpKXvqn+Nn\nu/QcyHUcxd9eoCo+CCAh\n=jHzP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/a79814a9ace386bccc80c4bf4ccb35198af575df","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGE3OTgxNGE5YWNlMzg2YmNjYzgwYzRiZjRjY2IzNTE5OGFmNTc1ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/e8f9a165c7b581894a16648974ee9e8c2b68706c","sha":"e8f9a165c7b581894a16648974ee9e8c2b68706c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/e8f9a165c7b581894a16648974ee9e8c2b68706c"}],"sha":"a79814a9ace386bccc80c4bf4ccb35198af575df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/a79814a9ace386bccc80c4bf4ccb35198af575df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/e8f9a165c7b581894a16648974ee9e8c2b68706c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T21:01:42Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T21:01:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let the e2e local registry accept twenty-ui (#25765)\n\n## What\n\n`create-app-e2e-minimal` fails for every pull request that runs it, at\nthe \"Publish packages to local registry\" step:\n\n```\n➤ YN0041: Invalid authentication (as an unknown user)\n➤ YN0000: Failed with errors in 0s 813ms\nError: Process completed with exit code 1\n```\n\nThe workflow publishes `twenty-client-sdk twenty-ui twenty-sdk\ncreate-twenty-app`, but `.github/verdaccio-config.yaml` grants `publish`\nto only three of them. `twenty-ui` falls through to the `''**''` entry,\nwhich sets `access` and a proxy but no `publish`, and verdaccio defaults\npublish to `$authenticated`. The job authenticates with a placeholder\n`npmAuthToken` and no htpasswd user, so the request is rejected as an\nunknown user.\n\nThis has been failing since `twenty-ui` joined the publishable set. It\nis not intermittent: retries fail identically, because nothing about it\ndepends on timing.\n\nMain looks unaffected only because the job is gated on changes under\n`packages/create-twenty-app/**`, `packages/twenty-sdk/**`,\n`packages/twenty-client-sdk/**` and `packages/twenty-shared/**`. Most\npushes to main touch none of those, so the job is skipped and the run is\ngreen. On the runs where main did execute it, it failed with this same\nerror.\n\n## How\n\n`twenty-ui` gets the same rule the other published packages already\nhave, so the local registry accepts it without authentication like its\nsiblings.\n\nAdding the rule rather than dropping `twenty-ui` from\n`PUBLISHABLE_PACKAGES`, because its version is aligned with the SDK''s,\nso the scaffolded app resolves `twenty-ui` at the CI version from this\nregistry. Removing it from the list would move the failure to the\ninstall step instead of fixing it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Reproduced and fixed locally, running verdaccio exactly as the job\ndoes. Publishing a package named `twenty-ui` against the current config\nfails with `E401 Unable to authenticate`, which is this failure; against\nthe config in this PR the same publish succeeds with `+\ntwenty-ui@0.0.0-authtest`.\n- The config parses, and every package the workflow publishes now has a\npublish rule.\n- The failure and its cause were read from the job logs of a run that\nexecuted the step, and confirmed identical on a run from `main`.\n- Size is not a concern for this registry''s default 10 MB body limit: a\nclean `twenty-ui` build is about 11 MB across 872 artifacts before\ncompression, so the tarball lands well under it.","tree":{"sha":"b25e2ec7dc608c11d2818a0273205ad4dc785d9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/b25e2ec7dc608c11d2818a0273205ad4dc785d9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/e8f9a165c7b581894a16648974ee9e8c2b68706c","verification":{"payload":"tree b25e2ec7dc608c11d2818a0273205ad4dc785d9f\nparent 0a0836208a6e889fa6a625f0d5dbc87779d9ce06\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789074102 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789074102 +0000\n\nLet the e2e local registry accept twenty-ui (#25765)\n\n## What\n\n`create-app-e2e-minimal` fails for every pull request that runs it, at\nthe \"Publish packages to local registry\" step:\n\n```\n➤ YN0041: Invalid authentication (as an unknown user)\n➤ YN0000: Failed with errors in 0s 813ms\nError: Process completed with exit code 1\n```\n\nThe workflow publishes `twenty-client-sdk twenty-ui twenty-sdk\ncreate-twenty-app`, but `.github/verdaccio-config.yaml` grants `publish`\nto only three of them. `twenty-ui` falls through to the `''**''` entry,\nwhich sets `access` and a proxy but no `publish`, and verdaccio defaults\npublish to `$authenticated`. The job authenticates with a placeholder\n`npmAuthToken` and no htpasswd user, so the request is rejected as an\nunknown user.\n\nThis has been failing since `twenty-ui` joined the publishable set. It\nis not intermittent: retries fail identically, because nothing about it\ndepends on timing.\n\nMain looks unaffected only because the job is gated on changes under\n`packages/create-twenty-app/**`, `packages/twenty-sdk/**`,\n`packages/twenty-client-sdk/**` and `packages/twenty-shared/**`. Most\npushes to main touch none of those, so the job is skipped and the run is\ngreen. On the runs where main did execute it, it failed with this same\nerror.\n\n## How\n\n`twenty-ui` gets the same rule the other published packages already\nhave, so the local registry accepts it without authentication like its\nsiblings.\n\nAdding the rule rather than dropping `twenty-ui` from\n`PUBLISHABLE_PACKAGES`, because its version is aligned with the SDK''s,\nso the scaffolded app resolves `twenty-ui` at the CI version from this\nregistry. Removing it from the list would move the failure to the\ninstall step instead of fixing it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Reproduced and fixed locally, running verdaccio exactly as the job\ndoes. Publishing a package named `twenty-ui` against the current config\nfails with `E401 Unable to authenticate`, which is this failure; against\nthe config in this PR the same publish succeeds with `+\ntwenty-ui@0.0.0-authtest`.\n- The config parses, and every package the workflow publishes now has a\npublish rule.\n- The failure and its cause were read from the job logs of a run that\nexecuted the step, and confirmed identical on a run from `main`.\n- Size is not a concern for this registry''s default 10 MB body limit: a\nclean `twenty-ui` build is about 11 MB across 872 artifacts before\ncompression, so the tarball lands well under it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoxrGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuLEQAHovyRkDBIUEW7mhTOYM9Xux\n1Ch+Nr+CsCkWlRKn10TjWyQfidhgaKZ6CD2RCNtDxNz6PxvW36csSEZKL10rAuAS\nQhU+vslhMvHYUCAwhTPG24d3s1MNGzl8cofCT7mkTbN/0L8f/fyxjZJNrUguMx1H\nkGVaLVdPsfrA8ekR5wwXUMzJjsSBL83e+oRwWEIqfdY4mKxr3iDJY7Nk4rJVAey2\ngP9cE5tCiLYk/RdrhZUp4Btw0xzcnA7nXyceY//h02ybhmolHNkmQFnekH+kKL2y\ntQB+trNaw0HAwq3zuUPwYhicSJPx5fqTaRdbFtQTVmLgttilLMEbBYQqgsfshCqq\niEu3J/J0Hc5H5OALsks81OegpT9jmkd393bvRdphqcVVU9tevzGDjDYshTPD2CEl\nuFMSwHJG/JQtodJwt6rEevjNj0tghqZMGH3t3XtCRvo2FtpxJGHGvjaFIBVNCmsT\n7Me1ojVmy1WMx3yEf1FbkA/Yi+f3pUa01aq5uVcYKB0HSeN3Envtm7iFaJhUeYft\nWZQU9yE3s5lPdZKvLgMoXk0sgjF2jbxljIu6jeDElPZsWqQ33DniSsqJ7/xDZ33p\nsVHTytPKEhne/IYIAejZQQ4O3/z+Vn4zh8nxrCryPZr6+Ee7jlYULVSB118JL3V0\nisBVIzGL9lBsNMbvTpf0\n=UVSb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/e8f9a165c7b581894a16648974ee9e8c2b68706c","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGU4ZjlhMTY1YzdiNTgxODk0YTE2NjQ4OTc0ZWU5ZThjMmI2ODcwNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/0a0836208a6e889fa6a625f0d5dbc87779d9ce06","sha":"0a0836208a6e889fa6a625f0d5dbc87779d9ce06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/0a0836208a6e889fa6a625f0d5dbc87779d9ce06"}],"sha":"e8f9a165c7b581894a16648974ee9e8c2b68706c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/e8f9a165c7b581894a16648974ee9e8c2b68706c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/0a0836208a6e889fa6a625f0d5dbc87779d9ce06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:38:28Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:38:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Refuse to pull an application into a project that already defines another (#25750)\n\n## What\n\n`yarn twenty pull -u <other application>` in a project that already\ndefines one silently repointed the project at the other application and\nleft both applications'' entities in the same tree.\n`src/application.config.ts` was rewritten to the new identity, the\nprevious application''s objects stayed where they were, and the report\nsaid nothing.\n\nThe damage only surfaced later, on the next plan, as a wall of raw\nerrors:\n\n```\n3. ENTITY_ALREADY_EXISTS: Cannot create navigationMenuItem: universalIdentifier \"b80b9e60-…\"\n   already exists in navigationMenuItem maps from application \"b30a4560-…\"\n```\n\n## How\n\nPull refuses when `-u` names an application other than the one the\nproject''s `defineApplication()` file declares:\n\n```\nThis project already defines application b30a4560-fedb-4ccd-904a-3788762c7d33.\n\n  Pulling 5b1e7c2a-3d4f-4e5a-9b6c-7d8e9f0a1b2c here would leave two applications in one tree.\n  Pull it into a different directory instead.\n```\n\nThe check runs before the export, so a mistyped or mistaken identifier\ncosts nothing and touches neither the tree nor the server.\n\nIt also refuses when the project declares an application whose\nidentifier cannot be read, which the scanner records the same way as no\ndeclaration at all. Left alone, that case would have let the pull\nthrough and written the new application over the very file it could not\nevaluate:\n\n```\nThis project declares an application, but its identifier could not be read.\n\n  Pulling 5b1e7c2a-3d4f-4e5a-9b6c-7d8e9f0a1b2c here could overwrite that declaration.\n  Run `yarn install` so the file can be evaluated, then pull again.\n```\n\nEverything else is unchanged: `-u` naming the application the tree\nalready declares still pulls, a project that declares no application yet\nstill accepts any `-u`, and pull with no `-u` still reads the identity\nfrom the tree.\n\nNo flag is added to force the old behaviour. Re-pointing a tree at a\ndifferent application is not something to do in place, and a fresh\ndirectory is both the safe and the obvious way to get it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New spec on the check: refuses a different identifier and names both\napplications, refuses an unreadable declaration, and allows the matching\nidentifier, a tree with no application, and a pull that passes no\nidentifier.\n- The pull page documents the restriction.\n- Verified live against a dev workspace: pulling the SDK app into a tree\npulled from Custom is refused with the message above,\n`application.config.ts` still holds the Custom identifier afterwards,\nand pulling Custom again into the same tree still succeeds.","tree":{"sha":"1b44133d953d84403bf620eb967a3861d5f6716c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/1b44133d953d84403bf620eb967a3861d5f6716c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/0a0836208a6e889fa6a625f0d5dbc87779d9ce06","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b44133d953d84403bf620eb967a3861d5f6716c\nparent b3adebbe9162051489118ea0fbabbb9297375091\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789072708 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789072708 +0200\n\nRefuse to pull an application into a project that already defines another (#25750)\n\n## What\n\n`yarn twenty pull -u <other application>` in a project that already\ndefines one silently repointed the project at the other application and\nleft both applications'' entities in the same tree.\n`src/application.config.ts` was rewritten to the new identity, the\nprevious application''s objects stayed where they were, and the report\nsaid nothing.\n\nThe damage only surfaced later, on the next plan, as a wall of raw\nerrors:\n\n```\n3. ENTITY_ALREADY_EXISTS: Cannot create navigationMenuItem: universalIdentifier \"b80b9e60-…\"\n   already exists in navigationMenuItem maps from application \"b30a4560-…\"\n```\n\n## How\n\nPull refuses when `-u` names an application other than the one the\nproject''s `defineApplication()` file declares:\n\n```\nThis project already defines application b30a4560-fedb-4ccd-904a-3788762c7d33.\n\n  Pulling 5b1e7c2a-3d4f-4e5a-9b6c-7d8e9f0a1b2c here would leave two applications in one tree.\n  Pull it into a different directory instead.\n```\n\nThe check runs before the export, so a mistyped or mistaken identifier\ncosts nothing and touches neither the tree nor the server.\n\nIt also refuses when the project declares an application whose\nidentifier cannot be read, which the scanner records the same way as no\ndeclaration at all. Left alone, that case would have let the pull\nthrough and written the new application over the very file it could not\nevaluate:\n\n```\nThis project declares an application, but its identifier could not be read.\n\n  Pulling 5b1e7c2a-3d4f-4e5a-9b6c-7d8e9f0a1b2c here could overwrite that declaration.\n  Run `yarn install` so the file can be evaluated, then pull again.\n```\n\nEverything else is unchanged: `-u` naming the application the tree\nalready declares still pulls, a project that declares no application yet\nstill accepts any `-u`, and pull with no `-u` still reads the identity\nfrom the tree.\n\nNo flag is added to force the old behaviour. Re-pointing a tree at a\ndifferent application is not something to do in place, and a fresh\ndirectory is both the safe and the obvious way to get it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New spec on the check: refuses a different identifier and names both\napplications, refuses an unreadable declaration, and allows the matching\nidentifier, a tree with no application, and a pull that passes no\nidentifier.\n- The pull page documents the restriction.\n- Verified live against a dev workspace: pulling the SDK app into a tree\npulled from Custom is refused with the message above,\n`application.config.ts` still holds the Custom identifier afterwards,\nand pulling Custom again into the same tree still succeeds.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoxVECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGTsQAKNABoGjiPFY3I/MN0v542F0\n70zZhjHH8mdQC/rET/T495hT9EJU07SoiNfEv4v5ivvQAdjcA+vV2PE+iQX93iUf\nbI3ehvsvOzyOdULKjKIh26JrbXjLQAfShQtdkvaIALP2/5cXywetk4FvabNFqknw\n45aK0sfNfquJg2mhSvnc1afOIudYjEP7gQgT0fl8iEOo2CLBFvYUPmbJaAr574n+\n7h2L2KJemA/SF/ITD2IGoSMnoaEmVDvx9RBtBW4QdRfum4Osk7QvfPQkIARxzMlg\nsIRCL71EEbexhANep1wdDmSj0L5uSr9vqjotxWQa7ZwnzIYKeQxihfhmQNFzAOq2\ncrws/31kNF0TmavdxvGmdyoFdmjJQjUX2PKPVQTGYNfRXB3bFUlR855VkBhYg+ii\nGa0pV+zekZqH2EObblIB/PGMXRMTMJSGlNYD5HobgKCPJCbdbgDQMFi0ioGlNGSM\no+SjJENFbzFGhNDAmq4Fcq6P7i6hTrBfKmHt+PejHq+jgwt2O4BSZC0CeIfwME17\nk7X8qlWBjicyUh6cEqeLyz6eCQiCNVLrYdb8tAuqBTSeEBoKCCavV26djBduXRaH\nuOGJ/JXV5ZkMeK2AiDkIHcpr3nS4ySK2Z9Me2fKy84pN205wQw9yoqeETUknNuQj\nUBqbI6hcax80jToHcoxN\n=2uhK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/0a0836208a6e889fa6a625f0d5dbc87779d9ce06","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDBhMDgzNjIwOGE2ZTg4OWZhNmE2MjVmMGQ1ZGJjODc3NzlkOWNlMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/b3adebbe9162051489118ea0fbabbb9297375091","sha":"b3adebbe9162051489118ea0fbabbb9297375091","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b3adebbe9162051489118ea0fbabbb9297375091"}],"sha":"0a0836208a6e889fa6a625f0d5dbc87779d9ce06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/0a0836208a6e889fa6a625f0d5dbc87779d9ce06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19412894?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonapara","id":19412894,"login":"Bonapara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDEyODk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b3adebbe9162051489118ea0fbabbb9297375091/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:35:35Z","email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:35:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: share floating reference scale calculation (#25762)\n\nThe table and record-detail inline editors duplicated the same\nreference-scale calculation. Extract it into `getFloatingReferenceScale`\nand reuse it from both offset callbacks, preserving their existing\nbehavior.\n\nAddresses the final cleanup comment on #25667, which merged while this\nchange was being prepared.\n\nValidation: targeted lint and formatting pass. The unchanged positioning\nbehavior was verified in the #25667 preview at 125%, including table\neditors and the record-detail date picker. No additional tests are\nneeded for this extraction.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25762?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"9e4b2a2f47ece7b2f67dab9b702911be14d31199","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/9e4b2a2f47ece7b2f67dab9b702911be14d31199"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/b3adebbe9162051489118ea0fbabbb9297375091","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e4b2a2f47ece7b2f67dab9b702911be14d31199\nparent 5a03d6a2a5d8f4f363f57d7fa86c1633279ec0d3\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789072535 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789072535 +0200\n\nrefactor: share floating reference scale calculation (#25762)\n\nThe table and record-detail inline editors duplicated the same\nreference-scale calculation. Extract it into `getFloatingReferenceScale`\nand reuse it from both offset callbacks, preserving their existing\nbehavior.\n\nAddresses the final cleanup comment on #25667, which merged while this\nchange was being prepared.\n\nValidation: targeted lint and formatting pass. The unchanged positioning\nbehavior was verified in the #25667 preview at 125%, including table\neditors and the record-detail date picker. No additional tests are\nneeded for this extraction.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25762?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-ge