TzfBtdoAKGIzYWRlYmJlOTE2MjA1MTQ4OTExOGVhMGZiYWJiYjkyOTczNzUwOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/5a03d6a2a5d8f4f363f57d7fa86c1633279ec0d3","sha":"5a03d6a2a5d8f4f363f57d7fa86c1633279ec0d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5a03d6a2a5d8f4f363f57d7fa86c1633279ec0d3"}],"sha":"b3adebbe9162051489118ea0fbabbb9297375091","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b3adebbe9162051489118ea0fbabbb9297375091"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5a03d6a2a5d8f4f363f57d7fa86c1633279ec0d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:11:21Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:11:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai): keep catalog efforts under an AI_PROVIDERS override and fix tier UI findings (#25753)\n\nFollow-up to #25721, from a QA pass on twenty-main after it deployed.\n\n## What broke on twenty-main\n\nThe instance runs an `AI_PROVIDERS` override (twenty-infra''s\n`ai-models-config`) written before the catalog carried efforts and\nbenchmarks. A custom provider replaced the built-in provider of the same\nname wholesale, so every model it listed lost `efforts`, `benchmark` and\n`benchmarkByEffort`. Every tier chain entry pinned at an effort\n(`openai/gpt-5.6-luna@low` and so on) became unreachable, and each tier\nfell to the last-resort model: `/client-config` there resolved Extra\nFast, Balanced and Extra Smart to `azure-foundry/gpt-5.4`, with no\nefforts and no benchmarks on any model.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Override merge**: a custom provider still decides which models exist\nand keeps its own credentials, labels and prices, but a model the\ncatalog knows inherits what describes the model itself. Under a provider\nthe catalog has (`openai`, `anthropic`, `google`), a model of the same\nname inherits every catalog field the custom entry does not set;\n`benchmark` merges metric by metric and `benchmarkByEffort` effort by\neffort. Under a provider the catalog does not have (Bedrock, Azure, a\ngateway), a model inherits only `efforts`, `benchmark` and\n`benchmarkByEffort` from the catalog model it serves, matched by name\nwith route segments and deployment stamps dropped\n(`eu.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7` and `claude-haiku-4-5-v1:0` join their\nrows; `gpt-4.1` still matches itself first). This is what the config\nvariable''s description already promised (\"deep-merged on top of the\nbuilt-in catalog\"), and it means the cloud catalogs never need to carry\nbenchmark numbers. Inherited efforts still go through the existing SDK\nfilter, so an OpenAI-compatible gateway, whose SDK has no reasoning\noption, offers none. Unit spec added; the live check could not run\nlocally because custom providers are an entitlement this dev instance\ndoes not have.\n- **Nearest rung before the registry head**: a tier whose chain names\nnothing available (an instance with two models, or an admin who disabled\na chain''s last entry) used to land on whatever the catalog listed first\nfor that provider, possibly a weaker or deprecated model than the\nneighbouring tier. It now walks its neighbours'' chains by distance,\nlower rung first at equal distance, and the registry fallback prefers a\ncurrent model over a deprecated one. Anthropic-only with Fable disabled\nnow gives Extra Smart Opus 5 from the Smart chain instead of Sonnet 4.6\nfrom the catalog head.\n- **One cost basis per comparison**: the preview table and the slider\ndeltas use Artificial Analysis cost per task only when every tier has\none, otherwise the blended per-token price for all, through one shared\npredicate. Before, the table mixed `$0.45 / 1M tokens` rows with `$5.86\n/ task` rows, since Luna at low, medium and high have no cost per task\nyet while Sol, Astra and Opus 5 do.\n- **Agent page render loop**: the agent settings page logged \"Maximum\nupdate depth exceeded\" continuously and re-set the form on every render.\n`useNavigateApp` returned a new function on every render, and the agent\nload effect lists it as a dependency next to `resetForm`, which was also\nrecreated each render; each render re-ran the effect, which set state,\nwhich rendered again. The hook now returns a memoized function, as\n`useSnackBar` already does, and the form state callbacks are memoized\ntoo. Three other pages list `navigateApp` in effect dependencies and get\nthe same fix. The loop predates #25721, which only touched a default\nconstant in the form state hook; this clone''s history starts at a\nsnapshot commit, so I cannot date it further back. Verified gone in the\nbrowser.\n\nThe steward that curates the cloud catalogs is updated to the tier\nchains in twentyhq/twenty-factory#114 (merged); its prose relies on the\nmerge above so it does not copy benchmark numbers into\n`ai-models-config`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Server: oxlint, ai-models and client-config specs pass (81 tests).\n- Front: oxlint, `tsgo`, suites under `modules/ai`, `pages/settings/ai`,\n`modules/settings/ai`, `hooks` and `modules/ai/components` pass.\n- Browser on merged main with the real catalog: Models tab with pins at\nan effort persisting as `anthropic/claude-opus-5@high`, preview table on\none unit, admin panel default models with effort, composer bars opening\nthe slider with keyboard stepping, agent page without the loop.\n\n## Left as is\n\n- Per-token cost deltas read as `+2122%` on the slider; a multiplier\nformat would read better but is a design call.\n- Opening the tier dropdown does not move focus to the slider, so arrow\nkeys work only after a Tab.\n- The agent page still loads the agent into form state through an\neffect. Initialising the form from the loaded agent instead (mount the\nform once the query resolves, keyed by agent id) would remove that\neffect class entirely and is a larger restructure of the page than this\nPR should carry.\n- twenty-infra''s `values.yaml` files still set\n`AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_RECOMMENDED`, which nothing reads any more, and set\n`_FAST` and `_SMART` to bare ids; the three new tier variables are unset\nthere and fall back to the self-hoster chains.","tree":{"sha":"2a00c6137c9f032a42697cfaaa284ca55730dd38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/2a00c6137c9f032a42697cfaaa284ca55730dd38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/5a03d6a2a5d8f4f363f57d7fa86c1633279ec0d3","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a00c6137c9f032a42697cfaaa284ca55730dd38\nparent 0d5ada9a466ad1bef8e0880ae1c04465b4dd9974\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789071081 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789071081 +0200\n\nfix(ai): keep catalog efforts under an AI_PROVIDERS override and fix tier UI findings (#25753)\n\nFollow-up to #25721, from a QA pass on twenty-main after it deployed.\n\n## What broke on twenty-main\n\nThe instance runs an `AI_PROVIDERS` override (twenty-infra''s\n`ai-models-config`) written before the catalog carried efforts and\nbenchmarks. A custom provider replaced the built-in provider of the same\nname wholesale, so every model it listed lost `efforts`, `benchmark` and\n`benchmarkByEffort`. Every tier chain entry pinned at an effort\n(`openai/gpt-5.6-luna@low` and so on) became unreachable, and each tier\nfell to the last-resort model: `/client-config` there resolved Extra\nFast, Balanced and Extra Smart to `azure-foundry/gpt-5.4`, with no\nefforts and no benchmarks on any model.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Override merge**: a custom provider still decides which models exist\nand keeps its own credentials, labels and prices, but a model the\ncatalog knows inherits what describes the model itself. Under a provider\nthe catalog has (`openai`, `anthropic`, `google`), a model of the same\nname inherits every catalog field the custom entry does not set;\n`benchmark` merges metric by metric and `benchmarkByEffort` effort by\neffort. Under a provider the catalog does not have (Bedrock, Azure, a\ngateway), a model inherits only `efforts`, `benchmark` and\n`benchmarkByEffort` from the catalog model it serves, matched by name\nwith route segments and deployment stamps dropped\n(`eu.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7` and `claude-haiku-4-5-v1:0` join their\nrows; `gpt-4.1` still matches itself first). This is what the config\nvariable''s description already promised (\"deep-merged on top of the\nbuilt-in catalog\"), and it means the cloud catalogs never need to carry\nbenchmark numbers. Inherited efforts still go through the existing SDK\nfilter, so an OpenAI-compatible gateway, whose SDK has no reasoning\noption, offers none. Unit spec added; the live check could not run\nlocally because custom providers are an entitlement this dev instance\ndoes not have.\n- **Nearest rung before the registry head**: a tier whose chain names\nnothing available (an instance with two models, or an admin who disabled\na chain''s last entry) used to land on whatever the catalog listed first\nfor that provider, possibly a weaker or deprecated model than the\nneighbouring tier. It now walks its neighbours'' chains by distance,\nlower rung first at equal distance, and the registry fallback prefers a\ncurrent model over a deprecated one. Anthropic-only with Fable disabled\nnow gives Extra Smart Opus 5 from the Smart chain instead of Sonnet 4.6\nfrom the catalog head.\n- **One cost basis per comparison**: the preview table and the slider\ndeltas use Artificial Analysis cost per task only when every tier has\none, otherwise the blended per-token price for all, through one shared\npredicate. Before, the table mixed `$0.45 / 1M tokens` rows with `$5.86\n/ task` rows, since Luna at low, medium and high have no cost per task\nyet while Sol, Astra and Opus 5 do.\n- **Agent page render loop**: the agent settings page logged \"Maximum\nupdate depth exceeded\" continuously and re-set the form on every render.\n`useNavigateApp` returned a new function on every render, and the agent\nload effect lists it as a dependency next to `resetForm`, which was also\nrecreated each render; each render re-ran the effect, which set state,\nwhich rendered again. The hook now returns a memoized function, as\n`useSnackBar` already does, and the form state callbacks are memoized\ntoo. Three other pages list `navigateApp` in effect dependencies and get\nthe same fix. The loop predates #25721, which only touched a default\nconstant in the form state hook; this clone''s history starts at a\nsnapshot commit, so I cannot date it further back. Verified gone in the\nbrowser.\n\nThe steward that curates the cloud catalogs is updated to the tier\nchains in twentyhq/twenty-factory#114 (merged); its prose relies on the\nmerge above so it does not copy benchmark numbers into\n`ai-models-config`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Server: oxlint, ai-models and client-config specs pass (81 tests).\n- Front: oxlint, `tsgo`, suites under `modules/ai`, `pages/settings/ai`,\n`modules/settings/ai`, `hooks` and `modules/ai/components` pass.\n- Browser on merged main with the real catalog: Models tab with pins at\nan effort persisting as `anthropic/claude-opus-5@high`, preview table on\none unit, admin panel default models with effort, composer bars opening\nthe slider with keyboard stepping, agent page without the loop.\n\n## Left as is\n\n- Per-token cost deltas read as `+2122%` on the slider; a multiplier\nformat would read better but is a design call.\n- Opening the tier dropdown does not move focus to the slider, so arrow\nkeys work only after a Tab.\n- The agent page still loads the agent into form state through an\neffect. Initialising the form from the loaded agent instead (mount the\nform once the query resolves, keyed by agent id) would remove that\neffect class entirely and is a larger restructure of the page than this\nPR should carry.\n- twenty-infra''s `values.yaml` files still set\n`AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_RECOMMENDED`, which nothing reads any more, and set\n`_FAST` and `_SMART` to bare ids; the three new tier variables are unset\nthere and fall back to the self-hoster chains.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqow7pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkPEQAJOlkw8+EjIlNNuIKS0w1mY/\n9p+FYYESm9orj0+9n1/KjVR2WpqyFWwxzaqDGyP9h6H6PsIzoe6FDqR4a2JdBBKn\nFiMzLWcISzDcEZ0pKLvDsXGXIjxUaqwSnstzi3p0mEDhjNpZdEKhI3k7eAp26heb\nRVEjMykKWyJi+jFUHfcMxLEHkUscS/pSzsgzY4OlOpR5cxLB+Srp0lZ7414KKM+o\nYPdBHMnC2/Cq4BIWzRh5bYclC++TK2a6h6jwBVI5AFbg2rnzHOZbc30qk4VolbkG\nkY6Wv9lCY2YcRIGfhkYxO+Nq24erJZJQMQ6RU/Pbr61chPgFzbELvyyXW6CmzXzA\nijpQVR+x45w8TCgbQnHO8DF7g+vtAatN1BZ4lv4wA8r2IEYbATu/et4hDp330oZn\nA1ZmeOGMx9lP5Ank5353nwe9UHBah9b2u72NX2c1VkzXY+dm/XgkuUwSyRoDSkB5\n5+oeOlVOlIy3EEY/W3BL/QCi9jZWmFvtsPJxgAXvsN/rClh5kK15LU/1MMaE5SJ9\n55rGqlTreLwCZCavsHOZ+3+mLNNhuvGNVuYdx5b82ZU2fP1jA3ByG9iYmYEOsZ/k\n9F9ko4tNCb6943QTRcJQi7Ndlvc7S4fe+sfE0KDxrTXGnjFw1XYJC5WzBdsEc7U7\n1+dSYktBPUkv5QgOSwPU\n=lkcn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/5a03d6a2a5d8f4f363f57d7fa86c1633279ec0d3","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDVhMDNkNmEyYTVkOGY0ZjM2M2Y1N2Q3ZmE4NmMxNjMzMjc5ZWMwZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/0d5ada9a466ad1bef8e0880ae1c04465b4dd9974","sha":"0d5ada9a466ad1bef8e0880ae1c04465b4dd9974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/0d5ada9a466ad1bef8e0880ae1c04465b4dd9974"}],"sha":"5a03d6a2a5d8f4f363f57d7fa86c1633279ec0d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5a03d6a2a5d8f4f363f57d7fa86c1633279ec0d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19412894?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonapara","id":19412894,"login":"Bonapara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDEyODk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/0d5ada9a466ad1bef8e0880ae1c04465b4dd9974/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:06:34Z","email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:06:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix dropdown anchoring at non-default interface scales (#25667)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix dropdowns drifting offscreen when the interface scale differs from\n100%. Use fixed viewport positioning for portaled dropdowns, cancel root\nzoom on the positioning wrapper, and restore the selected scale on its\ncontents. This also covers expanded-list menus and removes the obsolete\nabsolute-position override from the record command menu.\n\nThe regression story checks anchoring and scaled content dimensions at\n90%, 100%, 110%, 125%, and the mobile base scale.\n\n## Preview verification\n\nCaptured from the [deployed\npreview](https://harry-backed-chester-offerings.trycloudflare.com/settings/experience)\nat commit `f265a0c`. At both 90% and 125%, the open scale menu stays\naligned beneath its selector and remains fully visible. Restored the\npreview to 100% afterward.\n\nCI lint, typecheck, build, unit tests, and all Storybook test shards\npassed.\n\n### 90% interface scale\n\n![Dropdown anchored at 90% interface\nscale](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bf3b2687-87ba-4c4c-b9c9-ae438b241722)\n\n### 125% interface scale\n\n![Dropdown anchored at 125% interface\nscale](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7827135b-1d4f-44f6-93de-a1d1460dfb88)","tree":{"sha":"3a58419c15d07a6fb0d34efe2b65caae905cacad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/3a58419c15d07a6fb0d34efe2b65caae905cacad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/0d5ada9a466ad1bef8e0880ae1c04465b4dd9974","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a58419c15d07a6fb0d34efe2b65caae905cacad\nparent 2b545a7cbdb4b6c4918ccba24218d8849dc5f1c5\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789059994 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789059994 +0000\n\nFix dropdown anchoring at non-default interface scales (#25667)\n\n## Summary\n\nFix dropdowns drifting offscreen when the interface scale differs from\n100%. Use fixed viewport positioning for portaled dropdowns, cancel root\nzoom on the positioning wrapper, and restore the selected scale on its\ncontents. This also covers expanded-list menus and removes the obsolete\nabsolute-position override from the record command menu.\n\nThe regression story checks anchoring and scaled content dimensions at\n90%, 100%, 110%, 125%, and the mobile base scale.\n\n## Preview verification\n\nCaptured from the [deployed\npreview](https://harry-backed-chester-offerings.trycloudflare.com/settings/experience)\nat commit `f265a0c`. At both 90% and 125%, the open scale menu stays\naligned beneath its selector and remains fully visible. Restored the\npreview to 100% afterward.\n\nCI lint, typecheck, build, unit tests, and all Storybook test shards\npassed.\n\n### 90% interface scale\n\n![Dropdown anchored at 90% interface\nscale](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bf3b2687-87ba-4c4c-b9c9-ae438b241722)\n\n### 125% interface scale\n\n![Dropdown anchored at 125% interface\nscale](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7827135b-1d4f-44f6-93de-a1d1460dfb88)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqouOqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA