16c28853da71c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5e7cbb4a4606363bd78e939705a16c28853da71c"}],"sha":"eb170d4e465c7cccf75f210ac6ad960d2c17001e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/eb170d4e465c7cccf75f210ac6ad960d2c17001e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177449033?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MauryaQbit","id":177449033,"login":"MauryaQbit","node_id":"U_kgDOCpOoSQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MauryaQbit","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5e7cbb4a4606363bd78e939705a16c28853da71c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T16:24:05Z","email":"dhananjaymaury366@gmail.com","name":"Dhananjay Maurya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T16:24:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: republish twenty-ui as MIT (1.0.0-alpha.2) to resolve stale AGPL artifacts (#25738)\n\nFixes #25722.\n\n## Problem\n#23564 (merged 2026-07-30) relicensed the app-development packages to\nMIT, but npm still serves builds that predate the relicensing:\n\n- twenty-ui@1.0.0-alpha.0 (latest) and 1.0.0-alpha.1 (alpha tag, both\npublished 2026-06-24): AGPL-3.0 on the registry, old root LICENSE in the\ntarball.\n- twenty-shared@0.41.0-canary (published 2025-01-24): AGPL-3.0.\n\nMeanwhile twenty-sdk, twenty-client-sdk, and create-twenty-app (all\npublished after 2026-07-30) are correctly MIT. The repo itself is\nalready correct (license: MIT plus per-package MIT LICENSE).\n\nIn practice, create-twenty-app scaffolds apps pinning \"twenty-ui\":\n\"1.0.0-alpha.1\" and the generated front component imports from\ntwenty-ui/data-display and twenty-ui/icon — the exact scenario #23564\nwas written to prevent.\n\n## What this PR does\n- Bumps packages/twenty-ui/package.json 1.0.0-alpha.1 to 1.0.0-alpha.2\nso the next publish ships the post-#23564 package.json (license: MIT)\nand MIT LICENSE.\n- Adds LICENSE explicitly to twenty-ui files so the MIT text is always\nin the tarball (verified: npm pack --dry-run lists package/LICENSE, 1.1\nkB MIT, license=MIT).\n- Points the create-twenty-app scaffold template at 1.0.0-alpha.2.\n- Syncs English docs (front-components.mdx, project-structure.mdx),\ncodex-plugin references, and the cross-doc-contracts.js validator.\n\n## Why twenty-shared is intentionally untouched\npackages/twenty-shared/package.json is private:true with no version — it\nis only consumed via workspace:* (bundled at build time; twenty-sdk and\ntwenty-client-sdk list it under devDependencies, never via the registry)\nand the scaffold template does not depend on it. There is nothing to\nrepublish; republishing would mean making an internal package public\nagain. Instead, a maintainer should run npm deprecate on\ntwenty-shared@0.41.0-canary pointing at this issue. The in-repo state\n(license: MIT plus MIT LICENSE) is already correct.\n\n## Maintainer follow-up needed (cannot be done in a PR)\n1. Publish 1.0.0-alpha.2 from packages/twenty-ui, then promote it to\nlatest (currently latest still points at the stale 1.0.0-alpha.0; alpha\npoints at 1.0.0-alpha.1).\n2. npm deprecate the stale artifacts: twenty-ui@1.0.0-alpha.0,\ntwenty-ui@1.0.0-alpha.1, and twenty-shared@0.41.0-canary.\n3. Confirm npm view twenty-ui@1.0.0-alpha.2 license returns MIT and\npackage/LICENSE in the tarball is the MIT text.\n\n## Verification done\n- npm view confirms both published twenty-ui versions are AGPL-3.0 and\npredate #23564; repo is MIT.\n- npm pack --dry-run on the bumped package includes package/LICENSE\n(MIT) with license=MIT.\n- No test pins the old version (only the template literal, docs, and\nvalidator — all updated); twenty-apps examples use caret ranges that\nresolve forward to alpha.2 automatically, and root yarn.lock uses\nworkspace:*, so no lockfile churn is needed.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25738?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"2097d0e82925806364224428a796679ca3798b42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/2097d0e82925806364224428a796679ca3798b42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/5e7cbb4a4606363bd78e939705a16c28853da71c","verification":{"payload":"tree 2097d0e82925806364224428a796679ca3798b42\nparent fdec2d8bbdf0628fda3baf4025c8145a49156c83\nauthor Dhananjay Maurya <dhananjaymaury366@gmail.com> 1789057445 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789057445 +0200\n\nfix: republish twenty-ui as MIT (1.0.0-alpha.2) to resolve stale AGPL artifacts (#25738)\n\nFixes #25722.\n\n## Problem\n#23564 (merged 2026-07-30) relicensed the app-development packages to\nMIT, but npm still serves builds that predate the relicensing:\n\n- twenty-ui@1.0.0-alpha.0 (latest) and 1.0.0-alpha.1 (alpha tag, both\npublished 2026-06-24): AGPL-3.0 on the registry, old root LICENSE in the\ntarball.\n- twenty-shared@0.41.0-canary (published 2025-01-24): AGPL-3.0.\n\nMeanwhile twenty-sdk, twenty-client-sdk, and create-twenty-app (all\npublished after 2026-07-30) are correctly MIT. The repo itself is\nalready correct (license: MIT plus per-package MIT LICENSE).\n\nIn practice, create-twenty-app scaffolds apps pinning \"twenty-ui\":\n\"1.0.0-alpha.1\" and the generated front component imports from\ntwenty-ui/data-display and twenty-ui/icon — the exact scenario #23564\nwas written to prevent.\n\n## What this PR does\n- Bumps packages/twenty-ui/package.json 1.0.0-alpha.1 to 1.0.0-alpha.2\nso the next publish ships the post-#23564 package.json (license: MIT)\nand MIT LICENSE.\n- Adds LICENSE explicitly to twenty-ui files so the MIT text is always\nin the tarball (verified: npm pack --dry-run lists package/LICENSE, 1.1\nkB MIT, license=MIT).\n- Points the create-twenty-app scaffold template at 1.0.0-alpha.2.\n- Syncs English docs (front-components.mdx, project-structure.mdx),\ncodex-plugin references, and the cross-doc-contracts.js validator.\n\n## Why twenty-shared is intentionally untouched\npackages/twenty-shared/package.json is private:true with no version — it\nis only consumed via workspace:* (bundled at build time; twenty-sdk and\ntwenty-client-sdk list it under devDependencies, never via the registry)\nand the scaffold template does not depend on it. There is nothing to\nrepublish; republishing would mean making an internal package public\nagain. Instead, a maintainer should run npm deprecate on\ntwenty-shared@0.41.0-canary pointing at this issue. The in-repo state\n(license: MIT plus MIT LICENSE) is already correct.\n\n## Maintainer follow-up needed (cannot be done in a PR)\n1. Publish 1.0.0-alpha.2 from packages/twenty-ui, then promote it to\nlatest (currently latest still points at the stale 1.0.0-alpha.0; alpha\npoints at 1.0.0-alpha.1).\n2. npm deprecate the stale artifacts: twenty-ui@1.0.0-alpha.0,\ntwenty-ui@1.0.0-alpha.1, and twenty-shared@0.41.0-canary.\n3. Confirm npm view twenty-ui@1.0.0-alpha.2 license returns MIT and\npackage/LICENSE in the tarball is the MIT text.\n\n## Verification done\n- npm view confirms both published twenty-ui versions are AGPL-3.0 and\npredate #23564; repo is MIT.\n- npm pack --dry-run on the bumped package includes package/LICENSE\n(MIT) with license=MIT.\n- No test pins the old version (only the template literal, docs, and\nvalidator — all updated); twenty-apps examples use caret ranges that\nresolve forward to alpha.2 automatically, and root yarn.lock uses\nworkspace:*, so no lockfile churn is needed.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25738?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqotmlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADTgQACRDlCHpXEn8JPeRQuCDWIFR\n8zxf1dOLdfz+5TjnMBxYpsSlcnJNOyyHY6ztrhxzWPxsassq7RtlgYFs7UBSzkOi\npPL7HfxtjUi+xua7TCvOGtC0aP5dxhJEIBC17fjHLUyLBI2rJ418rjwwOUiOp8e4\nhPhxdaav5MCXXudxyOItfA2ygQ1FJHcZyPakocEBkwuJuRQ/Lw8URiNf1UXpD+Ce\nDlIUe1+YfucFrez3IfnMf5yuAM1aOxJJOYYEAfOnY//GGY/IKospOH8qemcc0qkX\nUA+AvopLyH+VVc1+cZsYlcelPLPVTiKOXYAfymo4FL3bn+UEuSHi+yK4Q148n3l/\nV/uJM3ePT1UPbgxCBX9Dz20zKGDRM2xR9fgXc3FaITU93wbH1LsJx1/bUm1Dzubz\nk+iCkMRETbTLKV/yI5+wJvm4tsutXs/tILroNX/S0mN47GckBcTU8uVvEDsN93He\nRG23Jo5luj4Vcz186KwMpg4CDHilDCPCDN72QEdroFuFCCUkdlou/TLZTAhAQ8Ea\nHyJbqZ2cTioqNUXVSdaKaaG6Ctl8PAUxv1jJINZTfBEjNlEbhO3eSHgV70PpYM1Y\nPG9e5UlKALxZIfUGXoSAfWE43b+BjyFfHKVrIHm43WZK1ljQa+/gQDK5nQ8yGJfu\nsKfneOZRCzZDIQuXeEwu\n=yXAq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/5e7cbb4a4606363bd78e939705a16c28853da71c","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDVlN2NiYjRhNDYwNjM2M2JkNzhlOTM5NzA1YTE2YzI4ODUzZGE3MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/fdec2d8bbdf0628fda3baf4025c8145a49156c83","sha":"fdec2d8bbdf0628fda3baf4025c8145a49156c83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/fdec2d8bbdf0628fda3baf4025c8145a49156c83"}],"sha":"5e7cbb4a4606363bd78e939705a16c28853da71c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5e7cbb4a4606363bd78e939705a16c28853da71c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/fdec2d8bbdf0628fda3baf4025c8145a49156c83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T16:17:50Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T16:17:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Migrate twenty-ui Radio and RadioGroup (#25715)\n\nRadio previously created a separate group for each option, while\nRadioGroup cloned its children. This migrates the family to one Base UI\ngroup with shared selection, keyboard navigation, and controlled or\nuncontrolled state. Radio now takes a required value, children for its\nlabel, and sm/md sizes; native props, refs, render composition, and\ncancelable change details pass through.\n\nMigrates CardPicker, settings cards, onboarding plan choices,\nspreadsheet sheet/header selection, and the renderer gallery. Removes\nthe legacy enums and Radio.Group alias. Card labels use their visible\ntitles and descriptions, and expanded editable content stays outside\noption labels.\n\nSpreadsheetImportSingleSelectTable owns the RadioGroup, radio column,\nand selection handlers. SpreadsheetImportTable handles shared grid\nstyling and configuration. The header step uses the dedicated selection\ncomponent with one selected row index and a change callback. The grid\nowns keyboard navigation across virtualized rows; the validation step\nkeeps its existing checkbox selection.\n\nValidation: 650 UI unit tests, 15 UI Chromium stories with axe/Argos,\nand 8 frontend Chromium/Argos integration stories pass. Table coverage\nincludes row/radio clicks, callback counts, keyboard navigation through\nall 60 virtualized rows, stable keys after reordering, and checkbox\nselection. Both UI typechecks, frontend and renderer typechecks,\nlint/formatting, library build, and bundle/package size checks pass.\nLight/dark catalogs and frontend snapshots were visually checked. Native\nform reset uses controlled state with onReset because Base UI 1.8 does\nnot reset uncontrolled group state.\n\nRenderer validation: both input-gallery play functions pass against the\nCI artifact. The exact known-failure expectations reflect the migrated\nfixtures: CardPicker renders in both runtimes, while unselected radios\nstill require sandbox DOM support for matches, and React radio groups\nrequire compareDocumentPosition.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25715?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"1d28392f2d67b1469ef04b6a08eaaa6879116dfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/1d28392f2d67b1469ef04b6a08eaaa6879116dfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/fdec2d8bbdf0628fda3baf4025c8145a49156c83","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d28392f2d67b1469ef04b6a08eaaa6879116dfc\nparent 187c1e8b76728a22f1cd704e9ab61dde5e984cd6\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1789057070 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789057070 +0000\n\nMigrate twenty-ui Radio and RadioGroup (#25715)\n\nRadio previously created a separate group for each option, while\nRadioGroup cloned its children. This migrates the family to one Base UI\ngroup with shared selection, keyboard navigation, and controlled or\nuncontrolled state. Radio now takes a required value, children for its\nlabel, and sm/md sizes; native props, refs, render composition, and\ncancelable change details pass through.\n\nMigrates CardPicker, settings cards, onboarding plan choices,\nspreadsheet sheet/header selection, and the renderer gallery. Removes\nthe legacy enums and Radio.Group alias. Card labels use their visible\ntitles and descriptions, and expanded editable content stays outside\noption labels.\n\nSpreadsheetImportSingleSelectTable owns the RadioGroup, radio column,\nand selection handlers. SpreadsheetImportTable handles shared grid\nstyling and configuration. The header step uses the dedicated selection\ncomponent with one selected row index and a change callback. The grid\nowns keyboard navigation across virtualized rows; the validation step\nkeeps its existing checkbox selection.\n\nValidation: 650 UI unit tests, 15 UI Chromium stories with axe/Argos,\nand 8 frontend Chromium/Argos integration stories pass. Table coverage\nincludes row/radio clicks, callback counts, keyboard navigation through\nall 60 virtualized rows, stable keys after reordering, and checkbox\nselection. Both UI typechecks, frontend and renderer typechecks,\nlint/formatting, library build, and bundle/package size checks pass.\nLight/dark catalogs and frontend snapshots were visually checked. Native\nform reset uses controlled state with onReset because Base UI 1.8 does\nnot reset uncontrolled group state.\n\nRenderer validation: both input-gallery play functions pass against the\nCI artifact. The exact known-failure expectations reflect the migrated\nfixtures: CardPicker renders in both runtimes, while unselected radios\nstill require sandbox DOM support for matches, and React radio groups\nrequire compareDocumentPosition.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25715?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqotg9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANSQQAC6EqT8wVRY+pMINi+g1IkQO\n+sPNRNbTs7hyzBUJYaOHAZTE8Mkx2HjfLuL1oDL4fZfs9VKKdxi3yp4QR8JT/mt8\nx06kXY5WRVqwxhWpgKCkiU/OHEC+B36eoFyv0lBfRP/ipcscaKaNKNrVjBrSipis\nbBxAJ384leNdR7nYdjRuLOh06fEElbmqRwe1BzyezBgqwalUReJbCG5qphV/ErEg\no0njS8PfpuCBk6GQqALh+mTBnGfXdbxJ5W5j/6JkAPNek+2A6Nr/dYPlUQdMIvFP\n3By2OzPZfOdRomDPBqELUNkhGpaXG1WquPpnc7nD6hlKpHMvY1AWQ9Ikm68ul6xZ\nuDHyz/Z2+1spRV9E6v6Z686QYNhbN2mQ0o63jwy/OJfdN/PoN4zD8YP02A4pTWiD\nkg4RM5pISXXRXAIQaTHUc43IgMIGjPGPtng2De/6YC8cryM2EzLMEizES3rWzXdw\naW+IeIR7bQPPcwEpYqyHRBYo2T/59zWbeq7YxRd67WvhF54YwBkN35iy8KjeZog3\nej48za9JuB3zCZjnAYlH3KMRE+ZeJASwqwe4lgBLbAYDraX7HDVL7pbocYhZnNaC\n9c54nveSpOwYr1cHKfVqrgZmr3vWyYAfb1lyJv/o0gfaja921SrKly2z0vp5+/Oe\nLDD6tnbbzJkkSrz5ycdq\n=a//S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/fdec2d8bbdf0628fda3baf4025c8145a49156c83","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGZkZWMyZDhiYmRmMDYyOGZkYTNiYWY0MDI1YzgxNDVhNDkxNTZjODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/187c1e8b76728a22f1cd704e9ab61dde5e984cd6","sha":"187c1e8b76728a22f1cd704e9ab61dde5e984cd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/187c1e8b76728a22f1cd704e9ab61dde5e984cd6"}],"sha":"fdec2d8bbdf0628fda3baf4025c8145a49156c83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/fdec2d8bbdf0628fda3baf4025c8145a49156c83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312387581?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/breken-ai","id":312387581,"login":"breken-ai","node_id":"U_kgDOEp6n_Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/breken-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/187c1e8b76728a22f1cd704e9ab61dde5e984cd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T16:10:15Z","email":"support@brekfuz.com","name":"breken"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T16:10:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(messaging): don''t delete messages still present in another folder''s delta sync (#25751)\n\nRelated: #25749 (and possibly the still-unresolved \"Synced but missing\"\nreports #16679, #13397, #13884, #16284)\n\n## Mechanism\n\nMicrosoft delta sync runs per folder. When a message is moved between\nfolders, the old folder''s delta returns `@removed` for the message''s\nimmutable Graph ID while the new folder''s delta returns that same ID as\npresent. `MessagingMessageListFetchService.processMessageListFetch`\nflattens all folders'' present IDs into `messageExternalIds` and all\nfolders'' deletion IDs into `messageExternalIdsToDelete`, then passes the\ndeletion union unchanged to\n`deleteMessagesChannelMessageAssociationsAndRelatedOrphans` - which\ndeletes the association and hard-deletes the now-orphaned `message` row,\neven though another folder returned that same message as present in the\nsame sync cycle.\n\nThat produces exactly the reported shape: the message imports\nsuccessfully (message + participants + `messageLinked` timelineActivity\nall created), then disappears on a later sync with no user-visible\nerror, leaving orphaned `timelineActivity` rows and contact timestamps\nbehind. Any folder move (archive, mailbox rules, conversation-history\nmoves) can trigger it, and how often depends on each user''s mailbox\nbehavior - which fits the \"some messages, not others\" distribution.\n\nThis is a concrete, reproducible mechanism consistent with the data in\n#25749; we did not verify each of the 56 reported orphans individually.\n\n## Fix\n\nNew util `filterMessageExternalIdsToDelete`: subtracts the sync cycle''s\npresent-ID set from the combined deletion candidates, and dedupes\ndeletion events returned by multiple folders. A message any folder still\nreports as present is never sent to the orphan cleaner in that cycle.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew spec `filter-message-external-ids-to-delete.util.spec.ts`:\n- keeps a message when one folder removes it while another still returns\nit (the moved-message case)\n- deduplicates deletion events returned by multiple folders\n\nRed/green verified against the actual logic (pre-fix the deletion set\nretains `moved-message`; post-fix it contains only `deleted-message`).\nFull TS suite not run (no local install); the change is a pure exported\nhelper plus a call-site swap, and the spec exercises both paths.\n\n> Built by breken, your AI support engineer - breken.ai - this one''s on\nus.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25751?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"03f7d16e7594114849caf1bb9b20528d96487331","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/03f7d16e7594114849caf1bb9b20528d96487331"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/187c1e8b76728a22f1cd704e9ab61dde5e984cd6","verification":{"payload":"tree 03f7d16e7594114849caf1bb9b20528d96487331\nparent feda5ea96035f8dda75458a9845111153d77d97d\nauthor breken <support@brekfuz.com> 1789056615 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789056615 +0000\n\nfix(messaging): don''t delete messages still present in another folder''s delta sync (#25751)\n\nRelated: #25749 (and possibly the still-unresolved \"Synced but missing\"\nreports #16679, #13397, #13884, #16284)\n\n## Mechanism\n\nMicrosoft delta sync runs per folder. When a message is moved between\nfolders, the old folder''s delta returns `@removed` for the message''s\nimmutable Graph ID while the new folder''s delta returns that same ID as\npresent. `MessagingMessageListFetchService.processMessageListFetch`\nflattens all folders'' present IDs into `messageExternalIds` and all\nfolders'' deletion IDs into `messageExternalIdsToDelete`, then passes the\ndeletion union unchanged to\n`deleteMessagesChannelMessageAssociationsAndRelatedOrphans` - which\ndeletes the association and hard-deletes the now-orphaned `message` row,\neven though another folder returned that same message as present in the\nsame sync cycle.\n\nThat produces exactly the reported shape: the message imports\nsuccessfully (message + participants + `messageLinked` timelineActivity\nall created), then disappears on a later sync with no user-visible\nerror, leaving orphaned `timelineActivity` rows and contact timestamps\nbehind. Any folder move (archive, mailbox rules, conversation-history\nmoves) can trigger it, and how often depends on each user''s mailbox\nbehavior - which fits the \"some messages, not others\" distribution.\n\nThis is a concrete, reproducible mechanism consistent with the data in\n#25749; we did not verify each of the 56 reported orphans individually.\n\n## Fix\n\nNew util `filterMessageExternalIdsToDelete`: subtracts the sync cycle''s\npresent-ID set from the combined deletion candidates, and dedupes\ndeletion events returned by multiple folders. A message any folder still\nreports as present is never sent to the orphan cleaner in that cycle.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew spec `filter-message-external-ids-to-delete.util.spec.ts`:\n- keeps a message when one folder removes it while another still returns\nit (the moved-message case)\n- deduplicates deletion events returned by multiple folders\n\nRed/green verified against the actual logic (pre-fix the deletion set\nretains `moved-message`; post-fix it contains only `deleted-message`).\nFull TS suite not run (no local install); the change is a pure exported\nhelper plus a call-site swap, and the spec exercises both paths.\n\n> Built by breken, your AI support engineer - breken.ai - this one''s on\nus.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25751?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqotZ3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgZ0QACDp+ewUYBmRqP62m59Iwz22\nH+Yggw8bCDlfL0GlgUJ3sy4S3mbPfhY5pK3i/pLycVu6e9HRRe9gE+uFAarTm2bM\ndzypqLHvuMohmYfId/EJtTkQ9RQofl16CW5upEFRDaeeH/m4j5p8TtHUrZ+kf/1/\njeUOnvZwMiAC4y2MZJTfIFLWO2UJnLWy06WtOjGJXrqnXkp4PZxe0ghY3SsxZqxw\n9QIANc+T6G2lg/ZnEX/hv7j1A8TeRVxhtOVXeMaVc5l5pkK40Xkd1I9eXbc+lvjP\nwNOG1CvBJuaOXEer+qoUb9vzZYj+R1/vfwrriHWYvqrYy8fP++rDXP0YA4vGTZo9\nyiCsqtPnnRVPB1ayhquor3Wt2p+OP0NZA/AUWMxCDzspmVfJC8opaS+SWw4fPvVL\nl8VnWHWPUcAecMYl9pStRasAgeERvsmrR8k0qd//p0MiLq3qi/M6P4JRnj5qe5rI\nppug3lrJt8zQ54j5wIW/pYf25m5fcauv8jiKs6/ds4LmIspQFuY7fK3/LCKRQg0y\nngP91zitvezN33+vLOxovn9FqkVIYc1Kt2bEefMwNPMtCW/cDIhgaXuXhzw35SL+\n5hbp7CQIwUMPz45/hUW/+Z6H1T3CvIRL2YkxNQ3k6ZDLhuyfPXa1Wv9xJy+eA9Ef\ny1aYtuhM17uQbb1usa7g\n=ilW2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/187c1e8b76728a22f1cd704e9ab61dde5e984cd6","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDE4N2MxZThiNzY3MjhhMjJmMWNkNzA0ZTlhYjYxZGRlNWU5ODRjZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/feda5ea96035f8dda75458a9845111153d77d97d","sha":"feda5ea96035f8dda75458a9845111153d77d97d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/feda5ea96035f8dda75458a9845111153d77d97d"}],"sha":"187c1e8b76728a22f1cd704e9ab61dde5e984cd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/187c1e8b76728a22f1cd704e9ab61dde5e984cd6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81605929?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulrahmancodes","id":81605929,"login":"abdulrahmancodes","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNjA1OTI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/feda5ea96035f8dda75458a9845111153d77d97d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:31:45Z","email":"81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdul Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:31:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Acknowledge Slack file attachments in the assistant (#25695)\n\n## Problem\n\nThree related failures around files shared with the Slack assistant:\n\n1. **A DM with a file and a caption was dropped silently.**\n`parseSlackAssistantRequest` rejected every message carrying a subtype,\nand Slack still stamps user uploads with `file_share` ([their\nchangelog](https://api.slack.com/changelog/2018-05-file-threads-soon-tread):\nthe subtype is discontinued but \"we will continue sending it via the\nEvents API until further notice\"; the Node SDK''s `FileShareMessageEvent`\ntypes `subtype` as a required `\"file_share\"`). So \"what do you make of\nthis?\" plus a PDF got no reply at all.\n2. **A mention with an attachment and no caption got the generic\ngreeting.** Empty normalised text produced an `emptyRequest`, answered\nwith \"Hi! Ask me anything about your CRM\".\n3. **Files shared earlier in a thread were invisible.**\n`SlackThreadMessage` had no `files` field, and\n`buildSlackConversationMessages` dropped any message without text, so a\nfile-only message never reached the replayed history.\n\n## Scope of the fix\n\nThe app has no `files:read` scope, so it cannot open a file, and adding\nthe scope would force every existing installer to reauthorise. File\n*metadata* rides along in the message payload, so naming a file costs no\nnew scope. This change therefore acknowledges attachments rather than\nreading them, and is careful never to imply the assistant read something\nit cannot read.\n\n- `SlackThreadMessage.files` and `SlackInboundEvent.files`, backed by a\nnew `SlackMessageFile` type.\n- `file_share` allowlisted in the subtype gate. Every other subtype is\nstill rejected, bot uploads are still filtered by `bot_id`, and the\nexisting channel + timestamp dedupe prevents double-handling against the\n`app_mention` event for the same upload.\n- File-only messages stay in the replayed history as `<@U123>: [shared a\nfile: proposal.pdf]`; a caption plus a file appends the same bracket on\nits own line.\n- The greeting is replaced when the mention carries an attachment:\n\"Thanks for the file: `proposal.pdf`. I can see its name but I can''t\nopen it, so tell me what you''d like done and I''ll take it from there…\".\n- The agent prompt gains a section whenever files appear in the request\nor the history: they \"reach you as names only… never claim to have read\none and never guess what is inside\".\n\n`requestText` is deliberately untouched. `resolveSlackRunAsForRequest`\ncompares the stored `requestText` against the live Slack message text\nbefore running with the member''s own permissions; synthesising a file\ndescription into it would have silently downgraded every file-carrying\nrequest to the app''s own role.\n\nSlack Connect hands back stub file objects (`file_access:\n\"check_file_info\"`) with no usable name, so name resolution falls back\nto `title` and then to a placeholder rather than printing `undefined`.\n\n## Treating a file name as untrusted input\n\nA file name is text a member or a bot chooses, and it ends up in two\nplaces that deserve care. Review feedback on this PR drove the\nfollowing, and it is the part most worth a careful read:\n\n- **In the agent prompt**, names sit in their own delimited block,\nquoted one per line, introduced as untrusted text from Slack members and\nbots that never authorises an action. Names are flattened to a single\nline and capped at 100 characters, so one cannot forge a section break\nor pad out the prompt.\n- **In the Slack reply**, each name goes in a code span after backticks\nand angle brackets are stripped, so a name cannot re-emit a channel\nmention or a disguised link as bot-authored markup. This holds on the\nmrkdwn fallback path too.\n- **In replayed history**, bracket characters are stripped so a name\ncannot close the `[shared a file: …]` frame the app generates.\n\nThe file list and the replayed history are built from one shared\n`selectSlackConversationMessages` window, so the agent is never told\nabout a file it has no message for. Bot-shared files are deliberately\nincluded: a bot name is more untrusted than a member''s, not less, and\nexcluding them would leave a file visible in history with nothing\nmarking it unreadable.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew coverage for a file with a caption, a file without a caption, a file\nin thread history, the unnamed-file fallback, `file_share` DMs with and\nwithout a caption, the window trimming, and the three untrusted-name\npaths above. Two integration tests: a file-only mention names the\nattachment, and a `file_share` DM gets queued.\n\nLocally, `yarn lint`, `yarn typecheck` and `yarn test:unit` (655 tests)\npass. The integration suite cannot run locally because its global setup\nrejects the checked-in dev API key; CI spawns a server and mints its\nown, and `slack (local)` and `slack (dockerhub-latest)` are both green,\nso the new integration tests do execute there.","tree":{"sha":"ab8b7b4b9f2f8f8a152a75aecac7ed8d7bb474c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/ab8b7b4b9f2f8f8a152a75aecac7ed8d7bb474c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/feda5ea96035f8dda75458a9845111153d77d97d","verification":{"payload":"tree ab8b7b4b9f2f8f8a152a75aecac7ed8d7bb474c5\nparent e50205734704b1aa6a00c6bf6448849f001b7216\nauthor Abdul Rahman <81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1789054305 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789054305 +0000\n\nAcknowledge Slack file attachments in the assistant (#25695)\n\n## Problem\n\nThree related failures around files shared with the Slack assistant:\n\n1. **A DM with a file and a caption was dropped silently.**\n`parseSlackAssistantRequest` rejected every message carrying a subtype,\nand Slack still stamps user uploads with `file_share` ([their\nchangelog](https://api.slack.com/changelog/2018-05-file-threads-soon-tread):\nthe subtype is discontinued but \"we will continue sending it via the\nEvents API until further notice\"; the Node SDK''s `FileShareMessageEvent`\ntypes `subtype` as a required `\"file_share\"`). So \"what do you make of\nthis?\" plus a PDF got no reply at all.\n2. **A mention with an attachment and no caption got the generic\ngreeting.** Empty normalised text produced an `emptyRequest`, answered\nwith \"Hi! Ask me anything about your CRM\".\n3. **Files shared earlier in a thread were invisible.**\n`SlackThreadMessage` had no `files` field, and\n`buildSlackConversationMessages` dropped any message without text, so a\nfile-only message never reached the replayed history.\n\n## Scope of the fix\n\nThe app has no `files:read` scope, so it cannot open a file, and adding\nthe scope would force every existing installer to reauthorise. File\n*metadata* rides along in the message payload, so naming a file costs no\nnew scope. This change therefore acknowledges attachments rather than\nreading them, and is careful never to imply the assistant read something\nit cannot read.\n\n- `SlackThreadMessage.files` and `SlackInboundEvent.files`, backed by a\nnew `SlackMessageFile` type.\n- `file_share` allowlisted in the subtype gate. Every other subtype is\nstill rejected, bot uploads are still filtered by `bot_id`, and the\nexisting channel + timestamp dedupe prevents double-handling against the\n`app_mention` event for the same upload.\n- File-only messages stay in the replayed history as `<@U123>: [shared a\nfile: proposal.pdf]`; a caption plus a file appends the same bracket on\nits own line.\n- The greeting is replaced when the mention carries an attachment:\n\"Thanks for the file: `proposal.pdf`. I can see its name but I can''t\nopen it, so tell me what you''d like done and I''ll take it from there…\".\n- The agent prompt gains a section whenever files appear in the request\nor the history: they \"reach you as names only… never claim to have read\none and never guess what is inside\".\n\n`requestText` is deliberately untouched. `resolveSlackRunAsForRequest`\ncompares the stored `requestText` against the live Slack message text\nbefore running with the member''s own permissions; synthesising a file\ndescription into it would have silently downgraded every file-carrying\nrequest to the app''s own role.\n\nSlack Connect hands back stub file objects (`file_access:\n\"check_file_info\"`) with no usable name, so name resolution falls back\nto `title` and then to a placeholder rather than printing `undefined`.\n\n## Treating a file name as untrusted input\n\nA file name is text a member or a bot chooses, and it ends up in two\nplaces that deserve care. Review feedback on this PR drove the\nfollowing, and it is the part most worth a careful read:\n\n- **In the agent prompt**, names sit in their own delimited block,\nquoted one per line, introduced as untrusted text from Slack members and\nbots that never authorises an action. Names are flattened to a single\nline and capped at 100 characters, so one cannot forge a section break\nor pad out the prompt.\n- **In the Slack reply**, each name goes in a code span after backticks\nand angle brackets are stripped, so a name cannot re-emit a channel\nmention or a disguised link as bot-authored markup. This holds on the\nmrkdwn fallback path too.\n- **In replayed history**, bracket characters are stripped so a name\ncannot close the `[shared a file: …]` frame the app generates.\n\nThe file list and the replayed history are built from one shared\n`selectSlackConversationMessages` window, so the agent is never told\nabout a file it has no message for. Bot-shared files are deliberately\nincluded: a bot name is more untrusted than a member''s, not less, and\nexcluding them would leave a file visible in history with nothing\nmarking it unreadable.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew coverage for a file with a caption, a file without a caption, a file\nin thread history, the unnamed-file fallback, `file_share` DMs with and\nwithout a caption, the window trimming, and the three untrusted-name\npaths above. Two integration tests: a file-only mention names the\nattachment, and a `file_share` DM gets queued.\n\nLocally, `yarn lint`, `yarn typecheck` and `yarn test:unit` (655 tests)\npass. The integration suite cannot run locally because its global setup\nrejects the checked-in dev API key; CI spawns a server and mints its\nown, and `slack (local)` and `slack (dockerhub-latest)` are both green,\nso the new integration tests do execute there.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqos1xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALrUQAGpzL6YnvuR0g6cm5Y00rgfG\npeXVZ6wSPVzY4bG0NRArdF0WQC5WQsAF3Nc1x+aIa/eRmzey7YdxqGLbQQDHvME5\nKiIXkWz/y0nY4SfrCzkqf+dRIf2UKMkgjBXCmbUuxYONh6mWisqiQTHw1IGFSFa1\nOgQ9VdgN0XDX2OFN15O52zD/5hSThGRxJ3/6F0obsRYbw0iCRMqioNkllFmCAYah\nNnMl95+Cr52Qklrps6hT3QBoPjwRMfq4eD9TaK/fjnRqGDcv7hhbnB36AJQljCB/\nxhfDbkhDR6V7axAe9Pxxs8qObFL/fg4cXnzs11dBnlxyWOLNLmCYKouvjZTDdFN3\nOHJClczY4u7brg/SJqyJ0Lz5af5xAs2FiilKvd6+4lyhDhSH5NTrlH4vLzfzhh/A\nEVuppDfXFCcqnXgoGxPoFscsDo6+YHUSl1gkRCIXoqNiZUTR5WSf959ADfjBpcJ6\n3PJuGxP0CCwtra9nOcusKbVKeYk8fSkuzNVwrgIoszzMCGYiYE1FG8Qq8f3dugoh\nQbhGkp60cm3HS4ZAhQF4R+ukbphvUj0hth0NdBUPD8uLwaGEsG3Svb4bDUrLZT9k\nW5qMtcG/IFiW2/cbu2JpK8oRuXbTPbC+H5UrOTjlJzhuFjdbCuSnrEJ8JKfG/qUM\nKkcrh9kvRLGpQRGx7zPK\n=VD7n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/feda5ea96035f8dda75458a9845111153d77d97d","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGZlZGE1ZWE5NjAzNWY4ZGRhNzU0NThhOTg0NTExMTE1M2Q3N2Q5N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/e50205734704b1aa6a00c6bf6448849f001b7216","sha":"e50205734704b1aa6a00c6bf6448849f001b7216","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/e50205734704b1aa6a00c6bf6448849f001b7216"}],"sha":"feda5ea96035f8dda75458a9845111153d77d97d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/feda5ea96035f8dda75458a9845111153d77d97d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62795688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/neo773","id":62795688,"login":"neo773","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzk1Njg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/e50205734704b1aa6a00c6bf6448849f001b7216/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:19:20Z","email":"62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com","name":"neo773"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:19:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Extract email body text without building a DOM (#25422)\n\nRewrites inbound email body extraction. It built a jsdom document and\nran DOMPurify plus planer over it, which cost ~60ms of blocking CPU per\nmessage and retained memory that no GC reclaimed. Nothing downstream\nneeded a DOM: `html-to-text` already parses with htmlparser2, and\n`sanitize-html` allowlists over the same parser.\n\nFixes #25315.\n\n## Performance\n\nMeasured on 631 real production messages (496 over Gmail and Graph\nacross 14 workspaces, 135 over IMAP across 6 accounts on 5 hosting\nproviders).\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Per message | 60.5 ms | **~2 ms** |\n| Google corpus | — | **65.6x** |\n| Microsoft corpus | — | **49.1x** |\n| Memory retained per message | ~0.8 MB, never released | **0** |\n| Retained after 600 messages | 450 MB | **0 MB** |\n| Full HTML parses per message | 3, plus one reparse per element | **2,\nboth streaming** |\n| Reply parser invocations | every message | **1 of 4 branches** |\n\nThe dominant cost was not jsdom existing. planer sets `innerHTML` on\nevery element twice, and each write reparses that subtree; that\nmachinery only existed so it could hand back HTML, and we only ever\nwanted text. The leak was jsdom''s `createNodeIterator`, which DOMPurify\ncalls on every sanitize.\n\n## Call stack\n\n```\nBEFORE                                          AFTER\n\nextractMessageBodyText                          extractMessageTextWithoutQuotedHistory\n├─ new JSDOM('''')                                ├─ readBodyAsText\n├─ createDOMPurify(window)                      │  └─ convertHtmlToText\n├─ purify.sanitize                              │     ├─ sanitizeHtml          htmlparser2\n│  ├─ createHTMLDocument      parse #1          │     ├─ renderHtmlWithQuoteMarkers\n│  └─ createNodeIterator      leaks 0.8 MB      │     └─ removeQuotedMarkup\n├─ planer.extractFromHtml                       ├─ stripQuotedHistory\n│  ├─ createEmailDocument     parse #2          │  ├─ removeSpaceStuffing\n│  ├─ createEmailDocument     parse #3          │  ├─ toAnalysableLines\n│  ├─ cutBlockQuote           XPath             │  ├─ describeCaretQuoting\n│  ├─ cutFromBlock            XPath             │  ├─ findQuoteHeaderIndex\n│  ├─ addCheckpoints          innerHTML/element │  └─ removeCaretQuotedFragments\n│  ├─ replaceBreakTags        reserialise       │     └─ email-reply-parser\n│  └─ deleteQuotationTags     innerHTML/element ├─ sanitizeString\n├─ convert                                      └─ normalizeMessageText\n├─ email-reply-parser         always\n├─ sanitizeString\n└─ normalizeMessageText\n```\n\n## Behaviour\n\n`extractMessageBodyText` returned the body minus the quoted history, so\nit is renamed to say that.\n\nQuote detection covers 20 languages, including Chinese, Japanese, Korean\nand Russian. CJK ends an attribution with a fullwidth colon, which no\nprevious pattern could match. Danish `Fra:/Sendt:` is the case reported\nin #25315.\n\nThree defects surfaced against real mail and are fixed here:\n`gmail_quote` and `OLK_SRC_BODY_SECTION` were cut to end of message,\ndestroying a signature or legal disclaimer written after the quote; RFC\n3676 space stuffed quoting was never stripped; and `cid:` image\nreferences pasted into the text alternative were left in the body.\n\n## Files\n\n```\npackages/twenty-server/src/modules/messaging/message-import-manager/\n├── types/\n│   ├── caret-quoting.type.ts                       A\n│   └── message-body.type.ts                        A\n├── utils/\n│   ├── extract-message-text-without-quoted-history.util.ts   A  entry point\n│   ├── read-body-as-text.util.ts                   A  text part, else html\n│   │\n│   ├── convert-html-to-text.util.ts                A  sanitize, render, cut\n│   ├── message-html-sanitize-options.constant.ts   A\n│   ├── render-html-with-quote-markers.util.ts      A\n│   ├── remove-quoted-markup.util.ts                A\n│   ├── quote-markers.constant.ts                   A\n│   ├── html-quote-selectors.constant.ts            A\n│   │\n│   ├── strip-quoted-history.util.ts                A  the four branches\n│   ├── to-analysable-lines.util.ts                 A\n│   ├── describe-caret-quoting.util.ts              A\n│   ├── find-quote-header-index.util.ts             A\n│   ├── remove-space-stuffing.util.ts               A\n│   ├── remove-caret-quoted-fragments.util.ts       R  was extract-text-without-reply-quotations\n│   ├── quote-header-patterns.constant.ts           A  20 languages\n│   │\n│   ├── create-html-to-text-converter.util.ts       D\n│   └── extract-message-body-text.util.ts           D\n└── drivers/\n    ├── gmail/utils/parse-and-format-gmail-message.util.ts     M\n    ├── imap/services/imap-get-messages.service.ts             M\n    └── microsoft/services/microsoft-get-messages.service.ts   M\n\npackages/twenty-server/@types/planer.d.ts                      D\npackages/twenty-server/package.json                            M  planer out, sanitize-html in\n.yarn/patches/email-reply-parser-npm-2.3.5-...patch            A\n```\n\n`isQuoteHeader` reversed each line once per regex, 31 times per line.\nThe patch hoists the reverse out of the loop, 3.4x on that pass with\nidentical output.\n\n`sanitize-html` is pinned to 2.17.5, the newest release resolving\nhtmlparser2 within major 10. 2.17.6 moved to htmlparser2 12, which is\nESM only.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25422?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"7f07e760c9391bec6f482f612d9a602b5a3e253a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/7f07e760c9391bec6f482f612d9a602b5a3e253a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/e50205734704b1aa6a00c6bf6448849f001b7216","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f07e760c9391bec6f482f612d9a602b5a3e253a\nparent 6e16c71c64f11d164ee6660d3a23eccd4c5705c9\nauthor neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com> 1789053560 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789053560 +0000\n\nExtract email body text without building a DOM (#25422)\n\nRewrites inbound email body extraction. It built a jsdom document and\nran DOMPurify plus planer over it, which cost ~60ms of blocking CPU per\nmessage and retained memory that no GC reclaimed. Nothing downstream\nneeded a DOM: `html-to-text` already parses with htmlparser2, and\n`sanitize-html` allowlists over the same parser.\n\nFixes #25315.\n\n## Performance\n\nMeasured on 631 real production messages (496 over Gmail and Graph\nacross 14 workspaces, 135 over IMAP across 6 accounts on 5 hosting\nproviders).\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Per message | 60.5 ms | **~2 ms** |\n| Google corpus | — | **65.6x** |\n| Microsoft corpus | — | **49.1x** |\n| Memory retained per message | ~0.8 MB, never released | **0** |\n| Retained after 600 messages | 450 MB | **0 MB** |\n| Full HTML parses per message | 3, plus one reparse per element | **2,\nboth streaming** |\n| Reply parser invocations | every message | **1 of 4 branches** |\n\nThe dominant cost was not jsdom existing. planer sets `innerHTML` on\nevery element twice, and each write reparses that subtree; that\nmachinery only existed so it could hand back HTML, and we only ever\nwanted text. The leak was jsdom''s `createNodeIterator`, which DOMPurify\ncalls on every sanitize.\n\n## Call stack\n\n```\nBEFORE                                          AFTER\n\nextractMessageBodyText                          extractMessageTextWithoutQuotedHistory\n├─ new JSDOM('''')                                ├─ readBodyAsText\n├─ createDOMPurify(window)                      │  └─ convertHtmlToText\n├─ purify.sanitize                              │     ├─ sanitizeHtml          htmlparser2\n│  ├─ createHTMLDocument      parse #1          │     ├─ renderHtmlWithQuoteMarkers\n│  └─ createNodeIterator      leaks 0.8 MB      │     └─ removeQuotedMarkup\n├─ planer.extractFromHtml                       ├─ stripQuotedHistory\n│  ├─ createEmailDocument     parse #2          │  ├─ removeSpaceStuffing\n│  ├─ createEmailDocument     parse #3          │  ├─ toAnalysableLines\n│  ├─ cutBlockQuote           XPath             │  ├─ describeCaretQuoting\n│  ├─ cutFromBlock            XPath             │  ├─ findQuoteHeaderIndex\n│  ├─ addCheckpoints          innerHTML/element │  └─ removeCaretQuotedFragments\n│  ├─ replaceBreakTags        reserialise       │     └─ email-reply-parser\n│  └─ deleteQuotationTags     innerHTML/element ├─ sanitizeString\n├─ convert                                      └─ normalizeMessageText\n├─ email-reply-parser         always\n├─ sanitizeString\n└─ normalizeMessageText\n```\n\n## Behaviour\n\n`extractMessageBodyText` returned the body minus the quoted history, so\nit is renamed to say that.\n\nQuote detection covers 20 languages, including Chinese, Japanese, Korean\nand Russian. CJK ends an attribution with a fullwidth colon, which no\nprevious pattern could match. Danish `Fra:/Sendt:` is the case reported\nin #25315.\n\nThree defects surfaced against real mail and are fixed here:\n`gmail_quote` and `OLK_SRC_BODY_SECTION` were cut to end of message,\ndestroying a signature or legal disclaimer written after the quote; RFC\n3676 space stuffed quoting was never stripped; and `cid:` image\nreferences pasted into the text alternative were left in the body.\n\n## Files\n\n```\npackages/twenty-server/src/modules/messaging/message-import-manager/\n├── types/\n│   ├── caret-quoting.type.ts                       A\n│   └── message-body.type.ts                        A\n├── utils/\n│   ├── extract-message-text-without-quoted-history.util.ts   A  entry point\n│   ├── read-body-as-text.util.ts                   A  text part, else html\n│   │\n│   ├── convert-html-to-text.util.ts                A  sanitize, render, cut\n│   ├── message-html-sanitize-options.constant.ts   A\n│   ├── render-html-with-quote-markers.util.ts      A\n│   ├── remove-quoted-markup.util.ts                A\n│   ├── quote-markers.constant.ts                   A\n│   ├── html-quote-selectors.constant.ts            A\n│   │\n│   ├── strip-quoted-history.util.ts                A  the four branches\n│   ├── to-analysable-lines.util.ts                 A\n│   ├── describe-caret-quoting.util.ts              A\n│   ├── find-quote-header-index.util.ts             A\n│   ├── remove-space-stuffing.util.ts               A\n│   ├── remove-caret-quoted-fragments.util.ts       R  was extract-text-without-reply-quotations\n│   ├── quote-header-patterns.constant.ts           A  20 languages\n│   │\n│   ├── create-html-to-text-converter.util.ts       D\n│   └── extract-message-body-text.util.ts           D\n└── drivers/\n    ├── gmail/utils/parse-and-format-gmail-message.util.ts     M\n    ├── imap/services/imap-get-messages.service.ts             M\n    └── microsoft/services/microsoft-get-messages.service.ts   M\n\npackages/twenty-server/@types/planer.d.ts                      D\npackages/twenty-server/package.json                            M  planer out, sanitize-html in\n.yarn/patches/email-reply-parser-npm-2.3.5-...patch            A\n```\n\n`isQuoteHeader` reversed each line once per regex, 31 times per line.\nThe patch hoists the reverse out of the loop, 3.4x on that pass with\nidentical output.\n\n`sanitize-html` is pinned to 2.17.5, the newest release resolving\nhtmlparser2 within major 10. 2.17.6 moved to htmlparser2 12, which is\nESM only.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25422?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.sv