://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/e50205734704b1aa6a00c6bf6448849f001b7216","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGU1MDIwNTczNDcwNGIxYWE2YTAwYzZiZjY0NDg4NDlmMDAxYjcyMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/6e16c71c64f11d164ee6660d3a23eccd4c5705c9","sha":"6e16c71c64f11d164ee6660d3a23eccd4c5705c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/6e16c71c64f11d164ee6660d3a23eccd4c5705c9"}],"sha":"e50205734704b1aa6a00c6bf6448849f001b7216","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/e50205734704b1aa6a00c6bf6448849f001b7216"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/6e16c71c64f11d164ee6660d3a23eccd4c5705c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:04:19Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:04:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: sync AI model catalog (#25745)\n\nAutomated daily sync of the AI model catalog.\n\n- Model identity, pricing, context windows and availability come from\n[models.dev](https://models.dev).\n- Intelligence, speed and cost per task come from [Artificial\nAnalysis](https://artificialanalysis.ai/),\n  which requires `ARTIFICIAL_ANALYSIS_API_KEY`.\n\nNew models meeting inclusion criteria (tool calling, pricing data,\ncontext limits) are added\nautomatically. Benchmark data is best-effort: a model Artificial\nAnalysis has not rated keeps\nevery other field and simply carries no `benchmark` entry.\n\n**Please review before merging** and check the coverage summary below\nfor models that silently\nstopped matching.\n\n### Benchmark coverage\n\n- General-purpose models with an intelligence index: **51/80** (64%)\n- Declared effort variants with an index measured at their own effort:\n**69/113** (61%)\n- General-purpose models with a cost per task: **24/80** (30%)\n- Specialized models excluded from the denominator: 10\n\n<details><summary>General-purpose models with no matched intelligence\nindex</summary>\n\n- openai/gpt-5-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.2-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.3-codex-spark\n- openai/gpt-5.5-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.6\n- openai/gpt-5.4-pro\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\n- anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\n- anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5\n- google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview-customtools\n- mistral/mistral-small-2506\n- mistral/open-mixtral-8x22b\n- mistral/open-mixtral-8x7b\n- mistral/open-mistral-7b\n- mistral/mistral-medium-latest\n- mistral/mistral-medium-2604\n- mistral/mistral-large-2512\n- mistral/ministral-8b-latest\n- mistral/mistral-nemo\n- mistral/mistral-small-latest\n- mistral/mistral-large-latest\n- mistral/mistral-large-2411\n- mistral/mistral-small-2603\n- mistral/mistral-medium-2505\n- mistral/ministral-3b-latest\n- mistral/mistral-medium-2508\n- xai/grok-4.20-0309-reasoning\n- xai/grok-build-0.1\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Effort variants with no reading at their own\neffort</summary>\n\n- openai/gpt-6-astra@minimal\n- openai/gpt-5.4@medium\n- openai/gpt-5.4@high\n- openai/gpt-5.5@max\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5@high\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-6@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-6@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-7@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-7@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-7@xhigh\n- anthropic/claude-fable-5@low\n- anthropic/claude-fable-5@medium\n- anthropic/claude-fable-5@high\n- anthropic/claude-fable-5@xhigh\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-8@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-8@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-8@high\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-8@xhigh\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-5@xhigh\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101@high\n- google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview@low\n- google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview@medium\n- google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview@high\n- google/gemini-3.6-flash@minimal\n- google/gemini-3.6-flash@low\n- google/gemini-3.6-flash@medium\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash@low\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite@minimal\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite@low\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite@medium\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite@high\n- google/gemini-3-flash-preview@minimal\n- google/gemini-3-flash-preview@low\n- google/gemini-3-flash-preview@medium\n- google/gemini-3-flash-preview@high\n- mistral/mistral-small-latest@none\n- mistral/mistral-small-latest@high\n- xai/grok-4.5@low\n- xai/grok-4.5@medium\n\n</details>\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25745?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\nCo-authored-by: FelixMalfait <6399865+FelixMalfait@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdea90a85608514f1a0353e8f791fd6d7962f91c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/bdea90a85608514f1a0353e8f791fd6d7962f91c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/6e16c71c64f11d164ee6660d3a23eccd4c5705c9","verification":{"payload":"tree bdea90a85608514f1a0353e8f791fd6d7962f91c\nparent 99a0e1c39f4f35f2139456ce3e8aa3d5b7159080\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789052659 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789052659 +0200\n\nchore: sync AI model catalog (#25745)\n\nAutomated daily sync of the AI model catalog.\n\n- Model identity, pricing, context windows and availability come from\n[models.dev](https://models.dev).\n- Intelligence, speed and cost per task come from [Artificial\nAnalysis](https://artificialanalysis.ai/),\n  which requires `ARTIFICIAL_ANALYSIS_API_KEY`.\n\nNew models meeting inclusion criteria (tool calling, pricing data,\ncontext limits) are added\nautomatically. Benchmark data is best-effort: a model Artificial\nAnalysis has not rated keeps\nevery other field and simply carries no `benchmark` entry.\n\n**Please review before merging** and check the coverage summary below\nfor models that silently\nstopped matching.\n\n### Benchmark coverage\n\n- General-purpose models with an intelligence index: **51/80** (64%)\n- Declared effort variants with an index measured at their own effort:\n**69/113** (61%)\n- General-purpose models with a cost per task: **24/80** (30%)\n- Specialized models excluded from the denominator: 10\n\n<details><summary>General-purpose models with no matched intelligence\nindex</summary>\n\n- openai/gpt-5-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.2-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.3-codex-spark\n- openai/gpt-5.5-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.6\n- openai/gpt-5.4-pro\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\n- anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\n- anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5\n- google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview-customtools\n- mistral/mistral-small-2506\n- mistral/open-mixtral-8x22b\n- mistral/open-mixtral-8x7b\n- mistral/open-mistral-7b\n- mistral/mistral-medium-latest\n- mistral/mistral-medium-2604\n- mistral/mistral-large-2512\n- mistral/ministral-8b-latest\n- mistral/mistral-nemo\n- mistral/mistral-small-latest\n- mistral/mistral-large-latest\n- mistral/mistral-large-2411\n- mistral/mistral-small-2603\n- mistral/mistral-medium-2505\n- mistral/ministral-3b-latest\n- mistral/mistral-medium-2508\n- xai/grok-4.20-0309-reasoning\n- xai/grok-build-0.1\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Effort variants with no reading at their own\neffort</summary>\n\n- openai/gpt-6-astra@minimal\n- openai/gpt-5.4@medium\n- openai/gpt-5.4@high\n- openai/gpt-5.5@max\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5@high\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-6@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-6@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-7@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-7@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-7@xhigh\n- anthropic/claude-fable-5@low\n- anthropic/claude-fable-5@medium\n- anthropic/claude-fable-5@high\n- anthropic/claude-fable-5@xhigh\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-8@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-8@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-8@high\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-8@xhigh\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-5@xhigh\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101@low\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101@medium\n- anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101@high\n- google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview@low\n- google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview@medium\n- google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview@high\n- google/gemini-3.6-flash@minimal\n- google/gemini-3.6-flash@low\n- google/gemini-3.6-flash@medium\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash@low\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite@minimal\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite@low\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite@medium\n- google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite@high\n- google/gemini-3-flash-preview@minimal\n- google/gemini-3-flash-preview@low\n- google/gemini-3-flash-preview@medium\n- google/gemini-3-flash-preview@high\n- mistral/mistral-small-latest@none\n- mistral/mistral-small-latest@high\n- xai/grok-4.5@low\n- xai/grok-4.5@medium\n\n</details>\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25745?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\nCo-authored-by: FelixMalfait <6399865+FelixMalfait@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqosbzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKl8QADOZjnCDC7n13/4Jjbrfxn5/\nNa9QXrpHWsGTnS2geziz/vun/ZtudUdaWU4zUUCXeJ5Hoy6ll22yt+dKE5uxFgSn\nWqizTAxJeYfYXM0WUVoYmYMu6Rg4R5tGcyWH4DRdK//DNsr7DpqS0ktsJue7ryEs\nSdoeNsvy7kpExt6BzR9+va9fMOLSgRuBTOsEJHNyM6FrRcxiBQx4i08nXBYa8qtj\nZOm9qkjqb1Nma1OxcwcCFgHvxo1kZGBdk+e82BAdqP6IBx/6pjgOZ95wjNz73eMo\nmD6WhlhBp7XMwWnsbgkse67oGDIjfZWZ7x7IEZkuglqt+IP2Z/gA/5GNu7hVu/8j\n2aJtHNnQS/o4IGSbplmQ7OuMn6PzaW5bHr4waTEKJ/MNjlPZlZbGz1cx2Ga7qMhs\nH1VU4L3Np3kKJ6yIXVvWwSgqDmD8tIH0NVrjx/AebLnnd8qDdhhDGSK3Hf5yy34n\ntdGbOVnvg1oTwf75D4YJcJVqLW77W9U4Fa0sawo7AC+zL+UsaOaAbR0RQY/izyU9\ntyuuCLRI94VtXq3t4LO4C2subEtiyyY/TwTxgCnVjXoSijAY/LK77yNiZX150jhi\nVTWt9Z4Zktib2jB4sZWpIQOCa6u2bPhQoX/YcNTAxNw5jCSRTusgIXMVhdWJiXie\nmYJYUzbiD6kbVXSmwWxw\n=tDq/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/6e16c71c64f11d164ee6660d3a23eccd4c5705c9","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDZlMTZjNzFjNjRmMTFkMTY0ZWU2NjYwZDNhMjNlY2NkNGM1NzA1Yzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/99a0e1c39f4f35f2139456ce3e8aa3d5b7159080","sha":"99a0e1c39f4f35f2139456ce3e8aa3d5b7159080","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/99a0e1c39f4f35f2139456ce3e8aa3d5b7159080"}],"sha":"6e16c71c64f11d164ee6660d3a23eccd4c5705c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/6e16c71c64f11d164ee6660d3a23eccd4c5705c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/99a0e1c39f4f35f2139456ce3e8aa3d5b7159080/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:00:23Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:00:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ai): replace model pickers with a five-tier model slider (#25721)\n\n## What\n\nUsers no longer pick a model by name. They pick a tier on a slider:\nExtra Fast, Fast, Balanced, Smart, Extra Smart. The slider follows the\nFigma design: tier name, two deltas versus Balanced, five stops. Below\nBalanced the deltas are speed and cost, above it cost and intelligence,\nso each side shows the two figures that explain the trade.\n\n### Two layers, nothing else\n\n- **Instance**: one ordered model chain per tier\n(`AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_EXTRA_FAST`, `_FAST`, `_BALANCED`, `_SMART`,\n`_EXTRA_SMART`), plus the existing `AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_DISABLED`. The\nadmin panel \"Default Models\" card has one select per tier. Out of the\nbox, one provider key makes every tier resolve.\n- **Workspace**: `aiChatModelTier`, `aiAgentModelTier`,\n`isAutoModelSelectionEnabled` and `aiModelIdByTier`. With automatic\nselection on (the default) the workspace uses the instance chains.\nTurning it off shows one select per tier to pin a concrete model;\nunpinned tiers still fall back to the instance chain.\n\n### The chains are an effort ladder\n\nEach chain entry pins an effort (`provider/model@effort`), so a tier\nruns at the effort its benchmark is measured at and one model family can\nback neighbouring tiers at different speeds. OpenAI goes Luna at `low`,\n`medium` and `high`, then Sol at `high` and Astra at `xhigh`; Google\nsits second in every chain and climbs Gemini 3.8 Flash from `low` to\n`high`; Anthropic goes Sonnet 5 `low`/`medium`/`high`, Opus 5 `high`,\nFable 5.1 `xhigh`; xAI goes Grok 4.5 `low`/`medium` then Grok 4.6\n`medium`/`high`/`xhigh`. Small models such as GPT-5.4 nano and Gemini\n3.5 Flash Lite dropped out: they were dominated by the next model up at\na lower effort. Terra dropped out for the same reason: Luna at `high`\nscores above Terra at `medium` at a tenth of the price.\n\nVariants are labelled by what the level means, \"GPT-5.6 Luna (no\nreasoning)\", \"GPT-5.6 Luna (low reasoning)\", since `none` runs the model\nwithout reasoning and is therefore faster and scores lower than `low`.\n\nPer-effort benchmarks come from #25730 and the first sync that carried\nthem, #25731, is merged in. With it the OpenAI ladder reads 22 / 26 / 32\n/ 43 / 53 on intelligence and 103 / 103 / 105 / 63 / 49 tokens per\nsecond, and the Anthropic and Google entries have readings at their own\neffort too. A variant still without one (Grok 4.5 at `low` and `medium`,\nMistral Small at `none`, and the speed of Gemini 3.8 Flash below `high`)\nshows its base model''s reading dimmed, with a tooltip saying it was not\nmeasured at this effort (`ClientAiModelConfig.isBenchmarkInherited`).\nDisabling a base model in the admin panel disables every effort it can\nbe pinned at.\n\n### Pinning a model, at an effort\n\nEvery pin select (workspace Models tab, the agent picker''s Advanced\nlink, the admin default per tier) lists base models and, for a model\nthat declares reasoning levels, a second select for the level. The pin\nis stored as `provider/model@effort`, and the registry resolves any\ndeclared effort by id, whether or not a chain lists it. Undeclared\nefforts stay unreachable.\n\n### Where the slider shows up\n\n- Chat composer and the question card: five small bars filled up to the\ncurrent tier, which open the slider in a dropdown. `null` selection\nfollows the workspace chat tier.\n- Agent settings and the workflow AI node: `AiModelPicker`, the slider\ninline plus an \"Advanced\" link to pin one exact model for that agent.\n- Agents store `workspace-default-model` by default and follow the\nworkspace agent tier. They can also store a tier id or a concrete model\nid (SDK manifests and the API keep accepting both).\n\n### Removed\n\n- Recommended models end to end: config variable, preference field, both\nadmin mutations, the admin table, `isRecommended` on both DTOs.\n- The per-workspace allowlist (`useRecommendedModels`,\n`enabledAiModelIds`) and the two utils that evaluated it.\n- `fastModel`, `smartModel` and the long-deprecated `routerModel`\nworkspace columns.\n- Front hooks `useAiModelOptions`, `useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability`,\nthe per-picker model lists, and the `AUTO_SELECT_FAST_MODEL_ID` /\n`AUTO_SELECT_SMART_MODEL_ID` aliases.\n\nThe removed GraphQL fields are why `api-breaking-changes` is red; only\ntwenty-front read them.\n\n## Defaults and migration\n\n- New workspaces default to **Fast** for chat and agents (GPT-5.6 Luna\nat medium effort, then Gemini 3.8 Flash at medium on instances without\nan OpenAI key), per the discussion that these are good enough for most\nuse.\n- Upgrade is a fast command (adds the tier columns, changes the agent\ndefault) plus a slow command (data + drops the old columns). The slow\ncommand is what carries earlier picks over: until it runs, every\nworkspace reads as automatic selection on Fast.\n- A workspace that had picked a concrete smart model keeps it as a pin\nand stays on the Smart tier for chat and agents. One that only picked a\nfast model keeps that pin on Fast. Every other workspace moves to\nautomatic selection with the new defaults. Rows edited in the new UI\nbefore the slow command runs are left alone.\n- Agents still on `default-smart-model` (the old default nobody chose)\nor the legacy `auto` id become `workspace-default-model`.\n`default-fast-model` and concrete ids are kept as is.\n- Self-hosters: `AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_FAST` and `_SMART` keep their names\nbut now back tiers; `AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_RECOMMENDED` is dropped.\n\n## Preview table and cost\n\nThe Models tab shows speed (tokens/s), intelligence index and cost per\ntier from the catalog benchmarks. Cost is Artificial Analysis''s cost per\ntask (the price of one task of its intelligence index run at that\neffort, so reasoning volume counts) when the catalog carries it, and\notherwise a blended price per 1M tokens (3:1 input to output) with the\nunit spelled out. The slider''s cost delta uses the same basis on both\nsides of the comparison.\n\nThe catalog sync so far read the legacy `/api/v2/data/llms/models`\nendpoint and looked for `cost_per_task` at the top level, which that\nendpoint never returned, so no model carried a cost per task. The sync\nnow reads the documented `/api/v2/language/models/free` endpoint page by\npage, takes speed from `performance` and cost from\n`artificial_analysis_intelligence_index_cost.cost_per_task.total_cost`,\nand the coverage summary on each sync PR reports how many models got a\ncost. The first run after merge fills the column; triggering \"AI Catalog\nSync\" manually is the quickest way to see it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tsgo` clean on twenty-shared, twenty-server (including\n`tsconfig.scripts.json`), twenty-front and twenty-client-sdk. oxlint and\noxfmt clean on every changed file.\n- Server unit specs around ai-models, ai-chat, ai-billing, agent\nexecution, workspace, admin-panel, client-config, the upgrade commands\nand the catalog sync scripts pass. Front suites under `modules/ai`,\n`modules/settings/ai`, `pages/settings/ai`, `settings/admin-panel`,\n`client-config` and the workflow AI node pass. New specs cover\n`getAiModelTierFromModelId`, `useAiModelTiers`, `useAgentChatModelId`,\n`getNearestAiModelTier`, `getPercentDelta`,\n`getAiModelBlendedCostPerMillionTokens`, `parseAiModelVariantId`, the\nslow migration command and the paginated benchmark fetch.\n- Agent integration suites pass against a reset test database (the\nevent-logs suite needs ClickHouse, not available locally).\n- `database:migrate:generate` reports no schema diff after the\nhand-written command, so the SQL matches the entities.\n- `/client-config` on a local server resolves the five tiers to the\nladder heads and lists each base model''s reasoning levels.\n- Manually checked in the browser: Models tab (auto and manual with a\npin persisted to `aiModelIdByTier`), preview table, chat composer slider\n(keyboard and mouse), agent settings picker, admin default models.\n- The new Artificial Analysis endpoint could not be called from the\ndevelopment container (no API key there); the reader follows the\ndocumented response schema and is unit-tested against it.\n\n## Follow-ups (not in this PR)\n\n- Data residency and ZDR preferences as filters on the chain, as\nsketched in the design.\n- Deriving the default chains from catalog benchmarks instead of the\nhardcoded lists, now that per-effort readings exist.\n- Whether the unpinned base entry should report the provider default''s\nreading instead of the ceiling (left open in #25730).\n- An efforts field on the custom provider \"new model\" form, so a custom\nmodel can be pinned at an effort without editing `AI_PROVIDERS` by hand.\n- The agent detail page logs a \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" loop on\nevery tab, including Role, where nothing from this PR is mounted. It\nlooks pre-existing and is worth a separate look.","tree":{"sha":"cf0e6b139fb2a7ead98a1e84c045599d9281ff94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/cf0e6b139fb2a7ead98a1e84c045599d9281ff94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/99a0e1c39f4f35f2139456ce3e8aa3d5b7159080","verification":{"payload":"tree cf0e6b139fb2a7ead98a1e84c045599d9281ff94\nparent 5d0914ca496d00694a63fdb6c6b8f86d781faae8\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789052423 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789052423 +0200\n\nfeat(ai): replace model pickers with a five-tier model slider (#25721)\n\n## What\n\nUsers no longer pick a model by name. They pick a tier on a slider:\nExtra Fast, Fast, Balanced, Smart, Extra Smart. The slider follows the\nFigma design: tier name, two deltas versus Balanced, five stops. Below\nBalanced the deltas are speed and cost, above it cost and intelligence,\nso each side shows the two figures that explain the trade.\n\n### Two layers, nothing else\n\n- **Instance**: one ordered model chain per tier\n(`AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_EXTRA_FAST`, `_FAST`, `_BALANCED`, `_SMART`,\n`_EXTRA_SMART`), plus the existing `AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_DISABLED`. The\nadmin panel \"Default Models\" card has one select per tier. Out of the\nbox, one provider key makes every tier resolve.\n- **Workspace**: `aiChatModelTier`, `aiAgentModelTier`,\n`isAutoModelSelectionEnabled` and `aiModelIdByTier`. With automatic\nselection on (the default) the workspace uses the instance chains.\nTurning it off shows one select per tier to pin a concrete model;\nunpinned tiers still fall back to the instance chain.\n\n### The chains are an effort ladder\n\nEach chain entry pins an effort (`provider/model@effort`), so a tier\nruns at the effort its benchmark is measured at and one model family can\nback neighbouring tiers at different speeds. OpenAI goes Luna at `low`,\n`medium` and `high`, then Sol at `high` and Astra at `xhigh`; Google\nsits second in every chain and climbs Gemini 3.8 Flash from `low` to\n`high`; Anthropic goes Sonnet 5 `low`/`medium`/`high`, Opus 5 `high`,\nFable 5.1 `xhigh`; xAI goes Grok 4.5 `low`/`medium` then Grok 4.6\n`medium`/`high`/`xhigh`. Small models such as GPT-5.4 nano and Gemini\n3.5 Flash Lite dropped out: they were dominated by the next model up at\na lower effort. Terra dropped out for the same reason: Luna at `high`\nscores above Terra at `medium` at a tenth of the price.\n\nVariants are labelled by what the level means, \"GPT-5.6 Luna (no\nreasoning)\", \"GPT-5.6 Luna (low reasoning)\", since `none` runs the model\nwithout reasoning and is therefore faster and scores lower than `low`.\n\nPer-effort benchmarks come from #25730 and the first sync that carried\nthem, #25731, is merged in. With it the OpenAI ladder reads 22 / 26 / 32\n/ 43 / 53 on intelligence and 103 / 103 / 105 / 63 / 49 tokens per\nsecond, and the Anthropic and Google entries have readings at their own\neffort too. A variant still without one (Grok 4.5 at `low` and `medium`,\nMistral Small at `none`, and the speed of Gemini 3.8 Flash below `high`)\nshows its base model''s reading dimmed, with a tooltip saying it was not\nmeasured at this effort (`ClientAiModelConfig.isBenchmarkInherited`).\nDisabling a base model in the admin panel disables every effort it can\nbe pinned at.\n\n### Pinning a model, at an effort\n\nEvery pin select (workspace Models tab, the agent picker''s Advanced\nlink, the admin default per tier) lists base models and, for a model\nthat declares reasoning levels, a second select for the level. The pin\nis stored as `provider/model@effort`, and the registry resolves any\ndeclared effort by id, whether or not a chain lists it. Undeclared\nefforts stay unreachable.\n\n### Where the slider shows up\n\n- Chat composer and the question card: five small bars filled up to the\ncurrent tier, which open the slider in a dropdown. `null` selection\nfollows the workspace chat tier.\n- Agent settings and the workflow AI node: `AiModelPicker`, the slider\ninline plus an \"Advanced\" link to pin one exact model for that agent.\n- Agents store `workspace-default-model` by default and follow the\nworkspace agent tier. They can also store a tier id or a concrete model\nid (SDK manifests and the API keep accepting both).\n\n### Removed\n\n- Recommended models end to end: config variable, preference field, both\nadmin mutations, the admin table, `isRecommended` on both DTOs.\n- The per-workspace allowlist (`useRecommendedModels`,\n`enabledAiModelIds`) and the two utils that evaluated it.\n- `fastModel`, `smartModel` and the long-deprecated `routerModel`\nworkspace columns.\n- Front hooks `useAiModelOptions`, `useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability`,\nthe per-picker model lists, and the `AUTO_SELECT_FAST_MODEL_ID` /\n`AUTO_SELECT_SMART_MODEL_ID` aliases.\n\nThe removed GraphQL fields are why `api-breaking-changes` is red; only\ntwenty-front read them.\n\n## Defaults and migration\n\n- New workspaces default to **Fast** for chat and agents (GPT-5.6 Luna\nat medium effort, then Gemini 3.8 Flash at medium on instances without\nan OpenAI key), per the discussion that these are good enough for most\nuse.\n- Upgrade is a fast command (adds the tier columns, changes the agent\ndefault) plus a slow command (data + drops the old columns). The slow\ncommand is what carries earlier picks over: until it runs, every\nworkspace reads as automatic selection on Fast.\n- A workspace that had picked a concrete smart model keeps it as a pin\nand stays on the Smart tier for chat and agents. One that only picked a\nfast model keeps that pin on Fast. Every other workspace moves to\nautomatic selection with the new defaults. Rows edited in the new UI\nbefore the slow command runs are left alone.\n- Agents still on `default-smart-model` (the old default nobody chose)\nor the legacy `auto` id become `workspace-default-model`.\n`default-fast-model` and concrete ids are kept as is.\n- Self-hosters: `AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_FAST` and `_SMART` keep their names\nbut now back tiers; `AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_RECOMMENDED` is dropped.\n\n## Preview table and cost\n\nThe Models tab shows speed (tokens/s), intelligence index and cost per\ntier from the catalog benchmarks. Cost is Artificial Analysis''s cost per\ntask (the price of one task of its intelligence index run at that\neffort, so reasoning volume counts) when the catalog carries it, and\notherwise a blended price per 1M tokens (3:1 input to output) with the\nunit spelled out. The slider''s cost delta uses the same basis on both\nsides of the comparison.\n\nThe catalog sync so far read the legacy `/api/v2/data/llms/models`\nendpoint and looked for `cost_per_task` at the top level, which that\nendpoint never returned, so no model carried a cost per task. The sync\nnow reads the documented `/api/v2/language/models/free` endpoint page by\npage, takes speed from `performance` and cost from\n`artificial_analysis_intelligence_index_cost.cost_per_task.total_cost`,\nand the coverage summary on each sync PR reports how many models got a\ncost. The first run after merge fills the column; triggering \"AI Catalog\nSync\" manually is the quickest way to see it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tsgo` clean on twenty-shared, twenty-server (including\n`tsconfig.scripts.json`), twenty-front and twenty-client-sdk. oxlint and\noxfmt clean on every changed file.\n- Server unit specs around ai-models, ai-chat, ai-billing, agent\nexecution, workspace, admin-panel, client-config, the upgrade commands\nand the catalog sync scripts pass. Front suites under `modules/ai`,\n`modules/settings/ai`, `pages/settings/ai`, `settings/admin-panel`,\n`client-config` and the workflow AI node pass. New specs cover\n`getAiModelTierFromModelId`, `useAiModelTiers`, `useAgentChatModelId`,\n`getNearestAiModelTier`, `getPercentDelta`,\n`getAiModelBlendedCostPerMillionTokens`, `parseAiModelVariantId`, the\nslow migration command and the paginated benchmark fetch.\n- Agent integration suites pass against a reset test database (the\nevent-logs suite needs ClickHouse, not available locally).\n- `database:migrate:generate` reports no schema diff after the\nhand-written command, so the SQL matches the entities.\n- `/client-config` on a local server resolves the five tiers to the\nladder heads and lists each base model''s reasoning levels.\n- Manually checked in the browser: Models tab (auto and manual with a\npin persisted to `aiModelIdByTier`), preview table, chat composer slider\n(keyboard and mouse), agent settings picker, admin default models.\n- The new Artificial Analysis endpoint could not be called from the\ndevelopment container (no API key there); the reader follows the\ndocumented response schema and is unit-tested against it.\n\n## Follow-ups (not in this PR)\n\n- Data residency and ZDR preferences as filters on the chain, as\nsketched in the design.\n- Deriving the default chains from catalog benchmarks instead of the\nhardcoded lists, now that per-effort readings exist.\n- Whether the unpinned base entry should report the provider default''s\nreading instead of the ceiling (left open in #25730).\n- An efforts field on the custom provider \"new model\" form, so a custom\nmodel can be pinned at an effort without editing `AI_PROVIDERS` by hand.\n- The agent detail page logs a \"Maximum update depth exceeded\" loop on\nevery tab, including Role, where nothing from this PR is mounted. It\nlooks pre-existing and is worth a separate look.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqosYHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ40QAKYRcdr92XnLteAlknvIsrGV\nxT4hzNtnTkvZMfSHVe9Lh+2zigZTB6yLq/GZbKaKRpapDJLMm/kVkOhAhvxHXzDv\nLEU+m6nneTdh/Uxe3M/K0Y+66Bw2yAy9H7aUv7x70Ej/pLt/RrHB58sQSvCkfhsI\nG32czQUxeSyk1nVK7hz6d8IwWK3aBtwUXxMLaXkRcdca1789WRtM6C2fPEAm9Y7T\nZcpE5DT7KXyVqc4GYBu47EZy1AwwZdfE8U2NDl1Bjwl1HnsOioTd9rKHr4cI4W4l\naWqBm78zH9sK6F9YArYJ0XaiGNiQolywqj8lpjKF0/uYNDYKrkdhFjvGeAH+LxhC\nBf9n2WghbhsVMPxPk6wqRdljSZPxtArOvZgdZDrwVc4CYZ21b+WZ5MLe82xdKzXA\ncYGeIIdScWPgZQv39DuAkTGQOpwxpCCumYCiNhnFYu0XOxAZoB4AhLz0znCKi6ku\nLy8/MFGHptQPcYlyQSWr/Rgw82s7zJ9wMQfw3h+emlKk6b3ETr2NleDxrxdnQlgF\nFX/XSM8K21YV5X3vhl9whhFeOVVEpmy5Le25/vaDNTB/IOOzPf7N5ti8Smt3WSJB\nUGne01vw8k6rhovl9S37JG2zjSxMgRQC3tIE5c1WVtDhMxoZXt0wrbt9+2aFML8G\nHoEva0nXUwYulzQ16vvq\n=ceej\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/99a0e1c39f4f35f2139456ce3e8aa3d5b7159080","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDk5YTBlMWMzOWY0ZjM1ZjIxMzk0NTZjZTNlOGFhM2Q1YjcxNTkwODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/5d0914ca496d00694a63fdb6c6b8f86d781faae8","sha":"5d0914ca496d00694a63fdb6c6b8f86d781faae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5d0914ca496d00694a63fdb6c6b8f86d781faae8"}],"sha":"99a0e1c39f4f35f2139456ce3e8aa3d5b7159080","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/99a0e1c39f4f35f2139456ce3e8aa3d5b7159080"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51697796?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ijreilly","id":51697796,"login":"ijreilly","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNjk3Nzk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijreilly","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5d0914ca496d00694a63fdb6c6b8f86d781faae8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:53:16Z","email":"51697796+ijreilly@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:53:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(enterprise): keep self-hosted licenses valid while Stripe retries a failed payment (#25515)\n\n## Problem\n\n`/api/enterprise/validate` only issued a validity token for `active` and\n`trialing` subscriptions, so a `past_due` subscription got a 403 the day\nafter a charge failed, while Stripe was still retrying the invoice.\n\nA self-hosted Enterprise customer hit exactly this. Their trial ended\n2026-08-10 and the first real invoice failed. The subscription went\n`past_due` on 08-11 and every nightly refresh was refused from then on.\nTheir last token expired on 08-17 and the instance lost its enterprise\nfeatures, a week before Stripe stopped retrying and cancelled the\nsubscription on 08-24.\n\nSettings > Enterprise didn''t explain any of this: in the `past_due`\nstate it said \"Fix the payment issue to keep your enterprise features\nactive\" when those features had already been switched off.\n\n## Change\n\n`validate` now also issues a token to a `past_due` subscription, for as\nlong as Stripe is still retrying the payment.\n\n| Stripe status | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `active`, `trialing` | licensed, normal 7-day token |\n| `past_due`, retry scheduled | grace, token valid until one day after\nthe next scheduled retry |\n| `past_due`, retries exhausted | rejected |\n| `canceled`, `unpaid`, `incomplete`, `incomplete_expired`, `paused` |\nrejected (unchanged) |\n\nGrace is based on `next_payment_attempt`. For a `past_due` subscription,\nvalidation lists the subscription''s open invoices and uses the latest\nscheduled retry among them. It looks at every open invoice rather than\n`latest_invoice`, because a newer invoice that was voided, or a new\nbilling-cycle invoice, can hide a retry still running on an older one.\nStripe calculates `next_payment_attempt` from the retry settings in the\ndashboard, so grace follows the configured retry schedule without a\nseparate setting to keep in sync, and it ends when Stripe stops\nretrying. The one-day margin covers the daily 04:00 UTC validation job,\nso an instance doesn''t lose its license between a retry and the next\ncheck. A retry time more than a day in the past is treated as stale and\nrejected. Token expiry is the earliest of the default lifetime, any\nscheduled cancellation, and the grace deadline.\n\n`unpaid` stays rejected, since Stripe''s documentation says to revoke\naccess in that state.\n\nGrace tokens still carry `status: \"valid\"`, so instances on older\nversions get grace without upgrading. The customer above is on v2.20.0.\nWith this change their instance would have kept its license until Stripe\nstopped retrying on 08-24.\n\n## Settings page\n\nIn the `past_due` state, Settings > Enterprise decides whether features\nare active from the instance''s own validity token rather than from the\nStripe status, so the page matches what the instance can actually do. No\nnew API fields are needed: the status query already returns the token''s\nexpiry.\n\n- valid token: orange status dot, \"Your enterprise features stay active\nwhile we retry it\", a `Features active until` row showing the token''s\nexpiry, and a reminder to update the payment method before that date.\nThe expiry is already the earliest of the default lifetime, any\nscheduled cancellation and the retry deadline, so it is when access\nreally ends, including the day of access left after the last failed\nretry.\n- no valid token, typically once retries are exhausted: red dot,\nfeatures disabled, and a note that a cancelled subscription can''t be\nreactivated. Once Stripe cancels, the customer has to start a new\nsubscription. The follow-up PR #25620 handles that case without letting\na returning server take a new free trial each time it re-subscribes.\n\nThe status dot has a new `warning` variant for the grace state.\n\n**In grace**\n\n<img width=\"800\" alt=\"In grace\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc2670e7-a31e-43c5-95e6-46ec98fe0f11\"\n/>\n\n**Retries exhausted**\n\n<img width=\"800\" alt=\"Retries exhausted\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52e5f325-0fc5-47e1-a52f-98b170dc79d8\"\n/>\n\n## Also fixed\n\n- `getSubscriptionCurrentPeriodEnd` read the period end from the\nsubscription object, but with the API version the SDK pins\n(`2026-02-25.clover`) Stripe returns it on subscription items. The\nhelper always returned null, which quietly disabled the\n`cancel_at_period_end` token cap and the \"Renews on\" row. It now reads\nthe item.\n- `.env.example` said the validity token defaults to 30 days. The code\nuses 7.\n\n## Tests\n\nWebsite enterprise suite: 67 passing.\n`resolve-subscription-license-state.test.ts` covers every status, a\npending retry, a retry that has just run, a stale retry, retries\nexhausted, and grace following the retry schedule rather than the\nbilling period. `find-next-payment-attempt.test.ts` covers a retry on an\nolder open invoice when a newer one has none, several invoices being\nretried, and no retry at all. `subscription-current-period.test.ts`\ncovers reading the period end from the subscription item.\n`sign-validity-token.test.ts` covers the grace cap, a grace deadline\ncombined with a scheduled cancellation, and the `valid` status on grace\ntokens. Typecheck and lint pass on all three packages.\n\nNot checked against a real Stripe account: when exactly\n`next_payment_attempt` is set and cleared, and in particular whether it\nis already set when a subscription first becomes `past_due`. Worth\nconfirming in test mode.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n`/api/enterprise/seats` returns HTTP 200 with `{success: false}` when it\ndoes nothing, and `reportSeats()` only checks `response.ok`, so the\nnightly job logs success without syncing anything. Left for a separate\nPR.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25515?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"3b3ae6ba1514efbc6a9872d256b1a33930c3ef49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/3b3ae6ba1514efbc6a9872d256b1a33930c3ef49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/5d0914ca496d00694a63fdb6c6b8f86d781faae8","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b3ae6ba1514efbc6a9872d256b1a33930c3ef49\nparent bd46d9de6313bab561f6ba48cf4fa2c9f68b5678\nauthor Marie <51697796+ijreilly@users.noreply.github.com> 1789051996 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789051996 +0000\n\nfix(enterprise): keep self-hosted licenses valid while Stripe retries a failed payment (#25515)\n\n## Problem\n\n`/api/enterprise/validate` only issued a validity token for `active` and\n`trialing` subscriptions, so a `past_due` subscription got a 403 the day\nafter a charge failed, while Stripe was still retrying the invoice.\n\nA self-hosted Enterprise customer hit exactly this. Their trial ended\n2026-08-10 and the first real invoice failed. The subscription went\n`past_due` on 08-11 and every nightly refresh was refused from then on.\nTheir last token expired on 08-17 and the instance lost its enterprise\nfeatures, a week before Stripe stopped retrying and cancelled the\nsubscription on 08-24.\n\nSettings > Enterprise didn''t explain any of this: in the `past_due`\nstate it said \"Fix the payment issue to keep your enterprise features\nactive\" when those features had already been switched off.\n\n## Change\n\n`validate` now also issues a token to a `past_due` subscription, for as\nlong as Stripe is still retrying the payment.\n\n| Stripe status | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `active`, `trialing` | licensed, normal 7-day token |\n| `past_due`, retry scheduled | grace, token valid until one day after\nthe next scheduled retry |\n| `past_due`, retries exhausted | rejected |\n| `canceled`, `unpaid`, `incomplete`, `incomplete_expired`, `paused` |\nrejected (unchanged) |\n\nGrace is based on `next_payment_attempt`. For a `past_due` subscription,\nvalidation lists the subscription''s open invoices and uses the latest\nscheduled retry among them. It looks at every open invoice rather than\n`latest_invoice`, because a newer invoice that was voided, or a new\nbilling-cycle invoice, can hide a retry still running on an older one.\nStripe calculates `next_payment_attempt` from the retry settings in the\ndashboard, so grace follows the configured retry schedule without a\nseparate setting to keep in sync, and it ends when Stripe stops\nretrying. The one-day margin covers the daily 04:00 UTC validation job,\nso an instance doesn''t lose its license between a retry and the next\ncheck. A retry time more than a day in the past is treated as stale and\nrejected. Token expiry is the earliest of the default lifetime, any\nscheduled cancellation, and the grace deadline.\n\n`unpaid` stays rejected, since Stripe''s documentation says to revoke\naccess in that state.\n\nGrace tokens still carry `status: \"valid\"`, so instances on older\nversions get grace without upgrading. The customer above is on v2.20.0.\nWith this change their instance would have kept its license until Stripe\nstopped retrying on 08-24.\n\n## Settings page\n\nIn the `past_due` state, Settings > Enterprise decides whether features\nare active from the instance''s own validity token rather than from the\nStripe status, so the page matches what the instance can actually do. No\nnew API fields are needed: the status query already returns the token''s\nexpiry.\n\n- valid token: orange status dot, \"Your enterprise features stay active\nwhile we retry it\", a `Features active until` row showing the token''s\nexpiry, and a reminder to update the payment method before that date.\nThe expiry is already the earliest of the default lifetime, any\nscheduled cancellation and the retry deadline, so it is when access\nreally ends, including the day of access left after the last failed\nretry.\n- no valid token, typically once retries are exhausted: red dot,\nfeatures disabled, and a note that a cancelled subscription can''t be\nreactivated. Once Stripe cancels, the customer has to start a new\nsubscription. The follow-up PR #25620 handles that case without letting\na returning server take a new free trial each time it re-subscribes.\n\nThe status dot has a new `warning` variant for the grace state.\n\n**In grace**\n\n<img width=\"800\" alt=\"In grace\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc2670e7-a31e-43c5-95e6-46ec98fe0f11\"\n/>\n\n**Retries exhausted**\n\n<img width=\"800\" alt=\"Retries exhausted\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52e5f325-0fc5-47e1-a52f-98b170dc79d8\"\n/>\n\n## Also fixed\n\n- `getSubscriptionCurrentPeriodEnd` read the period end from the\nsubscription object, but with the API version the SDK pins\n(`2026-02-25.clover`) Stripe returns it on subscription items. The\nhelper always returned null, which quietly disabled the\n`cancel_at_period_end` token cap and the \"Renews on\" row. It now reads\nthe item.\n- `.env.example` said the validity token defaults to 30 days. The code\nuses 7.\n\n## Tests\n\nWebsite enterprise suite: 67 passing.\n`resolve-subscription-license-state.test.ts` covers every status, a\npending retry, a retry that has just run, a stale retry, retries\nexhausted, and grace following the retry schedule rather than the\nbilling period. `find-next-payment-attempt.test.ts` covers a retry on an\nolder open invoice when a newer one has none, several invoices being\nretried, and no retry at all. `subscription-current-period.test.ts`\ncovers reading the period end from the subscription item.\n`sign-validity-token.test.ts` covers the grace cap, a grace deadline\ncombined with a scheduled cancellation, and the `valid` status on grace\ntokens. Typecheck and lint pass on all three packages.\n\nNot checked against a real Stripe account: when exactly\n`next_payment_attempt` is set and cleared, and in particular whether it\nis already set when a subscription first becomes `past_due`. Worth\nconfirming in test mode.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n`/api/enterprise/seats` returns HTTP 200 with `{success: false}` when it\ndoes nothing, and `reportSeats()` only checks `response.ok`, so the\nnightly job logs success without syncing anything. Left for a separate\nPR.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25515?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqosRsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9UkQAF3CB4vuPbeFjDNzH+CkujM2\nUJQ7CeusFe3KcxZhhR6BI6jxdbYx3d+Fr2qW7ICLZa3/UzK56o35fDV+Oc6NwLWj\ntIDwYA5vLYZ6tSPfF/rJvGXd9/R2ZvwexWhEx5QjFnrtBmlAr0Ma3gTTVgJt2b4F\nG2pdh2yowPKzsZHAuqkdWwCl9Wh9VgwEpvSDzrke8J+hXcjrvIa/TpXh7d17kPv3\nExzSx3bZ192btbg7OvTxbfdk4JnITvl55auMNZek2999rvNfIs05rRJUx2HYyZm6\nx1x3KoJp8kOBXc0xkvgsyKlw4RlTZ/GXlr5jcWYX+pn1RLbYq8CkFDV43pRmgaSC\nPdIZz4JQAA8DOWSqEXVu59hppJCMfyUZM8sjjq78jY0aZTzlLF82PXC4rpNZDtES\nBlFufeo4UGv9WZHu16uhIVCjx5JvhEnmlpTCyRwOaL9zf4wnpiAZ7jp9joWH288g\nfaqttxk/9KMUpWtkIwpexsXIoVVfJ4juHtygoUDK15mIYvMZuAoNaVRD25RubFBq\nzHaWessr/nfaMagwOPTN0UCibY0TYpSIzsOA0gugRJQ8dEyAU/zLVsXylZDZdPQ9\nmAYKu2SJWh1nflfmr0Vg/aIpiwbGuv0xjB50NletmbTGfh9cTYm80aOOUX0hRwZf\ncjBzdVicg3tgHTupDx3K\n=FbFs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/5d0914ca496d00694a63fdb6c6b8f86d781faae8","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDVkMDkxNGNhNDk2ZDAwNjk0YTYzZmRiNmM2YjhmODZkNzgxZmFhZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/bd46d9de6313bab561f6ba48cf4fa2c9f68b5678","sha":"bd46d9de6313bab561f6ba48cf4fa2c9f68b5678","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/bd46d9de6313bab561f6ba48cf4fa2c9f68b5678"}],"sha":"5d0914ca496d00694a63fdb6c6b8f86d781faae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/5d0914ca496d00694a63fdb6c6b8f86d781faae8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29927851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/martmull","id":29927851,"login":"martmull","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/bd46d9de6313bab561f6ba48cf4fa2c9f68b5678/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:47:13Z","email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:47:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add batch delivery to database-event-triggered logic functions (#25726)\n\n## What\n\nA logic function can now opt into receiving **one job per batch of\ndatabase events** instead of one job per event, via a new `batchSize`\noption on `databaseEventTriggerSettings`.\n\n```\nfilteredEvents\n  -> batchSize undefined  ->  1 job per event, payload = { ...batchEventInfo, ...event }   (unchanged)\n  -> batchSize defined    ->  group by (userId, userWorkspaceId)\n                                -> chunk by min(batchSize, clamp)\n                                  -> 1 job, payload = { ...batchEventInfo, events: [...] }\n```\n\n## Why\n\n`last-contact` listens on `messageParticipant.updated` /\n`calendarEventParticipant.updated`. During a mailbox sync this creates\none logic function job per participant, so a 50k-message mailbox\nproduces ~150 000 jobs. `logicFunctionQueue` is shared by every app of\nevery workspace, and `ApplicationJobEnqueueThrottlerService` admits only\n500 jobs per minute per application and silently drops the excess, so\nthe app loses most of its updates during a sync while starving every\nother app.\n\nBatching at 100 turns ~150 000 jobs into ~1 500, which keeps the\nthrottle from tripping (it already counts jobs, not events).\n\n## How\n\nThe whole feature lives in `transform-event-batch-to-event-payloads.ts`,\nthe only 1:1 explosion in the pipeline. Batch events already exist end\nto end and travel intact, so the emission layer, the event emitter and\n`entity-events-to-db.listener.ts` are untouched.\n\n`userId` / `userWorkspaceId` are lifted out of each event onto the job\ndata and drive the executor''s auth context, so a job carries exactly one\nauth context. Events are therefore grouped by `(userId,\nuserWorkspaceId)` and only then chunked. During an import all events\nshare the system context, so this yields a single group.\n\n`updatedFields` filtering still runs before chunking.\n\n## Config\n\n`LOGIC_FUNCTION_DATABASE_EVENT_MAX_BATCH_SIZE` (default 200) clamps the\nauthor-supplied `batchSize`. Setting it to `1` reverts every batched\ntrigger to one-job-per-event without redeploying any app. A static\n`MAX_EVENTS_PER_TRIGGER_JOB` (500) bounds the Redis job payload even if\nthe config variable is raised.\n\n`databaseEventTriggerSettings` is a `jsonb` column exposed through\n`graphqlTypeJson` and copied opaquely from the manifest, so no\nmigration, GraphQL schema change, DTO change or flat-entity change is\nneeded.\n\n## Backwards compatibility\n\nLogic functions that do not set `batchSize` keep today''s behavior byte\nfor byte, including the payload shape. Because the split happens inside\nthe per-logic-function loop, one emitted batch can simultaneously feed\nan app with no `batchSize` and an app with `batchSize: 100`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- regression lock: no `batchSize` produces output identical to today\n- exact division, remainder chunk, clamping above the maximum,\n`maxBatchSize: 1` kill switch\n- events with different `userId`s never share a job\n- `updatedFields` filtering applied before chunking\n- `batchSize` on a non-`updated` operation still batches\n- a batched and an unbatched logic function on the same emitted batch\n- SDK: `batchSize` of `0`, `-1`, `1.5` rejected; a valid one passes\nthrough\n\n## Docs\n\n`DatabaseEventBatchPayload` is exported from both `twenty-sdk` entry\npoints (`logic-function/index.ts` and `define/index.ts`) so app authors\ncan actually import it, and `logic-functions.mdx` documents `batchSize`\nand the batch payload shape.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\nMigrating `last-contact` to `batchSize` is a separate PR.\n\n[Review in\ncubic](https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25726?utm_source=github)","tree":{"sha":"80e6a7dd4cba1a416533948cac31b42bf43a625f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/80e6a7dd4cba1a416533948cac31b42bf43a625f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/bd46d9de6313bab561f6ba48cf4fa2c9f68b5678","verification":{"payload":"tree 80e6a7dd4cba1a416533948cac31b42bf43a625f\nparent b453166a78f164eaccea77cdf7e660b86d8bdca9\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1789051633 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789051633 +0000\n\nAdd batch delivery to database-event-triggered logic functions (#25726)\n\n## What\n\nA logic function can now opt into receiving **one job per batch of\ndatabase events** instead of one job per event, via a new `batchSize`\noption on `databaseEventTriggerSettings`.\n\n```\nfilteredEvents\n  -> batchSize undefined  ->  1 job per event, payload = { ...batchEventInfo, ...event }   (unchanged)\n  -> batchSize defined    ->  group by (userId, userWorkspaceId)\n                                -> chunk by min(batchSize, clamp)\n                                  -> 1 job, payload = { ...batchEventInfo, events: [...] }\n```\n\n## Why\n\n`last-contact` listens on `messageParticipant.updated` /\n`calendarEventParticipant.updated`. During a mailbox sync this creates\none logic function job per participant, so a 50k-message mailbox\nproduces ~150 000 jobs. `logicFunctionQueue` is shared by every app of\nevery workspace, and `ApplicationJobEnqueueThrottlerService` admits only\n500 jobs per minute per application and silently drops the excess, so\nthe app loses most of its updates during a sync while starving every\nother app.\n\nBatching at 100 turns ~150 000 jobs into ~1 500, which keeps the\nthrottle from tripping (it already counts jobs, not events).\n\n## How\n\nThe whole feature lives in `transform-event-batch-to-event-payloads.ts`,\nthe only 1:1 explosion in the pipeline. Batch events already exist end\nto end and travel intact, so the emission layer, the event emitter and\n`entity-events-to-db.listener.ts` are untouched.\n\n`userId` / `userWorkspaceId` are lifted out of each event onto the job\ndata and drive the executor''s auth context, so a job carries exactly one\nauth context. Events are therefore grouped by `(userId,\nuserWorkspaceId)` and only then chunked. During an import all events\nshare the system context, so this yields a single group.\n\n`updatedFields` filtering still runs before chunking.\n\n## Config\n\n`LOGIC_FUNCTION_DATABASE_EVENT_MAX_BATCH_SIZE` (default 200) clamps the\nauthor-supplied `batchSize`. Setting it to `1` reverts every batched\ntrigger to one-job-per-event without redeploying any app. A static\n`MAX_EVENTS_PER_TRIGGER_JOB` (500) bounds the Redis job payload even if\nthe config variable is raised.\n\n`databaseEventTriggerSettings` is a `jsonb` column exposed through\n`graphqlTypeJson` and copied opaquely from the manifest, so no\nmigration, GraphQL schema change, DTO change or flat-entity change is\nneeded.\n\n## Backwards compatibility\n\nLogic functions that do not set `batchSize` keep today''s behavior byte\nfor byte, including the payload shape. Because the split happens inside\nthe per-logic-function loop, one emitted batch can simultaneously feed\nan app with no `batchSize` and an app with `batchSize: 100`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- regression lock: no `batchSize` produces output identical to today\n- exact division, remainder chunk, clamping above the maximum,\n`maxBatchSize: 1` kill switch\n- events with different `userId`s never share a job\n- `updatedFields` filtering applied before chunking\n- `batchSize` on a non-`updated` operation still batches\n- a batched and an unbatched logic function on the same emitted batch\n- SDK: `batchSize` of `0`, `-1`, `1.5` rejected; a valid one passes\nthrough\n\n## Docs\n\n`DatabaseEventBatchPayload` is exported from both `twenty-sdk` entry\npoints (`logic-function/index.ts` and `define/index.ts`) so app authors\ncan actually import it, and `logic-functions.mdx` documents `batchSize`\nand the batch payload shape.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\nMigrating `last-contact` to `batchSize` is a separate PR.\n\n[Review in\ncubic](https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25726?utm_source=github)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqosMCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMuYQADuG3U8tdVyDGHmOVt4Stcse\nGcSxU98KxfXa+V0xLP6zp6W4wVTGSoTzzrduZB8bcscIA7M/bHD3fdmsUDFkqABw\nSK5dqe5d5lBMpGZ64drpvitJleFAz1nQDshbQVBiQBV3/AMk3Q7dkvyaV6FYQVzD\ngxKAp378hzIiUQK50ez/rGHDVj7qar7lLvRvlIIgGaChKigQIqzP7nga1/OaQt+0\nvC01C3R51KgL1npApm53c82xXerZvKUS7YAcSOKAsNpR4Y3ncbEkpQVNLsvi/Uwg\nW5we/Yq4i5UTz5Eo6/BT9jeSxah5YGG87egbi7N1ao/U8VGrt3r9FY7776JnDQop\n0Vc4u1iYR+S/fbCslSq176MPmVskKcfOSMgJ0lP+NthVuPe4PYhjvmKIpF7UyFGE\nJu5qpoJ5a4pJEuG50qvC1/VmkK+l8zOJTeZejoJi4KXdyZqGMr/M9S2JZgvrVglE\nfDZ1Yi+nW0tQYA7NBYsM9+3WeCNGBUdKaLbzwkASP1ll1eiMBSYUuGDCq8SW6yD5\nYfTe1tK1mYcfz/ntkJp4oK82AwRcab+ZwK306zkn5eGH6hMICwQEHtVbgBlU1R7X\nYX8Twt+r6pMwIaQvOsagRuRLweM5Ix1Zdi7CQNdXEeMiTSuexejUcwNFb8MNanRW\n84DzDZR+IMslgCVvQa8w\n=1pnf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/bd46d9de6313bab561f6ba48cf4fa2c9f68b5678","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGJkNDZkOWRlNjMxM2JhYjU2MWY2YmE0OGNmNGZhMmM5ZjY4YjU2Nzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/b453166a78f164eaccea77cdf7e660b86d8bdca9","sha":"b453166a78f164eaccea77cdf7e660b86d8bdca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b453166a78f164eaccea77cdf7e660b86d8bdca9"}],"sha":"bd46d9de6313bab561f6ba48cf4fa2c9f68b5678","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/bd46d9de6313bab561f6ba48cf4fa2c9f68b5678"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62770500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hktitof","id":62770500,"login":"hktitof","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzcwNTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hktitof","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b453166a78f164eaccea77cdf7e660b86d8bdca9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:28:55Z","email":"62770500+hktitof@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdellatif Anaflous"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:28:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflow): stop email steps sending from another member''s account (#25709)\n\n> **Context:** fixes #25703 (workflow Send Email step picks the first\nconnected account of the whole workspace when connectedAccountId is\nempty). The caller-scoped fallback already exists in the email composer,\nit just never receives a caller identity from workflow runs\n\n## Summary\n\n- a send-email or draft-email step with an empty connectedAccountId fell\nback to the first connected account of the whole workspace ordered by\ncreation (getDefaultConnectedAccountIdOrThrow in\nemail-composer.service.ts returns allAccounts[0].id when userWorkspaceId\nis undefined)\n- in a multi-user workspace that account can belong to another member,\nso the step fails with \"Connected account is not an SMTP provider\" when\nthat member has an IMAP/SMTP-only account, or it would silently send as\nthat member\n- ToolBackedWorkflowAction builds the tool context with the workspace id\nonly, while the composer resolves the caller-scoped fallback from\nuserWorkspaceId in that context, so the workflow path never had one\n- email workflow actions now resolve the workflow run caller through\nWorkflowExecutionContextService (the same MANUAL-run definition the\npermission checks use) and pass its userWorkspaceId down to the tool;\nruns without a user caller keep the workspace-wide fallback\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. npx jest\npackages/twenty-server/src/modules/workflow/workflow-executor/workflow-actions/mail-sender/__tests__/send-email.workflow-action.spec.ts\n--config=packages/twenty-server/jest.config.mjs\n2. Expected: the caller identity propagation cases pass, the tool\ncontext carries the run caller''s userWorkspaceId for a MANUAL run\n3. Actual (raw output on untouched main 88fe4360):\n\n```\nFAIL twenty-server packages/twenty-server/src/modules/workflow/workflow-executor/workflow-actions/mail-sender/__tests__/send-email.workflow-action.spec.ts\n  ● SendEmailWorkflowAction › caller identity propagation › passes the run caller userWorkspaceId to the tool for user-driven runs\n\n    expect(jest.fn()).toHaveBeenCalledWith(...expected)\n\n    Expected: Anything, ObjectContaining {\"userWorkspaceId\": \"20202020-3333-4333-8333-333333333333\", \"workspaceId\": \"workspace-1\"}\n    Received: {\"body\": \"hi\", \"connectedAccountId\": \"account-1\", \"files\": [], \"recipients\": {\"to\": \"test@example.com\"}, \"subject\": \"Test\"}, {\"workspaceId\": \"workspace-1\"}\n\n    Number of calls: 1\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n- the spec is 18/18 green with the fix and 1 red without it (stashed the\nfix sources over the spec and re-ran, identical failure)\n- draft-email spec 7/7 green, whole workflow-executor tree 39 suites /\n437 tests green, whole tool tree 28 suites / 189 tests green\n- tsgo typecheck clean, oxlint + oxfmt clean on the touched files\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25709?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c54661414d379830efcaed5ce37882009c77fea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/2c54661414d379830efcaed5ce37882009c77fea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/b453166a78f164eaccea77cdf7e660b86d8bdca9","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c54661414d379830efcaed5ce37882009c77fea\nparent 0dc40c8764e07797b3b1b991a5ee52600449cc1f\nauthor Abdellatif Anaflous <62770500+hktitof@user