hub.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b1701251d4aca0910f3ad0bcdb0532999600fecb"}],"sha":"fa9870536abce97ef2cb9622d9d1941443704bd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/fa9870536abce97ef2cb9622d9d1941443704bd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142569587?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ehconitin","id":142569587,"login":"ehconitin","node_id":"U_kgDOCH9wcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b1701251d4aca0910f3ad0bcdb0532999600fecb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:41:55Z","email":"142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nitin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:41:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Granola 4/8: Connect Granola webhooks and live synchronization (#25573)\n\nRegisters a signed Granola webhook and syncs notes as events arrive.\n\n- Server-route resolver with a SERVER-scoped claim per registration,\nStandard Webhooks signature check against the resolver''s receipt time,\nand a worker that upserts the note.\n- Key type is detected at registration: Granola answers a scope that\ndoes not match the key type with a 400 on `scopes`, so workspace scope\nis tried first and personal/public only on that error.\n- Registration repair: re-enables a disabled endpoint on request,\nrepairs a changed destination URL, retires and cleans up replaced\nendpoints, cleans up interrupted registrations.\n- Uninstall removes the endpoint and app KV state.\n- Settings: Live sync card with Active / Paused / Not set up, Resume and\nSet up actions, and automatic first registration after connecting.\nErrors from Granola (plan without webhooks, bad scopes) are shown\ninline.\n- Concurrent registrations from two admins are not serialized; app KV\nhas no compare-and-set.\n\nStack 4/8. Review against `ehco/granola-3-note-mapping`; merge in order\nand retain base branches until dependent PRs are retargeted.\n\nReview order:\n\n1. [Add the Granola application\nscaffold](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25570)\n2. [Add Granola API access and credential\nsettings](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25571)\n3. [Map Granola notes into Call\nRecordings](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25572)\n4. [Connect Granola webhooks and live\nsynchronization](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25573)\n5. [Import Granola history and recover missed\nupdates](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25574)\n6. [Expose Granola notes to workflows and\nAI](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25575)\n7. [Filter Granola synchronization by\nfolder](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25576)\n8. [Add Granola listing copy and setup\ndocumentation](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25577)","tree":{"sha":"4b55aeb802897228e2eaff93c5c2d4eaac2bf7ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/4b55aeb802897228e2eaff93c5c2d4eaac2bf7ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/b1701251d4aca0910f3ad0bcdb0532999600fecb","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b55aeb802897228e2eaff93c5c2d4eaac2bf7ec\nparent 2e5dd38ddf4bf8b91db496b988323ac99555b16e\nauthor nitin <142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com> 1789047715 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789047715 +0000\n\nGranola 4/8: Connect Granola webhooks and live synchronization (#25573)\n\nRegisters a signed Granola webhook and syncs notes as events arrive.\n\n- Server-route resolver with a SERVER-scoped claim per registration,\nStandard Webhooks signature check against the resolver''s receipt time,\nand a worker that upserts the note.\n- Key type is detected at registration: Granola answers a scope that\ndoes not match the key type with a 400 on `scopes`, so workspace scope\nis tried first and personal/public only on that error.\n- Registration repair: re-enables a disabled endpoint on request,\nrepairs a changed destination URL, retires and cleans up replaced\nendpoints, cleans up interrupted registrations.\n- Uninstall removes the endpoint and app KV state.\n- Settings: Live sync card with Active / Paused / Not set up, Resume and\nSet up actions, and automatic first registration after connecting.\nErrors from Granola (plan without webhooks, bad scopes) are shown\ninline.\n- Concurrent registrations from two admins are not serialized; app KV\nhas no compare-and-set.\n\nStack 4/8. Review against `ehco/granola-3-note-mapping`; merge in order\nand retain base branches until dependent PRs are retargeted.\n\nReview order:\n\n1. [Add the Granola application\nscaffold](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25570)\n2. [Add Granola API access and credential\nsettings](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25571)\n3. [Map Granola notes into Call\nRecordings](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25572)\n4. [Connect Granola webhooks and live\nsynchronization](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25573)\n5. [Import Granola history and recover missed\nupdates](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25574)\n6. [Expose Granola notes to workflows and\nAI](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25575)\n7. [Filter Granola synchronization by\nfolder](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25576)\n8. [Add Granola listing copy and setup\ndocumentation](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25577)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqorO0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAH8QABdS3bdhPzi37ryJ8yP4sCnL\nm19HbHDOC+OOUuRToOcfhHY2G/qvS6GS9Reb+A5Gbzaz+xgQvzs0tuD3Pnfc+F4d\naw3uGhAL8HC3UH9sL9L7VOGQxpamUspava0eKh0emouvLsEP7uN9BCsMI4ahoaYg\n7NhPIPcNyXGb0PkT3zZfHjDLdb3CLfPcAk37jk7k1e9Rc5PMu0Tu2DoGvPtbDakP\nrFFLpLv6ByoTQv1URxve4lDbEubMn7W1Lx2+oWytrToQtioC5gUTYvoRbd4lCuDB\nXwJpSaYQW9eGiNZJIXZLQJ67/aJVFsQsHQ607MQUtl+e1QyCB3sbPJ9+wr/yTlnc\nALrWDT1pjX6c6yOFvL8pg+4tYIie4K8k2kRvLX27ZK+fQZR/AfCAcBBZUQqcfhfB\n7HIt234Hmtx+RqXqoUfxWSlLODEb6JqRJaQqQHMlIKUNMcaiVXgRzlihiKP0tLw9\nSrCpiAMwI6HFO/pNEfdbaj7ML3xV7ayaGZSv2b9wavMHB+pLLTEjtEwilbmjdSFv\nFpPsIk97u+w/j5LqmwZDStUd8937Iy7g/ZBVo2yqYLQGIgqwKS0BqpPEqO9d7vTG\nO0k9xWRPiRGNS+atxqEvglt0/YoNlbhuOyKwHOQUKZf35MBx1Fnj/kjGqZV37DfB\n7Hv+L6OhoxypJPSodkP/\n=eeM7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/b1701251d4aca0910f3ad0bcdb0532999600fecb","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGIxNzAxMjUxZDRhY2EwOTEwZjNhZDBiY2RiMDUzMjk5OTYwMGZlY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/2e5dd38ddf4bf8b91db496b988323ac99555b16e","sha":"2e5dd38ddf4bf8b91db496b988323ac99555b16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/2e5dd38ddf4bf8b91db496b988323ac99555b16e"}],"sha":"b1701251d4aca0910f3ad0bcdb0532999600fecb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b1701251d4aca0910f3ad0bcdb0532999600fecb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142569587?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ehconitin","id":142569587,"login":"ehconitin","node_id":"U_kgDOCH9wcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/2e5dd38ddf4bf8b91db496b988323ac99555b16e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:41:03Z","email":"142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nitin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:41:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(apps): preserve vetted status during catalog sync (#25725)\n\nCatalog sync currently resets an admin''s Vetted choice to match the\nhardcoded marketplace list. For example, manually vetting an app outside\nthat list succeeds, but a later sync clears the setting.\n\nPreserve the stored `isVetted` value in both existing-registration\nupdate paths, and apply the hardcoded default only when creating a\nregistration. No UI changes or database migration are needed.\n\nAdds four integration cases to the existing catalog suite covering\nvetting and unvetting, with and without a manifest. Each case verifies\nthe initial default, changes the setting through the admin API, runs the\nreal registration service''s catalog upsert, and reads the setting back\nthrough the admin API. No mocks are added.\n\nValidation:\n- Formatting, non-type-aware lint, and `git diff --check` pass.\n- Integration execution was attempted but stopped while loading the Jest\nconfiguration because this worktree cannot resolve `dotenv` and\n`ts-jest`; no test cases ran.\n- Full type validation remains incomplete: type-aware lint could not\nlocate `tsgolint`, and the direct type check was stopped after producing\nno output.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25725?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"0ca60be217622d7460f54d0297ff2bdd91d5c23f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/0ca60be217622d7460f54d0297ff2bdd91d5c23f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/2e5dd38ddf4bf8b91db496b988323ac99555b16e","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ca60be217622d7460f54d0297ff2bdd91d5c23f\nparent 6b8f454b445b1c45173257d9313d2c6a0682e9cb\nauthor nitin <142569587+ehconitin@users.noreply.github.com> 1789047663 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789047663 +0000\n\nfix(apps): preserve vetted status during catalog sync (#25725)\n\nCatalog sync currently resets an admin''s Vetted choice to match the\nhardcoded marketplace list. For example, manually vetting an app outside\nthat list succeeds, but a later sync clears the setting.\n\nPreserve the stored `isVetted` value in both existing-registration\nupdate paths, and apply the hardcoded default only when creating a\nregistration. No UI changes or database migration are needed.\n\nAdds four integration cases to the existing catalog suite covering\nvetting and unvetting, with and without a manifest. Each case verifies\nthe initial default, changes the setting through the admin API, runs the\nreal registration service''s catalog upsert, and reads the setting back\nthrough the admin API. No mocks are added.\n\nValidation:\n- Formatting, non-type-aware lint, and `git diff --check` pass.\n- Integration execution was attempted but stopped while loading the Jest\nconfiguration because this worktree cannot resolve `dotenv` and\n`ts-jest`; no test cases ran.\n- Full type validation remains incomplete: type-aware lint could not\nlocate `tsgolint`, and the direct type check was stopped after producing\nno output.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25725?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqorN/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXnUQABka5SDDyLIwEApCFdzk74lc\nD1ovA/HMc9c1e2pmDaXJn4pM6Hec6SGgn9xAxQNuKGja/4ltIhC4gpAGkv4NhI+A\nYU2a8q1+vP4WxHX1gKw6VDjDRIeXbI20o9wu/CDeAq7LDVjG6ZXxzTWAIgEa2hGI\n5Z3fazxjbtRxiLqIAENB+IJZvsHQ0Zsrj6kDL1JYosmgIhKjaPmFcx5FhsZw9FDc\nYlt7Fqhx2r1x7NuuiLqTcAvxJf1y/su1YDIgJwQXEz5C8XCtC7FkbRUBfwkXRpkJ\nW92RWDAMPkUQS1MP2y0mx5/LV+snpOls+5YGy34vYoNV5kZV2qKKgB0pEE+SK7YD\nmcXayCVGv7KUzUG02SmEJ1HlHh3fuad9M8FTV1F7rkz1ZsoBfYY7baFEQh313d1M\nfL7wgzGjKG9JoJFGk87P7X8ovI0UplmYc8yG0a+xHX03n4ul5DAHevNpyMBsNU1R\nZm+y81rAxlZRvHwPKqVgfKRfWqIQvKVogwEHZqDm5Lbq634xezqULO47ygNSGAX8\nQdEg8i9vtA78G3uPNQoZ/C2fpOH5umAMSICvusI+9FIs7/oTVbSjqL+vrh4fnDRQ\nM5itTjQsXbv36P5jVF5seFzkQZ89ghZt2oOj/+EMsatrpQdvc1IMEvUs3J+iOD2F\nD9uX436B5CZe3sOR3rR2\n=CSp1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/2e5dd38ddf4bf8b91db496b988323ac99555b16e","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDJlNWRkMzhkZGY0YmY4YjkxZGI0OTZiOTg4MzIzYWM5OTU1NWIxNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/6b8f454b445b1c45173257d9313d2c6a0682e9cb","sha":"6b8f454b445b1c45173257d9313d2c6a0682e9cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/6b8f454b445b1c45173257d9313d2c6a0682e9cb"}],"sha":"2e5dd38ddf4bf8b91db496b988323ac99555b16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/2e5dd38ddf4bf8b91db496b988323ac99555b16e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81605929?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulrahmancodes","id":81605929,"login":"abdulrahmancodes","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNjA1OTI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/6b8f454b445b1c45173257d9313d2c6a0682e9cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:30:56Z","email":"81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdul Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:30:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Resolve Slack mention tokens before the assistant prompt is built (#25694)\n\n## Problem\n\nWhen someone writes `@twenty create a follow-up task for @alice`, the\nagent receives Alice as a raw `<@U04ABC>` token with no glossary and no\nway to resolve it.\n\n`normalizeSlackRequestText` only calls `stripSlackBotMention`, which\nremoves the bot''s own mention; every other mention token survives\nverbatim into `requestText`. Replayed history has the same problem,\nsince `buildSlackConversationMessages` formats authors as `<@userid>:\ntext`. The agent has no escape hatch either: `slack-assistant.role.ts`\ngrants read on `workspaceMember` but not on `slackUserLink`, so it\ncannot map an id to a member even if it tried.\n\nPrinting the messages actually handed to the agent:\n\n```\nREQUEST TEXT >>> create a follow-up task for <@U04ABC> about <#C0GEN|general>\nAGENT SEES >>> [\n  { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"<@U04ABC>: I own Acme\" },\n  { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"...Dana asks from Slack:\\ncreate a follow-up task for <@U04ABC> about <#C0GEN|general>\" }\n]\n```\n\n## Change\n\nThe worker rewrites mention tokens in the live request and in the\nreplayed history before building the prompt.\n\n| Case | Substitution |\n| --- | --- |\n| Membership confirmed | `@Alice Martin (workspace member 8f3a…)` |\n| Named, membership not confirmed | `@Bob Lee (membership not\nconfirmed)` |\n| Slack cannot identify them | `@unknown Slack user U04ABC` |\n| The assistant itself | `you` |\n| History author | `@Alice Martin:` — name only |\n\nChannel references (`<#C123|general>` → `#general`), user groups\n(`<!subteam^S01|@sales>` → `@sales`) and broadcasts (`<!here>` →\n`@here`) are decoded from the token itself with no lookup. Slack link\nsyntax `<https://…|label>` is left alone.\n\n**Membership is only ever claimed, never denied.** The app can learn\nthat a member is confirmed; it cannot learn that someone is not one. So\nan unconfirmed mention says exactly that, and the glossary tells the\nagent to search by name and to report that it could not confirm who they\nare, rather than announcing that they are not a member.\n\n**A history author is not a mention.** Naming who spoke needs a display\nname, not a member id the agent is told to act on, so authors carry no\nmembership claim and do not pull the glossary into the prompt on their\nown.\n\n### Design notes\n\n**Trust policy is shared with run-as.** A mention resolves a member by\nthe same rules as `resolveSlackRunAsWorkspaceMemberId`: a hand-picked\nconsented link is authoritative (and one naming nobody settles the\nquestion), and everything else re-earns its member from the account''s\nlive verified email, so a stale `AUTO` row cannot name the wrong\nassignee for a write-capable agent. `isManualConsentedSlackUserLink` and\n`isLinkableSlackIdentity` hold those two decisions for both paths.\n\n**Links are keyed by the mentioned user''s own Slack team.** The manual\nlink flow deliberately stores a guest''s or Slack Connect member''s own\nteam id, so grouping mentions by `team_id` before querying the composite\nkey is what makes an external member resolve instead of appearing\nunlinked.\n\n**Placement.** `resolveSlackRunAsForRequest` compares the normalized\nstored `requestText` against the live Slack message text to decide\nwhether the requester''s permissions apply. Rewriting mentions any\nearlier silently breaks that equality check and every request falls back\nto the app''s own role, so the call sits after run-as resolution in the\nworker. Moving it back above `resolveSlackRunAsForRequest` reintroduces\nthat bug, and no test would point at the cause.\n\n**Cost.** Lookups are batched: one link query across all teams, one\nemail revalidation query, one member-name query, and bounded\n`users.info` calls. A request with no mentions and no history makes no\nextra calls; a threaded follow-up still resolves its authors'' names,\nwhich is what naming them requires. The whole resolution is raced\nagainst a short timeout so a slow Slack or Core API cannot eat the\nagent''s budget.\n\nNo role changes were needed: the default function role already reads\n`slackUserLink` and `workspaceMember`.\n\n**Merged with main.** #25700 landed a `runWithTimeout` helper while this\nbranch carried an equivalent `racePromiseAgainstTimeout`. This branch\ndrops its own and uses `runWithTimeout`, so the package keeps one\ntimeout helper rather than two.\n\n### Deliberately not in this PR\n\nReviewers raised moving the identity mapping out of the request prose\ninto a structured higher-trust channel with opaque references, folding\nresolution into one typed domain service that also carries provenance,\nand adding an agent-level eval proving hostile names and forged labels\nare ignored. All three are worth doing and are a change of their own;\nwhat this PR shares is the policy, which is what let the two resolvers\ndisagree.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Unit tests for token rewriting, the batched multi-team link query, and\nlabel resolution: confirmed member, unconfirmed, unknown, a deleted\nmember, the lookup cap, Slack unreachable, an unresolvable installed\nteam, and hostile display names.\n- Regression tests for the three trust cases: a stale `AUTO` link is\nrevalidated rather than trusted, a pending or declined manual link keeps\nthe member''s own email match, and a consented link naming nobody does\nnot fall back to an email match.\n- Regression tests for Slack Connect: the multi-team filter shape, a\nlink stored under an external team, and the guard that an external or\nrestricted account still cannot resolve a member by email.\n- The worker integration test drives an unlinked mention, an\nunresolvable one and a channel reference end to end and asserts no raw\ntoken reaches the agent.\n\n`yarn lint`, `yarn typecheck`, 716 unit tests and 59 integration tests\nagainst a live local server all pass.","tree":{"sha":"9f100e336dad69fa681ef2941c8d9e9d60e92d09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/9f100e336dad69fa681ef2941c8d9e