), user groups\n(`<!subteam^S01|@sales>` → `@sales`) and broadcasts (`<!here>` →\n`@here`) are decoded from the token itself with no lookup. Slack link\nsyntax `<https://…|label>` is left alone.\n\n**Membership is only ever claimed, never denied.** The app can learn\nthat a member is confirmed; it cannot learn that someone is not one. So\nan unconfirmed mention says exactly that, and the glossary tells the\nagent to search by name and to report that it could not confirm who they\nare, rather than announcing that they are not a member.\n\n**A history author is not a mention.** Naming who spoke needs a display\nname, not a member id the agent is told to act on, so authors carry no\nmembership claim and do not pull the glossary into the prompt on their\nown.\n\n### Design notes\n\n**Trust policy is shared with run-as.** A mention resolves a member by\nthe same rules as `resolveSlackRunAsWorkspaceMemberId`: a hand-picked\nconsented link is authoritative (and one naming nobody settles the\nquestion), and everything else re-earns its member from the account''s\nlive verified email, so a stale `AUTO` row cannot name the wrong\nassignee for a write-capable agent. `isManualConsentedSlackUserLink` and\n`isLinkableSlackIdentity` hold those two decisions for both paths.\n\n**Links are keyed by the mentioned user''s own Slack team.** The manual\nlink flow deliberately stores a guest''s or Slack Connect member''s own\nteam id, so grouping mentions by `team_id` before querying the composite\nkey is what makes an external member resolve instead of appearing\nunlinked.\n\n**Placement.** `resolveSlackRunAsForRequest` compares the normalized\nstored `requestText` against the live Slack message text to decide\nwhether the requester''s permissions apply. Rewriting mentions any\nearlier silently breaks that equality check and every request falls back\nto the app''s own role, so the call sits after run-as resolution in the\nworker. Moving it back above `resolveSlackRunAsForRequest` reintroduces\nthat bug, and no test would point at the cause.\n\n**Cost.** Lookups are batched: one link query across all teams, one\nemail revalidation query, one member-name query, and bounded\n`users.info` calls. A request with no mentions and no history makes no\nextra calls; a threaded follow-up still resolves its authors'' names,\nwhich is what naming them requires. The whole resolution is raced\nagainst a short timeout so a slow Slack or Core API cannot eat the\nagent''s budget.\n\nNo role changes were needed: the default function role already reads\n`slackUserLink` and `workspaceMember`.\n\n**Merged with main.** #25700 landed a `runWithTimeout` helper while this\nbranch carried an equivalent `racePromiseAgainstTimeout`. This branch\ndrops its own and uses `runWithTimeout`, so the package keeps one\ntimeout helper rather than two.\n\n### Deliberately not in this PR\n\nReviewers raised moving the identity mapping out of the request prose\ninto a structured higher-trust channel with opaque references, folding\nresolution into one typed domain service that also carries provenance,\nand adding an agent-level eval proving hostile names and forged labels\nare ignored. All three are worth doing and are a change of their own;\nwhat this PR shares is the policy, which is what let the two resolvers\ndisagree.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Unit tests for token rewriting, the batched multi-team link query, and\nlabel resolution: confirmed member, unconfirmed, unknown, a deleted\nmember, the lookup cap, Slack unreachable, an unresolvable installed\nteam, and hostile display names.\n- Regression tests for the three trust cases: a stale `AUTO` link is\nrevalidated rather than trusted, a pending or declined manual link keeps\nthe member''s own email match, and a consented link naming nobody does\nnot fall back to an email match.\n- Regression tests for Slack Connect: the multi-team filter shape, a\nlink stored under an external team, and the guard that an external or\nrestricted account still cannot resolve a member by email.\n- The worker integration test drives an unlinked mention, an\nunresolvable one and a channel reference end to end and asserts no raw\ntoken reaches the agent.\n\n`yarn lint`, `yarn typecheck`, 716 unit tests and 59 integration tests\nagainst a live local server all pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqorEgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfD8QAIMWF4m72AQSlq5zEA2pE969\nnAeWvZj6NXmDOb2Y9ENzHrGkmQEFwAWsE9xiJF76Q6aihQOASjrW6LapC5c5TbAO\nGreVOEFxVZLYzabF53Xx6/S1JKHsoUh2mmYRqZChQVX/nFq0ZpE2ESpwI7Pq5EM/\nEk88URALRD6u3wVJ4bjByjM5R2GbJXLUthTF4BCvzJp9K84x+TEm47ASahTK/927\nGucCBCgR31+rHqJf9gYKqDY3xXu/vjAfTXw5SA4VB7kUOfF+bZWkysIu7zqXy0em\nMEGO0220z+psw3DygjOIEhpArfophQQXO++tUeG9NTYGnJq/Ku9AkOvGRZ1h92VX\nih1Olw0APfQkQ7qhz8JxXrhB93dn9szFrt4zYZhptWTR8zu3lyQqo9FfCtlxpUCQ\nh9rm0ehBuIPfpoIfTuWDAjeyXfxfsOYz2b+9ExL6kBGfxUJX1vZ/Yzu8EEnUtkRk\nIRoBf5/U/u9pwB3yX+CUa4A55lx1DB40jGdS49ojBlez/i/VMzDTIYduhI6NB1Jm\np0+rAnUak0o2DXT+FKuXJhFWStjXg6DgL2gzMGNzSPQxpqDDchK+k5Pi14B9qfjG\noUYX1UxrN1YGwLA66gmjcE/9Y2G+f/Jf1L6KL3VQsvTKTvTn702z8gWA3Knx+2xN\nmlKHtZeOM6i6loKqLOB1\n=y5vY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/6b8f454b445b1c45173257d9313d2c6a0682e9cb","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDZiOGY0NTRiNDQ1YjFjNDUxNzMyNTdkOTMxM2QyYzZhMDY4MmU5Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/da9870e4b7cf37cf2b90ecfbd0e117f9627ca100","sha":"da9870e4b7cf37cf2b90ecfbd0e117f9627ca100","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/da9870e4b7cf37cf2b90ecfbd0e117f9627ca100"}],"sha":"6b8f454b445b1c45173257d9313d2c6a0682e9cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/6b8f454b445b1c45173257d9313d2c6a0682e9cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20565303?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NiklasDah","id":20565303,"login":"NiklasDah","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTY1MzAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NiklasDah","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/da9870e4b7cf37cf2b90ecfbd0e117f9627ca100/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:21:36Z","email":"n@ni-da.de","name":"Niklas Dahmen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:21:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix AWS region validation across partitions (#25720)\n\nTwenty rejects valid region names such as `eusc-de-east-1` and\n`us-gov-west-1` during configuration validation. The existing regex\nrejects 10 of the 46 regions listed in AWS''s partition data, including\nEuropean Sovereign Cloud, GovCloud, and ISO regions.\n\nExpand the format check to accept longer prefixes and an extra name\nsegment. Allow multi-digit region numbers to match AWS''s own format\nrules. The shared decorator covers Lambda, Lambda layer bucket, and SES\nregion settings.\n\nAdd inline regression cases for one region from each of the eight\npartitions in [AWS''s\npartitions.json](https://github.com/boto/botocore/blob/e3ae2081184335ff69687f8dacc798e58715af1d/botocore/data/partitions.json),\nplus tests for malformed names and multi-digit numbers.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25720?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"74c96f129a205ee52c6cd594e17bdd07b1950bc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/74c96f129a205ee52c6cd594e17bdd07b1950bc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/da9870e4b7cf37cf2b90ecfbd0e117f9627ca100","verification":{"payload":"tree 74c96f129a205ee52c6cd594e17bdd07b1950bc0\nparent aea02a5aa08099c7681d820a3b99a9aba10573d1\nauthor Niklas Dahmen <n@ni-da.de> 1789046496 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789046496 +0200\n\nFix AWS region validation across partitions (#25720)\n\nTwenty rejects valid region names such as `eusc-de-east-1` and\n`us-gov-west-1` during configuration validation. The existing regex\nrejects 10 of the 46 regions listed in AWS''s partition data, including\nEuropean Sovereign Cloud, GovCloud, and ISO regions.\n\nExpand the format check to accept longer prefixes and an extra name\nsegment. Allow multi-digit region numbers to match AWS''s own format\nrules. The shared decorator covers Lambda, Lambda layer bucket, and SES\nregion settings.\n\nAdd inline regression cases for one region from each of the eight\npartitions in [AWS''s\npartitions.json](https://github.com/boto/botocore/blob/e3ae2081184335ff69687f8dacc798e58715af1d/botocore/data/partitions.json),\nplus tests for malformed names and multi-digit numbers.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25720?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoq7gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHvcQAC1iq16AP2DWGegi/kRKva5g\n09X8x4iuPCwfj0V8s5Ldu0OsnUXB8vARlErOA19Mvy5y1QjbRL9Yplx/bxyY4v1s\nGakbZsNrNcPaiZCMIW7OmjlcEkt/y/dIDKt5H23YKNRyaNFBpIhHLfhW463LDdRf\nqLhV76edUy8vV+845slCJ5fHLByEUUjD8DQ3IbPEkSbcnCDEqMh0sgJs6f38sgxF\nKHiJ1kIVZN1zptltVZWwg2TsPnDSrJMNeYn8hEmW9zIYVFN1nB4wbVAF1aD/6BDz\nOUmEomeQh3oyQjdswgRJV4T8NhdmTUffe38Mp46A9Vm6T9pDjnuBowAp48yImLDS\nP18q/lFL3jmAJ1lh4Pq6gjZYd9ttV5TokM7Y8qe/Jap/2nQIVbXq6K8Dn3YUfmIV\nLSpl82MlhgcboJpOj9fHCD