7ba802"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62795688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/neo773","id":62795688,"login":"neo773","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzk1Njg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/ad72bbaa09e65e116e99214fd3e53dfc30467cba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:06:30Z","email":"62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com","name":"neo773"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:06:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop servicing webhook subscriptions for suspended workspaces (#25657)\n\nEvery sync cron scopes its work to active workspaces, but the webhook\ningress did not. A suspended workspace kept its provider subscriptions\nand kept being pushed to, so its channels parked in a stage no cron\nwould ever drain and every notification failed. In prod that left 160\ncalendar channels stuck for up to 12 days, all of them in suspended\nworkspaces, while 518 calendar and 512 message channels still held a\nlive subscription.\n\nSuspension already funnels through `WorkspaceService.suspendWorkspace`,\nso it emits an event and the webhook module listens, rather than a cron\nrediscovering the same state change every hour. `reactivateWorkspace`\nemits the mirror event and the same listener recreates the subscriptions\nsuspension expired.\n\nScope is `SUSPENDED` only. `PROVISIONED_WORKSPACE_ACTIVATION_STATUSES`\nis `[CREATED, ACTIVE, SUSPENDED]`, so `INACTIVE` means never provisioned\nrather than switched off, and `CREATED` is mid-onboarding and still\nneeds to create subscriptions.\n\nIndependent of #25656 — either can merge first.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25657?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"8754da30633447cba923a0adbac580939f7548a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/8754da30633447cba923a0adbac580939f7548a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/ad72bbaa09e65e116e99214fd3e53dfc30467cba","verification":{"payload":"tree 8754da30633447cba923a0adbac580939f7548a7\nparent cda10bebf0a7d409043dcf99646036a9601254b4\nauthor neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com> 1789045590 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789045590 +0000\n\nStop servicing webhook subscriptions for suspended workspaces (#25657)\n\nEvery sync cron scopes its work to active workspaces, but the webhook\ningress did not. A suspended workspace kept its provider subscriptions\nand kept being pushed to, so its channels parked in a stage no cron\nwould ever drain and every notification failed. In prod that left 160\ncalendar channels stuck for up to 12 days, all of them in suspended\nworkspaces, while 518 calendar and 512 message channels still held a\nlive subscription.\n\nSuspension already funnels through `WorkspaceService.suspendWorkspace`,\nso it emits an event and the webhook module listens, rather than a cron\nrediscovering the same state change every hour. `reactivateWorkspace`\nemits the mirror event and the same listener recreates the subscriptions\nsuspension expired.\n\nScope is `SUSPENDED` only. `PROVISIONED_WORKSPACE_ACTIVATION_STATUSES`\nis `[CREATED, ACTIVE, SUSPENDED]`, so `INACTIVE` means never provisioned\nrather than switched off, and `CREATED` is mid-onboarding and still\nneeds to create subscriptions.\n\nIndependent of #25656 — either can merge first.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25657?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoqtnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7aYQADankw57S4o9eirKUDzjaM1e\nBhY+OQbo2lYsbhZYc7LdfpudvOEHnubd362t8ylr4lXj88Nib4Vp0ee+g0UpWCTk\npXZHUlp0x7ayOcA8P8JPNfFkAUCZtbfnw7cRN6C+iMGJ0b77qH5RfZHZ/L30v/I+\n2nbIt/1fYpflkTXftoPpNOKCjq6Z8A61m2OdllfizTqmy4fMAaaIO4Ton2s8cr50\nb7OW9zidG+CYDpkq1xUYHpxRoHzuA66KL6z7v6FnhZ0NE1R1f+VHWORyolZ5fGh+\nKnGgRGQng3xevg92/XTRPcDqMZ6QFn64zuIOUaQU0CuxaClUr/Bo3mdk+3AhnMZl\nagGjrdB77DRZKmz/+PD61jL3Bnz1FFhw7rmlElG80B+1+jfyjN3qfY6M2d5qpPwB\n3V2TBhhWHxCR1W5PYRIy5P5sJMqQrcDA4GNp6mMIC2nP8NwO+tw/aVDezHI+kuoC\n6x30kdQRfzm2SSIZc34ar9SNdXNgPeQsAsgpMBT6/Sa2JTi/jKwQ/gJWpISjc8Wx\nVJLani52J4icOmRT3vhhdOC5RQhWDsUSY/AMlun3G/zqhBk6eRRFJm765t1eU6G/\nZz6To9x0yxFMJF7MOy9bO/BLMSjNsRIqjMcL6GU5P9dWjNADp7kTr/eTGHg622VQ\nCLVTKPoFV+8w1m9fcz1P\n=1RYL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/ad72bbaa09e65e116e99214fd3e53dfc30467cba","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGFkNzJiYmFhMDllNjVlMTE2ZTk5MjE0ZmQzZTUzZGZjMzA0NjdjYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/cda10bebf0a7d409043dcf99646036a9601254b4","sha":"cda10bebf0a7d409043dcf99646036a9601254b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/cda10bebf0a7d409043dcf99646036a9601254b4"}],"sha":"ad72bbaa09e65e116e99214fd3e53dfc30467cba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/ad72bbaa09e65e116e99214fd3e53dfc30467cba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62795688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/neo773","id":62795688,"login":"neo773","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzk1Njg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/cda10bebf0a7d409043dcf99646036a9601254b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:46:18Z","email":"62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com","name":"neo773"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:46:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Accept CalDAV calendars that do not publish a component set (#25729)\n\nFixes #25683\n\nRFC 4791 §5.2.3 makes `supported-calendar-component-set` optional, and\nstates that in its absence the server accepts every component type.\nTwenty read an absent set as \"VEVENT unsupported\", so connecting a\nPurelymail account failed with `No calendar with event support found`.\n\ntsdav ran the same stricter filter inside `fetchCalendars` until 2.2.1,\nso the calendar never reached our filter — the range is bumped past that\nfix. A calendar that does publish a set without VEVENT is still skipped.\n\nIntegration coverage proxies Radicale (which always publishes the\nproperty) to strip it off the wire.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25729?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"f177eee7899f28fc04d337a7c0b06d0ad8597ab4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/f177eee7899f28fc04d337a7c0b06d0ad8597ab4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/cda10bebf0a7d409043dcf99646036a9601254b4","verification":{"payload":"tree f177eee7899f28fc04d337a7c0b06d0ad8597ab4\nparent eca522c2c4f98e6abed0fdba913267eb1275d0b2\nauthor neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com> 1789044378 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789044378 +0000\n\nAccept CalDAV calendars that do not publish a component set (#25729)\n\nFixes #25683\n\nRFC 4791 §5.2.3 makes `supported-calendar-component-set` optional, and\nstates that in its absence the server accepts every component type.\nTwenty read an absent set as \"VEVENT unsupported\", so connecting a\nPurelymail account failed with `No calendar with event support found`.\n\ntsdav ran the same stricter filter inside `fetchCalendars` until 2.2.1,\nso the calendar never reached our filter — the range is bumped past that\nfix. A calendar that does publish a set without VEVENT is still skipped.\n\nIntegration coverage proxies Radicale (which always publishes the\nproperty) to strip it off the wire.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25729?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoqaqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjkgQAFwQ5bo9TP7/wlB8th7M77Wf\n7syTy/HkBoArod2A1sjqQNbzfsFodYhrB+/PM7YhLhb5z3s45kSFd/5HMzfOMqXH\nk8ioPoDca/vbTMlWvOOljONUA2rsZy2zuMbWEhgqOGbodwOuVBnLwnQ1IHlwVEeb\nCn5r1hXH1lMymUbu3vl/R84m+VAtmJMInEvbw18yMA7mIEWr/8FUkhldnQ7lco+N\nrnNSD5/TmFeW2dY9P6RACcbOFCQHPMkYcgzu1lzZHsHsTZ6l7ANtQbP3hjGaiuUa\nGVpYZDEH0Vbc1sgxbnPBKofL2i3pik0GUqkP7CqJoCK6WJuY4Zt3v1GANMvqMy39\nsuXoGBA6ykjmS8K2qyv2WyIFMYv9R7s+E8yMBIXqPC61ds3mpIQzzEriaE09n9PI\ndnoh8Upy1CyHgNxY/Cqg3TOPXDt3RjJe1BQ+dKtgrU0o2WR3zj2WQYR9a8qgJWNE\nSTxa3VatVV8uKRlnKowf5mEwNX9paalXy5vi11D3s4QvF1Sv4sZkdjmAnF0uc/XG\nSj927VxkseDZUzNYk6e9rQoKLP7ho1MY666koiEVniFxRHNvh+av1h4z1YAwuB9P\nv1NJQ5XDTp7l0JjH3ANxYJu1B4GbrvCfjJNzlSXScRL5NA4d1YVR32NgztPFVHkN\nkWChhyzhBkQ1DHYEevw7\n=ub7g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/cda10bebf0a7d409043dcf99646036a9601254b4","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGNkYTEwYmViZjBhN2Q0MDkwNDNkY2Y5OTY0NjAzNmE5NjAxMjU0YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/eca522c2c4f98e6abed0fdba913267eb1275d0b2","sha":"eca522c2c4f98e6abed0fdba913267eb1275d0b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/eca522c2c4f98e6abed0fdba913267eb1275d0b2"}],"sha":"cda10bebf0a7d409043dcf99646036a9601254b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/cda10bebf0a7d409043dcf99646036a9601254b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29927851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/martmull","id":29927851,"login":"martmull","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/eca522c2c4f98e6abed0fdba913267eb1275d0b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:44:47Z","email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:44:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Revert \"Revert \"Record sharing 5/14: evaluate record shares in memory for events\"\" (#25650)\n\nReverts twentyhq/twenty#25649\n\nFifth PR of the record-sharing stack, stacked on #25428 (shareWith on\ncreate, merged). Inert while every object is OPEN or the flag is off.\n\n## What changes\n\nSubscriptions, webhooks, workflow database-event triggers and\nlogic-function database-event triggers have a record in hand and no SQL.\nFor objects whose readability is `PRIVATE`, with\n`IS_RECORD_SHARING_ENABLED` on, each consumer fetches the share rows of\nthe event batch once (`RecordShareService.findByRecordIds`) and\nevaluates the same rule as the SQL gate in memory\n(`isRecordSharedWithPrincipals`, read level):\n\n- subscriptions: the subscriber''s principals (everyone, workspace\nmember, roles), evaluated next to the existing role-predicate check; the\nowning application bypasses;\n- logic-function triggers: everyone plus the application''s default role,\nthe owning application bypasses;\n- workflow triggers: everyone plus the role the run would execute with\n(the standard application''s default role, else admin), objects owned by\nthe standard application bypass, matching the execution context;\n- webhooks: everyone only, since a webhook carries no identity.\n\n`SYSTEM` and `APPLICATION` readability are mirrored the same way\n(`resolveRecordShareGateKind`): denied for everyone, or for every\nconsumer but the owning application.\n\n## Known gaps\n\n- Nested-relation hydration in subscription payloads still runs under\nthe writer''s context, so related `PRIVATE` records are gated with the\nwriter''s principals (no gate when the writer is a system context).\nFixing it needs a subscriber auth context rebuilt from the stream''s\nserializable one; it is tracked as a follow-up.\n- Webhooks and workflow triggers still do not evaluate role predicates;\nonly the share rule is wired, as the plan states.\n- Timeline activities and the audit log keep persisting the event diff\nas before.\n- `INHERITED` objects (#25439) are treated as open by the in-memory\nrule; the timeline guard (#25454) is where a private note''s linked\nrecords get gated in memory.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Unit: the memory rule over a fixture table, and the gate kind per\nreadability and ownership; one PRIVATE case in each existing consumer\nspec (unshared record dropped, shared record passes).\n- Integration\n`record-share-twin-object-records-permissions.integration-spec.ts`: over\nthe same share rows, `findMany` and `updateMany` through the API return\nexactly the records the memory rule accepts, for the admin, a member,\nthe API key and everyone-only principals.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #25421 readability level (merged)\n2. #25425 recordShare object and service (merged)\n3. #25426 read and write gate (merged)\n4. #25428 shareWith on create (merged)\n5. **This PR**: in-memory twin for events (replaces #25429)\n6. #25438 call recordings PRIVATE\n7. #25439 INHERITED objects\n8. #25441 mailbox and calendar share rows (auto-closed as a stale draft,\nbranch `claude/adversarial-agents-impl-vq7601-pr9` intact)\n9. #25445 messages and calendar events PRIVATE\n10. #25443 manual sharing and ownership (server)\n11. #25446 Share action and dialog (front)\n12. #25444 sharingRule entity\n13. #25447 sharing rule metadata API\n14. #25453 rule recalculation\n15. #25454 timeline guard for private linked records\n16. #25457 Settings Sharing tab and level changes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec0e43acdff765befcd6b7181a3e6cc36e4171df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/ec0e43acdff765befcd6b7181a3e6cc36e4171df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/eca522c2c4f98e6abed0fdba913267eb1275d0b2","verification":{"payload":"tree ec0e43acdff765befcd6b7181a3e6cc36e4171df\nparent 9989ec6bca575adeba5507b3cf8a7625adcfc3a6\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1789044287 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789044287 +0000\n\nRevert \"Revert \"Record sharing 5/14: evaluate record shares in memory for events\"\" (#25650)\n\nReverts twentyhq/twenty#25649\n\nFifth PR of the record-sharing stack, stacked on #25428 (shareWith on\ncreate, merged). Inert while every object is OPEN or the flag is off.\n\n## What changes\n\nSubscriptions, webhooks, workflow database-event triggers and\nlogic-function database-event triggers have a record in hand and no SQL.\nFor objects whose readability is `PRIVATE`, with\n`IS_RECORD_SHARING_ENABLED` on, each consumer fetches the share rows of\nthe event batch once (`RecordShareService.findByRecordIds`) and\nevaluates the same rule as the SQL gate in memory\n(`isRecordSharedWithPrincipals`, read level):\n\n- subscriptions: the subscriber''s principals (everyone, workspace\nmember, roles), evaluated next to the existing role-predicate check; the\nowning application bypasses;\n- logic-function triggers: everyone plus the application''s default role,\nthe owning application bypasses;\n- workflow triggers: everyone plus the role the run would execute with\n(the standard application''s default role, else admin), objects owned by\nthe standard application bypass, matching the execution context;\n- webhooks: everyone only, since a webhook carries no identity.\n\n`SYSTEM` and `APPLICATION` readability are mirrored the same way\n(`resolveRecordShareGateKind`): denied for everyone, or for every\nconsumer but the owning application.\n\n## Known gaps\n\n- Nested-relation hydration in subscription payloads still runs under\nthe writer''s context, so related `PRIVATE` records are gated with the\nwriter''s principals (no gate when the writer is a system context).\nFixing it needs a subscriber auth context rebuilt from the stream''s\nserializable one; it is tracked as a follow-up.\n- Webhooks and workflow triggers still do not evaluate role predicates;\nonly the share rule is wired, as the plan states.\n- Timeline activities and the audit log keep persisting the event diff\nas before.\n- `INHERITED` objects (#25439) are treated as open by the in-memory\nrule; the timeline guard (#25454) is where a private note''s linked\nrecords get gated in memory.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Unit: the memory rule over a fixture table, and the gate kind per\nreadability and ownership; one PRIVATE case in each existing consumer\nspec (unshared record dropped, shared record passes).\n- Integration\n`record-share-twin-object-records-permissions.integration-spec.ts`: over\nthe same share rows, `findMany` and `updateMany` through the API return\nexactly the records the memory rule accepts, for the admin, a member,\nthe API key and everyone-only principals.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #25421 readability level (merged)\n2. #25425 recordShare object and service (merged)\n3. #25426 read and write gate (merged)\n4. #25428 shareWith on create (merged)\n5. **This PR**: in-memory twin for events (replaces #25429)\n6. #25438 call recordings PRIVATE\n7. #25439 INHERITED objects\n8. #25441 mailbox and calendar share rows (auto-closed as a stale draft,\nbranch `claude/adversarial-agents-impl-vq7601-pr9` intact)\n9. #25445 messages and calendar events PRIVATE\n10. #25443 manual sharing and ownership (server)\n11. #25446 Share action and dialog (front)\n12. #25444 sharingRule entity\n13. #25447 sharing rule metadata API\n14. #25453 rule recalculation\n15. #25454 timeline guard for private linked records\n16. #25457 Settings Sharing tab and level changes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoqZQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsEAQAFSNbG7iELXXYhU5Kb/G8b1p\nSTE23Qxt3dGyGhGSxsqMo84RRH8DKfQaeduuBZSHxEvgmb7UomnKRn9M77AKFwjs\nDRkgkYBoF2lkfugvPUrWvbPHyKynXq9Dg/WmFeRTquPibh+OuXcOzIUCoiermDUN\no2HSeWLng4374wCksTHFkxxpuA1yhwFwHyqfJYUWe9FFH9e92ryrLkUl2S+ydKuz\nIY6aXZqxlRAgmMgbwIiLLgLB/4awR4dlt46TuifRseDxuYXz/kpO6/bRxSE3A7IH\nxxvl6x0bYej5gDrNmOtAUdowvTRbdesZEx6glmltwzO7nOQGES27E/wYyjQvcrWP\nlR6oMF0de9ALvi7akQch29ejLnzSeIpAHt65RqoCQhGbDqIDLHIZltnn3CKHWWiD\n/GJdXzVJxOF2VbAQpAsBuEwZ40oyI4Bc5SCZS8qK0i0IG7J4+fKAtKh0TiBDdpw/\nMB7VZYveySqXi5Lm/LxHdlBrxg1ulGZLIhcPnjZYgrQzZVTxnx4s/4LqgU1PcCYP\nMfQebP8F0yHnMtLblN+t95gMx3KYz1fEeUzhkr3Xr+9Fj9QwXks86jzMvbUpzcc9\nX78QRUqf/a0JOeMw1pacuvsdKBeJZxGoZ8dwlzbE4aONN8Azva6jf8LXq671LLJ5\ndKGf/9FzvBpY8bUs5Ope\n=l/nt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/eca522c2c4f98e6abed0fdba913267eb1275d0b2","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGVjYTUyMmMyYzRmOThlNmFiZWQwZmRiYTkxMzI2N2ViMTI3NWQwYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/9989ec6bca575adeba5507b3cf8a7625adcfc3a6","sha":"9989ec6bca575adeba5507b3cf8a7625adcfc3a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9989ec6bca575adeba5507b3cf8a7625adcfc3a6"}],"sha":"eca522c2c4f98e6abed0fdba913267eb1275d0b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/eca522c2c4f98e6abed0fdba913267eb1275d0b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9989ec6bca575adeba5507b3cf8a7625adcfc3a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:17:25Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:17:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Score effort variants from the benchmark rows taken at their own effort (#25730)\n\nFollow-up to #25696, which made effort a model parameter but left\nbenchmarks as one reading per base model, so a pinned variant such as\n`openai/gpt-5.6-luna@low` carried none.\n\n## What was wrong\n\nArtificial Analysis publishes one row per reasoning effort (`GPT-5.6 Sol\n(max)`, `GPT-5.6 Sol (low)`, `Claude Opus 5 (Adaptive Reasoning, Max\nEffort)`). The sync erased that distinction: name normalization strips\nevery parenthesised suffix, so all of a model''s rows collided under one\nkey and the highest-scoring row won. Every committed number is therefore\nthe model''s ceiling (Claude models at max effort, GPT-5.6 at `(max)`,\nGrok at `(high)`), and the registry blanked the benchmark on variants\nbecause the ceiling was measured at another effort.\n\n## What changes\n\n- **Fetch.** Each row''s effort is parsed from its display name\n(`parseArtificialAnalysisEffort`: a bare level such as `(high)` or\n`(xhigh)`, an `X Effort` segment, or `Non-reasoning` for `none`; dates,\nfallbacks and a bare `Reasoning` name nothing). The row is filed under\nthe bare key as before, which keeps the ceiling, and also under\n`key@effort`.\n- **Match.** For each effort a model declares in its `efforts` list, the\nrow filed at that effort is read through the same candidate resolution\nthe base lookup uses (so rolling aliases still resolve). A declared\neffort with no row of its own stays blank: the ceiling was measured at\nanother effort and would overstate it.\n- **Catalog and overlay.** A model gains `benchmarkByEffort`, keyed by\neffort, and every reading now carries `effort`, the level it was\nmeasured at, so the base entry''s ceiling is labelled rather than\nimplied. The overlay nests the per-effort readings (with their aliases)\nunder the model''s existing entry; the top-level fields are unchanged, so\na consumer reading only those keeps working.\n- **Registry.** A variant now receives `benchmarkByEffort[effort]` from\nits base model, or nothing.\n- **Read-back.** When the Artificial Analysis fetch fails, the committed\noverlay is restored including its per-effort rows, so a bad run cannot\nstrip them.\n- **Coverage report.** The daily sync PR body gains a second line,\ndeclared effort variants with an index measured at their own effort, and\na collapsible list of the variants still without one. That list is where\nvocabulary gaps will show up (an effort Artificial Analysis spells in a\nway the parser does not know).\n\nSchema: `effort` is optional on `aiModelBenchmarkSchema`;\n`benchmarkByEffort` is an optional `z.partialRecord` over the effort\nenum. No migration, no GraphQL change: benchmarks are not exposed to the\nclient on main today.\n\n## What this PR does not do\n\n- **The committed JSON files are unchanged.** Filling\n`benchmarkByEffort` needs the Artificial Analysis key, which only the\ndaily sync has; a dry run here falls back to the committed overlay and\nfinds 113 declared variants with no reading, as expected. The next\nscheduled sync PR will carry the first per-effort readings.\n- Coverage will be partial by construction. Artificial Analysis spells\nefforts as `(low)`/`(medium)`/`(high)`/`(xhigh)`/`(max)` for OpenAI,\nGoogle and xAI, but its Claude rows are `Adaptive Reasoning, Max Effort`\nwith no lower efforts published, and some models have a single row.\nThose variants stay blank; the UI can show the base reading greyed with\nits `effort` label rather than inventing a number.\n- The unpinned base entry keeps the ceiling it has today. Whether it\nshould move to the provider default''s row is a product call left open on\npurpose.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 34 new or updated tests: the effort parser on the row names Artificial\nAnalysis actually publishes; per-effort filing and tie-breaking in the\nfetch; per-effort matching with rolling-alias resolution and the\nblank-rather-than-ceiling rule; catalog and overlay embedding with\nstable key order; read-back of nested readings dated when taken; overlay\nintegrity including that an effort is scored only where the model\ndeclares it. Touched suites: 18 pass, 142 tests.\n- Typecheck, oxlint and oxfmt clean on every changed file.\n- `ai-catalog-sync --dry-run --report` against live models.dev data\ncompletes and renders both gap lists.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_011LWnxYvEvLR8VBEGA6uCKV)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25730?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"893bbda255adb503ee5ec9dd2485a50d99ce47f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/893bbda255adb503ee5ec9dd2485a50d99ce47f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/9989ec6bca575adeba5507b3cf8a7625adcfc3a6","verification":{"payload":"tree 893bbda255adb503ee5ec9dd2485a50d99ce47f4\nparent d12b9e4e91261a57a6675e8181d69f3c4aa22e65\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789042645 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789042645 +0200\n\nScore effort variants from the benchmark rows taken at their own effort (#25730)\n\nFollow-up to #25696, which made effort a model parameter but left\nbenchmarks as one reading per base model, so a pinned variant such as\n`openai/gpt-5.6-luna@low` carried none.\n\n## What was wrong\n\nArtificial Analysis publishes one row per reasoning effort (`GPT-5.6 Sol\n(max)`, `GPT-5.6 Sol (low)`, `Claude Opus 5 (Adaptive Reasoning, Max\nEffort)`). The sync erased that distinction: name normalization strips\nevery parenthesised suffix, so all of a model''s rows collided under one\nkey and the highest-scoring row won. Every committed number is therefore\nthe model''s ceiling (Claude models at max effort, GPT-5.6 at `(max)`,\nGrok at `(high)`), and the registry blanked the benchmark on variants\nbecause the ceiling was measured at another effort.\n\n## What changes\n\n- **Fetch.** Each row''s effort is parsed from its display name\n(`parseArtificialAnalysisEffort`: a bare level such as `(high)` or\n`(xhigh)`, an `X Effort` segment, or `Non-reasoning` for `none`; dates,\nfallbacks and a bare `Reasoning` name nothing). The row is filed under\nthe bare key as before, which keeps the ceiling, and also under\n`key@effort`.\n- **Match.** For each effort a model declares in its `efforts` list, the\nrow filed at that effort is read through the same candidate resolution\nthe base lookup uses (so rolling aliases still resolve). A declared\neffort with no row of its own stays blank: the ceiling was measured at\nanother effort and would overstate it.\n- **Catalog and overlay.** A model gains `benchmarkByEffort`, keyed by\neffort, and every reading now carries `effort`, the level it was\nmeasured at, so the base entry''s ceiling is labelled rather than\nimplied. The overlay nests the per-effort readings (with their aliases)\nunder the model''s existing entry; the top-level fields are unchanged, so\na consumer reading only those keeps working.\n- **Registry.** A variant now receives `benchmarkByEffort[effort]` from\nits base model, or nothing.\n- **Read-back.** When the Artificial Analysis fetch fails, the committed\noverlay is restored including its per-effort rows, so a bad run cannot\nstrip them.\n- **Coverage report.** The daily sync PR body gains a second line,\ndeclared effort variants with an index measured at their own effort, and\na collapsible list of the variants still without one. That list is where\nvocabulary gaps will show up (an effort Artificial Analysis spells in a\nway the parser does not know).\n\nSchema: `effort` is optional on `aiModelBenchmarkSchema`;\n`benchmarkByEffort` is an optional `z.partialRecord` over the effort\nenum. No migration, no GraphQL change: benchmarks are not exposed to the\nclient on main today.\n\n## What this PR does not do\n\n- **The committed JSON files are unchanged.** Filling\n`benchmarkByEffort` needs the Artificial Analysis key, which only the\ndaily sync has; a dry run here falls back to the committed overlay and\nfinds 113 declared variants with no reading, as expected. The next\nscheduled sync PR will carry the first per-effort readings.\n- Coverage will be partial by construction. Artificial Analysis spells\nefforts as `(low)`/`(medium)`/`(high)`/`(xhigh)`/`(max)` for OpenAI,\nGoogle and xAI, but its Claude rows are `Adaptive Reasoning, Max Effort`\nwith no lower efforts published, and some models have a single row.\nThose variants stay blank; the UI can show the base reading greyed with\nits `effort` label rather than inventing a number.\n- The unpinned base entry keeps the ceiling it has today. Whether it\nshould move to the provider default''s row is a product call left open on\npurpose.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 34 new or updated tests: the effort parser on the row names Artificial\nAnalysis actually publishes; per-effort filing and tie-breaking in the\nfetch; per-effort matching with rolling-alias resolution and the\nblank-rather-than-ceiling rule; catalog and overlay embedding with\nstable key order; read-back of nested readings dated when taken; overlay\nintegrity including that an effort is scored only where the model\ndeclares it. Touched suites: 18 pass, 142 tests.\n- Typecheck, oxlint and oxfmt clean on every changed file.\n- `ai-catalog-sync --dry-run --report` against live models.dev data\ncompletes and renders both gap lists.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_011LWnxYvEvLR8VBEGA6uCKV)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25730?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\