39892d3c4172ece6cf5fd04c8aaac67e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:54:13Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:54:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Migrate twenty-ui Toggle to Switch (#25678)\n\nReplaces `Toggle` with Base UI''s `Switch` and migrates frontend and\nrenderer consumers to `checked` / `onCheckedChange` and `sm` / `md`\nsizes. Forwards native props, refs, uncontrolled state, and render\ncomposition; preserves dimensions and colors while adding keyboard focus\nstyling and RTL thumb movement.\n\nMoves the app-specific advanced settings control into\n`twenty-front/src/modules/ui/input/components` as\n`AdvancedSettingsSwitch`, using Linaria, theme CSS variables, and a\nlocalized default label. Updates its frontend callers, moves interaction\ncoverage alongside it, and removes it from twenty-ui''s exports and the\nshared-component gallery.\n\nRenames all on/off switch components in this migration, including\n`MenuItemSwitch`, `CommandMenuItemSwitch`,\n`FormBooleanFieldSwitchInput`, `SettingsOptionCardContentSwitch`,\n`NewFieldDefaultVisibilitySwitch`, `TwoFactorAuthenticationSwitch`,\n`ImpersonationSwitch`, and\n`SettingsAdminApplicationRegistrationGeneralSwitches`. Updates their\nfiles, props types, styles, exports, imports, stories, and test mocks.\nMenu switches now use `checked`, `onCheckedChange`, and `size` (`sm` /\n`md`), matching the underlying Switch API. Settings cards use\n`switchCentered` for alignment. Wrapper behavior is preserved.\n\nForm switches use the setting description as their accessible name and\npreserve boolean-only change callbacks. The form example uses controlled\nstate for native reset because Base UI 1.8 does not reset uncontrolled\nswitches.\n\nValidation: Switch and frontend browser stories pass, including label\nactivation, keyboard interaction, accessible naming, and wrapper\nbehavior. All 11 Switch conformance checks, direct UI/frontend/renderer\ntypechecks, changed-file lint/formatting, and the clean UI build pass.\nThe renamed menu and frontend wrapper stories and affected frontend unit\ntests pass. The rebuilt library contains no stale Toggle or Advanced\nsettings component exports.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25678?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"7d65e46348046df7f5d5675c1d21ca3c12ff642f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/7d65e46348046df7f5d5675c1d21ca3c12ff642f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/d63910e39892d3c4172ece6cf5fd04c8aaac67e1","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d65e46348046df7f5d5675c1d21ca3c12ff642f\nparent 9c4ff45eaeb29f673c4d4315e0eb699d321695d3\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1789030453 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789030453 +0000\n\nMigrate twenty-ui Toggle to Switch (#25678)\n\nReplaces `Toggle` with Base UI''s `Switch` and migrates frontend and\nrenderer consumers to `checked` / `onCheckedChange` and `sm` / `md`\nsizes. Forwards native props, refs, uncontrolled state, and render\ncomposition; preserves dimensions and colors while adding keyboard focus\nstyling and RTL thumb movement.\n\nMoves the app-specific advanced settings control into\n`twenty-front/src/modules/ui/input/components` as\n`AdvancedSettingsSwitch`, using Linaria, theme CSS variables, and a\nlocalized default label. Updates its frontend callers, moves interaction\ncoverage alongside it, and removes it from twenty-ui''s exports and the\nshared-component gallery.\n\nRenames all on/off switch components in this migration, including\n`MenuItemSwitch`, `CommandMenuItemSwitch`,\n`FormBooleanFieldSwitchInput`, `SettingsOptionCardContentSwitch`,\n`NewFieldDefaultVisibilitySwitch`, `TwoFactorAuthenticationSwitch`,\n`ImpersonationSwitch`, and\n`SettingsAdminApplicationRegistrationGeneralSwitches`. Updates their\nfiles, props types, styles, exports, imports, stories, and test mocks.\nMenu switches now use `checked`, `onCheckedChange`, and `size` (`sm` /\n`md`), matching the underlying Switch API. Settings cards use\n`switchCentered` for alignment. Wrapper behavior is preserved.\n\nForm switches use the setting description as their accessible name and\npreserve boolean-only change callbacks. The form example uses controlled\nstate for native reset because Base UI 1.8 does not reset uncontrolled\nswitches.\n\nValidation: Switch and frontend browser stories pass, including label\nactivation, keyboard interaction, accessible naming, and wrapper\nbehavior. All 11 Switch conformance checks, direct UI/frontend/renderer\ntypechecks, changed-file lint/formatting, and the clean UI build pass.\nThe renamed menu and frontend wrapper stories and affected frontend unit\ntests pass. The rebuilt library contains no stale Toggle or Advanced\nsettings component exports.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25678?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqonBFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5s0QACYt+mWHlt+jV0Bx/aJHV+YJ\nMqn/cSWVy8MucJ29lxlv7dDPqe9RcFq2AYIE1qLpJAH4cR8+jIBFvORTOnn3YZct\nE7AmqT/Jr7CDtXBxHnkmvAOZzRmnAbbGoiBEgkbhrfHNcixZmxfESjGiWoHJoyI3\nicM27E+zhMFeOLfvGfVDiEP0YfStfRUK/6Vek9bYXdirq4cnT37JX5kkHApt9dom\nbtEBcEKj7n/FuqRaEHT8tVcKHRJx5ndIJfUjNF4zScqOFbDrSQwRUadwu//hqtNf\nHrE0WudlnivgFJy2T+k5bW2+L6Fs7dpFzUFCtwF5YZj17zdhea9tl7eLAK/7rQ6q\nlPxFBK1qx+CrXGz1qQ9Tb4urcEXA5MpEZuowdbrVnnxbS70bcs6epz1GyMkWFwe+\ndJzKesqZMzGK1IRDy+pRaa5SvxHCv2+W3S0EJlZudq9MFDvM7k6ko7kHN5PTJsaS\ntDwlHzsnbKzFoVgV50wHUMDbtmtR3xx+TD5J71qpsXbpMWmiY4hAfRciiWzot351\nmdUv8Dv01NUvpYLTbSoddhH1aYGi9qewLqB1oO9LV5y8/NJgw+WfI2n7NIi1f4BB\n5iPP6gdcF20NDD2zhQ0t71DNsvPFIFBy2/ffDJcjzR71WFrorVagknkvwk0oZKke\n4i2W/XqIKH2PpwHUqFcd\n=9acm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/d63910e39892d3c4172ece6cf5fd04c8aaac67e1","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGQ2MzkxMGUzOTg5MmQzYzQxNzJlY2U2Y2Y1ZmQwNGM4YWFhYzY3ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/9c4ff45eaeb29f673c4d4315e0eb699d321695d3","sha":"9c4ff45eaeb29f673c4d4315e0eb699d321695d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9c4ff45eaeb29f673c4d4315e0eb699d321695d3"}],"sha":"d63910e39892d3c4172ece6cf5fd04c8aaac67e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/d63910e39892d3c4172ece6cf5fd04c8aaac67e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119600397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/twenty-pr-author","id":322546524,"login":"twenty-pr-author[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOEzmrXA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/twenty-pr-author%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9c4ff45eaeb29f673c4d4315e0eb699d321695d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:39:26Z","email":"322546524+twenty-pr-author[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"twenty-pr-author[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:39:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Refresh self-hosted Google default to Gemini 3.8 Flash (#25713)\n\n## Refresh the self-hosted Google default to Gemini 3.8 Flash\n\nSelf-hosters'' default model lists are hardcoded, but their catalog\n(`ai-providers.json`) is\nregenerated daily from models.dev. The Google entry in those lists had\nfallen behind what''s\nalready in that catalog — an instance whose only configured key is\nGoogle was resolving its\nchat/setup defaults to a weaker, more expensive model than a better one\nsitting right next to it.\n\n**File:**\n`packages/twenty-server/.../ai-models/utils/load-default-model-preferences.util.ts`\n\n| List | Was | Now | Why |\n|------|-----|-----|-----|\n| `DEFAULT_FAST_MODELS` | `google/gemini-3.7-flash` |\n`google/gemini-3.8-flash` | Same family, newer; idx 39.6 → 41.2, 329 →\n343 tok/s, **same price** ($0.75/$3.75). |\n| `DEFAULT_SMART_MODELS` | `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview` |\n`google/gemini-3.8-flash` | Preview is strictly dominated: idx **30.4 →\n41.2**, price **$2/$12 → $0.75/$3.75**, speed **128 → 343 tok/s**. |\n| `DEFAULT_RECOMMENDED_MODELS` | `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview` |\n`google/gemini-3.8-flash` | Same as smart — a stronger, cheaper Google\nentry in the picker. |\n\nNo catalog price values were touched. These are provider-preference id\nlists, resolved by\nfirst-available provider; `gemini-3.8-flash` is present in\n`ai-providers.json`, so every list\nstill resolves. `gemini-3.1-pro-preview` remains available in workspace\nsettings / admin.\n\n### Why 3.8-flash clears the smart/chat bar\nThe chat surface runs multi-step tool-calling with reasoning over a\nlarge context.\n`gemini-3.8-flash` has reasoning enabled, a ~1M-token context, and an\nArtificial-Analysis\nintelligence index of **41.2** — above `gpt-5.6-luna` (37.5) and\n`claude-sonnet-5` (38.4),\nboth of which we already trust on this surface. The entry it replaces\nsat at **30.4**, below\nall of them. (Benchmarks from twenty''s own `ai-model-benchmarks.json`,\nArtificial Analysis.)\n\n### Alternative rejected\nKeeping a Gemini *Pro* entry for the smart tier: there is no\ncurrent-generation Gemini Pro in\nthe catalog better than the preview — `gemini-3.1-pro-preview` (idx\n30.4) is the newest Pro, and\n`gemini-3.8-flash` beats it on intelligence, price, and speed. Flash is\nthe strongest Gemini we\ncan offer right now.\n\n### Not done here — needs a human\nThe **cloud** recommended picker (twenty-infra) still lists\n`gemini-3.1-pro-preview`, which is\ndominated by `gpt-5.6-terra` (same $2/$12, idx 42.3 vs 30.4) already in\nthat list. Swapping in\n`gemini-3.8-flash` requires adding it to the cloud catalogs first, and\nthat entry needs\n`cachedInputCostPerMillionTokens` (0.075) and `maxOutputTokens` (65536)\n— neither is in the\nmodels.dev snapshot this run was given, and the live models.dev does not\ncarry the model, so I\ncould not source those two values. Someone with Google''s pricing page\ncan finish the cloud swap.\n\n### Arrivals reviewed, no cloud action\n`gpt-6-astra` and `claude-fable-5-1` (premium frontier, $10/$50; top\ntier already covered by\n`claude-opus-5` at half the price, and both <10 days old), `grok-4.6`\n(amazon-bedrock-only,\ndev/staging, 62 tok/s — already in self-hoster lists),\n`gemini-3.7-flash` (superseded by 3.8),\nand `gemini-flash-latest` (a floating alias) were all considered and\nleft out.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25713?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\nCo-authored-by: twenty-pr-author[bot] <twenty-pr-author[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"17a3103df9e17737a193fc96adea983bc3901018","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/17a3103df9e17737a193fc96adea983bc3901018"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/9c4ff45eaeb29f673c4d4315e0eb699d321695d3","verification":{"payload":"tree 17a3103df9e17737a193fc96adea983bc3901018\nparent 9b3e4d0745065e575d8522e5ce40c39755c389ea\nauthor twenty-pr-author[bot] <322546524+twenty-pr-author[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789029566 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789029566 +0200\n\nRefresh self-hosted Google default to Gemini 3.8 Flash (#25713)\n\n## Refresh the self-hosted Google default to Gemini 3.8 Flash\n\nSelf-hosters'' default model lists are hardcoded, but their catalog\n(`ai-providers.json`) is\nregenerated daily from models.dev. The Google entry in those lists had\nfallen behind what''s\nalready in that catalog — an instance whose only configured key is\nGoogle was resolving its\nchat/setup defaults to a weaker, more expensive model than a better one\nsitting right next to it.\n\n**File:**\n`packages/twenty-server/.../ai-models/utils/load-default-model-preferences.util.ts`\n\n| List | Was | Now | Why |\n|------|-----|-----|-----|\n| `DEFAULT_FAST_MODELS` | `google/gemini-3.7-flash` |\n`google/gemini-3.8-flash` | Same family, newer; idx 39.6 → 41.2, 329 →\n343 tok/s, **same price** ($0.75/$3.75). |\n| `DEFAULT_SMART_MODELS` | `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview` |\n`google/gemini-3.8-flash` | Preview is strictly dominated: idx **30.4 →\n41.2**, price **$2/$12 → $0.75/$3.75**, speed **128 → 343 tok/s**. |\n| `DEFAULT_RECOMMENDED_MODELS` | `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview` |\n`google/gemini-3.8-flash` | Same as smart — a stronger, cheaper Google\nentry in the picker. |\n\nNo catalog price values were touched. These are provider-preference id\nlists, resolved by\nfirst-available provider; `gemini-3.8-flash` is present in\n`ai-providers.json`, so every list\nstill resolves. `gemini-3.1-pro-preview` remains available in workspace\nsettings / admin.\n\n### Why 3.8-flash clears the smart/chat bar\nThe chat surface runs multi-step tool-calling with reasoning over a\nlarge context.\n`gemini-3.8-flash` has reasoning enabled, a ~1M-token context, and an\nArtificial-Analysis\nintelligence index of **41.2** — above `gpt-5.6-luna` (37.5) and\n`claude-sonnet-5` (38.4),\nboth of which we already trust on this surface. The entry it replaces\nsat at **30.4**, below\nall of them. (Benchmarks from twenty''s own `ai-model-benchmarks.json`,\nArtificial Analysis.)\n\n### Alternative rejected\nKeeping a Gemini *Pro* entry for the smart tier: there is no\ncurrent-generation Gemini Pro in\nthe catalog better than the preview — `gemini-3.1-pro-preview` (idx\n30.4) is the newest Pro, and\n`gemini-3.8-flash` beats it on intelligence, price, and speed. Flash is\nthe strongest Gemini we\ncan offer right now.\n\n### Not done here — needs a human\nThe **cloud** recommended picker (twenty-infra) still lists\n`gemini-3.1-pro-preview`, which is\ndominated by `gpt-5.6-terra` (same $2/$12, idx 42.3 vs 30.4) already in\nthat list. Swapping in\n`gemini-3.8-flash` requires adding it to the cloud catalogs first, and\nthat entry needs\n`cachedInputCostPerMillionTokens` (0.075) and `maxOutputTokens` (65536)\n— neither is in the\nmodels.dev snapshot this run was given, and the live models.dev does not\ncarry the model, so I\ncould not source those two values. Someone with Google''s pricing page\ncan finish the cloud swap.\n\n### Arrivals reviewed, no cloud action\n`gpt-6-astra` and `claude-fable-5-1` (premium frontier, $10/$50; top\ntier already covered by\n`claude-opus-5` at half the price, and both <10 days old), `grok-4.6`\n(amazon-bedrock-only,\ndev/staging, 62 tok/s — already in self-hoster lists),\n`gemini-3.7-flash` (superseded by 3.8),\nand `gemini-flash-latest` (a floating alias) were all considered and\nleft out.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25713?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\nCo-authored-by: twenty-pr-author[bot] <twenty-pr-author[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqomy+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAew4QAA8/9fm2rOeFerycp50RjuJa\nJ6tu2vwkXH6nLyIQ5G280HCIa0sbXs7fD2K2tSRMJr0jzmIAGDb0sfbZkVoz92pB\ntJDxjqu335g4bjE2J9MrcrnJIsQIrpGtBvWA8bLxDL3kGhkYzwuhAXLBVZnLeZ4M\n1gHfjMF/ve4HLxgJ2N/mvqsZh9bl5JFOh1nzU3nMRA8kJTXJc7oo4YtXR2I+SthD\nkec/qskYNW6vHCbUyXvitrRIVfZSGEctib0LnBrazdpbiW9wdP5oMpUL1ubgnoGM\n/xn/IALIkeaCVnAQiA6VIZ6waQcd+azabniZtPzc4azdiyDxTImyFrUNsvf7334r\nLZpnyjqSWSCr0eSV+m1I2cW5v1NvSHl8u1exSyAOSGlh3vIyMpzvo/HojAzGpwKN\n730yrcdQ+pPvKejYfxeiBtxSNPRKpY0kVtfq9QbYyAKZeAUTYih6355rp+qjx0UF\nRfwIxuBUMefps+0x2ronJIdxjl6e7esGqsrEKxfZX9hs9VsGjYTq9t2FQIHEeWGB\n59v8mPCeNlfH7wNb2eXVqOZ7/SzcFC10jec3CyRt/rjGMuqdISZQaT/9KgoEMTKH\nbp5mUUf4L5uHDa4+ExkQ4SiqJnafE+8sQP89Ok1lqJe4/sh/2BLWHsDZihAj1Wpn\nqrDPVRw3yvTH6+C0B+za\n=8XjS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/9c4ff45eaeb29f673c4d4315e0eb699d321695d3","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDljNGZmNDVlYWViMjlmNjczYzRkNDMxNWUwZWI2OTlkMzIxNjk1ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/9b3e4d0745065e575d8522e5ce40c39755c389ea","sha":"9b3e4d0745065e575d8522e5ce40c39755c389ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9b3e4d0745065e575d8522e5ce40c39755c389ea"}],"sha":"9c4ff45eaeb29f673c4d4315e0eb699d321695d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9c4ff45eaeb29f673c4d4315e0eb699d321695d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45695613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9b3e4d0745065e575d8522e5ce40c39755c389ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:24:02Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:24:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(usage-limit): cap webhook calls per workspace at enqueue time (#25673)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a `WEBHOOK` speed limit to the usage-limit engine and enforces it\nwhere webhook delivery jobs are enqueued.\n\n- `UsageResourceType.WEBHOOK` / `UsageOperationType.WEBHOOK_CALL`, with\na single workspace-scoped default bucket:\n`WEBHOOK_CALL_RATE_LIMITING_LIMIT` (60) per\n`WEBHOOK_CALL_RATE_LIMITING_TTL_IN_MS` (60s). Overridable per workspace\nthrough a `usageLimit` row like every other speed limit. No server-wide\nbucket: webhook targets are customer-owned URLs, so there is no shared\ndownstream to protect.\n- `CallWebhookJobsJob` and `CallWebhookJobsForMetadataJob` run their\nfan-out through `WebhookRateLimitService` before chunking. What the\nbucket refuses is never enqueued, so the webhook queue only holds work\nthat will actually be delivered. `CallWebhookJob` is untouched.\n- The token bucket script gains partial grants: `tryConsumeUpTo` asks\nfor one slot per call in the batch and gets back how many were granted,\nin one Redis round trip and one bucket build. `tryConsume` keeps the\nall-or-nothing behaviour the API and email paths rely on, and their call\nsites are unchanged.\n- A refused call is dropped, not deferred. The trace is a single\n`logger.warn` naming the workspace, the dropped count and the limit,\nplus `job/webhook-call-throttled`, which is comparable against\n`job/webhook-call-completed`. **The workspace itself sees nothing** — a\ndropped delivery leaves no webhook-log row, by design, to avoid one row\nper dropped call.\n- Gated behind `IS_WEBHOOK_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED`. Flag off means every\nevent is admitted untouched, so shipping this changes nothing until a\nworkspace is opted in.\n\nTwo behaviours worth knowing before enabling it on a workspace:\n\n- Metadata webhooks draw from the same budget, so a large schema\nmigration spends the same 60/min as record events.\n- A fan-out job that dies mid-enqueue re-spends its tokens on the BullMQ\nretry, which under-delivers rather than double-delivers.\n\n## Why\n\nWebhook delivery is the last fan-out path with no ceiling.\n`CallWebhookJob` posts everything it is handed, and the only volume\ncontrol anywhere in the chain is a `chunk(20)` that groups calls into\njobs. One bulk import, or one integration subscribed to `*.*`, turns\ninto an unbounded burst against the customer''s endpoint and against our\noutbound capacity, with nothing a workspace or an operator can turn\ndown.\n\nThe API and email paths already went through the usage-limit speed\ntooling, so this reuses the same bucket engine, the same override table\nand the same fail-open behaviour rather than adding a second throttling\nmechanism.\n\nEnforcing at enqueue rather than at delivery matters: the fan-out job is\nthe first and only point that knows how many calls one workspace is\nabout to make, and it sits upstream of every delivery job, so refused\ncalls never enter the queue at all.\n\n## Test\n\n- New integration spec\n`test/integration/usage-limit/webhook-rate-limit.integration-spec.ts`,\nalongside the API one: flag on, a workspace override of 2 calls per 60s,\na real receiver, five records created in a burst, exactly two deliveries\nland and stay at two. Not run locally, first execution is CI.\n- No unit spec on `WebhookRateLimitService`: it is a DI service whose\nlogic is one `tryConsumeUpTo` call and a slice, so per the backend\ntesting convention it is covered by the integration test rather than by\na mock-heavy service spec.\n- `usage-limit-speed.service.spec.ts` is unchanged and still passes: the\nscript''s return contract stayed compatible, granted count replaces the\nadmitted flag.\n- `oxlint`, `oxfmt` and `tsgo --noEmit` clean on `twenty-server` and\n`twenty-shared`; GraphQL artifacts regenerated (metadata, admin, sdk\nclient).","tree":{"sha":"a90740bab3463fa60b8a4ddf38fe2feaa8cda0a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/a90740bab3463fa60b8a4ddf38fe2feaa8cda0a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/9b3e4d0745065e575d8522e5ce40c39755c389ea","verification":{"payload":"tree a90740bab3463fa60b8a4ddf38fe2feaa8cda0a8\nparent 8500b16fd4842017ed617f926bae3ff13e34db53\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1789028642 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789028642 +0000\n\nfeat(usage-limit): cap webhook calls per workspace at enqueue time (#25673)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a `WEBHOOK` speed limit to the usage-limit engine and enforces it\nwhere webhook delivery jobs are enqueued.\n\n- `UsageResourceType.WEBHOOK` / `UsageOperationType.WEBHOOK_CALL`, with\na single workspace-scoped default bucket:\n`WEBHOOK_CALL_RATE_LIMITING_LIMIT` (60) per\n`WEBHOOK_CALL_RATE_LIMITING_TTL_IN_MS` (60s). Overridable per workspace\nthrough a `usageLimit` row like every other speed limit. No server-wide\nbucket: webhook targets are customer-owned URLs, so there is no shared\ndownstream to protect.\n- `CallWebhookJobsJob` and `CallWebhookJobsForMetadataJob` run their\nfan-out through `WebhookRateLimitService` before chunking. What the\nbucket refuses is never enqueued, so the webhook queue only holds work\nthat will actually be delivered. `CallWebhookJob` is untouched.\n- The token bucket script gains partial grants: `tryConsumeUpTo` asks\nfor one slot per call in the batch and gets back how many were granted,\nin one Redis round trip and one bucket build. `tryConsume` keeps the\nall-or-nothing behaviour the API and email paths rely on, and their call\nsites are unchanged.\n- A refused call is dropped, not deferred. The trace is a single\n`logger.warn` naming the workspace, the dropped count and the limit,\nplus `job/webhook-call-throttled`, which is comparable against\n`job/webhook-call-completed`. **The workspace itself sees nothing** — a\ndropped delivery leaves no webhook-log row, by design, to avoid one row\nper dropped call.\n- Gated behind `IS_WEBHOOK_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED`. Flag off means every\nevent is admitted untouched, so shipping this changes nothing until a\nworkspace is opted in.\n\nTwo behaviours worth knowing before enabling it on a workspace:\n\n- Metadata webhooks draw from the same budget, so a large schema\nmigration spends the same 60/min as record events.\n- A fan-out job that dies mid-enqueue re-spends its tokens on the BullMQ\nretry, which under-delivers rather than double-delivers.\n\n## Why\n\nWebhook delivery is the last fan-out path with no ceiling.\n`CallWebhookJob` posts everything it is handed, and the only volume\ncontrol anywhere in the chain is a `chunk(20)` that groups calls into\njobs. One bulk import, or one integration subscribed to `*.*`, turns\ninto an unbounded burst against the customer''s endpoint and against our\noutbound capacity, with nothing a workspace or an operator can turn\ndown.\n\nThe API and email paths already went through the usage-limit speed\ntooling, so this reuses the same bucket engine, the same override table\nand the same fail-open behaviour rather than adding a second throttling\nmechanism.\n\nEnforcing at enqueue rather than at delivery matters: the fan-out job is\nthe first and only point that knows how many calls one workspace is\nabout to make, and it sits upstream of every delivery job, so refused\ncalls never enter the queue at all.\n\n## Test\n\n- New integration spec\n`test/integration/usage-limit/webhook-rate-limit.integration-spec.ts`,\nalongside the API one: flag on, a workspace override of 2 calls per 60s,\na real receiver, five records created in a burst, exactly two deliveries\nland and stay at two. Not run locally, first execution is CI.\n- No unit spec on `WebhookRateLimitService`: it is a DI service whose\nlogic is one `tryConsumeUpTo` call and a slice, so per the backend\ntesting convention it is covered by the integration test rather than by\na mock-heavy service spec.\n- `usage-limit-speed.service.spec.ts` is unchanged and still passes: the\nscript''s return contract stayed compatible, granted count replaces the\nadmitted flag.\n- `oxlint`, `oxfmt` and `tsgo --noEmit` clean on `twenty-server` and\n`twenty-shared`; GraphQL artifacts regenerated (metadata, admin, sdk\nclient).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqomkyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1/IQAFxkhMuicpp2cd48fNvkKA43\nZIVLxnDbGLky7qvYHm7jay+UUAJ5XKjBvk8OWLv1uf3xt6LIDT5oAbg80oVUNdT7\nYkx4FW521+ngasOiY242ro3coF+F3txRA+rykyeNbzJlZl6hfMvHFPLHOQXcznNx\nqQwMUcISGXTo6gy6QlJkSzZArjDt8WhnvC/fkVFiI+EqgKYH5pL4ki3f1kMyVSrL\noxw937mgbpr3V7W8ubjcQ4D4t8+8dk2bm/JL4VhpGCgq8gSE7GHHvoYxjLXorAjQ\nY/f2nuJma1ZcHrJ3tPvFxtKQI1rpoU3T48LDEJngIWJ2LWYZ4ZW/1UfSvmXBr0Ah\nZck+isnodxz3TGWoeMKEeRvvW9N43Gjun8SHuhq37B76IJB21Tqr326j58iYXh8w\nT9DrTa6TVfjnycuiX0ZRCs6WCK6iR2Js59j5z/YCBvkkuD6ZhuiiuIv5WASKqpyP\nbfcDg/lT8DngvI+iwHLQXcwm5Kcj8jub2I/cn/51qyMJjgHkgjuchDbcny8Xu8FE\nl/V5zd/zbEO7fjYbz+nB8r6g5mYtFzJ06nrYlQEW+lk497InFRkuXJkBxFCpbLuc\nPY1g6Hb4ZLtf3D96fgBAMQ1+TTMF1yEELPO39VsvLp4Jx42yw8ADjMOmpsvCDF1I\nwk9gYtIYiYj77IunSzqQ\n=V6aR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/9b3e4d0745065e575d8522e5ce40c39755c389ea","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDliM2U0ZDA3NDUwNjVlNTc1ZDg1MjJlNWNlNDBjMzk3NTVjMzg5ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/8500b16fd4842017ed617f926bae3ff13e34db53","sha":"8500b16fd4842017ed617f926bae3ff13e34db53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8500b16fd4842017ed617f926bae3ff13e34db53"}],"sha":"9b3e4d0745065e575d8522e5ce40c39755c389ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9b3e4d0745065e575d8522e5ce40c39755c389ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8500b16fd4842017ed617f926bae3ff13e34db53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:18:13Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:18:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade the AI SDK to v7 (#25704)\n\nStacked on #25696 until it merged (squash `8fc71f4f`); the base is\n`main` now and the branch carries a merge of main, so the diff below is\nthe upgrade alone.\n\n## What moves\n\n| package | from | to |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ai` (server, shared, front) | 6.0.97 | 7.0.93 |\n| `@ai-sdk/anthropic` | ^3.0.83 | ^4.0.49 |\n| `@ai-sdk/openai` | ^3.0.70 | ^4.0.60 |\n| `@ai-sdk/azure` | ^3.0.55 | ^4.0.63 |\n| `@ai-sdk/google` | ^3.0.81 | ^4.0.64 |\n| `@ai-sdk/mistral` | ^3.0.38 | ^4.0.39 |\n| `@ai-sdk/xai` | ^3.0.94 | ^4.0.54 |\n| `@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock` | ^4.0.116 | ^5.0.76 |\n| `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` | ^2.0.49 | ^3.0.44 |\n| `@ai-sdk/provider-utils` | ^4.0.28 | ^5.0.36 |\n| `@ai-sdk/provider` (transitive) | 3.0.10 | 4.0.10 |\n| `@sentry/node`, `@sentry/nestjs`, `@sentry/profiling-node` | ^10.59.0\n| ^10.73.0 |\n\n**Why these exact versions.** The repo''s Yarn config has\n`npmMinimalAgeGate: 3d`, which quarantines anything published in the\nlast three days; today that rules out the 7.0.97 line (`All versions\nsatisfying \"7.0.97\" are quarantined`). The set above is the newest one\nthat clears the gate *transitively*: every package pins\n`@ai-sdk/provider@4.0.10` and `@ai-sdk/provider-utils@5.0.36`, so the\ntree holds one copy of each.\n\n**Why Sentry moves.** Its Vercel AI integration needs 10.62.0+ to\ninstrument AI SDK v7 at all, and its docs say not to combine it with the\nSDK''s own `registerTelemetry` / `@ai-sdk/otel`. So Sentry stays the one\ntelemetry path and `@ai-sdk/otel` is deliberately not added.\n\n## The structural change: ESM only\n\nv7 packages are ESM-only (`\"type\": \"module\"`, no `require` export\ncondition) and require Node 22+. The server is a CommonJS NestJS build.\nOn the repo''s Node 24, `require()` of an ESM graph is native: verified\nhere by requiring `ai` and every provider package from a CommonJS script\nand instantiating Anthropic and OpenAI models (spec `v4`). Types resolve\nthrough each package''s root `types` entry under our node10 module\nresolution, and the front is ESM already. What had to change:\n\n- jest''s CommonJS runtime cannot load them, so `ai`, `@ai-sdk/*` and\ntheir one ESM-only dependency `@workflow/serde` join the swc transform\nallowlists of twenty-server (the unit config and the integration config,\nwhich keeps its own list) and twenty-front.\n- `@ai-sdk/provider-utils@5` instantiates a `TextDecoder` while being\nimported and jsdom has none, so the front''s jest setup polyfills\n`TextEncoder`/`TextDecoder` from `node:util`, next to its existing\nweb-streams polyfills.\n\n## Code migration, by hand\n\n`npx @ai-sdk/codemod v7` was not usable on this codebase: it renamed\nevery object key named `system` to `instructions` in unrelated code\n(view field groups, icon maps, labels), double-nested\n`outputTokenDetails.outputTokenDetails` where the code already used the\nv6 usage shape, and rewrote twenty''s own `cachedInputTokens` DTO fields\nas if they were SDK usage objects. Its output was reverted and the\nmigration done by hand, guided by the typechecker plus a sweep for the\naliases v7 still accepts as deprecated (they compile, so nothing flags\nthem).\n\n- Renames: `experimental_telemetry` → `telemetry`, `stepCountIs` →\n`isStepCount`, `onStepFinish` → `onStepEnd`,\n`experimental_onToolCallFinish` → `onToolExecutionEnd` (its event\nexposes `toolExecutionMs` instead of `durationMs`),\n`experimental_repairToolCall` → `repairToolCall`, `system` →\n`instructions` on the three SDK calls that used it, `LanguageModelV3*` →\n`LanguageModelV4*` with the Gemini middleware on `specificationVersion:\n''v4''`, and `result.toUIMessageStream(...)` → the stateless\n`toUIMessageStream({ stream: result.stream, ... })` with `onEnd`.\n- **Chat system message.** v7 rejects `role: ''system''` inside `messages`\nby default. The chat prompt carried one with the Bedrock cache point as\n`providerOptions`, so it moves to `instructions`, which accepts a\n`SystemModelMessage`, rather than opting into `allowSystemInMessages`.\n- **Telemetry metadata.** v7''s `TelemetryOptions` has no `metadata`. The\nsix identifiers twenty attaches to every AI call (workspace, user,\nagent, thread, turn, stream) now travel as `runtimeContext` and are\nopted into telemetry through `includeRuntimeContext`; `buildAiTelemetry`\nreturns both halves and the seven call sites spread it. Caveat: Sentry\n10.73''s v7 instrumentation maps only `functionId` onto spans, so\nagent/thread/turn/stream ids are not on Sentry AI spans until Sentry\nreads runtime context; workspace and user ids still arrive through\n`beforeSendSpan`. Span names stay `ai.<operation>`, so the\n`tracesSampler` rule keeping them at 100% is unaffected.\n- **Tool execution.** `ToolSet` now widens `execute` to a union no\nargument satisfies, and `ToolExecutionOptions.context` is required; the\ntwo places that invoke a tool by name (MCP executor, tool-provider)\nnarrow to the exported `ToolExecuteFunction` and pass `context:\nundefined`. `Tool.description` may now be a function; the descriptor\nindex keeps string descriptions only, since a per-call description needs\na tool context it does not have.\n- **Chat job spec.** The job no longer calls\n`result.toUIMessageStream()`, so its spec stops faking that method: the\nfake now yields model stream parts and the real v7 `toUIMessageStream`\nbuilds the chunks, the response message and the end event the job\nconsumes. This is the one suite that could not run in the development\ncontainer (it imports the unbuilt `twenty-emails` sibling), which is why\nCI caught it rather than the local run.\n\n## Behaviour change to know about\n\n`result.usage` now spans all steps of a run; it was the final step only.\nCredits were already decremented per step in `onStepEnd`, so billing\ndoes not change. What changes is the executor''s reported usage and cost\nper run (the workflow step logs), which become the true total instead of\nthe last step''s.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Typecheck: twenty-server clean (the only errors are the pre-existing\nunbuilt `twenty-client-sdk` / `twenty-sdk` siblings in this\nenvironment), twenty-front `typecheck` target clean, twenty-shared\nbuilds clean against the v7 types.\n- Lint and format clean on every changed file.\n- twenty-server jest, every suite under `metadata-modules/ai`,\n`core-modules/tool-provider`, `core-modules/tool`, `api/mcp`, the\nworkflow AI-agent action and the metadata tools: 93 suites pass, 619\ntests, plus the chat job suite (23 tests) once `twenty-emails` was\nbuilt.\n- Integration jest config: a probe spec importing a value from\n`twenty-shared/ai` reproduces CI''s `Cannot use import statement outside\na module` on the previous allowlist and passes on the new one.\n- twenty-shared: 234 suites, 1882 tests pass.\n- twenty-front, every suite under `modules/ai` (the only front directory\nimporting `ai`): 60 suites, 422 tests pass.\n- Runtime: CommonJS `require()` of `ai` and all nine provider packages\nsucceeds and instantiates models, on Node 22.22 here (the feature needs\n22.12+; the repo runs 24).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_011LWnxYvEvLR8VBEGA6uCKV)_\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25704?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture>``&lt;source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;&lt;source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"&gt;&lt;img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;``</picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"c22855fdffef2e547f5196b08bfd2352ddd7fe99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/c22855fdffef2e547f5196b08bfd2352ddd7fe99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/8500b16fd4842017ed617f926bae3ff13e34db53","verification":{"payload":"tree c22855fdffef2e547f5196b08bfd2352ddd7fe99\nparent 8fc71f4f545c35916f4b6f2c4633706eda526d88\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789028293 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789028293 +0200\n\nUpgrade the AI SDK to v7 (#25704)\n\nStacked on #25696 until it merged (squash `8fc71f4f`); the base is\n`main` now and the branch carries a merge of main, so the diff below is\nthe upgrade alone.\n\n## What moves\n\n| package | from | to |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ai` (server, shared, front) | 6.0.97 | 7.0.93 |\n| `@ai-sdk/anthropic` | ^3.0.83 | ^4.0.49 |\n| `@ai-sdk/openai` | ^3.0.70 | ^4.0.60 |\n| `@ai-sdk/azure` | ^3.0.55 | ^4.0.63 |\n| `@ai-sdk/google` | ^3.0.81 | ^4.0.64 |\n| `@ai-sdk/mistral` | ^3.0.38 | ^4.0.39 |\n| `@ai-sdk/xai` | ^3.0.94 | ^4.0.54 |\n| `@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock` | ^4.0.116 | ^5.0.76 |\n| `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` | ^2.0.49 | ^3.0.44 |\n| `@ai-sdk/provider-utils` | ^4.0.28 | ^5.0.36 |\n| `@ai-sdk/provider` (transitive) | 3.0.10 | 4.0.10 |\n| `@sentry/node`, `@sentry/nestjs`, `@sentry/profiling-node` | ^10.59.0\n| ^10.73.0 |\n\n**Why these exact versions.** The repo''s Yarn config has\n`npmMinimalAgeGate: 3d`, which quarantines anything published in the\nlast three days; today that rules out the 7.0.97 line (`All versions\nsatisfying \"7.0.97\" are quarantined`). The set above is the newest one\nthat clears the gate *transitively*: every package pins\n`@ai-sdk/provider@4.0.10` and `@ai-sdk/provider-utils@5.0.36`, so the\ntree holds one copy of each.\n\n**Why Sentry moves.** Its Vercel AI integration needs 10.62.0+ to\ninstrument AI SDK v7 at all, and its docs say not to combine it with the\nSDK''s own `registerTelemetry` / `@ai-sdk/otel`. So Sentry stays the one\ntelemetry path and `@ai-sdk/otel` is deliberately not added.\n\n## The structural change: ESM only\n\nv7 packages are ESM-only (`\"type\": \"module\"`, no `require` export\ncondition) and require Node 22+. The server is a CommonJS NestJS build.\nOn the repo''s Node 24, `require()` of an ESM graph is native: verified\nhere by requiring `ai` and every provider package from a CommonJS script\nand instantiating Anthropic and OpenAI models (spec `v4`). Types resolve\nthrough each package''s root `types` entry under our node10 module\nresolution, and the front is ESM already. What had to change:\n\n- jest''s CommonJS runtime cannot load them, so `ai`, `@ai-sdk/*` and\ntheir one ESM-only dependency `@workflow/serde` join the swc transform\nallowlists of twenty-server (the unit config and the integration config,\nwhich keeps its own list) and twenty-front.\n- `@ai-sdk/provider-utils@5` instantiates a `TextDecoder` while being\nimported and jsdom has none, so the front''s jest setup polyfills\n`TextEncoder`/`TextDecoder` from `node:util`, next to its existing\nweb-streams polyfills.\n\n## Code migration, by hand\n\n`npx @ai-sdk/codemod v7` was not usable on this codebase: it renamed\nevery object key named `system` to `instructions` in unrelated code\n(view field groups, icon maps, labels), double-nested\n`outputTokenDetails.outputTokenDetails` where the code already used the\nv6 usage shape, and rewrote twenty''s own `cachedInputTokens` DTO fields\nas if they were SDK usage objects. Its output was reverted and the\nmigration done by hand, guided by the typechecker plus a sweep for the\naliases v7 still accepts as deprecated (they compile, so nothing flags\nthem).\n\n- Renames: `experimental_telemetry` → `telemetry`, `stepCountIs` →\n`isStepCount`, `onStepFinish` → `onStepEnd`,\n`experimental_onToolCallFinish` → `onToolExecutionEnd` (its event\nexposes `toolExecutionMs` instead of `durationMs`),\n`experimental_repairToolCall` → `repairToolCall`, `system` →\n`instructions` on the three SDK calls that used it, `LanguageModelV3*` →\n`LanguageModelV4*` with the Gemini middleware on `specificationVersion:\n''v4''`, and `result.toUIMessageStream(...)` → the stateless\n`toUIMessageStream({ stream: result.stream, ... })` with `onEnd`.\n- **Chat system message.** v7 rejects `role: ''system''` inside `messages`\nby default. The chat prompt carried one with the Bedrock cache point as\n`providerOptions`, so it moves to `instructions`, which accepts a\n`SystemModelMessage`, rather than opting into `allowSystemInMessages`.\n- **Telemetry metadata.** v7''s `TelemetryOptions` has no `metadata`. The\nsix identifiers twenty attaches to every AI call (workspace, user,\nagent, thread, turn, stream) now travel as `runtimeContext` and are\nopted into telemetry through `includeRuntimeContext`; `buildAiTelemetry`\nreturns both halves and the seven call sites spread it. Caveat: Sentry\n10.73''s v7 instrumentation maps only `functionId` onto spans, so\nagent/thread/turn/stream ids are not on Sentry AI spans until Sentry\nreads runtime context; workspace and user ids still arrive through\n`beforeSendSpan`. Span names stay `ai.<operation>`, so the\n`tracesSampler` rule keeping them at 100% is unaffected.\n- **Tool execution.** `ToolSet` now widens `execute` to a union no\nargument satisfies, and `ToolExecutionOptions.context` is required; the\ntwo places that invoke a tool by name (MCP executor, tool-provider)\nnarrow to the exported `ToolExecuteFunction` and pass `context:\nundefined`. `Tool.description` may now be a function; the descriptor\nindex keeps string descriptions only, since a per-call description needs\na tool context it does not have.\n- **Chat job spec.** The job no longer calls\n`result.toUIMessageStream()`, so its spec stops faking that method: the\nfake now yields model stream parts and the real v7 `toUIMessageStream`\nbuilds the chunks, the response message and the end event the job\nconsumes. This is the one suite that could not run in the development\ncontainer (it imports the unbuilt `twenty-emails` sibling), which is why\nCI caught it rather than the local run.\n\n## Behaviour change to know about\n\n`result.usage` now spans all steps of a run; it was the final step only.\nCredits were already decremented per step in `onStepEnd`, so billing\ndoes not change. What changes is the executor''s reported usage and cost\nper run (the workflow step logs), which become the true total instead of\nthe last step''s.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Typecheck: twenty-server clean (the only errors are the pre-existing\nunbuilt `twenty-client-sdk` / `twenty-sdk` siblings in this\nenvironment), twenty-front `typecheck` target clean, twenty-shared\nbuilds clean against the v7 types.\n- Lint and format clean on every changed file.\n- twenty-server jest, every suite under `metadata-modules/ai`,\n`core-modules/tool-provider`, `core-modules/tool`, `api/mcp`, the\nworkflow AI-agent action and the metadata tools: 93 suites pass, 619\ntests, plus the chat job suite (23 tests) once `twenty-emails` was\nbuilt.\n- Integration jest config: a probe spec importing a value from\n`twenty-shared/ai` reproduces CI''s `Cannot use import statement outside\na module` on the previous allowlist and passes on the new one.\n- twenty-shared: 234 suites, 1882 tests pass.\n- twenty-front, every suite under `modules/ai` (the only front directory\nimporting `ai`): 60 suites, 422 tests pass.\n- Runtime: CommonJS `require()` of `ai` and all nine provider packages\nsucceeds and instantiates models, on Node 22.22 here (the feature needs\n22.12+; the repo runs 24).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_011LWnxYvEvLR8VBEGA6uCKV)_\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25704?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture>``&lt;source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;&lt;source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"&gt;&lt;img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;``</picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqomfFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvPMQAF+KvVWCwcF70ZQf/Hw4zEXp\ng3+5u7fZFg5iX9e1sQ0WZw2BrpZx90aQltaTQmsck9UBxggPi1Jt9dJdTGJc/Tu6\ncgs2hxEAMFTjGiJJo6zTtO6l95pxLIfSBHs53HSaWvDLCi7OYaW4OmdigHPxtNUI\nAwHat1UzeTr51049vGp0LwGQZpg/lRz8ooO+GYgA2eK8dlp73xdkivm+alDxRfsP\nwjOi3rjBVC3iNGJC6OoS5NWJ+HAvUMnpOs9lbUs9v1X+Xndn+3+Y2BHalbAtXrTk\nnVZgYQhF39E7ONAOJRnMNfRdNU0w4ozMhmehoNwWQW0Au59BahYwPnq23Z+nmYKu\nHF+w6Ed/1ZFozCazgglkIUJxwg8CePvqQhaehbGyrbeeupBNMKTJKLPsFh+xtS+n\n/LOiL1gCSH1wzzdtcJWQYNQf8s2PCtl6A0NHOm7u8krh496q9z/7p/SoiMpdOhfG\nNl+ZAp8s+NfGh7jjXogdsZUjz1hL4err12+flpg3EPWt36z7CC13ZPEurW0puea/\nk48TqidToxcW/0QLdjycgv54FlxnDYSusJwDMuerOXMzmc+30QI4rmJNEVxaZ9ya\npqZKFp2OO7uqDqT48PfvbdeDuf0Wgj6d2dotqgrLDMC0OZcJYGFnr3QKYQ6BYKQb\nou+lWsnp8PsScEMMX39d\n=3u3z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/8500b16fd4842017ed617f926bae3ff13e34db53","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDg1MDBiMTZmZDQ4NDIwMTdlZDYxN2Y5MjZiYWUzZmYxM2UzNGRiNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/8fc71f4f545c35916f4b6f2c4633706eda526d88","sha":"8fc71f4f545c35916f4b6f2c4633706eda526d88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8fc71f4f545c35916f4b6f2c4633706eda526d88"}],"sha":"8500b16fd4842017ed617f926bae3ff13e34db53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8500b16fd4842017ed617f926bae3ff13e34db53"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8fc71f4f545c35916f4b6f2c4633706eda526d88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:14:25Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T08:14:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Deliver the Claude reasoning config and make effort a first-class model parameter (#25696)\n\nTwo changes that belong together: the executor''s reasoning config\nfinally reaches both providers, and effort becomes a parameter a model\ncan be pinned to, which is also the knob that controls what the first\nchange costs.\n\n## 1. The reasoning config never reached the API\n\nThe agent executor builds a thinking config for every reasoning-capable\nClaude model and passes it to `generateText`. Neither provider ever\nreceived it, for three reasons that had to be fixed together:\n\n1. **Direct Anthropic: discarded before the call.**\n`getCallLevelProviderOptions` replaced the whole `anthropic` object with\n`cacheControl`, dropping `thinking`. It now merges its call-level keys\ninto the caller''s options, for Anthropic, OpenAI and Azure alike (the\nlatter two had the same latent bug).\n2. **Bedrock: sent under a key the provider does not know.**\n`@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock` reads `reasoningConfig`, not `thinking`, and\nstrips unknown keys silently.\n3. **The shape was stale.** `thinking: { type: ''enabled'', budgetTokens\n}` is rejected on Claude 4.7+. Fixing 1 or 2 alone would have introduced\n400s on every current model.\n\nAdaptive thinking, and only adaptive thinking, is sent to Claude 4.6+\n(`isAdaptiveThinkingClaudeModel`, from the version in the id). The fixed\nbudget is gone everywhere. Models below 4.6 run without thinking, which\nis what they have effectively been doing all along.\n\n## 2. Effort as a first-class parameter\n\n**A model id can pin an effort: `provider/model@effort`**, e.g.\n`anthropic/claude-opus-5@low` or `openai/gpt-5.6-sol@max`. That is the\nwhole interface. Every place that already holds a model id\n(`AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_FAST` / `SMART` / `RECOMMENDED`, workspace enabled\nmodels, agent `modelId`, workflow step model) takes a variant unchanged:\nno migration, no new column, no new config type, and the env-var format\nself-hosters use stays what it was.\n\n- **Catalog** (`ai-providers.json`): a model lists the efforts it\naccepts, in the provider''s own vocabulary, e.g. `\"efforts\": [\"none\",\n\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", \"xhigh\", \"max\"]`. No list means the model runs\nat the provider default only, exactly as today. Filled for 26 models\nfrom the providers'' documentation: every Claude 4.5+, GPT-5.4, GPT-5.5,\nGPT-5.6 Sol/Luna/Terra, GPT-6 Astra, every Gemini 3.x model with\npublished thinking levels, Grok 4.5/4.6, Mistral Small.\n- **Registry**: a variant is materialized only when an operator lists it\nin one of the three preference lists (the admin mutations also accept a\nvariant of a registered model, which lists it). It inherits the base\nmodel''s prices and limits, is labelled `Claude Opus 5 (low)`, and\ncarries no benchmark, because a benchmark describes the effort it was\nmeasured at. The effort must be in the model''s list **and** expressible\nby the installed SDK (`AI_SDK_PACKAGE_EFFORTS`, one row per provider,\neach pinned to the SDK''s own option type so an SDK enum change fails the\nbuild here rather than a request); otherwise the variant is skipped with\na warning. Nothing can reach an undeclared effort by typing an id.\n- **Execution**: `buildReasoningProviderOptions` maps the pinned effort\nonto each provider''s parameter: `anthropic.effort`,\n`bedrock.reasoningConfig.maxReasoningEffort`, `openai.reasoningEffort`,\n`azure.reasoningEffort`, `google.thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel`,\n`mistral.reasoningEffort`, `xai.reasoningEffort`. This is the one place\nthe slider and per-effort benchmarks build on.\n- **Sync**: the catalog sync rebuilds `ai-providers.json` from\nmodels.dev, which knows nothing about efforts, so it now carries\n`efforts` (and the residency fields, which it cannot know either) over\nfrom the committed file.\n- **Picker**: listed variants are entries of their own, so \"two models\nwith min and max effort, switch between both\" is\n`openai/gpt-5.6-sol@low` and `openai/gpt-5.6-sol@max` in the recommended\nlist.\n\n## Behaviour changes, stated plainly\n\n1. Reasoning turns on for every Claude 4.6+ model in workflow steps and\nagent runs, on both providers. In prod-eu that is `claude-opus-5`,\n`claude-sonnet-5`, `claude-opus-4-7`, `claude-opus-4-6`,\n`claude-sonnet-4-6`; `claude-haiku-4-5` keeps running without thinking.\n2. **Chat sends the same options.** Opus 5 and Sonnet 5 already run\nadaptive thinking in chat today, because omitting `thinking` means\nadaptive on them; the explicit option only changes Opus 4.6/4.7/4.8 and\nSonnet 4.6. A pinned effort would be meaningless if chat ignored it, so\nchat and the executor now share one path.\n3. Agentless executor runs get the same options as agent runs; the\nreasoning config was gated on `agent` for no reason the code could\nexplain.\n4. Nothing changes for an id without `@effort`, and nothing changes for\na model without an `efforts` list.\n\nAdaptive thinking without a pinned effort runs at the provider default\n(`high` on Anthropic). Pinning `low` or `medium` on the default lists is\nhow spend is pulled back.\n\n## Deploy and self-hoster safety\n\n- No migration, no entity change, no new config variable. `efforts` is\nan optional catalog field; a catalog without it is valid and behaves as\ntoday.\n- Variants exist only where listed; a wrong value in a catalog yields a\nwarning and a missing variant, never a request the provider rejects. The\nSDK intersection covers the one known gap: the xAI Responses model\nforwards `low`/`medium`/`high` while Grok 4.6 also takes `xhigh`.\n- Cloud catalogs live in twenty-infra and carry no `efforts` yet; until\nthey do, cloud behaves as if this feature did not exist. Filling them\nbelongs with the residency data entry in twenty-infra#930.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\n- The workspace slider UI, and exposing `efforts` to the client (GraphQL\nfield + codegen). The server side is complete; the front only needs the\nlist.\n- Benchmarks keyed by (model, effort). The overlay is still one reading\nper model; a variant carries none rather than a number measured at\nanother effort.\n- The structured-output call at the end of an agent run still passes no\nprovider options.\n\n## Verification\n\n46 new tests, all on plain values: the capability check across every\nClaude generation, Bedrock composite ids and non-Claude ids; the\nprovider mapping for all seven providers with and without a pinned\neffort; call-level option merging for Anthropic, OpenAI and Azure;\nvariant id parsing including a Bedrock name with a colon and a\nnon-effort suffix; the SDK intersection; the sync carry-over; and the\ncommitted catalog declaring efforts only on reasoning models. Touched\nsuites: 17 pass, 120 tests. Lint, format and typecheck clean (the only\ntypecheck errors are the pre-existing unbuilt `twenty-emails` /\n`twenty-client-sdk` / `twenty-sdk` siblings in this environment).","tree":{"sha":"9512fe35cdd92970e65582cd1d6ca4198f14d81e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/9512fe35cdd92970e65582cd1d6ca4198f14d81e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/8fc71f4f545c35916f4b6f2c4633706eda526d88","verification":{"payload":"tree 9512fe35cdd92970e65582cd1d6ca4198f14d81e\nparent 6b6f70ebad9c9b3443c2af60386982ae37979fe1\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1789028065 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789028065 +0200\n\nDeliver the Claude reasoning config and make effort a first-class model parameter (#25696)\n\nTwo changes that belong together: the executor''s reasoning config\nfinally reaches both providers, and effort becomes a parameter a model\ncan be pinned to, which is also the knob that controls what the first\nchange costs.\n\n## 1. The reasoning config never reached the API\n\nThe agent executor builds a thinking config for every reasoning-capable\nClaude model and passes it to `generateText`. Neither provider ever\nreceived it, for three reasons that had to be fixed together:\n\n1. **Direct Anthropic: discarded before the call.**\n`getCallLevelProviderOptions` replaced the whole `anthropic` object with\n`cacheControl`, dropping `thinking`. It now merges its call-level keys\ninto the caller''s options, for Anthropic, OpenAI and Azure alike (the\nlatter two had the same latent bug).\n2. **Bedrock: sent under a key the provider does not know.**\n`@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock` reads `reasoningConfig`, not `thinking`, and\nstrips unknown keys silently.\n3. **The shape was stale.** `thinking: { type: ''enabled'', budgetTokens\n}` is rejected on Claude 4.7+. Fixing 1 or 2 alone would have introduced\n400s on every current model.\n\nAdaptive thinking, and only adaptive thinking, is sent to Claude 4.6+\n(`isAdaptiveThinkingClaudeModel`, from the version in the id). The fixed\nbudget is gone everywhere. Models below 4.6 run without thinking, which\nis what they have effectively been doing all along.\n\n## 2. Effort as a first-class parameter\n\n**A model id can pin an effort: `provider/model@effort`**, e.g.\n`anthropic/claude-opus-5@low` or `openai/gpt-5.6-sol@max`. That is the\nwhole interface. Every place that already holds a model id\n(`AI_MODELS_DEFAULT_FAST` / `SMART` / `RECOMMENDED`, workspace enabled\nmodels, agent `modelId`, workflow step model) takes a variant unchanged:\nno migration, no new column, no new config type, and the env-var format\nself-hosters use stays what it was.\n\n- **Catalog** (`ai-providers.json`): a model lists the efforts it\naccepts, in the provider''s own vocabulary, e.g. `\"efforts\": [\"none\",\n\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", \"xhigh\", \"max\"]`. No list means the model runs\nat the provider default only, exactly as today. Filled for 26 models\nfrom the providers'' documentation: every Claude 4.5+, GPT-5.4, GPT-5.5,\nGPT-5.6 Sol/Luna/Terra, GPT-6 Astra, every Gemini 3.x model with\npublished thinking levels, Grok 4.5/4.6, Mistral Small.\n- **Registry**: a variant is materialized only when an operator lists it\nin one of the three preference lists (the admin mutations also accept a\nvariant of a registered model, which lists it). It inherits the base\nmodel''s prices and limits, is labelled `Claude Opus 5 (low)`, and\ncarries no benchmark, because a benchmark describes the effort it was\nmeasured at. The effort must be in the model''s list **and** expressible\nby the installed SDK (`AI_SDK_PACKAGE_EFFORTS`, one row per provider,\neach pinned to the SDK''s own option type so an SDK enum change fails the\nbuild here rather than a request); otherwise the variant is skipped with\na warning. Nothing can reach an undeclared effort by typing an id.\n- **Execution**: `buildReasoningProviderOptions` maps the pinned effort\nonto each provider''s parameter: `anthropic.effort`,\n`bedrock.reasoningConfig.maxReasoningEffort`, `openai.reasoningEffort`,\n`azure.reasoningEffort`, `google.thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel`,\n`mistral.reasoningEffort`, `xai.reasoningEffort`. This is the one place\nthe slider and per-effort benchmarks build on.\n- **Sync**: the catalog sync rebuilds `ai-providers.json` from\nmodels.dev, which knows nothing about efforts, so it now carries\n`efforts` (and the residency fields, which it cannot know either) over\nfrom the committed file.\n- **Picker**: listed variants are entries of their own, so \"two models\nwith min and max effort, switch between both\" is\n`openai/gpt-5.6-sol@low` and `openai/gpt-5.6-sol@max` in the recommended\nlist.\n\n## Behaviour changes, stated plainly\n\n1. Reasoning turns on for every Claude 4.6+ model in workflow steps and\nagent runs, on both providers. In prod-eu that is `claude-opus-5`,\n`claude-sonnet-5`, `claude-opus-4-7`, `claude-opus-4-6`,\n`claude-sonnet-4-6`; `claude-haiku-4-5` keeps running without thinking.\n2. **Chat sends the same options.** Opus 5 and Sonnet 5 already run\nadaptive thinking in chat today, because omitting `thinking` means\nadaptive on them; the explicit option only changes Opus 4.6/4.7/4.8 and\nSonnet 4.6. A pinned effort would be meaningless if chat ignored it, so\nchat and the executor now share one path.\n3. Agentless executor runs get the same options as agent runs; the\nreasoning config was gated on `agent` for no reason the code could\nexplain.\n4. Nothing changes for an id without `@effort`, and nothing changes for\na model without an `efforts` list.\n\nAdaptive thinking without a pinned effort runs at the provider default\n(`high` on Anthropic). Pinning `low` or `medium` on the default lists is\nhow spend is pulled back.\n\n## Deploy and self-hoster safety\n\n- No migration, no entity change, no new config variable. `efforts` is\nan optional catalog field; a catalog without it is valid and behaves as\ntoday.\n- Variants exist only where listed; a wrong value in a catalog yields a\nwarning and a missing variant, never a request the provider rejects. The\nSDK intersection covers the one known gap: the xAI Responses model\nforwards `low`/`medium`/`high` while Grok 4.6 also takes `xhigh`.\n- Cloud catalogs live in twenty-infra and carry no `efforts` yet; until\nthey do, cloud behaves as if this feature did not exist. Filling them\nbelongs with the residency data entry in twenty-infra#930.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\n- The workspace slider UI, and exposing `efforts` to the client (GraphQL\nfield + codegen). The server side is complete; the front only needs the\nlist.\n- Benchmarks keyed by (model, effort). The overlay is still one reading\nper model; a variant carries none rather than a number measured at\nanother effort.\n- The structured-output call at the end of an agent run still passes no\nprovider options.\n\n## Verification\n\n46 new tests, all on plain values: the capability check across every\nClaude generation, Bedrock composite ids and non-Claude ids; the\nprovider mapping for all seven providers with and without a pinned\neffort; call-level option merging for Anthropic, OpenAI and Azure;\nvariant id parsing including a Bedrock name with a colon and a\nnon-effort suffix; the SDK intersection; the sync carry-over; and the\ncommitted catalog declaring efforts only on reasoning models. Touched\nsuites: 17 pass, 120 tests. Lint, format and typecheck clean (the only\ntypecheck errors are the pre-existing unbuilt `twenty-emails` /\n`twenty-client-sdk` / `twenty-sdk` siblings in this environment).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqombhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1V8QADlVVY0zALML21/7/GMXfHOQ\nNqIz3aGF9/fmT9d4tkKx/hfgIh4pbYtio1uLnWreZXmAmmBNfeb5Ogzv0AWWEDyc\ndiuvjdELt0Ut20x1WU09C9+V1p9SioeOHZtLW/qoTqVOuDKEg38/tM3a327e31It\nL0DoLy7Cx6RZJhymlKsI/MSF4thBsNHnEq5hzc1HfH6zjChNgHf8DXLhQnHUKiaG\nFdtqtR9j8e2hVJz0d+k8vKZ0ICD7YlCOFAz7X3OHUx2YA3hni8ipHo7nyhFmVVvv\nLMxvP768uR9KPTwTVMuGxAK4ytZXYHzgmgsQJ3dbWDLmr8GfnfoUEQVYBiKUtfnr\nNmRZUqhRq6AHykyUaqsKGul6VIhCgq73uwiHNLR84iA3XfBYIADnji3PaFL3V1+q\n9P1au+r7/DBUalpdPoFHgW6r+mNEmX4PfsmETiFi0mrkppfYj2DwwcEUUkz/2nZ6\n66e/r5lzmhc0+TDsoob+Y7lxXbk5W/bD7r4mH99emI1wH/tzFg9h/7cKXezZI30j\n/ZWtxHgrsKC1GphKhqtX/2xV6ZUluaG1i8Ep4d6KcnYrJX9GtsQUgJofnxYJSJPY\nVo0+zh1MJNue/eeuSKvRhPrKH5yVWikUoqNRE48VWrDzdvvzS357SXZzKKI3ZeK7\nt5Djr/4pMbFteGrRky2D\n=aH9N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/8fc71f4f545c35916f4b6f2c4633706eda526d88","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDhmYzcxZjRmNTQ1YzM1OTE2ZjRiNmYyYzQ2MzM3MDZlZGE1MjZkODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/6b6f70ebad9c9b3443c2af60386982ae37979fe1","sha":"6b6f70ebad9c9b3443c2af60386982ae37979fe1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/6b6f70ebad9c9b3443c2af60386982ae37979fe1"}],"sha":"8fc71f4f545c35916f4b6f2c4633706eda526d88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/8fc71f4f545c35916f4b6f2c4633706eda526d88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29927851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/martmull","id":29927851,"login":"martmull","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/6b6f70ebad9c9b3443c2af60386982ae37979fe1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T07:50:25Z","email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T07:50:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Clear logoFileId when the workspace logo is removed (#25711)\n\nRemoving a workspace logo left the workspace pointing at a deleted file.\n\n## Bug\n\n`updateWorkspace(data: { logo: null })` deletes the logo''s storage\nobject but never clears `logoFileId`. The `logo` resolver only checks\n`logoFileId`, so it keeps signing a URL for a file that no longer\nexists, and the UI shows a broken image.\n\n| Step | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Storage object | deleted | deleted |\n| `workspace.logoFileId` | **still set** | `null` |\n| `logo` resolver returns | signed URL → 404 | `''''` |\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen the payload removes the logo, the saved row also clears\n`logoFileId`:\n\n```ts\n...(payload.logo === null ? { logoFileId: null } : {}),\n```\n\nThe storage deletion that already runs after the save is unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `successful-workspace-logo-removal.integration-spec.ts`: seeds a\nreal logo with the existing `seedWorkspaceLogo` util, removes it, then\nchecks that the mutation returns `logo: ''''` and that\n`core.workspace.logoFileId` is `NULL`.\n\nTypecheck, lint and format are clean. I couldn''t run the integration\nsuite locally (the in-process app ran out of heap at the default ~4 GB),\nso CI is its first run.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25711?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"b62e7b536f295742ef8c172f7ddac1f0b9ff464e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/b62e7b536f295742ef8c172f7ddac1f0b9ff464e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/6b6f70ebad9c9b3443c2af60386982ae37979fe1","verification":{"payload":"tree b62e7b536f295742ef8c172f7ddac1f0b9ff464e\nparent c3853a09591c36c9338e2242963cc33fc0b68f21\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1789026625 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789026625 +0000\n\nClear logoFileId when the workspace logo is removed (#25711)\n\nRemoving a workspace logo left the workspace pointing at a deleted file.\n\n## Bug\n\n`updateWorkspace(data: { logo: null })` deletes the logo''s storage\nobject but never clears `logoFileId`. The `logo` resolver only checks\n`logoFileId`, so it keeps signing a URL for a file that no longer\nexists, and the UI shows a broken image.\n\n| Step | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Storage object | deleted | deleted |\n| `workspace.logoFileId` | **still set** | `null` |\n| `logo` resolver returns | signed URL → 404 | `''''` |\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen the payload removes the logo, the saved row also clears\n`logoFileId`:\n\n```ts\n...(payload.logo === null ? { logoFileId: null } : {}),\n```\n\nThe storage deletion that already runs after the save is unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `successful-workspace-logo-removal.integration-spec.ts`: seeds a\nreal logo with the existing `seedWorkspaceLogo` util, removes it, then\nchecks that the mutation returns `logo: ''''` and that\n`core.workspace.logoFileId` is `NULL`.\n\nTypecheck, lint and format are clean. I couldn''t run the integration\nsuite locally (the in-process app ran out of heap at the default ~4 GB),\nso CI is its first run.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25711?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqomFQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqz4QAKUSdEmbTjQEtTrwYv0UyTxq\nJi8+dWBtE5KuDRiWFYAGLclpUda/IK/r1eBwscVfwk7cqx1eyF6q9xvJzn41GVSA\nI7pCnYNbKyyLHAl9OmN8sBUvfuR6ii31djjm2d5C7DryCwmJljXIn219EOzBNis3\nOuG0dmH0c72rmI4e2Y5d441bK9Q1gHeKEDYsIgB31uD7AqKA/BZe8pOJgZfLLjvf\nAQJ1b3i1Gt0vwINcJrU98t87/iMTTJyct5/Ez0UM2I85P7TY2NO4gTlc9vWZWhME\njx3/OPowZQkEyjyohojDZvM6Xqy0qZRmNssyoTRHR/hV1PcinyAso8nNkxvWhyVo\nVs3gOJk9sVKoPpMNFmKz4YzuNtIIgrzym+g4yEyqEBn2VnPniAsTXRECSXTMInif\nius3/M4iTMDEy9LCO5TRkEs5Vs2nijCDg0D9goc61LfyGh+8XG8KHYOTfyg6gUHf\nJISQetfSd6gIix8uvL0O51Gra+HwZjsh9+4RrgZgMlVS6J6BFSp3GaSdv84D0Dll\nOiJdNnDdBOSq3w2U/tzzYW8iixeVv2LR3EgiXJunJLp2QOMyKYqXutuI1s5o9Npz\nlHpQF1Z/u/K1kBoXNBJZXCubGMAvlhVh34BHUAO9B1IknGHk7n4zWrOwF0naQWV3\nK3XAcLxHff0bE7c1NYEN\n=q/3q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/6b6f70ebad9c9b3443c2af60386982ae37979fe1","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDZiNmY3MGViYWQ5YzliMzQ0M2MyYWY2MDM4Njk4MmFlMzc5NzlmZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/c3853a09591c36c9338e2242963cc33fc0b68f21","sha":"c3853a09591c36c9338e2242963cc33fc0b68f21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/c3853a09591c36c9338e2242963cc33fc0b68f21"}],"sha":"6b6f70ebad9c9b3443c2af60386982ae37979fe1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/6b6f70ebad9c9b3443c2af60386982ae37979fe1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/c3853a09591c36c9338e2242963cc33fc0b68f21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T06:04:55Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T06:04:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: sync AI model catalog (#25710)\n\nAutomated daily sync of the AI model catalog.\n\n- Model identity, pricing, context windows and availability come from\n[models.dev](https://models.dev).\n- Intelligence, speed and cost per task come from [Artificial\nAnalysis](https://artificialanalysis.ai/),\n  which requires `ARTIFICIAL_ANALYSIS_API_KEY`.\n\nNew models meeting inclusion criteria (tool calling, pricing data,\ncontext limits) are added\nautomatically. Benchmark data is best-effort: a model Artificial\nAnalysis has not rated keeps\nevery other field and simply carries no `benchmark` entry.\n\n**Please review before merging** and check the coverage summary below\nfor models that silently\nstopped matching.\n\n### Benchmark coverage\n\n- General-purpose models with an intelligence index: **51/80** (64%)\n- Specialized models excluded from the denominator: 10\n\n<details><summary>General-purpose models with no matched intelligence\nindex</summary>\n\n- openai/gpt-5-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.2-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.3-codex-spark\n- openai/gpt-5.5-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.6\n- openai/gpt-5.4-pro\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-4