imitation\n\n`postSlackChannelWelcome` posts twice sequentially inside a 15s\nfunction, so its pathological worst case (~20.5s) still exceeds that\nbudget. It needs repeated request timeouts *and* rate limiting at once;\nthe realistic rate-limited case resolves in ~2s per post, since\n`chat.postMessage` is ~1/s per channel and a `Retry-After: 1` is waited\nout inside the budget. Closing the pathological case means raising that\nfunction''s `timeoutSeconds` or making the thread reply best-effort, both\nbehaviour changes to a function this PR otherwise does not touch, so it\nis left as a documented gap. Pre-PR that same path could hang for ~30\nminutes per post.\n\n`runWithTimeout` bounds caller latency without cancelling the losing\noperation, matching the existing deadline race''s semantics. The\nabandoned work is capped by the client and its result discarded; real\ncancellation would mean threading an `AbortSignal` through four utils.\n\n## Tests\n\n23 new unit tests across 6 files, covering the client defaults and\ncaller override, the rate-limit retry budget (including a first attempt\nthat has already spent it), the shared roster window across pages, the\ntimeout helper, the bounded context read (a hanging client acquisition\nand the shared deadline), and rate-limited answer delivery.\n\n- `yarn test:unit`: 639 passed, 91 files\n- `yarn lint` and `yarn typecheck` clean; `oxfmt --check` clean on all\n22 changed files\n- `yarn test` (integration) needs a live Twenty at `localhost:2020` and\nwas not run locally. It runs in CI as the `slack (local)` and `slack\n(dockerhub-latest)` jobs. Those tests mock Slack over msw with HTTP 200\n+ `ok: false` and never produce a 429 or a hang, so this change is inert\nfor them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqojkNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAw+cQABWYRD2Jg6ntCcJ/m1aLh0hx\nX3uhIt/aVCHOs0+n9ZZ5TmMft3KTnZc1ThxQwxMU6/J58pYWhfDZpkOEr7/HM5tT\nJyGr3aD4p2OZSvg1IpF+527Qku2hToEePaSoBoD0ToXSySk1Kroje9oL6iWPVImr\ny5PWNrS2s3xTHecbFB96nqV1if6IuCtnJzKqIbp+W9k4/naO2P1+5jDeBakPwSIw\nHNWtZAjtPcaSP7JCw30WVwq1ubjDxF0IbW9tn/DXi7Q4FbkOS1gx2hyd/tGLxC5p\ngCrzxdVyAD2PNnaoK2/6jTkQn4dVo4klkh+/hmfR+Y+4XgDqEvP0d/RSHANVfbh/\nKH/qVVeZz4sVHajCeUp1ZNMPjJp/wdo9tweBcup3e9ZbSjFKuxLcxN/Z7PDTSfOY\nOp2TkYHXG9C5twdiYInn5w+kpj7p8wIiYE8YGbR9P/ATsg+DEUmLIr/rv+/6sz9C\ncxWFxwH7/BUrVHbF8Z87nI6IYa8o9KSoWk8sBt1yBJlL+CiUbd153xLizb+BcTBh\nBMvvs4L0glWyzUDCrkkrhlEg7R2bx256VgOuWhY+f3AT6sBgizgWlJV/ciKc5Ibk\ncoB6TdBuC4Giuw3k/sQAmU7ww828ZP9LvnwsykkXCfVOwDrg5CY4mkGy+THzZyWf\navMfIsxwlScSPMoWhoOI\n=xswF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/88fe4360fea326fb8998a15c07db1bd003a9fe0d","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDg4ZmU0MzYwZmVhMzI2ZmI4OTk4YTE1YzA3ZGIxYmQwMDNhOWZlMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/a4f14ce193406f6d4a72e4be30e43f173d86f198","sha":"a4f14ce193406f6d4a72e4be30e43f173d86f198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/a4f14ce193406f6d4a72e4be30e43f173d86f198"}],"sha":"88fe4360fea326fb8998a15c07db1bd003a9fe0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/88fe4360fea326fb8998a15c07db1bd003a9fe0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81605929?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulrahmancodes","id":81605929,"login":"abdulrahmancodes","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNjA1OTI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/a4f14ce193406f6d4a72e4be30e43f173d86f198/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T00:52:50Z","email":"81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdul Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T00:52:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(server): run server route dispatch jobs ahead of the trigger fan-out (#25701)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen a server route resolver dispatches to a target logic function,\n`ServerRouteTriggerService.enqueueTargetFunction` adds one job to the\nlogic function queue at the queue''s default priority. That is the same\npriority as the database-event trigger fan-out, which puts every\nsubscribed logic function of every workspace on the same queue: Last\nContact on `person.updated`, `messageParticipant.updated` and\n`calendarEventParticipant.updated`, Call Recorder on `calendarEvent.*`.\nDuring a mailbox or calendar import that line is thousands of Lambda\nexecutions long, and the per-app enqueue throttle still lets through 500\njobs a minute per install and 2,000 a minute per app.\n\nA route dispatch is different from that fan-out: it is the tail of an\ninbound webhook that someone is waiting on. For the Slack assistant it\nis the step that creates the Slack Assistant Request record, and in\nproduction that record has been showing up minutes after the message,\nbefore the assistant worker even starts. The Slack app side of this was\naddressed in #25676; this is the server side.\n\n## What\n\n- Route dispatch jobs are enqueued with\n`SERVER_ROUTE_DISPATCH_JOB_PRIORITY` (1). Lower runs first in BullMQ, so\nthey go ahead of the trigger fan-out (queue default 4) and of\napplication-enqueued jobs (`ENQUEUE_JOB_PRIORITY`, 10) on the same\nqueue.\n- Nothing else changes: same queue, same retry limit and backoff, same\njob data.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- The change is two lines in `server-route-trigger.service.ts` plus the\nconstant. The job options type already declares `priority`, and the\nBullMQ driver already forwards an explicit priority over the queue\ndefault (`bullmq.driver.ts`, `options?.priority ??\nMESSAGE_QUEUE_WORKER_CONFIG[queueName].priority`).\n- No behavioural test exists for this service (its unit spec was removed\nin #24094); CI lint and typecheck cover the change.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01GWwrhW5s8bR2TVtKsQdSu2)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25701?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"a932dc48de09e5700daef019ad808304ae0eef16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/a932dc48de09e5700daef019ad808304ae0eef16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/a4f14ce193406f6d4a72e4be30e43f173d86f198","verification":{"payload":"tree a932dc48de09e5700daef019ad808304ae0eef16\nparent b29a8f267f2415dd0ea61537f1d5d2b913f80dad\nauthor Abdul Rahman <81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1789001570 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789001570 +0000\n\nfeat(server): run server route dispatch jobs ahead of the trigger fan-out (#25701)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen a server route resolver dispatches to a target logic function,\n`ServerRouteTriggerService.enqueueTargetFunction` adds one job to the\nlogic function queue at the queue''s default priority. That is the same\npriority as the database-event trigger fan-out, which puts every\nsubscribed logic function of every workspace on the same queue: Last\nContact on `person.updated`, `messageParticipant.updated` and\n`calendarEventParticipant.updated`, Call Recorder on `calendarEvent.*`.\nDuring a mailbox or calendar import that line is thousands of Lambda\nexecutions long, and the per-app enqueue throttle still lets through 500\njobs a minute per install and 2,000 a minute per app.\n\nA route dispatch is different from that fan-out: it is the tail of an\ninbound webhook that someone is waiting on. For the Slack assistant it\nis the step that creates the Slack Assistant Request record, and in\nproduction that record has been showing up minutes after the message,\nbefore the assistant worker even starts. The Slack app side of this was\naddressed in #25676; this is the server side.\n\n## What\n\n- Route dispatch jobs are enqueued with\n`SERVER_ROUTE_DISPATCH_JOB_PRIORITY` (1). Lower runs first in BullMQ, so\nthey go ahead of the trigger fan-out (queue default 4) and of\napplication-enqueued jobs (`ENQUEUE_JOB_PRIORITY`, 10) on the same\nqueue.\n- Nothing else changes: same queue, same retry limit and backoff, same\njob data.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- The change is two lines in `server-route-trigger.service.ts` plus the\nconstant. The job options type already declares `priority`, and the\nBullMQ driver already forwards an explicit priority over the queue\ndefault (`bullmq.driver.ts`, `options?.priority ??\nMESSAGE_QUEUE_WORKER_CONFIG[queueName].priority`).\n- No behavioural test exists for this service (its unit spec was removed\nin #24094); CI lint and typecheck cover the change.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01GWwrhW5s8bR2TVtKsQdSu2)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25701?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqof9yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzF4QAC8fuGtL2lBF20SctPJkOwnr\nMjjC11OQYTaW/NsfZS7QnOPjr4+9QFmg/v5ONAH8INv8V0eepCzU96hsefsjxVe2\nCQIJpWyjhUyAcXE3Z6SH1UujvdXELKZEEQc3m6aNPWrYhX5Mo0XB1Xr+qpiNyCzf\nsZWnth9I8DBpOdit9beAoqCMJHrx1NaZaLXp0L+AQAEpFhBmvfm2YQ8GMrSFcUPW\nkkwzM8JUhL6yXVMX+4M72/FJp5j2kIM6rlLyybjK7RYpDqktr6E2CqsU2SYXHiet\npl465kgxJHPar9K6UM/Ny4XifCKl3WOBIr1h63JSDxQ04S/zba/QwDCG/P41XyQJ\nzqz5ZuH3lGX61T+MxyVaC8EyX9aAphGBaw4fv1yw4hYonlayu4f99oRIvFJT07ui\neBdZvCjGl9M5LepvDpZwXFpXI2vhxvrFb+usWs1YoGf65gCFxpXHPmU2a2cVtknU\nQ0QEvQhKx/tBuSjVRs9dsF/bJ21HltFSQQ/lQQmBzu+ax1PwwwK6gCYVRJKvssVv\ngZNTe3xPL5kRW4Udf2PWIkKHqfbL4Q3BUu3zKhuI/bmXa9WIElmUeatI2ekOrUC8\nGp5gz8PCTZl4Dwn64k/cgexjYS+0MvfxdA3OSILsY0MOS1Pksh3nWJ/KT9rI0ouf\nooIj3bkMivbyB3+SL6Nx\n=H6xk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/a4f14ce193406f6d4a72e4be30e43f173d86f198","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGE0ZjE0Y2UxOTM0MDZmNmQ0YTcyZTRiZTMwZTQzZjE3M2Q4NmYxOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/b29a8f267f2415dd0ea61537f1d5d2b913f80dad","sha":"b29a8f267f2415dd0ea61537f1d5d2b913f80dad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b29a8f267f2415dd0ea61537f1d5d2b913f80dad"}],"sha":"a4f14ce193406f6d4a72e4be30e43f173d86f198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/a4f14ce193406f6d4a72e4be30e43f173d86f198"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62795688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/neo773","id":62795688,"login":"neo773","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzk1Njg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b29a8f267f2415dd0ea61537f1d5d2b913f80dad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:52:54Z","email":"62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com","name":"neo773"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:52:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let marketers schedule a campaign for a later send (#25563)\n\nCloses twentyhq/core-team-issues#2540\n\nAdds `messageCampaign.scheduledAt`. The send side panel gains a Delivery\nsection: send now, or pick a date and time. A scheduled campaign moves\nto `SCHEDULED` and a delayed job on the delayed-jobs queue revalidates\nand sends it when its time comes, the same mechanism the workflow delay\naction uses.\n\nReopening the panel on a scheduled campaign offers to move it, or to\nsend ahead of the time it holds. The job only fires while the campaign\nstill names the time it was queued for, so rewriting that time calls the\nold send off with no job to remove. Cancel returns a scheduled campaign\nto your drafts, and the hourly recovery cron releases anything still\nscheduled an hour past due.\n\nBehind `IS_EMAIL_GROUP_ENABLED`. Verified end to end against a local\nstack: scheduled 5 minutes out, fired 3s after its time, 167 sent / 0\nfailed; rescheduling left the stale job to no-op rather than\ndouble-send.\n\nOne thing worth knowing at review time: `generated-metadata/graphql.ts`\nand the client SDK schema each carry a hand-added `scheduledAt` line on\n`SendMessageCampaignInput`, because codegen needs a running server.\nRegenerating produces the same result.\n\n## Scheduling a campaign\n\nPicking **Send later** prefills the next half hour and names the time\nzone. A time in the past blocks the send.\n\n| Delivery choice | Time picked |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Delivery\ndropdown](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8a919645-4f93-4678-a4b4-13712f916aa7)\n| ![Send later\nprefilled](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d4f792a7-4b62-4e13-adca-6d25381b92c1)\n|\n\n| Past time refused | Scheduled |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Invalid past\ntime](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f68e8900-2fbe-4bdb-b9c4-52d305710c17)\n| ![Scheduled\nconfirmation](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ebcc87a7-9ae6-4d94-b1df-2db1a81b5e80)\n|\n\n## Moving or overtaking a scheduled send\n\nReopening the panel shows the time the campaign is holding, and the\nbutton becomes **Reschedule campaign**. Switching to **Send now** sends\nahead of it.\n\n| Reschedule | Send ahead of the held time |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Reschedule\npanel](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/baed862d-e39c-4ef2-9de9-ced99d5680fc)\n| ![Send\nearly](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d55a057c-3e5b-44bd-a8a5-89e214b3c847)\n|\n\n## Scheduled state\n\nA scheduled campaign is read-only, keeps Cancel and Test, and shows its\nsend time on the record and in the list.\n\n| Record page | All campaigns |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Scheduled record\npage](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/be8884bc-0db0-4b9e-9e8f-1870e29fa0a7)\n| ![List with\nscheduled](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/727dca5c-fa3b-4f1d-a18a-518ded7ab228)\n|\n\n<details>\n<summary>Remaining screens</summary>\n\nDraft composer, the send panel before a choice is made, the calendar\nopen, the state just before scheduling, the confirmation after a\nreschedule, and the unschedule modal.\n\n![Campaigns\nlist](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/301ea4a8-d3d2-48fe-9b9a-e09e63f73611)\n![Draft\ncomposer](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3515222f-fbcc-4e4e-a5b7-25da9980409a)\n![Send panel, send\nnow](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c10bfeef-a78f-4e7e-9f70-a7e4fb2ed89f)\n![Calendar\nopen](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/47cbbe0f-def8-44a7-b3cd-425ccbd46980)\n![Ready to\nschedule](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a894dd0-3f5a-4df0-8e2d-f6fb0056ab35)\n![Rescheduled\nconfirmation](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b483981c-3935-4e8a-96d9-f566c401b9a9)\n![Unschedule\nmodal](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19304003-c981-4563-9152-4025762d084c)\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"d02cef8e59509c8021bb16bbbb89cc780a109726","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/d02cef8e59509c8021bb16bbbb89cc780a109726"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/b29a8f267f2415dd0ea61537f1d5d2b913f80dad","verification":{"payload":"tree d02cef8e59509c8021bb16bbbb89cc780a109726\nparent 9c787ab5dbe523090c0e801511f294aac4a29852\nauthor neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com> 1788987174 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788987174 +0200\n\nLet marketers schedule a campaign for a later send (#25563)\n\nCloses twentyhq/core-team-issues#2540\n\nAdds `messageCampaign.scheduledAt`. The send side panel gains a Delivery\nsection: send now, or pick a date and time. A scheduled campaign moves\nto `SCHEDULED` and a delayed job on the delayed-jobs queue revalidates\nand sends it when its time comes, the same mechanism the workflow delay\naction uses.\n\nReopening the panel on a scheduled campaign offers to move it, or to\nsend ahead of the time it holds. The job only fires while the campaign\nstill names the time it was queued for, so rewriting that time calls the\nold send off with no job to remove. Cancel returns a scheduled campaign\nto your drafts, and the hourly recovery cron releases anything still\nscheduled an hour past due.\n\nBehind `IS_EMAIL_GROUP_ENABLED`. Verified end to end against a local\nstack: scheduled 5 minutes out, fired 3s after its time, 167 sent / 0\nfailed; rescheduling left the stale job to no-op rather than\ndouble-send.\n\nOne thing worth knowing at review time: `generated-metadata/graphql.ts`\nand the client SDK schema each carry a hand-added `scheduledAt` line on\n`SendMessageCampaignInput`, because codegen needs a running server.\nRegenerating produces the same result.\n\n## Scheduling a campaign\n\nPicking **Send later** prefills the next half hour and names the time\nzone. A time in the past blocks the send.\n\n| Delivery choice | Time picked |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Delivery\ndropdown](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8a919645-4f93-4678-a4b4-13712f916aa7)\n| ![Send later\nprefilled](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d4f792a7-4b62-4e13-adca-6d25381b92c1)\n|\n\n| Past time refused | Scheduled |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Invalid past\ntime](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f68e8900-2fbe-4bdb-b9c4-52d305710c17)\n| ![Scheduled\nconfirmation](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ebcc87a7-9ae6-4d94-b1df-2db1a81b5e80)\n|\n\n## Moving or overtaking a scheduled send\n\nReopening the panel shows the time the campaign is holding, and the\nbutton becomes **Reschedule campaign**. Switching to **Send now** sends\nahead of it.\n\n| Reschedule | Send ahead of the held time |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Reschedule\npanel](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/baed862d-e39c-4ef2-9de9-ced99d5680fc)\n| ![Send\nearly](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d55a057c-3e5b-44bd-a8a5-89e214b3c847)\n|\n\n## Scheduled state\n\nA scheduled campaign is read-only, keeps Cancel and Test, and shows its\nsend time on the record and in the list.\n\n| Record page | All campaigns |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Scheduled record\npage](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/be8884bc-0db0-4b9e-9e8f-1870e29fa0a7)\n| ![List with\nscheduled](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/727dca5c-fa3b-4f1d-a18a-518ded7ab228)\n|\n\n<details>\n<summary>Remaining screens</summary>\n\nDraft composer, the send panel before a choice is made, the calendar\nopen, the state just before scheduling, the confirmation after a\nreschedule, and the unschedule modal.\n\n![Campaigns\nlist](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/301ea4a8-d3d2-48fe-9b9a-e09e63f73611)\n![Draft\ncomposer](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3515222f-fbcc-4e4e-a5b7-25da9980409a)\n![Send panel, send\nnow](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c10bfeef-a78f-4e7e-9f70-a7e4fb2ed89f)\n![Calendar\nopen](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/47cbbe0f-def8-44a7-b3cd-425ccbd46980)\n![Ready to\nschedule](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a894dd0-3f5a-4df0-8e2d-f6fb0056ab35)\n![Rescheduled\nconfirmation](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b483981c-3935-4e8a-96d9-f566c401b9a9)\n![Unschedule\nmodal](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19304003-c981-4563-9152-4025762d084c)\n\n</details>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoccmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9zIQAIHEqbdxLUPj0KVB3ywyVA6d\nwOz03hUemI5A10zvn8j9FSuHeH9pXzNOuC+T3p5oQg8d3b1EOUZQmv1LAhhpuQ7P\nPMmqGMCsjWShk0URiGoaRm/6AKBLXk3EzJS1aj/zaSiisZpVFbJ+KPiDN4FAVBUR\n1t+BIb/ovyaf/avrqNkPA1Pgj4sYP7FXqEj61gTngeaI18+FVLDPnlfgnrOYXuAs\njF6A6QSN+rg7DKUj+L73NgITjdknV0VZwaFt7i0t5yEi2q4Qtj7zUoNam0fNIlag\npop2CrEjNxy1T58S8ZP8dc+6lznCiLy0q9wPJAS7pxnLsR+aGT4XEcNr3LwSmfFn\nNbZ/ED/4Bir9HuyfILFJIKUItgW6Gdxsh8So1YlkfvyKwzVHQM4EuLUCiT62a6aL\noPt4ptlxQmX5vGCZgIU6RQx6T2F55g5rb0ZSDHVdX9Kr81fUWbXEodP2HGdlByMx\nWC/Kpi/y1dlP6q3xxq5D9o9oPmIufwpkuNJQzfxt+UIkf7IylqzrjO9UuvxfIb88\n1PeO+Vt7Q3/HvBh2g+3h6ivXFNhED9E09m8Q4x4fGgcwC5uf2WEMQpr2LeHi3F16\nqRWhuwrhalg5/kfzPtJWsyFFggEwcCpK07LMzozZuWSJWQ5rZYAQwl+HwkDaCKOd\noGle3KrCFANJIbsa4+Ae\n=daU3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/b29a8f267f2415dd0ea61537f1d5d2b913f80dad","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGIyOWE4ZjI2N2YyNDE1ZGQwZWE2MTUzN2YxZDVkMmI5MTNmODBkYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/9c787ab5dbe523090c0e801511f294aac4a29852","sha":"9c787ab5dbe523090c0e801511f294aac4a29852","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9c787ab5dbe523090c0e801511f294aac4a29852"}],"sha":"b29a8f267f2415dd0ea61537f1d5d2b913f80dad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/b29a8f267f2415dd0ea61537f1d5d2b913f80dad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9c787ab5dbe523090c0e801511f294aac4a29852/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:45:32Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:45:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(admin-panel): stop calling a metered line item''s quantity \"seats\" (#25698)\n\nFound while QA-ing the admin panel on twenty-main.com. A workspace''s\nBilling tab renders its resource-credit line item as **`1 seats`**.\n\nTwo things wrong with that, one cosmetic and one not:\n\n- It never agreed in number — every count read \"seats\".\n- More importantly it is false. `formatItemValue` labelled *every*\nsubscription item''s quantity as seats, but only a licensed base product\nsells seats. A resource-credit item is metered: it bills on usage, and\nthe quantity Stripe carries on it is bookkeeping that charges nothing.\nLabelling it seats tells an operator the workspace pays per user for\nsomething it does not.\n\n## What changed\n\nOnly a `BASE_PRODUCT` item is labelled seats now, pluralised through\nlingui. Other products show the bare count, which sits next to the\n`RESOURCE_CREDIT` tag the row already renders, so the number keeps its\ncontext without the formatter claiming to know what it counts.\n\n`includedCredits` gained the same number agreement (`1 credit/period`\nrather than `1 credits/period`).\n\nThe formatter moved to `utils/formatSubscriptionItemValue.ts` so the\nbehaviour is testable rather than sealed inside the component;\n`formatCurrency` went with it, being its only caller. The component\nkeeps a thin wrapper, so the call sites are unchanged.\n\nProduct keys are compared against the generated `BillingProductKey` enum\nrather than local string constants — the admin schema types `productKey`\nas a plain `String`, but this component already maps `planKey` onto the\ngenerated `BillingPlanKey` the same way.\n\n## Verification\n\n9 unit tests cover base-product vs metered vs unknown-product labelling,\nboth singular cases, the joined form, a zero quantity (kept, not read as\nabsent), and the empty item rendering an em dash.\n\nOne of them corrected an assumption of mine rather than the code:\n`Intl.NumberFormat` accepts any well-formed three-letter currency code,\nso `ZZZ` formats fine and only a malformed code reaches the\n`formatCurrency` fallback. The test now exercises that path with a\ngenuinely malformed code.\n\n`tsgo --noEmit` clean on twenty-front, oxlint 0 errors, format clean.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is on `main` already; it predates #25603 and is not a regression\nfrom it.\n\n## A separate defect in the same area, not fixed here\n\nThe workspace billing page renders `Credits` and `Total` as `-`.\n`useBillingSubscriptionCost` computes:\n\n```ts\nconst creditsSubtotalCents = currentResourceCreditSubscriptionItem?.unitAmount;\nconst totalCents =\n  isDefined(seatsSubtotalCents) && isDefined(creditsSubtotalCents)\n    ? seatsSubtotalCents + creditsSubtotalCents\n    : undefined;\n```\n\nso a resource-credit item with no `unitAmount` suppresses the total\nentirely — the page shows `Seats $12` and then no total at all.\n\nI reproduced this on a workspace created and subscribed from scratch\nduring QA, not only on existing ones.\n\nAn earlier version of this description asserted that this was stale\ncatalog data which a `billing:sync-plans-data` re-sync would clear. I\ncan''t support that: the price catalog is global, so a newly created\nworkspace reads the same price rows, and reproducing it there does not\ndistinguish bad data from a code path that cannot cope with a\nlegitimately absent unit amount (a tiered/metered Stripe price has\n`unit_amount: null` by design). Settling it needs a look at the stored\n`billingPrice` row or the Stripe price object, which I could not do from\nthe browser.\n\nEither way the `&&` looks worth revisiting: when credits contribute\nnothing, showing the seats subtotal beats showing nothing.","tree":{"sha":"cfd83564e028ca4bc0fd2912ad283fcd8725e7dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/cfd83564e028ca4bc0fd2912ad283fcd8725e7dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/9c787ab5dbe523090c0e801511f294aac4a29852","verification":{"payload":"tree cfd83564e028ca4bc0fd2912ad283fcd8725e7dc\nparent 1ceb09b5e655c608d83ef7941840af0d1777c91e\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1788986732 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788986732 +0200\n\nfix(admin-panel): stop calling a metered line item''s quantity \"seats\" (#25698)\n\nFound while QA-ing the admin panel on twenty-main.com. A workspace''s\nBilling tab renders its resource-credit line item as **`1 seats`**.\n\nTwo things wrong with that, one cosmetic and one not:\n\n- It never agreed in number — every count read \"seats\".\n- More importantly it is false. `formatItemValue` labelled *every*\nsubscription item''s quantity as seats, but only a licensed base product\nsells seats. A resource-credit item is metered: it bills on usage, and\nthe quantity Stripe carries on it is bookkeeping that charges nothing.\nLabelling it seats tells an operator the workspace pays per user for\nsomething it does not.\n\n## What changed\n\nOnly a `BASE_PRODUCT` item is labelled seats now, pluralised through\nlingui. Other products show the bare count, which sits next to the\n`RESOURCE_CREDIT` tag the row already renders, so the number keeps its\ncontext without the formatter claiming to know what it counts.\n\n`includedCredits` gained the same number agreement (`1 credit/period`\nrather than `1 credits/period`).\n\nThe formatter moved to `utils/formatSubscriptionItemValue.ts` so the\nbehaviour is testable rather than sealed inside the component;\n`formatCurrency` went with it, being its only caller. The component\nkeeps a thin wrapper, so the call sites are unchanged.\n\nProduct keys are compared against the generated `BillingProductKey` enum\nrather than local string constants — the admin schema types `productKey`\nas a plain `String`, but this component already maps `planKey` onto the\ngenerated `BillingPlanKey` the same way.\n\n## Verification\n\n9 unit tests cover base-product vs metered vs unknown-product labelling,\nboth singular cases, the joined form, a zero quantity (kept, not read as\nabsent), and the empty item rendering an em dash.\n\nOne of them corrected an assumption of mine rather than the code:\n`Intl.NumberFormat` accepts any well-formed three-letter currency code,\nso `ZZZ` formats fine and only a malformed code reaches the\n`formatCurrency` fallback. The test now exercises that path with a\ngenuinely malformed code.\n\n`tsgo --noEmit` clean on twenty-front, oxlint 0 errors, format clean.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is on `main` already; it predates #25603 and is not a regression\nfrom it.\n\n## A separate defect in the same area, not fixed here\n\nThe workspace billing page renders `Credits` and `Total` as `-`.\n`useBillingSubscriptionCost` computes:\n\n```ts\nconst creditsSubtotalCents = currentResourceCreditSubscriptionItem?.unitAmount;\nconst totalCents =\n  isDefined(seatsSubtotalCents) && isDefined(creditsSubtotalCents)\n    ? seatsSubtotalCents + creditsSubtotalCents\n    : undefined;\n```\n\nso a resource-credit item with no `unitAmount` suppresses the total\nentirely — the page shows `Seats $12` and then no total at all.\n\nI reproduced this on a workspace created and subscribed from scratch\nduring QA, not only on existing ones.\n\nAn earlier version of this description asserted that this was stale\ncatalog data which a `billing:sync-plans-data` re-sync would clear. I\ncan''t support that: the price catalog is global, so a newly created\nworkspace reads the same price rows, and reproducing it there does not\ndistinguish bad data from a code path that cannot cope with a\nlegitimately absent unit amount (a tiered/metered Stripe price has\n`unit_amount: null` by design). Settling it needs a look at the stored\n`billingPrice` row or the Stripe price object, which I could not do from\nthe browser.\n\nEither way the `&&` looks worth revisiting: when credits contribute\nnothing, showing the seats subtotal beats showing nothing.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqocVsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbakQABGVWBgWnGumSERWg3hz+pKN\nsbYhZ8ScHDWNS2EujcBli9qFDTEC7Ckz6B73LYIjndj/u9xviPZ16pApd8nXtF8k\n/NNjFZlkyyPClc5RNBFZSVfFshzvUcjKBcdmIi7Z6G8VcDZIUcgJqNDN8Pe2y4QK\nzwRUxxuEboen6sTgBM7z7+gj0Ngs/AA842U+0w0Twf9slU0Mgd8LXpEzkS0yQogV\nxxoZLV/1Zuv/8vRY+a7dDV7rdfj5t61dt/w5hQbgV58rR5NquFiy7BVXEzJ9aQKG\ngJM+ZV1rokFCdI92jltvOAtueFsBnwN46djTg6x9ppUAEmqUI0/FBpNBfFYasS9H\nQ/OfwBq/GrUNRpgL1VIpPsdt/pf71FRC4/OHDXgDnG6U9w3FCnaG5OhVDxpB7hBR\ngm+54sr1B99qsR/Atj36HsfiyV4RkMJ+qSXLAhQ9ug6HNBIIDYW5Tc0nqfhTpTdS\n/4McrorGo7LUiVDp9KtVZ7Gj8RqvwC0XBM70GDxFNbaWynUjsVYbYrBJ63wFoFBA\nBVKfZLBdIbaFXmypEkYf+8LFc7UGDpa93wqs60OZSebuW5qJmeF95b5wnAhlHRs7\nuTZVI++CAhbQuJ/ZZnk1/EdMnUxvojDfkKQLm+Dbbcj/xmOaBafR1Xcpebiik9Vp\nHRshpH+ZkSRQUI9vXsIi\n=BJsf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/9c787ab5dbe523090c0e801511f294aac4a29852","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDljNzg3YWI1ZGJlNTIzMDkwYzBlODAxNTExZjI5NGFhYzRhMjk4NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/1ceb09b5e655c608d83ef7941840af0d1777c91e","sha":"1ceb09b5e655c608d83ef7941840af0d1777c91e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/1ceb09b5e655c608d83ef7941840af0d1777c91e"}],"sha":"9c787ab5dbe523090c0e801511f294aac4a29852","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/9c787ab5dbe523090c0e801511f294aac4a29852"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/1ceb09b5e655c608d83ef7941840af0d1777c91e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:44:33Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:44:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(billing): stop writing a raw ISO timestamp into a credit grant''s reason (#25699)\n\nFound while QA-ing the admin panel on twenty-main.com. A carry-forward\ngrant''s Reason column reads:\n\n> Carried over from the period starting 2026-06-18T13:44:32.000Z\n\nThat string is composed by `billingCreditRolloverService`, persisted on\nthe grant, and rendered as-is in the admin panel''s grant table — where\nevery neighbouring column (`Granted`, `Expires`) shows a formatted date.\nSo the one field that explains *why* a grant exists is also the only one\nshowing a machine timestamp.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe date goes through `i18n.date`, the same formatter the billing emails\nalready use for `renewsAt`, with the same options. The reason now reads\n\"Carried over from the period starting June 18, 2026\".\n\nIt is pinned to `timeZone: ''UTC''`, which is the part worth a reviewer''s\nattention. Stripe''s period boundaries are UTC instants, and a boundary\nat `00:00Z` formatted in the server''s local zone renders as the previous\nday — the same class of shift that #25603 fixed when `date-fns` under\n`Europe/Paris` turned `2026-04-01T00:00Z` into March 31 and put a\ngrant''s expiry inside the period it was meant to close. Formatting a\nboundary is a narrower case than doing arithmetic on one, but it fails\nthe same way and reads as an off-by-one to whoever is auditing the\nledger.\n\n## What deliberately stays ISO\n\n- The rollover failure log (`billing-credit-rollover.service.ts:70`),\nwhich wants precision, not prose.\n- The idempotency keys (`rollover:` and `carry-forward:`), whose values\nmust not move — reformatting those would re-key every in-flight rollover\nand defeat the `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` that makes settlement\nre-runnable.\n\n## Verification\n\n3 unit tests: a mid-day instant, a UTC-midnight boundary, and a\nlate-evening boundary, each asserting the date stays on its own day.\n\nThe suite passes under `UTC`, `America/Los_Angeles`,\n`Pacific/Kiritimati`, `Europe/Paris` and `Australia/Lord_Howe` — the\nmidnight case is the one that fails without the UTC pin.\n\n215 tests pass across `billing` and `billing-webhook`. `tsgo --noEmit`,\ndiff lint and format all clean.\n\n## Scope\n\nReasons already written keep their ISO timestamps; this only affects\nrollovers from here on. Rewriting stored reasons would mean a data\nmigration over free text an operator may have edited, which is not worth\nit for a display nit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WUgiBH9NveL7LmjFpUqNyh)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25699?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"cf88ee3f48f3378e9d94cb720e89e27b05ac2c82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/cf88ee3f48f3378e9d94cb720e89e27b05ac2c82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/1ceb09b5e655c608d83ef7941840af0d1777c91e","verification":{"payload":"tree cf88ee3f48f3378e9d94cb720e89e27b05ac2c82\nparent 15955aeaae58e669bce1e197dfcd0cedb6d0b7a2\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1788986673 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788986673 +0200\n\nfix(billing): stop writing a raw ISO timestamp into a credit grant''s reason (#25699)\n\nFound while QA-ing the admin panel on twenty-main.com. A carry-forward\ngrant''s Reason column reads:\n\n> Carried over from the period starting 2026-06-18T13:44:32.000Z\n\nThat string is composed by `billingCreditRolloverService`, persisted on\nthe grant, and rendered as-is in the admin panel''s grant table — where\nevery neighbouring column (`Granted`, `Expires`) shows a formatted date.\nSo the one field that explains *why* a grant exists is also the only one\nshowing a machine timestamp.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe date goes through `i18n.date`, the same formatter the billing emails\nalready use for `renewsAt`, with the same options. The reason now reads\n\"Carried over from the period starting June 18, 2026\".\n\nIt is pinned to `timeZone: ''UTC''`, which is the part worth a reviewer''s\nattention. Stripe''s period boundaries are UTC instants, and a boundary\nat `00:00Z` formatted in the server''s local zone renders as the previous\nday — the same class of shift that #25603 fixed when `date-fns` under\n`Europe/Paris` turned `2026-04-01T00:00Z` into March 31 and put a\ngrant''s expiry inside the period it was meant to close. Formatting a\nboundary is a narrower case than doing arithmetic on one, but it fails\nthe same way and reads as an off-by-one to whoever is auditing the\nledger.\n\n## What deliberately stays ISO\n\n- The rollover failure log (`billing-credit-rollover.service.ts:70`),\nwhich wants precision, not prose.\n- The idempotency keys (`rollover:` and `carry-forward:`), whose values\nmust not move — reformatting those would re-key every in-flight rollover\nand defeat the `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` that makes settlement\nre-runnable.\n\n## Verification\n\n3 unit tests: a mid-day instant, a UTC-midnight boundary, and a\nlate-evening boundary, each asserting the date stays on its own day.\n\nThe suite passes under `UTC`, `America/Los_Angeles`,\n`Pacific/Kiritimati`, `Europe/Paris` and `Australia/Lord_Howe` — the\nmidnight case is the one that fails without the UTC pin.\n\n215 tests pass across `billing` and `billing-webhook`. `tsgo --noEmit`,\ndiff lint and format all clean.\n\n## Scope\n\nReasons already written keep their ISO timestamps; this only affects\nrollovers from here on. Rewriting stored reasons would mean a data\nmigration over free text an operator may have edited, which is not worth\nit for a display nit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WUgiBH9NveL7LmjFpUqNyh)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25699?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqocUxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbtsQAHQl2cK7DUhbs0WjGoXEiX/9\nxB4VFjKDG9vQd68GRl6gshu1rInlygTkhJBIQXnAqRwKoEMWmzWyjUfFOXgx3PYb\nWc89TZDsxWFpWq4twxJJREEqJz93/kB5L9szyDjTnIaekgJs3gpn2kVztkb6PhzH\nVzL+Z/nvlsCX7QujmS+yba5h6KZUq62EoPlqVj7QfKRzE1IEwE8ummznLBDcbA9z\nIjqna1EE4nb62/5W82yxV4eMrYygCIieOmvzV0FeaLZhYQzO4kA5FH2yuNSqx2tD\n9Zu+3z6yxFlKqk4OmfZ7UGzjhExRGFg7rrvHkx9CvzLPp0qhd+Hg39Kvog22nGHc\n0y2ghW+xA+bdc5kpVYW/UEpD7gQy1YvOCohuz0qMXKcxlwkNSQyD0da86EXxPzKZ\nfKKEj2ZWH/OQ7jHQ6v59hl6qS+9h8KHTobmrCPdsKK0DPFHhR3Zp+wA8JS015I0F\n3NXCwebHw2cRyrPeBYh4CwBw3IooctEPVzoqsvbCboOQN/Ma2kXFhqlVdpAtQPM2\nKnPY2FJeToxVceYufrPDZjy4pY3eqpAphQbc3+IOMhggaI4+0m4dhZx+Yt++ejge\n+EBgCGsYAH4a1zyZSKEZ5pRhN3L7Rkh2bIg11Y3baICoOlfyXDOZfcPgP/28a+ln\n49r/ikhGfuNjiMygsamA\n=hdZ6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/1ceb09b5e655c608d83ef7941840af0d1777c91e","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDFjZWIwOWI1ZTY1NWM2MDhkODNlZjc5NDE4NDBhZjBkMTc3N2M5MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/15955aeaae58e669bce1e197dfcd0cedb6d0b7a2","sha":"15955aeaae58e669bce1e197dfcd0cedb6d0b7a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/15955aeaae58e669bce1e197dfcd0cedb6d0b7a2"}],"sha":"1ceb09b5e655c608d83ef7941840af0d1777c91e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/1ceb09b5e655c608d83ef7941840af0d1777c91e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81605929?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulrahmancodes","id":81605929,"login":"abdulrahmancodes","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNjA1OTI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abdulrahmancodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/15955aeaae58e669bce1e197dfcd0cedb6d0b7a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:53:15Z","email":"81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdul Rahman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:53:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(slack): keep assistant feedback buttons on long answers (#25693)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe Slack assistant dropped its whole `blocks` array for answers over\n12,000 characters:\n\n```ts\nmessageBlocks:\n  responseText.length > SLACK_MARKDOWN_BLOCK_MAX_LENGTH\n    ? undefined\n    : buildSlackAssistantAnswerBlocks({ responseText, requestId: record.id }),\n```\n\nThat array carries the `context_actions` block holding the thumbs up /\nthumbs down `feedback_buttons`, whose `block_id` is the request id that\n`slack-assistant-feedback.ts` uses to tie a rating back to the record.\nNothing downstream re-added it: `getSlackChatMessageBodyFields` only\nemits `blocks` when `messageBlocks` is non-empty, and\n`getSlackMessageBodyFallbacks` only ever *removes* blocks. So the\nlongest answers, the ones most likely to be wrong, collected no quality\nsignal at all.\n\n## What the Slack API actually allows\n\nTwo limits shaped the fix, both verified against current docs:\n\n- The [markdown block\nreference](https://docs.slack.dev/reference/block-kit/blocks/markdown-block)\nstates the 12,000 character cap is **cumulative across all markdown\nblocks in a single payload**, not per block. Splitting a long answer\nover several markdown blocks buys nothing.\n-\n[`chat.postMessage`](https://docs.slack.dev/reference/methods/chat.postMessage/)\napplies the same 12,000 cap to `markdown_text`.\n\nSo a message body over 12,000 characters cannot be rendered in one Slack\nmessage by any route. The old escape hatch was not trading buttons for\ncontent, it dropped the buttons and hit the same wall anyway, degrading\nthrough `markdown_text` to unformatted `text`.\n\n## Change\n\n`buildSlackAssistantAnswerBlocks` now always returns both blocks. When\nthe answer exceeds the limit it shortens the markdown body and appends a\npointer to the full answer on the request record:\n\n> _Shortened to fit Slack. [Read the full answer in\nTwenty](…/object/slackAssistantRequest/&lt;id&gt;)_\n\nThe cut goes through `truncateOnGraphemeBoundary`, extracted from\n`readSlackBodyPreview` which already used `Intl.Segmenter` for this, so\nit cannot split a surrogate pair or a ZWJ emoji sequence. It then\nprefers the last line break in the budget, falling back to the last\nwhitespace boundary, so it stays out of the middle of a word or a URL.\n\nThe `block_id` is still the request id, so `slack-assistant-feedback.ts`\nis unchanged. `messageText` stays the full answer, so if Slack refuses\nblocks the existing markdown and plain text fallbacks still deliver it,\nand a very long answer never fails outright.\n\nAlso extracts `SLACK_ASSISTANT_REQUEST_OBJECT_NAME` to a shared\nconstant, now that both the worker and the block builder need it.\n\n## Frequency\n\nThis path is close to unreachable in practice. The assistant system\nprompt pushes hard for short replies (lead with the answer, at most 5\nrecords, one bullet each, no tables, no sign-offs), and 12,000\ncharacters is roughly 2,000 words. I could not sample real\n`slackAssistantRequest.responseText` lengths to confirm, so the fix is\ndeliberately kept small rather than a chunking system.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `yarn lint` — clean\n- `yarn typecheck` — clean\n- `yarn test:unit` — 630 passed\n- `yarn test` — 58 passed across 6 files, against a twenty-server built\nfrom this branch\n\nThe integration test for the over-limit case previously asserted\n`blocks` was `undefined`; it now asserts the `context_actions` block\nsurvives with `block_id === request.id`, that the markdown block stays\nwithin the limit, and that the record still stores the full untruncated\n`responseText`. Unit coverage adds the grapheme case: a family emoji\nwhose 11 code units do not divide the budget evenly, so a plain slice\nfails the test.\n\n## Not addressed\n\n`feedbackRating` is written to the record but is not surfaced anywhere:\nno view, filter, or aggregation reads it, so a rating is only visible to\nsomeone who opens the object and looks at the column. Worth a follow-up,\nbut out of scope here.","tree":{"sha":"72a9b3249c9f18fc5773e63c178ea99011271eaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/72a9b3249c9f18fc5773e63c178ea99011271eaa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/15955aeaae58e669bce1e197dfcd0cedb6d0b7a2","verification":{"payload":"tree 72a9b3249c9f18fc5773e63c178ea99011271eaa\nparent 40e95c5cfe19a15cb54da887c9cfda2441656145\nauthor Abdul Rahman <81605929+abdulrahmancodes@users.noreply.github.com> 1788983595 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788983595 +0000\n\nfix(slack): keep assistant feedback buttons on long answers (#25693)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe Slack assistant dropped its whole `blocks` array for answers over\n12,000 characters:\n\n```ts\nmessageBlocks:\n  responseText.length > SLACK_MARKDOWN_BLOCK_MAX_LENGTH\n    ? undefined\n    : buildSlackAssistantAnswerBlocks({ responseText, requestId: record.id }),\n```\n\nThat array carries the `context_actions` block holding the thumbs up /\nthumbs down `feedback_buttons`, whose `block_id` is the request id that\n`slack-assistant-feedback.ts` uses to tie a rating back to the record.\nNothing downstream re-added it: `getSlackChatMessageBodyFields` only\nemits `blocks` when `messageBlocks` is non-empty, and\n`getSlackMessageBodyFallbacks` only ever *removes* blocks. So the\nlongest answers, the ones most likely to be wrong, collected no quality\nsignal at all.\n\n## What the Slack API actually allows\n\nTwo limits shaped the fix, both verified against current docs:\n\n- The [markdown block\nreference](https://docs.slack.dev/reference/block-kit/blocks/markdown-block)\nstates the 12,000 character cap is **cumulative across all markdown\nblocks in a single payload**, not per block. Splitting a long answer\nover several markdown blocks buys nothing.\n-\n[`chat.postMessage`](https://docs.slack.dev/reference/methods/chat.postMessage/)\napplies the same 12,000 cap to `markdown_text`.\n\nSo a message body over 12,000 characters cannot be rendered in one Slack\nmessage by any route. The old escape hatch was not trading buttons for\ncontent, it dropped the buttons and hit the same wall anyway, degrading\nthrough `markdown_text` to unformatted `text`.\n\n## Change\n\n`buildSlackAssistantAnswerBlocks` now always returns both blocks. When\nthe answer exceeds the limit it shortens the markdown body and appends a\npointer to the full answer on the request record:\n\n> _Shortened to fit Slack. [Read the full answer in\nTwenty](…/object/slackAssistantRequest/&lt;id&gt;)_\n\nThe cut goes through `truncateOnGraphemeBoundary`, extracted from\n`readSlackBodyPreview` which already used `Intl.Segmenter` for this, so\nit cannot split a surrogate pair or a ZWJ emoji sequence. It then\nprefers the last line break in the budget, falling back to the last\nwhitespace boundary, so it stays out of the middle of a word or a URL.\n\nThe `block_id` is still the request id, so `slack-assistant-feedback.ts`\nis unchanged. `messageText` stays the full answer, so if Slack refuses\nblocks the existing markdown and plain text fallbacks still deliver it,\nand a very long answer never fails outright.\n\nAlso extracts `SLACK_ASSISTANT_REQUEST_OBJECT_NAME` to a shared\nconstant, now that both the worker and the block builder need it.\n\n## Frequency\n\nThis path is close to unreachable in practice. The assistant system\nprompt pushes hard for short replies (lead with the answer, at most 5\nrecords, one bullet each, no tables, no sign-offs), and 12,000\ncharacters is roughly 2,000 words. I could not sample real\n`slackAssistantRequest.responseText` lengths to confirm, so the fix is\ndeliberately kept small rather than a chunking system.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `yarn lint` — clean\n- `yarn typecheck` — clean\n- `yarn test:unit` — 630 passed\n- `yarn test` — 58 passed across 6 files, against a twenty-server built\nfrom this branch\n\nThe integration test for the over-limit case previously asserted\n`blocks` was `undefined`; it now asserts the `context_actions` block\nsurvives with `block_id === request.id`, that the markdown block stays\nwithin the limit, and that the record still stores the full untruncated\n`responseText`. Unit coverage adds the grapheme case: a family emoji\nwhose 11 code units do not divide the budget evenly, so a plain slice\nfails the test.\n\n## Not addressed\n\n`feedbackRating` is written to the record but is not surfaced anywhere:\nno view, filter, or aggregation reads it, so a rating is only visible to\nsomeone who opens the object and looks at the column. Worth a follow-up,\nbut out of scope here.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqobk7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAokQAERb5BbsAd4IMsfXtzdHtkR+\nFIaknU3E7WQ1USmTILyz9tTAmnXGm1MekfdJZhpU2mCU3zTc488YDvt7M4jZgWR/\nfQMO4riKXMX+AMmGNQLfMger5q6efA7Zoqa8r7qk9GhGRtrtJ07N2qiw3DXwz97M\n3BBZC2STJx8vxKSA0BSajJfP65eD4/dgY2JJQf4LNed4Ptrky3dsoXPdx6/jxcAx\ngXQUptJoTJE7tO/UoeKb52EYMZdAZW64Vb+uzxQK4NXuHTWU8QhU43liHa7DWVH2\nZGaoCNLAqBjYaUu8592NktdQQ2Cg2u2Zp88QdXxm/4LP5EzRUll0ShcH62QUtcSB\n075v20sURHLLoCqGy1MuGhkC4ijD5pgNd2GBpAinJNmOH5zVVYYQnB5FlNXamBPY\nSGsKApFGThFBntQPkw9subuf4ZGgN1MTopPBi1grgdJ4hfGTYTKoPbxUxk7+Y0i3\nMVlgkvysRrkLtYrGWp4S8apdtfez+0XKT6erKzm79RYd4Qt4tIrwarU1eyL0MuZJ\nwWnqzUKq1e5hgS1gs2Mf3NPORqn2sdi7opHEXljqbEihM6eJj/n8x+GaXgnBc+8H\nE0qIj+9KCfBU2cZ9X/SlgorOQZVzAOHD/EJ0p5ZvGbzlcwIfeeffkLo7TuuVuGbT\nWkKQmad3rYmpTguTrvq1\n=lDZd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/15955aeaae58e669bce1e197dfcd0cedb6d0b7a2","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDE1OTU1YWVhYWU1OGU2NjliY2UxZTE5N2RmY2QwY2VkYjZkMGI3YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/40e95c5cfe19a15cb54da887c9cfda2441656145","sha":"40e95c5cfe19a15cb54da887c9cfda2441656145","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/40e95c5cfe19a15cb54da887c9cfda2441656145"}],"sha":"15955aeaae58e669bce1e197dfcd0cedb6d0b7a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/15955aeaae58e669bce1e197dfcd0cedb6d0b7a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62795688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/neo773","id":62795688,"login":"neo773","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzk1Njg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/40e95c5cfe19a15cb54da887c9cfda2441656145/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:31:22Z","email":"62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com","name":"neo773"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:31:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Debounce calendar webhook syncs instead of throwing when one is running (#25656)\n\nProviders send one push per calendar change and the payload carries no\nevent data, so every notification enqueued its own sync job. On a queue\nwith concurrency 5 a burst ran several at once: one won the\ncompare-and-set on `syncStage`, the rest threw\n`CALENDAR_CHANNEL_SYNC_ALREADY_IN_PROGRESS` into Sentry and were retried\nby BullMQ.\n\nMeasured in prod over 6h: ~1270 of these jobs per hour, median gap\nbetween two jobs on the same channel is 18s, and a 30s window collapses\n46% of them. Collapsing a burst is safe because the sync fetches against\nthe stored sync cursor and picks up everything since the last run.\n\nLosing the race is a normal outcome, so the service returns it instead\nof throwing and the job reschedules a busy channel with bounded backoff.\n\nAlso fixes the integration drain barrier, which counted delayed jobs as\npending without ever advancing them, making any delayed job untestable.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25656?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"624cc2e6c9c180202af0d709cebef1a094bccaa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/624cc2e6c9c180202af0d709cebef1a094bccaa7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/40e95c5cfe19a15cb54da887c9cfda2441656145","verification":{"payload":"tree 624cc2e6c9c180202af0d709cebef1a094bccaa7\nparent ea401a1d3d402ad837701fed8263e15e44a0a4c9\nauthor neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com> 1788982282 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788982282 +0000\n\nDebounce calendar webhook syncs instead of throwing when one is running (#25656)\n\nProviders send one push per calendar change and the payload carries no\nevent data, so every notification enqueued its own sync job. On a queue\nwith concurrency 5 a burst ran several at once: one won the\ncompare-and-set on `syncStage`, the rest threw\n`CALENDAR_CHANNEL_SYNC_ALREADY_IN_PROGRESS` into Sentry and were retried\nby BullMQ.\n\nMeasured in prod over 6h: ~1270 of these jobs per hour, median gap\nbetween two jobs on the same channel is 18s, and a 30s window collapses\n46% of them. Collapsing a burst is safe because the sync fetches against\nthe stored sync cursor and picks up everything since the last run.\n\nLosing the race is a normal outcome, so the service returns it instead\nof throwing and the job reschedules a busy channel with bounded backoff.\n\nAlso fixes the integration drain barrier, which counted delayed jobs as\npending without ever advancing them, making any delayed job untestable.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25656?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqobQaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxkcQACWI2XPOsY7XfVJC5LQRX19t\nSQJh9SjhUpN1cUWfLVvD+KB059QCDFKfqfIg96bAdUQDtPCXhEQ93DU9Jlore+Re\nRBfOTwRMIVh4I8DKE7G6VK9a0rL6qaZBIDFqGm0kdlAQDkDE02A4xPmr8dKwgZ7Z\n5kKuQeC60ijZs/HeOAADXk7M9l17gQc9DsPIDoVKpskG4L8gR3+y3tPj3YfvhMuD\nO/1JoxW7iu6UZrfPll6N4khiWYdaY+AhhRxpS17lvoXWYu6V3dpTLxy3yD7OBHTx\nv+b/TVQdtX1p/Hd28kYhXOuor4mIGRMIaYCfGHPFcm9bkfyV4Q1KDldapNYlylxw\nR79ifUiDCYlwpzNxk96MPqam2iGxx21mlWAcAFqA2ESw0HHqrD6yxjvbHKrsBSq/\nkX3ezj4Q13I+iavkkQRDbymy7s40mB1D8scsvZ6psFDILdfwYtempjD/EL1vjEwc\nhd0pOBOL48OA8msdYEtcHcEGwY2Td11t6NFBGissEU+u9cWwmaIOUyInqA5z0Q/E\nYVY3seGJOTclapmV+dO9qtjUbBQ9QzUGBz9dpFRosRtOiQozqIIf4ka6N8isFv3m\nHlDICZrNE7dswBbLBuUTt/TlyvM+UyLfy2OjhmVXoq2VwJSpAOQxj+Waia+Clhk5\np3njsN4N86z7NJp3Z4Pm\n=ChM7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/40e95c5cfe19a15cb54da887c9cfda2441656145","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKDQwZTk1YzVjZmUxOWExNWNiNTRkYTg4N2M5Y2ZkYTI0NDE2NTYxNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/ea401a1d3d402ad837701fed8263e15e44a0a4c9","sha":"ea401a1d3d402ad837701fed8263e15e44a0a4c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/ea401a1d3d402ad837701fed8263e15e44a0a4c9"}],"sha":"40e95c5cfe19a15cb54da887c9cfda2441656145","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/40e95c5cfe19a15cb54da887c9cfda2441656145"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/ea401a1d3d402ad837701fed8263e15e44a0a4c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:59:34Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:59:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Export an application''s navigation menu items (#25687)\n\n## What\n\n`exportApplication` now returns an application''s navigation menu items.\nThis is the server half of the navigation slice of `yarn twenty pull`;\nwriting them as `defineNavigationMenuItem()` files follows in a separate\nPR, so `pull` ignores `manifest.navigationMenuItems` until then.\n\nIt matters most for the Custom application, where the sidebar is built\nthrough the UI. On a dev workspace its five navigation items were the\nlargest remaining block the export could not carry.\n\n## How\n\n- **An inverse converter** mirrors the forward one property by property.\nEvery compared property is emitted, the one rename is\n`targetObjectMetadataUniversalIdentifier` to\n`targetObjectUniversalIdentifier`, and each nullable slot is omitted\nrather than written as `null`, since every optional on\n`NavigationMenuItemManifest` is a bare `string`. An empty `name` is kept\nrather than dropped, because a folder is allowed to have one and the\nforward converter would turn a dropped value back into `null`, which\nwould diff forever.\n- **`reconstructNavigationMenuItemsManifest`** emits the collection\nordered by universal identifier and classifies what the manifest cannot\ncarry:\n- an item with a user workspace is `EXCLUDED` as a personal navigation\nitem, which is Twenty''s favourites mechanism and is structurally\nunexportable since the forward converter hardcodes the column to null;\n- an item pinned to a record is `EXCLUDED` under its own reason. It is\nnot personal, it is inexpressible: the manifest has no slot for the\ntarget record, and it points at workspace data rather than at metadata;\n- an item is `UNSUPPORTED` when one of its references would not resolve\non a fresh install, since a defined but unresolvable reference aborts\nthe migration rather than degrading. A target the application owns but\ndid not export is refused; a target the install recreates or already has\nis kept, which covers an engine-derived row (deterministic identifier,\nrecreated on install, for instance an object''s index view) and a row of\nanother application (resolved once that application is installed\nalongside);\n- a folder is a navigation item too and follows that same rule: an item\nheld by a folder of the application that was not exported is dropped, to\na fixed point because dropping a folder can orphan the items nested\nunder it, while a folder of another application is kept and a folder\nthat exists nowhere is dropped.\n- **One reference check for the four reasons.**\n`getUnresolvableObjectReason` was the object case of a rule the view,\npage layout and page layout widget reasons all need, so it becomes\n`getUnresolvableReferenceReason`, parameterised by the referenced\nmetadata name and picking the flat maps with\n`getMetadataFlatEntityMapsKey`. Its four callers are unchanged in\nbehaviour and wording.\n- The navigation branch in the classifier is **removed**. The\nreconstructor now emits one coverage row per item and owns both\nexclusions, so the branch could never fire again and would have hidden a\nreconstructor bug behind a plausible-looking status.\n- The compared-properties guard covers the kind, so a newly compared\nproperty fails compilation instead of silently going unexported.\n\nThe navigation item Twenty creates when an object is made in the UI is\nexported like any other row. The engine only creates it on the\nobject-creation path, never on the manifest sync path, so re-installing\nan exported manifest cannot double-create it, and dropping it would\nleave a clone without its sidebar entry.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Export integration spec: the fixture gains a navigation folder, an\nobject item inside it and a view item pointing at the engine-derived\nindex view of the application''s own object, with fixed identifiers named\nin the snapshot and asserted `EXPORTED`. Both dry-run gates still yield\nzero actions, and the snapshot is stable across two runs.\n- A converter parity spec (forward then inverse reproduces the manifest,\ninverse then forward compares as no diff, a minimal manifest emits no\nnulls, an empty name survives) and a reconstructor spec covering\nordering, both exclusions, the unsupported reasons, a target the\napplication does not own, an engine-derived target, a folder with its\nitems, a foreign folder, a folder that does not exist, and the nested\nfolder cascade.\n- Verified on a dev workspace: the Custom application''s five navigation\nitems now export, ordered by identifier and carrying only the properties\nthe workspace set, and a dry-run sync of the pulled tree reports no\nnavigation actions. The unsupported bucket dropped from 24 rows to 19.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25687?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"0ad56298de575ece29439381d6eee3b69ba96b98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/0ad56298de575ece29439381d6eee3b69ba96b98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/ea401a1d3d402ad837701fed8263e15e44a0a4c9","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ad56298de575ece29439381d6eee3b69ba96b98\nparent 801746815b0c3a183f3ad68b0ee52d25197ee36c\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1788976774 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788976774 +0000\n\nExport an application''s navigation menu items (#25687)\n\n## What\n\n`exportApplication` now returns an application''s navigation menu items.\nThis is the server half of the navigation slice of `yarn twenty pull`;\nwriting them as `defineNavigationMenuItem()` files follows in a separate\nPR, so `pull` ignores `manifest.navigationMenuItems` until then.\n\nIt matters most for the Custom application, where the sidebar is built\nthrough the UI. On a dev workspace its five navigation items were the\nlargest remaining block the export could not carry.\n\n## How\n\n- **An inverse converter** mirrors the forward one property by property.\nEvery compared property is emitted, the one rename is\n`targetObjectMetadataUniversalIdentifier` to\n`targetObjectUniversalIdentifier`, and each nullable slot is omitted\nrather than written as `null`, since every optional on\n`NavigationMenuItemManifest` is a bare `string`. An empty `name` is kept\nrather than dropped, because a folder is allowed to have one and the\nforward converter would turn a dropped value back into `null`, which\nwould diff forever.\n- **`reconstructNavigationMenuItemsManifest`** emits the collection\nordered by universal identifier and classifies what the manifest cannot\ncarry:\n- an item with a user workspace is `EXCLUDED` as a personal navigation\nitem, which is Twenty''s favourites mechanism and is structurally\nunexportable since the forward converter hardcodes the column to null;\n- an item pinned to a record is `EXCLUDED` under its own reason. It is\nnot personal, it is inexpressible: the manifest has no slot for the\ntarget record, and it points at workspace data rather than at metadata;\n- an item is `UNSUPPORTED` when one of its references would not resolve\non a fresh install, since a defined but unresolvable reference aborts\nthe migration rather than degrading. A target the application owns but\ndid not export is refused; a target the install recreates or already has\nis kept, which covers an engine-derived row (deterministic identifier,\nrecreated on install, for instance an object''s index view) and a row of\nanother application (resolved once that application is installed\nalongside);\n- a folder is a navigation item too and follows that same rule: an item\nheld by a folder of the application that was not exported is dropped, to\na fixed point because dropping a folder can orphan the items nested\nunder it, while a folder of another application is kept and a folder\nthat exists nowhere is dropped.\n- **One reference check for the four reasons.**\n`getUnresolvableObjectReason` was the object case of a rule the view,\npage layout and page layout widget reasons all need, so it becomes\n`getUnresolvableReferenceReason`, parameterised by the referenced\nmetadata name and picking the flat maps with\n`getMetadataFlatEntityMapsKey`. Its four callers are unchanged in\nbehaviour and wording.\n- The navigation branch in the classifier is **removed**. The\nreconstructor now emits one coverage row per item and owns both\nexclusions, so the branch could never fire again and would have hidden a\nreconstructor bug behind a plausible-looking status.\n- The compared-properties guard covers the kind, so a newly compared\nproperty fails compilation instead of silently going unexported.\n\nThe navigation item Twenty creates when an object is made in the UI is\nexported like any other row. The engine only creates it on the\nobject-creation path, never on the manifest sync path, so re-installing\nan exported manifest cannot double-create it, and dropping it would\nleave a clone without its sidebar entry.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Export integration spec: the fixture gains a navigation folder, an\nobject item inside it and a view item pointing at the engine-derived\nindex view of the application''s own object, with fixed identifiers named\nin the snapshot and asserted `EXPORTED`. Both dry-run gates still yield\nzero actions, and the snapshot is stable across two runs.\n- A converter parity spec (forward then inverse reproduces the manifest,\ninverse then forward compares as no diff, a minimal manifest emits no\nnulls, an empty name survives) and a reconstructor spec covering\nordering, both exclusions, the unsupported reasons, a target the\napplication does not own, an engine-derived target, a folder with its\nitems, a foreign folder, a folder that does not exist, and the nested\nfolder cascade.\n- Verified on a dev workspace: the Custom application''s five navigation\nitems now export, ordered by identifier and carrying only the properties\nthe workspace set, and a dry-run sync of the pulled tree reports no\nnavigation actions. The unsupported bucket dropped from 24 rows to 19.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25687?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoZ6WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA90oQAKhg4rdJpBRyRcYSVfwN4Dgk\npB/rDZ79ZanoIWam3FE5vcm23e20to4Fc3M5ZomAiKdcn6gtAOQO31m8MbGRWNMB\nLBSTPe84wNk3j2rIyBf/sMYEEuApYGCzo1qhGR1+uWIYAtZeyKFt5vENHmm5R2xS\nII5T08RvPZXG8YatC1sDL1uiyyiHHrXydk5kKQ4mk63ByFpSS7dD5QQb+hZFK1ci\n1uOlOxq8+e5NFhfTt3sLMQE/v8gcFZYFc5O5gSDNFRa/T1orlkbcItY4XiJDxm4y\nKdCRG+srgYTDH1UZJcMGmyr5eOYjfVWKryd2AnZGO8ivanyYEWwHJXSeQmEUByqg\nXXruzSWx4MzwU7DAkFBkvSp8i0/zLGYUNKVZvYEARYRJtz7DeEyIEsBlfizVph5M\n3SWDuEI50ul8LSswFqR0zsAJVapp7Z1kHQARwQZLQvi5TLo0bkjbd9NNjLTSHcVa\n/4j6NacWdEPdJY6KZAVTqSIxL8hyrmyIGScU8ITJMsLQWCoNefa3smxTzn6165Fj\nRB2KGNy3nFhYJ0MsHO9J+NJ4zL6T2BpfpsSrXMybIykALx7JwpN/Qh+G307j4COn\nRVPOAuFCr/RP4wKG9s1QomL2Xs7xruHu511JBMdm6JBRytPXkjZ+k0deRuLNJYnp\nUBPIfq/k6DHZjlf5UKIf\n=zHQV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/ea401a1d3d402ad837701fed8263e15e44a0a4c9","node_id":"C_kwDOTzfBtdoAKGVhNDAxYTFkM2Q0MDJhZDgzNzcwMWZlZDgyNjNlMTVlNDRhMGE0Yzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/melon-1999/twenty/commit/801746815b0c3a183f3ad68b0ee52d25197ee36c","sha":"801746815b0c3a183f3ad68b0ee52d25197ee36c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/801746815b0c3a183f3ad68b0ee52d25197ee36c"}],"sha":"ea401a1d3d402ad837701fed8263e15e44a0a4c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/ea401a1d3d402ad837701fed8263e15e44a0a4c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/commits/801746815b0c3a183f3ad68b0ee52d25197ee36c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:36:31Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:36:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: sync AI model catalog (#25691)\n\nAutomated daily sync of the AI model catalog.\n\n- Model identity, pricing, context windows and availability come from\n[models.dev](https://models.dev).\n- Intelligence, speed and cost per task come from [Artificial\nAnalysis](https://artificialanalysis.ai/),\n  which requires `ARTIFICIAL_ANALYSIS_API_KEY`.\n\nNew models meeting inclusion criteria (tool calling, pricing data,\ncontext limits) are added\nautomatically. Benchmark data is best-effort: a model Artificial\nAnalysis has not rated keeps\nevery other field and simply carries no `benchmark` entry.\n\n**Please review before merging** and check the coverage summary below\nfor models that silently\nstopped matching.\n\n### Benchmark coverage\n\n- General-purpose models with an intelligence index: **51/80** (64%)\n- Specialized models excluded from the denominator: 10\n\n<details><summary>General-purpose models with no matched intelligence\nindex</summary>\n\n- openai/gpt-5-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.2-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.3-codex-spark\n- openai/gpt-5.5-pro\n- openai/gpt-5.6\n- openai/gpt-5.4-pro\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\n- anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\n- anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5\n- anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5\n- google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview-customtools\n- mistral/mistral-small-2506\n- mistral/open-mixtral-8x22b\n- mistral/open-mixtral-8x7b\n- mistral/open-mistral-7b\n- mistral/mistral-medium-latest\n- mistral/mistral-medium-2604\n- mistral/mistral-large-2512\n- mistral/ministral-8b-latest\n- mistral/mistral-nemo\n- mistral/mistral-small-latest\n- mistral/mistral-large-latest\n- mistral/mistral-large-2411\n- mistral/mistral-small-2603\n- mistral/mistral-medium-2505\n- mistral/ministral-3b-latest\n- mistral/mistral-medium-2508\n- xai/grok-4.20-0309-reasoning\n- xai/grok-build-0.1\n\n</details>\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25691?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\nCo-authored-by: FelixMalfait <6399865+FelixMalfait@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"aeb6b2d97dfdf57d385d13686f9f2c4b946e5e59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/trees/aeb6b2d97dfdf57d385d13686f9f2c4b946e5e59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melon-1999/twenty/git/commits/801746815b0c3a183f3ad68b0ee52d25197ee36c","verification":{"payload":"tree aeb6b2d97dfdf57d385d13686f9f2c4b946e5e59\nparent 2f3f58300931c41b7a37da49e851794b97a20d5a\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1788971791 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788971791 +0200\n\nchore: sync AI model catalog (#25691)\n\nAutomated daily sync of the AI model catalog.\n\n- Model identity, pricing, context windows and availability come from\n[models.dev](https://models.dev).\n- Intelligence, speed and cost per task come from [Artificial\nAnalysis](