/f08217e480c595837c6a8eb1a9eacf66e081eeb1"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commit/5810000ba8ef9d1adcd012cbfbe811dbb4a47764","sha":"5810000ba8ef9d1adcd012cbfbe811dbb4a47764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/5810000ba8ef9d1adcd012cbfbe811dbb4a47764"}],"sha":"9a91961dafefa0e1cd17e447e7c4ac3edb078464","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/9a91961dafefa0e1cd17e447e7c4ac3edb078464"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/5810000ba8ef9d1adcd012cbfbe811dbb4a47764/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:08:40Z","email":"t@t","name":"t"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:10:43Z","email":"t@t","name":"t"},"message":"fix(security): stop the secret gate scanning files git cannot track\n\ncheck-secrets.sh runs `gitleaks dir` over the whole working tree. That includes\ngitignored content, so it reported 811 findings and blocked every push in this\nrepository. A gate that always fails is not a strict gate - it is one people\nlearn to bypass, which is worse than not having it.\n\nVerified before changing anything, rather than assuming they were noise:\n\n  git ls-files      ZERO of the 811 findings are in a tracked file\n  git check-ignore  every path below is gitignored, so none can reach a commit\n\n  799  playground/              vendored third-party scratch repos\n    5  src-tauri/target/        Rust build artefacts (.rmeta binaries)\n    2  .env                     local environment file\n    2  deploy/vps/.env{,.local} VPS env files\n    1  .cyberos/                local install state\n\nAdded to the existing allowlist, which already carries a `dist/` entry for\nexactly this reason (\"derived/gitignored build outputs\"), so this follows the\nprecedent in the file rather than inventing a mechanism.\n\nDetection is unchanged for anything git can track, and I checked that rather\nthan asserting it:\n\n  - `check-secrets.sh --probe-fixture` still fails on its planted AWS key\n  - a secret planted in tools/install/ (a tracked directory) is still detected\n\nSide effect worth having: the scan drops from 1.73 GB in 53s to 276 MB in 7s,\nbecause it no longer walks two gigabytes of other people''s repositories.\n\nNote on scope: this sits on the fin branch because it is what unblocks pushing\nat all. It is unrelated to the finance work and is a reasonable candidate to\ncherry-pick onto main on its own.\n\nThe deeper issue is left alone deliberately: the gate scans the working tree\nrather than what is actually being pushed, so any new gitignored directory will\nre-block it and need another allowlist entry. Making it scan tracked content\ninstead would fix the class, but that is a change to security tooling semantics\nand belongs to whoever owns this gate, not to a passing finance task.","tree":{"sha":"3afe5132a916379488e007ca45edc25a9977356a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/git/trees/3afe5132a916379488e007ca45edc25a9977356a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/git/commits/5810000ba8ef9d1adcd012cbfbe811dbb4a47764","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commit/5810000ba8ef9d1adcd012cbfbe811dbb4a47764","node_id":"C_kwDOTz96edoAKDU4MTAwMDBiYThlZjlkMWFkY2QwMTJjYmZiZTgxMWRiYjRhNDc3NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commit/ca18c66d9cb2d4e755e0288ec9167e2c9922e4bf","sha":"ca18c66d9cb2d4e755e0288ec9167e2c9922e4bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/ca18c66d9cb2d4e755e0288ec9167e2c9922e4bf"}],"sha":"5810000ba8ef9d1adcd012cbfbe811dbb4a47764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/5810000ba8ef9d1adcd012cbfbe811dbb4a47764"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/ca18c66d9cb2d4e755e0288ec9167e2c9922e4bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T17:01:32Z","email":"t@t","name":"t"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T17:01:32Z","email":"t@t","name":"t"},"message":"feat(fin): add fin_login_attempts for durable login rate limiting\n\nTASK-AUTH-102.\n\nThe finance app limited login attempts with a module-level Map. On Vercel\neach lambda instance has private memory, so the counter was per instance\nrather than per IP.\n\nMeasured against production on 2026-08-05, not inferred:\n  sequential  attempts 1-4 -> 401, 5-8 -> 429   (appeared to work)\n  parallel    12 concurrent attempts from the SAME already-locked-out IP\n              -> 12 x 401, every one allowed through\n\nConcurrency defeated it entirely. This matters more than it would in a\nprivate app: finance decision D-23 keeps all read endpoints public, so the\nadmin login is the only barrier in front of every write endpoint.\n\nAdds one table with the same posture as the other fin_* tables: RLS enabled\nand forced, a single tenant-scoped policy carrying USING and WITH CHECK, and\nno nil-UUID escape hatch (migration 0001 removed those deliberately).\n\nfinance_app is granted SELECT, INSERT and UPDATE but NOT DELETE. The login\npath never needs DELETE, and withholding it means a compromised application\ncredential cannot erase evidence of a brute-force attempt.\n\nVerified after applying: relrowsecurity=t, relforcerowsecurity=t,\nhas_table_privilege(finance_app, DELETE)=false.","tree":{"sha":"7134cbcfc7c93525dcc8a932f9c4933d667f0799","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/git/trees/7134cbcfc7c93525dcc8a932f9c4933d667f0799"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/git/commits/ca18c66d9cb2d4e755e0288ec9167e2c9922e4bf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commit/ca18c66d9cb2d4e755e0288ec9167e2c9922e4bf","node_id":"C_kwDOTz96edoAKGNhMThjNjZkOWNiMmQ0ZTc1NWUwMjg4ZWM5MTY3ZTJjOTkyMmU0YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commit/41264e2affb93da8aa167cde1da3ffd14c1956ec","sha":"41264e2affb93da8aa167cde1da3ffd14c1956ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/41264e2affb93da8aa167cde1da3ffd14c1956ec"}],"sha":"ca18c66d9cb2d4e755e0288ec9167e2c9922e4bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/ca18c66d9cb2d4e755e0288ec9167e2c9922e4bf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/41264e2affb93da8aa167cde1da3ffd14c1956ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:46:21Z","email":"t@t","name":"t"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:46:21Z","email":"t@t","name":"t"},"message":"feat(fin): least-privilege database role for the finance ledger (TASK-DATA-103)\n\nFirst migration for the fin service. The fin_* tables were created directly\nagainst the Supabase database and have never been in version control; this\ndoes not define them, it fixes how the application connects to them.\n\nThe finance app connects as `postgres`, which holds rolbypassrls. RLS is\nenabled AND forced on all four fin_* tables with correct tenant-scoped\npolicies carrying USING and WITH CHECK, and none of it applied, because\nBYPASSRLS exempts the role from row security entirely. Demonstrated on\n2026-08-05: with app.current_tenant_id set to a foreign tenant, a query\nstill returned another tenant''s row. Tenant isolation was resting solely on\nevery query in lib/db_pg.js remembering to filter by tenant_id.\n\n- creates finance_app: LOGIN, NOSUPERUSER, no DDL rights, and NOBYPASSRLS by\n  default (the keyword is deliberately not written, since only a superuser\n  may set it and Supabase''s postgres role is not one)\n- asserts rolbypassrls is false and raises rather than proceeding if not\n- grants SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on the four fin_* tables only\n- removes the nil-UUID escape hatch from all four policies, which granted\n  cross-tenant access to anyone able to set CFO_TENANT_ID, validated only as\n  UUID-shaped\n\nVerified against the live database as finance_app: correct tenant sees its\n58 lookups, a foreign tenant sees zero, no tenant set sees zero, pg_shadow\nis unreadable, CREATE TABLE is denied. The finance app''s full database\nsurface (import, settings, PDF-lock update, deletes) passes under the role.","tree":{"sha":"d58d57951edffb3610e5aaad3c978fc88dacff5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/git/trees/d58d57951edffb3610e5aaad3c978fc88dacff5b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/git/commits/41264e2affb93da8aa167cde1da3ffd14c1956ec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commit/41264e2affb93da8aa167cde1da3ffd14c1956ec","node_id":"C_kwDOTz96edoAKDQxMjY0ZTJhZmZiOTNkYThhYTE2N2NkZTFkYTNmZmQxNGMxOTU2ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commit/f08217e480c595837c6a8eb1a9eacf66e081eeb1","sha":"f08217e480c595837c6a8eb1a9eacf66e081eeb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/f08217e480c595837c6a8eb1a9eacf66e081eeb1"}],"sha":"41264e2affb93da8aa167cde1da3ffd14c1956ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/christymelan09-blip/cyberos/commits/41264e2affb93da8aa167cde1da3ffd14c1956ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9297971?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zintaen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zintaen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zintaen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zintaen/gists{/gist_id}","